E["npc:alanndarian-nightsong"] = {t="npc",n="Alanndarian Nightsong",z="darkshore",s="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf resident of Auberdine in Darkshore dedicated to tending to the region's beleaguered fauna. She works alongside travelers to remedy the blights plaguing the local wildlife, particularly the native striders and forest creatures corrupted by dark forces.",h="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf resident of Auberdine in Darkshore dedicated to tending to the region's...",sec={{t="A Caretaker in Auberdine",b="Situated in the coastal settlement of Auberdine, Alanndarian Nightsong watches over the fragile ecological balance of Darkshore. As mysterious taints seep into the soil and waters, the creatures of the ancient woods have begun to succumb to sickness and unnatural aggression. Alanndarian acts as a guardian and naturalist, seeking practical remedies to ease their suffering and restore their natural vigor.",sp=0},{t="Healing the Stront and Sick",b="Much of Alanndarian's attention is focused on identifying the root causes of the afflictions spreading through the local fauna. Through careful gathering of botanical reagents and researching the principal water sources of the region, she crafts salves and curative draughts. She enlists wandering adventurers to apply these cures directly to ailing forest creatures, attempting to stave off the spreading corruption before it permanently overtakes Darkshore's wildlife.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf naturalist located in the port town of Auberdine in Darkshore. She focuses on caring for afflicted local wildlife and finding herbal cures for the unnatural sicknesses plaguing the coast.",al={"alanndarian","who is alanndarian nightsong","alanndarian nightsong lore"}},{q="Where can Alanndarian Nightsong be found?",a="She makes her home in Auberdine, the primary night elf hub along the foggy coastline of Darkshore.",al={"alanndarian location","where is alanndarian","find alanndarian nightsong"}},{q="What tasks does she ask adventurers to perform?",a="Alanndarian asks adventurers to track down the sources of sickness tainting Darkshore's creatures, collect vital curative components from the wilderness, and administer remedies directly to ailing animals such as deer and striders.",al={"alanndarian quests","auberdine sick animal quests","what does alanndarian want"}},{q="Is she related to other Nightsongs?",a="Her surname connects her to other prominent night elves of the Nightsong lineage, such as Master Nightsong in Darnassus and Falara Nightsong, though her immediate daily focus remains the stewardship of Darkshore's wilderness.",al={"nightsong family","master nightsong relation","falara nightsong"}},{q="Why are the creatures in Darkshore sick?",a="The woodlands and waterways of Darkshore suffer from an creeping corruption seeping through ancient ruins and corrupted elementals, driving native wildlife to madness and wasting sickness.",al={"why are darkshore animals sick","corrupted striders darkshore","darkshore blight"}},{q="Can she train tallstrider pets?",a="Though rumor holds she has great knowledge of striders, she does not actively train tamed pets for hunters in the field, keeping her focus instead on wild populations.",al={"tallstrider trainer","strider training auberdine","train my strider"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alanndarian serves as a vital contact for Alliance travelers landing in Auberdine, helping newcomers understand the delicate state of northern Kalimdor's wilderness.",["race:NightElf"]="Her reverence for the forest and dedication to purifying corrupted wildlife reflect the core preservationist ideals of the kaldorei.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find a kindred spirit in Alanndarian's pursuit to identify waterborne taints and physically cure poisoned creatures across Darkshore.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters attuned to beast behaviors assist Alanndarian closely, using their tracking skills to locate wild striders and distressed game."},kw={"alanndarian","auberdine","cure","darkshore","kaldorei","nightsong","strider","wildlife"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:6124","quest:6123","quest:6122","quest:2178","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},src={"Alanndarian Nightsong"}}
E["npc:archaeologist-flagongut"] = {t="npc",n="Archaeologist Flagongut",z="darkshore",s="Archaeologist Flagongut is a dwarven scholar representing the Explorers' League, stationed within the Deepwater Tavern at Menethil Harbor. Though originally en route to the local dig at the Whelgar Excavation Site, he becomes an important contact for field reports traveling across the sea from Darkshore.",h="Archaeologist Flagongut is a dwarven scholar representing the Explorers' League, stationed within the...",sec={{t="A Scholar in Port",b="Archaeologist Flagongut can be found resting with a mug in hand at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. Like many members of Ironforge's Explorers' League, he traveled west across Khaz Modan aiming to assist with discoveries near the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands. Despite being far from the high halls of the library, he maintains vital ties with field researchers, helping process lost relics and reports ferried across the Great Sea from remote expeditions.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Field",b="Dwarven curiosity is rarely confined to one continent, and Flagongut finds himself sorting through the chaotic field research of absent-minded colleagues operating on the shores of Kalimdor. When relics or notes recovered from the excavation sites of Darkshore arrive at the harbor, Flagongut ensures the findings are cataloged and delivered onward to the senior league leadership back in Ironforge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Archaeologist Flagongut?",a="Flagongut is a dwarven researcher from the Explorers' League. He is stationed in Menethil Harbor's Deepwater Tavern, where he reviews excavation field work and communicates with dig sites.",al={"who is flagongut","flagongut npc","archaeologist flagongut lore"}},{q="Why is Flagongut at the Deepwater Tavern?",a="He originally arrived at Menethil Harbor to reach the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands. While in port, he uses the tavern as a base to handle mail, incoming artifacts, and correspondence from abroad.",al={"why is flagongut in menethil","flagongut location","what is flagongut doing here"}},{q="How is Flagongut connected to Darkshore?",a="Flagongut serves as the Wetlands contact for the long-running research chain started by Prospector Remtravel in Darkshore. Adventurers crossing from Auberdine to Menethil bring Remtravel's findings directly to Flagongut to be passed along to Ironforge.",al={"flagongut darkshore connection","why darkshore quest in wetlands"}},{q="What organization does he belong to?",a="He belongs to the Explorers' League, King Magni Bronzebeard's royal society dedicated to uncovering the ancient origins, relics, and history of the dwarven race across Azeroth.",al={"flagongut faction","flagongut explorers league"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Flagongut represents the far-reaching ambitions of the Explorers' League, proving that even a tavern by the sea can serve as an outpost for piecing together Titan secrets.",["faction:Alliance"]="Flagongut acts as a logistical bridge between the night elf lands of Darkshore and the eastern Alliance strongholds of Khaz Modan."},kw={"archaeologist","deepwater tavern","explorers' league","flagongut","menethil harbor","remtravel","whelgar"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:deepwater-tavern","topic:explorers-league","quest:729","zone:wetlands","zone:darkshore","topic:dwarf"},src={"Archaeologist Flagongut"}}
E["npc:archaeologist-hollee"] = {t="npc",n="Archaeologist Hollee",z="darkshore",s="Archaeologist Hollee is a dwarven researcher stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine. Working on behalf of dwarven excavation interests, she keeps tabs on archaeological findings and surveys throughout the ancient, fog-shrouded wilderness of Darkshore. She frequently coordinates with prospectors scouring the region for relics and geological anomalies.",h="Archaeologist Hollee is a dwarven researcher stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Scholar in Kaldorei Lands",b="While Darkshore is predominantly guarded and settled by the night elves, the presence of dwarven scholars like Archaeologist Hollee reflects Ironforge's growing curiosity about Kalimdor. The League of Arathor and the Explorers' League send representatives far across the seas to uncover traces of ancient history, and Darkshore's ruins offer tempting ground for study. Hollee makes her temporary base out of Auberdine, acting as a regional contact for wandering surveyors and expedition teams.",sp=0},{t="Keeping Tabs on Remtravel",b="A major part of Hollee's day-to-day work involves tracking her fellow field researchers, particularly the scatterbrained Prospector Remtravel. Entrusted with significant surveying tasks across the wild coast, Remtravel often wanders far afield without reporting back on schedule. Hollee frequently enlists travelers passing through Auberdine to track him down, recover missing survey data, and ensure that field research does not fall prey to the local wildlife or encroaching threats.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Archaeologist Hollee?",a="Archaeologist Hollee is a dwarf stationed in Auberdine in Darkshore. She conducts and oversees regional field research on behalf of dwarven archaeological efforts on the western continent.",al={"who is hollee","hollee darkshore","dwarf in auberdine"}},{q="Where can Hollee be found?",a="She is located in the coastal port town of Auberdine, situated on the northern coast of Darkshore.",al={"hollee location","where is archaeologist hollee"}},{q="Why are dwarves conducting research in Darkshore?",a="Following the third war and the deepening alliance between Ironforge and the night elves, dwarven researchers have traveled to Kalimdor to study ancient relics, geological formations, and long-buried history that might shed light on their own ancestry.",al={"why are dwarves in darkshore","ironforge in kalimdor"}},{q="What trouble does she need help with?",a="Hollee is primarily concerned with Prospector Remtravel, an absent-minded surveyor who wandered off into the southern reaches of Darkshore and failed to report back with his findings.",al={"hollee quests","absent minded prospector quest"}},{q="What is the relationship between Hollee and Prospector Remtravel?",a="They are colleagues working on the same excavation and survey efforts in Darkshore. While Remtravel does the practical fieldwork out among the ruins, Hollee coordinates reports and liaises with travelers from Auberdine.",al={"who is remtravel","remtravel and hollee"}},{q="Does Hollee belong to the Explorers' League?",a="She represents dwarven archaeological and prospecting expeditions allied with Ironforge, which are typically organized under the aegis of the Explorers' League operating out of the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"explorers league hollee","hollee faction"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a compatriot so far across the sea in the misty woods of Darkshore is a reminder of Ironforge's boundless thirst for uncovering ancient history.",["faction:Alliance"]="Hollee represents the cooperation between the Eastern Kingdoms and the night elves, utilizing Auberdine as a base to study Kalimdor's distant past."},kw={"archaeologist hollee","auberdine","darkshore","explorers league","ironforge","prospector remtravel","the absent minded prospector","trouble in darkshore"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:729","quest:730","topic:dwarf"},src={"Archaeologist Hollee"}}
E["npc:asterion"] = {t="npc",n="Asterion",z="darkshore",s="Asterion is an ancient Highborne spirit bound to the ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore. Once the trusted second to governor Athrikus Narassin ten millennia ago, he was mysteriously imprisoned in a magical moonstone seal that held him through mortal life and into the afterlife. Today, his specter remains shackled to the ruined shrine, surrounded by demonic beasts and dreaming of liberation.",h="Asterion is an ancient Highborne spirit bound to the ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Servant of Ancient Splendor",b="Before the Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor, Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran were sister cities blessed by Queen Azshara herself. Azshara appointed Athrikus Narassin to govern the twin settlements, and Asterion served as his right hand. Respected for both his physical combat prowess and his command of arcane sorcery, Asterion lived among the people of Bashal'Aran while frequently traveling between the sister cities to manage the needs of their citizens.",sp=0},{t="The Moonstone Prison",b="For reasons lost to time, Asterion fell out of favor with his master. Athrikus fashioned a powerful moonstone seal, forging an inescapable magical cage to confine Asterion within Bashal'Aran. The imprisonment stretched through centuries of agonizing confinement; worse still, when Asterion finally perished, he discovered death offered no release. His spirit remained bound to the ruined shrine, left behind when the world cracked open and demons overran the ancient settlement.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance from the Grave",b="Though vile satyrs and grells roam the ruins of Bashal'Aran feeding on residual arcane power, they shun the shrine where Asterion's ghost lingers. If an Alliance adventurer retrieves the moonstone seal from the satyrs and shatters it in Ameth'Aran, Asterion's spectral chains finally break. Yet freedom does not bring him peace; sensing that Athrikus Narassin still endures, the ancient mage turns his thoughts from ten thousand years of despair toward vengeance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is an ancient Highborne ghost found at the ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore. Before the Sundering, he was an accomplished mage and the second-in-command to governor Athrikus Narassin.",al={"asterion lore","who is the ghost in bashal'aran","ghost elf darkshore"}},{q="Why is Asterion imprisoned?",a="Athrikus Narassin bound Asterion using a magical moonstone seal. The exact reasons for their falling out remain unknown, but the sorcery was so potent that even Asterion's death failed to break the enchantment, trapping his ghost for millennia.",al={"why is asterion trapped","asterion prison","why did athrikus trap asterion"}},{q="Why don't the satyrs in Bashal'Aran attack him?",a="While the satyrs and grells in the ruins feast on the lingering arcane energies of Bashal'Aran, they keep their distance from the shrine where Asterion is bound. They held possession of the moonstone seal that anchors his captivity rather than meddling directly with his spirit.",al={"do satyrs attack asterion","why demons leave asterion alone"}},{q="Where did Asterion live in life?",a="Asterion made his home among the people of Bashal'Aran, traveling frequently south to its twin city of Ameth'Aran to tend to civic affairs under the authority of Queen Azshara's governor.",al={"asterion home","where was asterion from"}},{q="What happens after you free him?",a="Once his seal is shattered in Ameth'Aran, Asterion is finally released from his agonizing spectral prison. However, instead of passing peacefully into the afterlife, he realizes that his old tormentor Athrikus still lives and turns his focus toward revenge.",al={"what happens to asterion","does asterion move on","asterion vengeance"},sp=1},{q="Is Asterion hostile to modern night elves?",a="No. Despite being an ancient Highborne from Queen Azshara's court, Asterion is peaceful toward Alliance travelers and seeks their assistance in breaking his ancient magical bondage.",al={"is asterion friendly","asterion alliance"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Asterion is a tragic relic from before the Sundering, showing the cruel internal politics that consumed the Highborne even before Azshara invited the Burning Legion into their lands.",["class:Mage"]="In life, Asterion was celebrated for his mastery of the arcane alongside his prowess in physical combat, making him an intriguing study in early Kaldorei spellcraft.",["faction:Alliance"]="Asterion is one of the rare Highborne spirits willing to trust and aid Alliance adventurers, seeking their help to break his ten-thousand-year-old prison."},kw={"ameth'aran","asterion","athrikus","bashal'aran","darkshore","highborne","moonstone","narassin","satyr"},rel={"quest:954","zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:highborne","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance","zone:azshara"},src={"Asterion"}}
E["npc:balthule-shadowstrike"] = {t="npc",n="Balthule Shadowstrike",z="darkshore",s="Balthule Shadowstrike is a night elf scout stationed in northern Darkshore near the Tower of Althalaxx. Serving as a forward agent for Delgren the Purifier, he keeps watch over the sinister cultists and dark practitioners occupying the ancient elven ruins. Adventurers traveling along the northern coast are often directed to him to assist in unravelling and disrupting the dark rituals underway at the tower.",h="Balthule Shadowstrike is a night elf scout stationed in northern Darkshore near the Tower of Althalaxx.",sec={{t="A Scout in the Shadows",b="Perched in the wilderness just west of the Tower of Althalaxx, Balthule Shadowstrike maintains a lonely and perilous vigil. Darkshore's northern reaches are thick with restless spirits and shadowed ruins, but the activity around the tower poses a particularly acute threat. Balthule operates under the direction of Delgren the Purifier, observing the movements of dark casters who have crept into the ancient Highborne remnants.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Cult",b="The sorcerers and cultists who have claimed the Tower of Althalaxx are engaged in dark, forbidden magic, harvesting artifacts and souls from the surrounding ruins. Balthule relies on traveling Alliance champions to venture into the tower grounds, strike down the cultist leadership, and recover parchment and talismans that reveal the true scope of their summoning efforts.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is a night elf scout stationed in northern Darkshore. He acts as an advance scout and agent working in concert with Delgren the Purifier to monitor evil cultist activities in the area.",al={"who is balthule","balthule role","balthule shadowstrike npc"}},{q="Where is Balthule Shadowstrike located?",a="He is stationed in northern Darkshore, positioned just west of the ominous Tower of Althalaxx near the coastline.",al={"where is balthule","balthule location","find balthule shadowstrike"}},{q="What is his mission at the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="He was sent to spy upon the dark spellcasters and cultists who have taken up residence in the Tower of Althalaxx, helping to gather intelligence and coordinate strikes to disrupt their corrupt rituals.",al={"why is balthule here","what does balthule want","althalaxx quest guy"}},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance champion stationed along the road south of the tower who coordinates the campaign against the dark forces plaguing northern Darkshore. Balthule serves as his forward eyes and ears.",al={"who is delgren","balthule superior","delgren connection"}},{q="What kind of enemies occupy the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The tower and its surrounding grounds are overrun by dark cultists, sorcerers, and summoned demonic or shadowy minions bent on using ancient Highborne power for sinister purposes.",al={"who is in the tower","althalaxx enemies","tower of althalaxx cultists"}},{q="Why is the Alliance interested in these ruins?",a="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient elven structure. The presence of foul sorcery and demonic activity so close to elven lands represents a direct threat to the safety of Darkshore and the night elves of Darnassus.",al={"why care about the tower","alliance darkshore presence"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the desecration of ancient Kalimdor ruins by foul cultists is an outrage that Balthule seeks to avenge before the corruption spreads further into their lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="Balthule serves as an important forward contact for Alliance members sent north from Auberdine to excise the dark cultists operating around the Tower of Althalaxx.",["class:Rogue"]="Operating deep in hostile territory right under the noses of dangerous spellcasters, Balthule exemplifies the patience and vigilance of a true elven scout."},kw={"althalaxx","balthule","cultists","darkshore","delgren","mathystra","purifier","scout","shadowstrike"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","npc:delgren-the-purifier","quest:965","zone:darkshore","subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","topic:night-elf","topic:highborne"},src={"Balthule Shadowstrike"}}
E["npc:barithras-moonshade"] = {t="npc",n="Barithras Moonshade",z="darkshore",s="Barithras Moonshade is a night elf resident of Auberdine in Darkshore. Positioned within the coastal settlement, he seeks the help of adventurers willing to explore the shadowy wilderness and gather rare subterranean flora.",h="Barithras Moonshade is a night elf resident of Auberdine in Darkshore.",sec={{t="Resident of Auberdine",b="Standing watch within the village of Auberdine, Barithras Moonshade contributes to the night elves' efforts to study and manage the unsettled land of Darkshore. He directs travelers to venture into nearby subterranean caverns to harvest specific fungi, such as death cap mushrooms, for study and use.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Ancients",b="Beyond local flora, Barithras assists in guiding capable adventurers southward to make contact with Onu, one of the venerable ancients striving to heal Darkshore's tainted soil and soothe its restless natural spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Barithras Moonshade?",a="Barithras Moonshade is a night elf resident found in Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore. He tasks adventurers with investigating local flora and contacting guardians in the region.",al={"who is barithras","barithras moonshade","who is this night elf"}},{q="Where can I find Barithras Moonshade?",a="He can be found standing in the port settlement of Auberdine on the shores of Darkshore.",al={"barithras location","where is barithras","barithras moonshade location"}},{q="What tasks does Barithras give?",a="Barithras tasks travelers with entering nearby caverns to harvest mushrooms, such as the dangerous death cap, and later points adventurers southward to meet with the ancient Onu.",al={"barithras quests","what quests does barithras give","cave mushrooms quest"}},{q="Is Barithras related to the other Moonshades?",a="Several other night elves carry the Moonshade surname across Kalimdor, including Sentinels and Keepers, suggesting a shared lineage among their people.",al={"moonshade family","other moonshades","is barithras related to sentinel moonshade"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Barithras helps his kin in Auberdine safeguard Darkshore by monitoring its flora and maintaining ties with ancient forest guardians like Onu.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Those attuned to plant life will appreciate Barithras's interest in Darkshore's peculiar cavern-dwelling fungi."},kw={"auberdine","barithras","cave mushrooms","darkshore","death cap","moonshade","onu"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:947","topic:night-elf"},src={"Barithras Moonshade"}}
E["npc:cerellean-whiteclaw"] = {t="npc",n="Cerellean Whiteclaw",z="darkshore",s="Cerellean Whiteclaw is a night elf resting near the docks and inn of Auberdine in Darkshore. Haunted by the memory of his lost love from the ancient Sundering, he struggles to lay her restless spirit to peace.",h="Cerellean Whiteclaw is a night elf resting near the docks and inn of Auberdine in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Love Torn asunder",b="Ten thousand years ago, prior to the War of the Ancients, Cerellean Whiteclaw shared his life with Anaya Dawnrunner. When the demonic invasion tore ancient Kalimdor apart, Anaya perished in the destruction of her city, Ameth'Aran. Stricken with grief, Cerellean followed Malfurion Stormrage into the long druidic slumber, yet the Emerald Dream offered him little respite from her memory. Upon awakening millennia later, he wandered Darkshore in a grief-stricken haze, only to discover that Anaya's ghost remained bound to the very stones where she fell.",sp=0},{t="A Plea for Release",b="Though he yearns to grant Anaya peace, Cerellean cannot bear the sorrow of striking down her tormented shade himself. He appeals to passing travelers to venture south into the haunted ruins of Ameth'Aran, put her spirit to rest, and recover her pendant. Once freed, Anaya's shade briefly visits Cerellean on the docks of Auberdine, reassuring him of her enduring love and promising that they will one day be reunited in the afterlife.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Cerellean Whiteclaw?",a="Cerellean Whiteclaw is an ancient night elf residing near the docks of Auberdine in Darkshore. He mourns his lost love, Anaya Dawnrunner, who perished during the War of the Ancients ten millennia ago.",al={"who is cerellean","cerellean whiteclaw","auberdine docks elf"}},{q="Who was Anaya Dawnrunner?",a="Anaya Dawnrunner was Cerellean's beloved who lived in the ancient city of Ameth'Aran. She was killed during the War of the Ancients when the city fell to ruin, and her tortured spirit lingered among the wreckage for thousands of years.",al={"anaya dawnrunner","cerellean's love","cerellean lover"}},{q="Why doesn't Cerellean lay Anaya's spirit to rest himself?",a="Cerellean remains so deeply attached and heartbroken that he lacks the emotional strength to confront and destroy her ghostly form himself. He relies on sympathetic travelers to deliver her final release.",al={"why doesn't cerellean fight anaya","why need adventurer"}},{q="Where are the ruins of Ameth'Aran?",a="The ruins of Ameth'Aran lie in southern Darkshore, east of the main road. The area is haunted by ghosts of ancient kaldorei who perished during the Great Sundering.",al={"where is ameth'aran","anaya location","where is anaya"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Cerellean's tragic story reflects the deep, enduring scars left upon the kaldorei by the War of the Ancients and the Great Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="Like many druids, Cerellean entered the long slumber alongside Malfurion Stormrage, though the Emerald Dream proved unable to wash away his earthly heartbreak."},kw={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","auberdine","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","for love eternal","ghost","sundering"},rel={"quest:963","subzone:ameth-aran","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:night-elf"},src={"Cerellean Whiteclaw"}}
E["npc:delgren-the-purifier"] = {t="npc",n="Delgren the Purifier",z="darkshore",s="Delgren the Purifier is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post on the northern edge of Ashenvale. Operating alongside comrades Balthule Shadowstrike and Feero Ironhand, he aids the night elves in cleansing demonic and shadow magic threatening the frontier, with a particular focus on the sinister Cult of the Dark Strand.",h="Delgren the Purifier is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post on the northern edge of Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Crusader on the Kaldorei Frontier",b="Human paladins are a rare sight deep within the ancient forests of Kalimdor, but Delgren the Purifier arrived with a mission. Affiliated with the Argent Dawn, Delgren traveled west with a cadre of holy warriors determined to assist the Alliance's new night elf allies against the lingering evils of demons and undead remnants from the Third War. Stationed near the border of Darkshore and Ashenvale, he maintains a watchful vigil over travelers passing south from Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Dark Strand",b="Delgren's immediate crusade pits him directly against the Cult of the Dark Strand, a malevolent cabal operating around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. Teaming with the scout Balthule Shadowstrike, Delgren orchestrates strikes into the cult's territory, investigating their dark rituals and sending adventurers to strike down cultists, shatter their summoning focuses, and root out corrupt warlocks who dare traffic with demonic shadow.",sp=1},{t="An Unorthodox Mind",b="Despite his fierce devotion to the Holy Light and zealous nickname, Delgren possesses an unusual perspective on Kalimdor's tangled politics. Much to the annoyance and disdain of his conservative superiors, he took the time to learn Orcish. This rare linguistic skill hints at an unconventional mind—one that seeks to understand the enemies and neighbors sharing this untamed continent rather than relying solely on blind dogma.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post along the road in northern Ashenvale. As an agent of the Argent Dawn, he assists the night elves in defending their lands from demonic corruption, cultists, and lingering shadows left in the wake of the Legion's invasion.",al={"who is delgren","delgren lore","who is the paladin at maestras post"}},{q="Where can I find Delgren?",a="Delgren stands at Maestra's Post, a small night elven outpost in northwestern Ashenvale just south of the border trail leading into Darkshore.",al={"where is delgren","delgren location","delgren coordinates"}},{q="Why is a human paladin all the way out in Ashenvale?",a="Delgren journeyed west with a company of Argent Dawn paladins to offer aid to the Alliance's night elven allies. Their purpose is to help purge demonic incursions, undead remnants, and dark cults that threaten northern Kalimdor.",al={"why is delgren in ashenvale","why are there humans in ashenvale","delgren mission"}},{q="What is Delgren's connection to the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="Delgren and his companions monitor the corrupt activities radiating from the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. He directs adventurers to investigate the ruin, hunt the Cult of the Dark Strand, and dismantle their dark summoning practices.",al={"delgren althalaxx","tower of althalaxx quests","cult of the dark strand"}},{q="Why did Delgren learn Orcish?",a="Delgren learned Orcish to better comprehend the situation and inhabitants of Kalimdor, a decision that earned him notable disapproval from his superiors within the order who favored traditional Alliance isolationism.",al={"delgren speaks orcish","does delgren speak orcish","delgren orc language"}},{q="Who does Delgren work with at Maestra's Post?",a="He operates alongside Balthule Shadowstrike and Feero Ironhand, working as a coordinated unit to monitor border threats, handle logistics, and purge shadow cultists along the Ashenvale frontier.",al={"delgren companions","who is at maestras post"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Delgren represents the far reach of the Holy Light on Kalimdor, demonstrating how paladins adapt their crusade against demons and dark magic far beyond the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers heading south from Darkshore, Delgren and his companions provide a reassuring military foothold along the dangerous Ashenvale road.",["race:NightElf"]="Though traditional kaldorei are often skeptical of foreign creeds, Delgren's company has earned trust through their practical crusade against the demonic cults troubling ancient ruins."},kw={"althalaxx","argent dawn","ashenvale","balthule shadowstrike","cult of the dark strand","delgren","delgren the purifier","feero ironhand","maestra's post","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","npc:feero-ironhand","quest:965","topic:argent-dawn","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore"},src={"Delgren the Purifier"}}
E["npc:elder-starweave"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Starweave",z="darkshore",s="Elder Starweave is an ancestral night elf spirit honored during the Lunar Festival. Found resting at the port town of Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore, she shares the wisdom of ancient ages with passing pilgrims.",h="Elder Starweave is an ancestral night elf spirit honored during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Auberdine",b="Appearing as an ethereal shade among the coastal dwellings of Auberdine, Elder Starweave is one of the revered ancestors honored by the Cenarion Circle and the peoples of Kalimdor. While many travelers rush through the port on their way inland or across the sea, those who pause before her receive an ancestral blessing. Starweave speaks of celestial movements, observing that the stars of the modern era trace unfamiliar paths that serve as beacons of hope and fortitude for future generations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Starweave?",a="Elder Starweave is a night elf ancestral spirit who appears in Auberdine during the Lunar Festival to offer greetings, ancient wisdom, and Coins of Ancestry to travelers.",al={"elder starweave lore","who is starweave","starweave the elder"}},{q="Where can Elder Starweave be found?",a="She can be found lingering near the settlement of Auberdine along the shoreline of Darkshore.",al={"where is elder starweave","elder starweave location","starweave spot"}},{q="Why does she appear as a spirit?",a="She is an honored ancestor brought forth during the Lunar Festival, appearing in spiritual form so the living may pay respects to those who shaped the night elves' distant past.",al={"why is starweave a ghost","is starweave dead","why ghost"}},{q="Can Horde players speak to her?",a="Yes. Ancestral elders honored during the Lunar Festival welcome travelers of all affiliations, though Horde adventurers must navigate the Alliance-friendly port of Auberdine with caution.",al={"can horde visit starweave","horde elder starweave"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Meeting Elder Starweave in Darkshore connects kaldorei adventurers directly to their long lineage of forebears who looked to Elune and the stars through ancient cataclysms.",["class:Druid"]="Druids observing the festival find Starweave's celestial reflections aligned with the Cenarion teachings of renewal, memory, and harmony with the natural world."},kw={"ancestor","auberdine","coin of ancestry","darkshore","elder starweave","lunar festival","starweave"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:night-elf","quest:8721"},src={"Elder Starweave"}}
E["npc:gelkak-gyromast"] = {t="npc",n="Gelkak Gyromast",z="darkshore",s="Gelkak Gyromast is an ambitious gnome inventor found stranded along the foggy shoreline of Mist's Edge in northern Darkshore. Trapped far from friendly workshops, he struggles to deal with the chaotic malfunction of his mechanical creation, the Threshwackonator 4100.",h="Gelkak Gyromast is an ambitious gnome inventor found stranded along the foggy shoreline of Mist's Edge in...",sec={{t="Castaway on Mist's Edge",b="Perched on the desolate northern coast of Darkshore just west of the ancient Ruins of Mathystra, Gelkak Gyromast represents a peculiar sight among the gloomy night elven shores. Like many enterprising gnomes, Gyromast brought intricate, untested engineering marvels into the wild, only to find the untamed world far more volatile than expected. Stranded on the misty sands, his immediate concern is dealing with the fallout of his rogue machine, the Threshwackonator 4100, and securing whatever salvage remains.",sp=0},{t="The Threshwackonator Malfunction",b="Rather than serving its intended purpose, Gyromast's mechanical contraption went haywire amid the coastal wildlife. Unable to rein in the berserk automaton himself, the beleaguered inventor relies on passing adventurers to dismantle the Threshwackonator 4100 and help him exact vengeance for his ruined enterprise.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gelkak Gyromast?",a="Gelkak Gyromast is an eccentric gnome inventor stranded on the northern beach of Darkshore known as Mist's Edge, just west of the Ruins of Mathystra.",al={"gelkak","who is gelkak","gyromast"}},{q="Why is Gelkak stranded in Darkshore?",a="Gyromast traveled to Darkshore with his mechanical inventions, but an experiment gone wrong and a runaway automaton left him stranded on the desolate northern coast.",al={"why is gelkak here","gelkak darkshore"}},{q="What is the Threshwackonator 4100?",a="The Threshwackonator 4100 is Gelkak's mechanical creation. It malfunctioned completely, turning hostile and wandering the northern shoreline beyond its creator's control.",al={"threshwackonator","gelkak machine","robot"}},{q="What help does Gelkak need from travelers?",a="Gelkak asks capable adventurers to track down and destroy the rampaging Threshwackonator 4100 and assist in salvaging his lost mechanical parts.",al={"gelkak quests","gyromast quests"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Seeing a fellow gnome stranded on the edge of Kalimdor is a stark reminder of how quickly ambitious tinkering can backfire in the wild.",["profession:Engineering"]="Gelkak's predicament is a classic tale of engineering hubris, proving that even a device as impressive as the Threshwackonator 4100 needs an emergency off switch."},kw={"darkshore","gelkak gyromast","gnome inventor","mathystra","mist's edge","threshwackonator 4100"},rel={"subzone:mist-s-edge","quest:2098","quest:2078","subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","zone:darkshore","topic:gnome"},src={"Gelkak Gyromast"}}
E["npc:gorbold-steelhand"] = {t="npc",n="Gorbold Steelhand",z="darkshore",s="Gorbold Steelhand is a dwarven merchant stationed in Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore. Operating far from the snowy halls of Khaz Modan, he supplies travelers, crafters, and local night elves with general goods and trade supplies.",h="Gorbold Steelhand is a dwarven merchant stationed in Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Trader in Kalimdor",b="While most of Kalimdor's northern reaches are populated by the secretive night elves, Alliance outposts like Auberdine rely on merchants from across the Great Sea to keep trade moving. Gorbold Steelhand represents the far-reaching presence of Ironforge commerce in the region. Working alongside the kaldorei, he sells trade goods, reagents, crafting sundries, and tools to adventurers preparing to explore the treacherous shores and forests of Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="Maritime Ventures",b="Beyond stocking daily goods, Gorbold keeps a keen eye on the perilous coastal waters off Auberdine. Darkshore's reef-strewn waters are notorious for swallowing Alliance vessels, and merchants like Gorbold have a direct interest in the cargo lost beneath the waves. Travelers willing to dive into the deep ocean can often find him interested in the salvage and lost logs scattered across sunken wrecks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gorbold Steelhand?",a="Gorbold Steelhand is a dwarven general trade merchant based in the coastal port of Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"gorbold","who is gorbold steelhand","dwarf in auberdine"}},{q="What does Gorbold Steelhand sell?",a="He carries general trade supplies, crafting ingredients, gathering tools, and reagents such as vials and thread used by tradesfolk passing through Auberdine.",al={"what does gorbold sell","gorbold trade goods","gorbold vendor list"}},{q="Why is an Ironforge dwarf living in Darkshore?",a="Auberdine serves as a key Alliance transit hub connecting Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms. Dwarves frequently travel here for commerce, exploration, and supporting allied night elf operations.",al={"why is a dwarf here","why is gorbold in darkshore","ironforge in auberdine"}},{q="Does Gorbold offer any quests?",a="Yes, he directs adventurers toward sunken wreckage off the coast of Darkshore in the quest 'Deep Ocean, Vast Sea' to recover lost ship cargo.",al={"gorbold quest","deep ocean vast sea quest giver"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a familiar Ironforge face like Gorbold in the misty, nocturnal environment of Darkshore provides dwarven travelers a welcome reminder of home.",["faction:Alliance"]="Gorbold illustrates the practical cooperation between the eastern races of the Alliance and the night elves, keeping trade flowing across the Great Sea."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","deep ocean vast sea","gorbold","ironforge","merchant","steelhand","vendor"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:982","topic:dwarf"},src={"Gorbold Steelhand"}}
E["npc:gubber-blump"] = {t="npc",n="Gubber Blump",z="darkshore",s="Gubber Blump is a dwarf fisherman and trainer stationed along the shores of Auberdine in Darkshore. Positioned on the sands between the docks and the flight master, he is an enthusiastic lover of the angling craft and seafood, particularly fresh crab meat.",h="Gubber Blump is a dwarf fisherman and trainer stationed along the shores of Auberdine in Darkshore.",sec={{t="The Angler of Auberdine",b="While most dwarves find comfort beneath stone or beside a roaring forge, Gubber Blump prefers the misty coastline of Darkshore. Stationed along the beach at Auberdine, between the flight master and the ferry pier, Gubber teaches the art of fishing and sells basic angling gear to passing travelers. He holds a deep culinary appreciation for crab meat, though he frequently relies on adventurers to help secure his catches along the dangerous coast, as well as reclaim sentimental family fishing tackle.",sp=0},{t="Family Ties and Ocean Favors",b="Gubber is known to share candid stories about his family, notably his cousin Graun Blump, whom he insists possesses both a beard and an unusual odor. Travelers who lend a hand with his coastal errands—whether hauling in crawler legs or retrieving his family pole—often earn a thoughtful handwritten letter of thanks from Gubber, usually accompanied by a shiny fishing lure to encourage their future casts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gubber Blump?",a="Gubber Blump is a dwarf fishing trainer and vendor located on the beach in Auberdine, situated right between the village docks and the hippogryph master.",al={"who is gubber blump","gubber blump npc","where is gubber blump"}},{q="What does Gubber Blump teach or sell?",a="He trains novices in the fishing profession and stocks basic gear for prospective anglers, including standard fishing poles and shiny baubles.",al={"what does gubber sell","gubber blump trainer","darkshore fishing trainer"}},{q="What tasks does Gubber Blump give out?",a="Gubber asks travelers to recover his lost family fishing pole and gather fine crab meat from the coast in quests such as 'The Family and the Fishing Pole' and 'Fruit of the Sea'.",al={"gubber blump quests","fruit of the sea","the family and the fishing pole"}},{q="Who is Graun Blump?",a="Graun Blump is Gubber's dwarven cousin. Gubber candidly remarks that she sports a notable beard and has a rather unusual smell.",al={"graun blump","gubber blump cousin"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Gubber is passionate about coastal fare, particularly fresh reef crawler meat, making him a kindred spirit to cooks seeking ingredients from Darkshore's waters.",["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a dwarf happily settled on a foggy Kalimdor shoreline rather than in Khaz Modan is an uncommon sight, though his forthright banter about kin proves he has not lost his Ironforge roots."},kw={"auberdine","blump","darkshore","fishing","graun blump","gubber","reef crawler","shiny bauble"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:1141","quest:1138","topic:dwarf"},src={"Gubber Blump"}}
E["npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde"] = {t="npc",n="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",z="darkshore",s="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf residing in the coastal port of Auberdine. Stationed along the misty Darkshore coast, she watches the tides and directs travelers to investigate the strange remains washing ashore. Her concerns center on the mysterious sea creatures and massive turtles whose carcasses have begun littering the northern beaches.",h="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf residing in the coastal port of Auberdine.",sec={{t="Watcher of the Shifting Sands",b="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde makes her home in Auberdine, the bustling seaside haven of Darkshore. While many in town concern themselves with the forest or shipping across the Veiled Sea, Gwennyth keeps her gaze firmly on the coastline. The tides have recently turned grim, depositing the remains of colossal marine life onto the surf. To understand what is happening in the waters offshore, she relies on willing adventurers to scour the sands, retrieve skeletal samples, and bring back answers.",sp=0},{t="The Stranded Giants",b="The beaches north and south of Auberdine have seen an alarming influx of beached sea creatures and ancient sea turtles. Rather than letting their deaths go unnoticed, Gwennyth tasks travelers with inspecting these fallen titans. By studying the bones and discovering what drove these beasts ashore or took their lives, she hopes to piece together the hidden perils lurking off the shores of northern Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="She is a night elf inhabitant of Auberdine in Darkshore who studies the recent ecological disturbances along the shoreline. She enlists travelers to survey the beach and investigate strange wash-ups from the sea.",al={"who is gwennyth","gwennyth auberdine","gwennyth lore"}},{q="Where can I find Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="She can be found in the coastal settlement of Auberdine, situated near the beach and docks along the mist-shrouded coast of Darkshore.",al={"where is gwennyth","gwennyth location","find gwennyth"}},{q="Why is she interested in beached creatures?",a="The sudden deaths and beachings of massive sea turtles and mysterious marine behemoths point to an imbalance or unseen predator in the waters off Darkshore. Gwennyth seeks to understand the cause by examining remains recovered from along the coast.",al={"why beached turtles","why does she want bones","washed ashore quest"}},{q="What quests does Gwennyth offer?",a="She sends adventurers out on 'Washed Ashore' and serves as the turn-in point for various discoveries related to the beached sea creatures and beached sea turtles found along Darkshore's coastline.",al={"gwennyth quests","what does she give"}},{q="Is she part of the Cenarion Circle or the Sentinels?",a="She operates as an everyday resident of Auberdine rather than a sworn Cenarion druid or Sentinel commander, yet she shares her kin's deep concern for the health and balance of Darkshore's natural environment.",al={"gwennyth faction","is gwennyth a druid"}},{q="What does her name mean?",a="While fitting the rhythmic naming style of the kaldorei, her unusual surname 'Bly'Leggonde' is an anagram of 'Leggy Blonde', a playful touch from the world's creators.",al={"bly leggonde meaning","gwennyth name easter egg"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the unnatural death of great sea beasts off the shores of Darkshore is a troubling sign of imbalance in their ancestral lands, making Gwennyth's beachside watch especially urgent.",["class:Druid"]="Druids committed to preserving Kalimdor's natural harmony will find Gwennyth's reports of stranded marine life an alarming indicator of disturbance within the coastal ecosystem.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the Alliance's primary coastal port in northern Kalimdor; keeping its waterways and beaches safe from hidden threats is vital to all allied races venturing through."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea creature","beached sea turtle","blyleggonde","darkshore","gwennyth","kaldorei","veiled sea","washed ashore"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:3524","quest:4722","quest:4723","topic:night-elf"},src={"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde"}}
E["npc:huntress-kella-nightbow"] = {t="npc",n="Huntress Kella Nightbow",z="darkshore",s="Huntress Kella Nightbow is a skilled night elf scout and hunter serving the Alliance along the western coasts of Kalimdor. As a sentinel and tracker, she aids travelers navigating maritime routes toward northern lands such as Darkshore.",h="Huntress Kella Nightbow is a skilled night elf scout and hunter serving the Alliance along the western coasts...",sec={{t="Eyes of the Wild",b="Huntress Kella Nightbow embodies the traditional vigilance of the night elf sentinels. Deeply attuned to nature and the wild beasts of Kalimdor, she assists the Alliance by keeping watch over coastal pathways and offering guidance to those seeking passage to Auberdine and beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Huntress Kella Nightbow?",a="She is a night elf huntress and sentinel dedicated to guiding travelers and securing travel routes connected to dark coastal regions like Darkshore.",al={"who is kella nightbow","kella nightbow","huntress nightbow"}},{q="What faction does she belong to?",a="Huntress Kella Nightbow is loyal to the night elves of Darnassus and serves as part of the broader Alliance.",al={"is kella nightbow alliance","huntress kella faction"}},{q="Why would someone seek her out?",a="Travelers and hunters seek her guidance when navigating coastal passages or finding their way toward Auberdine and the wider night elf territories.",al={"kella nightbow purpose","why find kella nightbow"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As an experienced huntress attuned to the beasts of the wild, Kella is a familiar spirit to any tracker mastering the art of the hunt.",["race:NightElf"]="Kella represents the steadfast sentinels safeguarding night elf shores and keeping coastal transit safe for her kin."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","hunter","huntress","kella","nightbow","sentinel"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance","quest:9633","quest:6061"},src={"Huntress Kella Nightbow"}}
E["npc:kerlonian-evershade"] = {t="npc",n="Kerlonian Evershade",z="darkshore",s="Kerlonian Evershade is a night elf Druid of the Claw resting at the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore. Having recently awakened from the long slumber within the Emerald Dream, he requires aid navigating the corrupted wilds to reach the safety of Maestra's Post.",h="Kerlonian Evershade is a night elf Druid of the Claw resting at the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore.",sec={{t="Awakening in Darkshore",b="Kerlonian Evershade belongs to the Druids of the Claw, followers of the bear totem who spent centuries sleeping in barrows and communion with the Emerald Dream. Called to wake following the Third War, many druids emerged disoriented into a world ravaged by corruption. Found resting beneath the ancient trees of the Grove of the Ancients, Kerlonian is still shaking off the supernatural grogginess of his prolonged rest. His immediate concern is traveling safely through the troubled forests of Darkshore toward Maestra's Post on the border of Ashenvale.",sp=0},{t="A Treacherous Journey",b="The road out of the Grove of the Ancients is far from secure. The lingering aftermath of the Shattering of Mount Hyjal and the spreading blight in Darkshore have riled the local wildlife and brought hostile prowlers and grell close to the sacred clearings. Weakened from sleep and struggling with sudden bouts of exhaustion, Kerlonian relies on sympathetic travelers of the Alliance to protect him as he makes his way south to rejoin his fellow night elves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kerlonian Evershade?",a="Kerlonian Evershade is a night elf Druid of the Claw stationed near the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore. He recently woke from the Emerald Dream and needs assistance traveling safely through the woods.",al={"who is kerlonian","kerlonian evershade lore","druid in grove of the ancients"}},{q="Why does Kerlonian fall asleep while walking?",a="Like many Druids of the Claw who slept for centuries in barrow dens, Kerlonian is still suffering from the lingering stupor of the Emerald Dream. His body and mind have not fully adjusted to waking reality, causing sudden spells of drowsiness.",al={"why is kerlonian sleeping","sleeper has awakened quest druid","kerlonian sleepy"}},{q="Where is he trying to go?",a="He seeks safe passage south to Maestra's Post, a night elf outpost situated on the border between Darkshore and Ashenvale, where he can safely recuperate.",al={"kerlonian destination","where does kerlonian go","grove of the ancients escort destination"}},{q="What is a Druid of the Claw?",a="Druids of the Claw are night elf druids who venerate the bear ancient, Ursoc. They channel strength, resilience, and feral might, traditionally guarding barrows and night elf lands while spending ages asleep in the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is druid of the claw","druids of the claw lore"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druid adventurers will recognize Kerlonian's plight intimately, as all disciples of the Cenarion Circle must grapple with the heavy toll of deep communion with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elf travelers, guiding Kerlonian represents safeguarding one of their ancient defenders, freshly returned to a world vastly changed since the Third War."},kw={"darkshore","druid of the claw","emerald dream","evershade","grove of the ancients","kerlonian","the sleeper has awakened"},rel={"quest:5321","quest:952","quest:2561","zone:darkshore","topic:druid"},src={"Kerlonian Evershade"}}
E["npc:laird"] = {t="npc",n="Laird",z="darkshore",s="Laird is a night elf fish vendor found inside the seaside inn of Auberdine. Working along Darkshore's mist-shrouded coast, he provides trade goods and culinary recipes to travelers and fishermen braving the rugged shoreline.",h="Laird is a night elf fish vendor found inside the seaside inn of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Harbor Merchant",b="Situated inside the bustling inn of Auberdine, Laird sells fresh fish and supplies to sailors, locals, and journeying adventurers. Darkshore's waters are notoriously turbulent and rife with danger compared to the sheltered shores of Teldrassil, but Laird knows well that risk brings reward. For daring anglers willing to cast their lines along the misty beaches, the local catch yields a handsome profit.",sp=0},{t="Ties Across the Water",b="Laird remains closely connected to fishing operations across the channel in Teldrassil. He serves as an essential contact for courier runs between the island boughs of Rut'theran Village and the mainland port, receiving shipments from his fellow fisher Nessa Shadowsong and ensuring the lines of coastal commerce stay open.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Laird?",a="Laird is located indoors on the ground floor of the inn in Auberdine, the main Alliance settlement along the coast of Darkshore.",al={"laird location","where is laird","laird auberdine"}},{q="What does Laird sell?",a="He sells various caught fish and cooking ingredients, as well as the culinary instruction for preparing a Fillet of Frenzy.",al={"laird vendor","what does laird sell","laird wares"}},{q="What quests involve Laird?",a="Laird is the recipient of a delivery originating from Nessa Shadowsong at Rut'theran Village in the quest Flight to Auberdine, after which he asks adventurers to carry word back across the sea.",al={"laird quests","auberdine fish quest"}},{q="Why does Laird think Darkshore fishing is worthwhile despite the danger?",a="Laird notes that while the misty shoreline of Darkshore harbors far more hazards than the tranquil waters of Teldrassil, the abundant and exotic sea life makes the trade far more profitable for enterprising fishers.",al={"laird gossip","is darkshore good for fishing"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Culinary travelers visiting Darkshore often seek out Laird for his recipe on how to properly fillet and cook the fierce frenzy fish native to Kalimdor's waters.",["race:NightElf"]="Laird represents the everyday night elf tradesmen who have established themselves along the mainland shores to support Kalimdor's growing coastal network."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","fillet of frenzy","fish vendor","laird","nessa shadowsong"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:6342","quest:6343","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Laird"}}
E["npc:prospector-remtravel"] = {t="npc",n="Prospector Remtravel",z="darkshore",s="Prospector Remtravel is a dwarven archaeologist affiliated with the Explorers' League, stationed deep in the gloomy woodlands of Darkshore. He oversees an excavation site unearthing ancient relics, though his scattered focus and perilous surroundings leave him in constant need of assistance.",h="Prospector Remtravel is a dwarven archaeologist affiliated with the Explorers' League, stationed deep in the...",sec={{t="A Dwarven Dig in Elven Lands",b="Sent far across the sea by the Explorers' League, Prospector Remtravel established his dig site along the southern reaches of Darkshore. While the night elves are often protective of their ancestral territories, the League's insatiable drive to uncover the origins of Azeroth pushes prospectors into every forgotten corner. Remtravel's work unearths fossilized history and ancient stones, but the aggressive native wildlife and hostile local threats make managing a frontier dig almost more than one scatterbrained dwarf can handle.",sp=0},{t="The Absent-Minded Scholar",b="True to his reputation, Remtravel easily becomes lost in his own thoughts and research notes. Venturing too far from camp in search of fossils or lost artifacts frequently leads to disaster, leaving him cornered by predators or hostile creatures. Those who run across him in the wild usually find themselves tasked with safeguarding his fragile discoveries—and rescuing the prospector himself before the perils of Darkshore put an end to his mission.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="He is an archaeologist and surveyor from Ironforge representing the Explorers' League. He has established a small excavation camp in southern Darkshore to uncover ancient relics and fossils.",al={"who is remtravel","remtravel lore","who is the dwarf in darkshore"}},{q="Why is an Ironforge dwarf digging in Darkshore?",a="The Explorers' League is scouring the known world for titan artifacts, lost history, and ancient fossils. Darkshore is an ancient, ruined land with deep ties to the distant past, making it a prime site for dwarven archaeological investigation.",al={"why is a dwarf in darkshore","what is the explorers league doing in darkshore","why dig here"}},{q="Why is he called absent-minded?",a="Remtravel has a habit of losing track of his surroundings and his own equipment while absorbed in scholarly pursuits. He frequently wanders into dangerous territory without realizing the predators and beasts closing in around him.",al={"why absent minded","is remtravel crazy","what happened to remtravel"}},{q="Is Prospector Remtravel related to anyone in the League?",a="He is believed to be the adventurous uncle mentioned by Karna Remtravel, an explorer who credits her uncle with inspiring her passion for discovery and the wider world.",al={"remtravel family","karna remtravel uncle","who is karna remtravel"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Remtravel represents the Explorers' League's relentless determination to piece together dwarven origins, even when it requires pitching tents in the cold, damp woods of Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="While night elves tolerate peaceful Alliance guests, the League's noisy digging and disturbing of ancient soils often tests the patience of local sentinels and druids."},kw={"absent minded prospector","darkshore","explorers league","fossils","ironforge","prospector remtravel","remtravel","remtravels excavation"},rel={"subzone:remtravel-s-excavation","quest:729","topic:explorers-league","zone:darkshore","topic:dwarf","topic:night-elf"},src={"Prospector Remtravel"}}
E["npc:ranger-glynda-nal-shea"] = {t="npc",n="Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea",z="darkshore",s="Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea is a seasoned night elf sentry stationed in the coastal town of Auberdine. From her post near the town watch, she directs local defense efforts across Darkshore, dispatching travelers to eliminate lurking threats and investigate strange coastal phenomena.",h="Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea is a seasoned night elf sentry stationed in the coastal town of Auberdine.",sec={{t="Guardian of Auberdine",b="As Darkshore grapples with rising corruption and hostile incursions, Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea coordinates vital scout work from Auberdine. She keeps a watchful eye over the surrounding wilderness, relying on capable adventurers to maintain the perimeter and safeguard night elf holdings along the fog-shrouded coast.",sp=0},{t="Threats Along the Coast",b="Glynda is keenly focused on the mounting perils encroaching on the shorelines, particularly the emboldened murlocs gathering south of town. She oversees bounties on notorious menaces like Murkdeep and tasks scouts with examining curious artifacts, including a mysterious crimson crystal found embedded on the heights overlooking the sea.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea?",a="She is an elven ranger stationed in Auberdine who organizes scout patrols and defensive tasks across Darkshore on behalf of the night elf sentinels.",al={"glynda nal'shea","who is glynda","ranger glynda"}},{q="Where can Glynda Nal'Shea be found?",a="She is located in Auberdine, the main Alliance settlement in Darkshore, typically found near the sentinel watch and town entrances.",al={"glynda location","where is glynda","where to find glynda"}},{q="What quests does Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea offer?",a="She offers tasks dealing with regional hazards, including bounties like WANTED: Murkdeep! and investigations involving the mysterious red crystal along the cliffs of Darkshore.",al={"glynda quests","what does glynda give"}},{q="Why is Glynda concerned about Murkdeep?",a="Murkdeep is a vicious murloc chieftain responsible for attacks on night elf outposts and travelers along the southern coast, posing an ongoing threat to the security of Auberdine.",al={"who is murkdeep","why kill murkdeep"}},{q="What is the Red Crystal quest line?",a="It is a line of scout investigations initiated by Glynda, tasking adventurers with climbing the eastern cliffs of Darkshore to examine an odd, pulsing crystal and retrieve fragments for study.",al={"red crystal darkshore","the red crystal quest"}},{q="What faction does Glynda Nal'Shea serve?",a="She serves the night elves of Darnassus and acts as a military outpost commander for the Alliance in Darkshore.",al={"glynda faction","who does glynda work for"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Glynda Nal'Shea represents the ongoing vigilance required to protect the sacred shores of Kalimdor from aggressive beasts and ancient corruptions.",["class:Hunter"]="Fellow rangers and trackers will find kindred spirit in Glynda's sharp instincts and direct approach to eliminating wild beasts and shoreline predators.",["faction:Alliance"]="Glynda provides Alliance travelers arriving by boat from Teldrassil or the Eastern Kingdoms with essential bounties to secure Darkshore's perimeter."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","glynda","murkdeep","nal'shea","night elf","ranger","red crystal","sentinel"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:4740","quest:4811","quest:4812","quest:4813","quest:954"},src={"Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea"}}
E["npc:red-jack-flint"] = {t="npc",n="Red Jack Flint",z="darkshore",s="Red Jack Flint is a seasoned human mariner stationed within Menethil Keep in Menethil Harbor. A member of the crew of the vessel Maiden's Virtue, he serves as a point of contact for travelers seeking passage or contacts across the sea toward Kalimdor.",h="Red Jack Flint is a seasoned human mariner stationed within Menethil Keep in Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Sailor in Menethil Keep",b="Found inside the stone walls of Menethil Keep, Red Jack Flint is an experienced seafarer tied to the harbor's maritime trade. As part of the crew of the Maiden's Virtue, he navigates the dangerous sea routes linking the marshlands of Khaz Modan with distant shores. Rather than staying confined to naval routine, Flint directs capable adventurers to allies across the Great Sea, including contacts in Kalimdor like Fiora Longears.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Red Jack Flint?",a="Red Jack Flint is a human sailor and crew member of the Maiden's Virtue. He is stationed in Menethil Keep within Menethil Harbor, helping bridge contacts between the Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor.",al={"who is flint","red jack flint lore","what does flint do"}},{q="Where can Red Jack Flint be found?",a="He can be found resting inside Menethil Keep, the primary stone fortress defending Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"red jack flint location","where is flint","find red jack flint"}},{q="What ship does Red Jack Flint sail on?",a="He serves aboard the Maiden's Virtue, a merchant vessel operating out of Menethil Harbor.",al={"flints ship","what ship is red jack on","maidens virtue"}},{q="Who does Red Jack Flint send travelers to see?",a="He directs travelers to make contact with Fiora Longears, an associate situated across the Great Sea in Darkshore.",al={"flint quest","fiora longears connection","where does flint send you"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers charting courses across the sea from Khaz Modan, sailors like Red Jack Flint provide vital connections to outposts along Kalimdor's northern coast."},kw={"fiora longears","maidens virtue","menethil harbor","menethil keep","red jack flint","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-keep","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","quest:1132","zone:darkshore"},src={"Red Jack Flint"}}
E["npc:sentinel-aynasha"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Aynasha",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Aynasha is an operative of the night elven Sentinels serving in the wild borders of Darkshore. Tasked with scouting enemy movements and carrying critical intelligence, she regularly faces peril against hostile forces threatening northern Kalimdor.",h="Sentinel Aynasha is an operative of the night elven Sentinels serving in the wild borders of Darkshore.",sec={{t="On the Front Lines",b="As a scout and archer for the Sentinels, Aynasha is deployed to the dangerous frontiers where night elven lands clash with hostile incursions. Carrying out stealth missions and bearing urgent dispatches across rugged terrain, she relies on her marksmanship and survival instincts to evade enemy patrols and survive deep within contested territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Aynasha?",a="Aynasha is an active scout and archer within the night elven Sentinels, the primary military and defensive force protecting northern Kalimdor and its borders.",al={"who is aynasha","aynasha role","sentinel aynasha lore"}},{q="What threats does she monitor in Darkshore?",a="Operating along the fringes of Darkshore, she keeps watch over hostile encampments, rogue furbolg tribes, and foreign incursions that menace the night elf wilderness.",al={"aynasha enemies","darkshore threats","who is she fighting"}},{q="Why is she often isolated on the road?",a="Sentinels frequently travel alone or in small scouting pairs to carry urgent intelligence between posts without drawing unnecessary attention from hostile forces.",al={"why is she alone","aynasha solo mission","sentinel scout duties"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Aynasha represents the vigilant vanguard of the Kaldorei military, defending the ancient woods against encroaching foreign powers and wild corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers in Kalimdor, Sentinel scouts like Aynasha are vital points of contact along the dangerous wilderness roads."},kw={"archer","aynasha","darkshore","kaldorei","night elf","scout","sentinel"},rel={"zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","quest:5713"},src={"Sentinel Aynasha"}}
E["npc:sentinel-elissa-starbreeze"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze is a night elf guardian stationed in Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore. Operating from the upper floor of a lodge across the bridge, she monitors growing regional threats and directs travelers toward pressing concerns in the wilderness.",h="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze is a night elf guardian stationed in Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Vigilant Eye in Auberdine",b="While many Sentinels patrol the foggy coastline and woodlands directly, Elissa Starbreeze coordinates defensive efforts from Auberdine. Stationed on the upper level of the building just northeast across the bridge from the town inn, she stays alert to unusual disturbances in Darkshore. Her tasks frequently point adventurers toward remote points of interest, including the mysterious Tower of Althalaxx looming far to the north, ensuring that shadowy incursions do not take the coastal settlement unawares.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze?",a="She is located in Auberdine in Darkshore. Cross the small bridge northeast of the town's inn, and head up to the second floor of the building there to find her on duty.",al={"elissa starbreeze location","where is elissa starbreeze","auberdine starbreeze"}},{q="What is her duty in Darkshore?",a="As a member of the Night Elf Sentinels, she helps safeguard Auberdine by tracking potential dangers across Darkshore. She directs capable scouts and adventurers to investigate distant outposts and strange threats, such as the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"what does elissa do","elissa starbreeze role"}},{q="Does she have family among the night elves?",a="She shares the Starbreeze surname with several notable night elves across the lands, including priestesses and military officers such as Belysra Starbreeze and Lieutenant Morra Starbreeze.",al={"starbreeze family","who is elissa related to"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Sentinel Starbreeze represents the watchful, disciplined protection the Sentinels provide to Kalimdor's northern outposts like Auberdine.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers arriving from Teldrassil, Starbreeze serves as one of the early contacts directing aid deeper into the haunted wastes of Darkshore."},kw={"althalaxx","auberdine","darkshore","elissa starbreeze","night elf","sentinel"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","npc:elanaria","topic:night-elf"},src={"Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze"}}
E["npc:sentinel-onaeya"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Onaeya",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Onaeya is a night elf guardian stationed at Maestra's Post in northwestern Ashenvale, near the border with Darkshore. Tasked with holding the line against encroaching perils, she rallies capable Alliance adventurers to safeguard the forest and honor fallen defenders.",h="Sentinel Onaeya is a night elf guardian stationed at Maestra's Post in northwestern Ashenvale, near the...",sec={{t="A Guard on the Frontier",b="Maestra's Post serves as a critical wayside outpost along the road from Darkshore into the dense, contested canopy of Ashenvale. Sentinel Onaeya stands guard outside the settlement's main lodge, keeping a vigilant watch over travelers and coordinating defensive actions. Between hostile wildlife, corrupting forces, and border tensions, sentinels like Onaeya represent the first line of defense for night elf settlements in the region.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Post",b="When hostilities flare and the perimeter falls under pressure, Onaeya remains squarely focused on the battle at hand. She coordinates strikes against nearby threats and works to recover and honor fallen comrades, relying on capable adventurers arriving from Darkshore to reinforce the outpost's beleaguered defenders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Onaeya?",a="Sentinel Onaeya is a night elf sentinel stationed at Maestra's Post in northwestern Ashenvale. She acts as a quest giver and frontline defender, directing travelers to assist the outpost.",al={"onaeya","sentinel onaeya","who is onaeya"}},{q="Where is Sentinel Onaeya located?",a="She can be found standing just outside the main building at Maestra's Post, along the northern roadway in Ashenvale right below the border with Darkshore.",al={"onaeya location","where is sentinel onaeya","find onaeya"}},{q="What faction does Sentinel Onaeya belong to?",a="She is a member of the Night Elf Sentinels and is loyal to the Alliance. Horde adventurers will find her hostile on sight.",al={"onaeya faction","is onaeya alliance","onaeya friendly to horde"}},{q="Why is Sentinel Onaeya too busy to talk sometimes?",a="When Maestra's Post comes under attack or is actively threatened, Onaeya focuses entirely on defense, warning passersby that the post is in the middle of a skirmish.",al={"cant talk","onaeya in combat","were in a bit of a fight here"}},{q="What kind of tasks does Sentinel Onaeya give?",a="Onaeya recruits capable scouts and fighters to strike at nearby dangers, honor fallen defenders, and help keep the roads through northwestern Ashenvale clear for travelers.",al={"onaeya quests","what quests does onaeya have"}},{q="Why is Maestra's Post important to the Sentinels?",a="Maestra's Post acts as a crucial checkpoint connecting Darkshore's supply routes to the heart of Ashenvale. Holding it prevents hostile incursions from cutting off night elf travelers moving south.",al={"why maestras post","maestras post importance"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves traveling south from Darkshore, Onaeya represents the front line defending sacred Ashenvale woodland from external threats.",["faction:Alliance"]="Onaeya coordinates essential defensive tasks for Alliance travelers transitioning from the coastal wilds into the contested forests of Ashenvale.",["faction:Horde"]="As a dedicated sentinel holding Maestra's Post, Onaeya is an active enemy combatant guarding the northern approaches into Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","darkshore","maestra's post","night elf","onaeya","sentinel"},rel={"subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf","quest:5713"},src={"Sentinel Onaeya"}}
E["npc:sentinel-tysha-moonblade"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade is a night elf scout stationed along the main road of Darkshore, just west of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran. Tasked with patrolling the troubled coastal wilderness, she directs travelers and recruits aid to investigate the restless spirits haunting the shattered elven settlements nearby.",h="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade is a night elf scout stationed along the main road of Darkshore, just west of the...",sec={{t="Watch upon the Road",b="Standing sentinel along the overgrown highway of Darkshore, Tysha Moonblade keeps a vigilant eye over an increasingly unstable land. Directly to her east lie the haunted remnants of Ameth'Aran, where cursed Highborne ghosts and malevolent banshees linger among ancient stone pillars. Recognizing that Auberdine's limited defenses are stretched thin by threats across the coast, Tysha enlists capable adventurers passing by to uncover the history behind Ameth'Aran's tragic fall and put down the restless dead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Tysha Moonblade?",a="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade is a night elf guardian patrolling the main road in central Darkshore, stationed just west of the ruins of Ameth'Aran. She watches the route against wandering beasts and restless specters.",al={"who is tysha","tysha moonblade lore","sentinel tysha"}},{q="Where can I find Sentinel Tysha Moonblade?",a="She is posted along the north-south road in Darkshore, situated directly west across from the ancient ruin site of Ameth'Aran.",al={"tysha moonblade location","where is tysha","where is sentinel tysha"}},{q="What tasks does she give to adventurers?",a="Tysha directs travelers into the nearby ruins of Ameth'Aran to investigate the ancient tragedy that ruined the ancient night elf settlement, helping quiet the tormented ghosts that haunt its tumbled columns.",al={"tysha moonblade quests","fall of ametharan quest giver","what does tysha want"}},{q="Is she related to anyone else in Darkshore?",a="Sharing a surname, she is likely related to Mariner Moonblade, who can also be found serving night elf interests along the Darkshore coastline.",al={"mariner moonblade relation","tysha moonblade family"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Tysha represents the vigilant Sentinels trying to maintain peace over lands still scarred by the ancient Sundering, asking fellow night elves to lay their cursed ancestors to rest.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers making the journey south from Auberdine toward Ashenvale, Tysha is one of the few friendly outposts along an otherwise perilous, monster-infested road."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","darkshore","highborne","night elf","sentinel","tysha moonblade"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","quest:953","topic:night-elf"},src={"Sentinel Tysha Moonblade"}}
E["npc:terenthis"] = {t="npc",n="Terenthis",z="darkshore",s="Terenthis is a night elf druid stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine. Representing the Cenarion Circle, he is investigating the alarming corruption spreading through Darkshore and Teldrassil. He enlists capable travelers to gauge rising threats along the coast and assist local allies trapped by corrupted wildlife.",h="Terenthis is a night elf druid stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine.",sec={{t="Investigating the Taint",b="Sent to Auberdine by the Cenarion Circle, Terenthis focuses on tracking the spread of Fel Moss and other corruptive forces seeping into Darkshore from Teldrassil. The night elves view this creeping blight with immense concern, fearing the wild balance of northern Kalimdor may fracture completely if left unchecked. Terenthis works to uncover the root causes of the rot and devise ways to halt its advance before it consumes the forests.",sp=0},{t="A Plea from Grimclaw",b="Terenthis also acts as a liaison for dire emergencies in the field. When the loyal bear Grimclaw arrives in Auberdine wounded and alone, Terenthis recognizes that the creature's master, the druid Volcor, has run into grave trouble. Lacking the ability to leave his post, Terenthis directs passing adventurers into the wilderness to find Volcor, who has been ambushed and pinned down by aggressive furbolg tribes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Terenthis?",a="Terenthis is a night elf druid affiliated with the Cenarion Circle, currently residing in the harbor town of Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"terenthis lore","who is terenthis","terenthis auberdine"}},{q="Why is Terenthis in Auberdine?",a="He was dispatched to investigate how widely Fel Moss and magical corruption have spread from Teldrassil into Darkshore, seeking a way to put an end to the blight.",al={"what is terenthis doing","terenthis purpose","why is terenthis here"}},{q="What is the bear beside Terenthis doing there?",a="The bear, Grimclaw, sought out Terenthis in Auberdine for help after his master, the druid Volcor, was attacked and captured by hostile furbolgs.",al={"terenthis bear","grimclaw","why is there a bear in auberdine"}},{q="What organization does Terenthis belong to?",a="Terenthis is a member of the Cenarion Circle, the druidic order dedicated to preserving balance and safeguarding nature across Kalimdor.",al={"terenthis faction","is terenthis cenarion circle"}},{q="What threats is Terenthis most concerned with?",a="He is primarily concerned with Fel Moss corruption affecting the regional wildlife, as well as the rising hostility of local furbolg tribes that threaten travelers and druids alike.",al={"darkshore corruption","fel moss threat","terenthis concerns"}},{q="Does Terenthis offer any tasks to adventurers?",a="Yes. He directs adventurers to assess corrupting threats along the coast, coordinate with fellow druids like Thundris Windweaver, and mount a rescue for Volcor.",al={"terenthis quests","what does terenthis want"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Cenarion Circle brother, Terenthis represents the front line against the unnatural corruption spilling from Teldrassil into the mainland.",["race:NightElf"]="Terenthis exemplifies the kaldorei commitment to purifying their sacred lands from lingering fel taint and protecting innocent forest life."},kw={"auberdine","cenarion circle","darkshore","fel moss","furbolg","grimclaw","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:986","quest:984","quest:4761","quest:994","quest:995","topic:furbolg"},src={"Terenthis"}}
E["npc:tharnariun-treetender"] = {t="npc",n="Tharnariun Treetender",z="darkshore",s="Tharnariun Treetender is a night elf naturalist stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine in Darkshore. Dedicated to safeguarding the delicate balance of the wild, he monitors the creeping corruption afflicting the regional flora and fauna. Travelers passing through the port often find him calling upon allies to heal diseased beasts and protect nature from further decline.",h="Tharnariun Treetender is a night elf naturalist stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Guardian in Auberdine",b="Perched on the rugged coast of Darkshore, the port town of Auberdine faces threats on multiple fronts, from hostile satyrs to foul shoreline washaways. Tharnariun Treetender focuses his efforts squarely on the natural world that surrounds the village. Firmly believing that neglecting nature invites ruin, he spends his time observing the decline of the local woods and seeking ways to push back the sickness spreading across the forest floor.",sp=0},{t="Healing the Afflicted",b="Much of Darkshore's wildlife has fallen prey to strange plagues and corrupted blights, driving creatures mad and twisting peaceful animals into rabid threats. Rather than merely slaughtering them out of fear, Tharnariun seeks a remedy. Through carefully concocted cleansers and targeted efforts to eliminate the worst of the contagion, he endeavors to rescue what remains of the wilderness before the woodland falls entirely into decay.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Tharnariun Treetender?",a="Tharnariun is a night elf caretaker stationed in Auberdine along the coast of Darkshore. He dedicates his life to watching over the forest and diagnosing the unnatural afflictions troubling the local wildlife.",al={"who is tharnariun","tharnariun lore","tharnariunreetender"}},{q="Where can I find Tharnariun Treetender?",a="He is located in the night elf coastal village of Auberdine, situated on the western edge of the Darkshore wilderness.",al={"where is tharnariun","tharnariun treetender location","tharnariun map"}},{q="What problems is Tharnariun investigating in Darkshore?",a="He investigates the spreading corruption and foul plagues infecting the land and its wildlife, sending adventurers out to cleanse infected beasts and halt the blight.",al={"what does tharnariun want","tharnariun purpose","why help tharnariun"}},{q="Why does Tharnariun care so much about diseased animals?",a="As a protector of the wilds, Tharnariun believes that night elves cannot neglect nature without suffering the consequences. He works to cleanse the sick creatures rather than abandoning the forest to corruption.",al={"why save the beasts","tharnariun animal quest"}},{q="What quests does Tharnariun Treetender offer?",a="He directs adventurers through tasks involving the blighted lands and wildlife, notably 'Plagued Lands', 'Cleansing of the Infected', and 'Tharnariun's Hope'.",al={"tharnariun quests","tharnariun treetender tasks"}},{q="Is Tharnariun a druid?",a="While he shares the naturalist convictions of the Cenarion Circle regarding the preservation of beasts and flora, he acts primarily as a dedicated caretaker and treetender for the wilderness of Darkshore.",al={"is tharnariun druid","tharnariun class"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Tharnariun's warnings resonate deeply with their ancient duty to watch over the natural balance of northern Kalimdor.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find Tharnariun's concern for blighted wildlife closely aligned with their own sacred mission to restore harmony to corrupted lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the Alliance's primary coastal gateway in northern Kalimdor, making Tharnariun's defense of the surrounding woods vital to the outpost's safety."},kw={"auberdine","cleansing","corruption","darkshore","infected","kaldorei","plagued lands","tharnariun","treetender"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:2118","quest:2138","quest:2139","topic:night-elf"},src={"Tharnariun Treetender"}}
E["npc:vesprystus"] = {t="npc",n="Vesprystus",z="darkshore",s="Vesprystus is the night elf flight master stationed at the docks of Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil. He oversees the roost of trained hippogryphs that carry travelers between the great World Tree and mainland Kalimdor.",h="Vesprystus is the night elf flight master stationed at the docks of Rut'theran Village at the base of...",sec={{t="Keeper of the Rut'theran Roost",b="Perched at the southern base of Teldrassil in Rut'theran Village, Vesprystus tends the hippogryphs that bridge the isolated elven boughs to the rest of the world. While a magical portal connects Rut'theran directly to the canopy city of Darnassus above, crossing the sea toward Darkshore and the mainland requires wings. Vesprystus works in coordination with the flight master at Auberdine across the straight, ensuring safe passage for sentinels, emissaries, and adventurers journeying into Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Vesprystus fly travelers?",a="Vesprystus connects Rut'theran Village directly across the water to the port of Auberdine on the coast of Darkshore. From Auberdine, travelers can catch connecting hippogryph routes south toward Ashenvale and other night elf enclaves across Kalimdor.",al={"where can he take me","vesprystus flight paths","rut'theran flight route"}},{q="What creatures does Vesprystus tend?",a="He manages a roost of loyal night elf hippogryphs, ancient winged beasts native to northern Kalimdor. Night elves have raised and bonded with hippogryphs for generations to navigate forest canopies and rugged coastlines.",al={"what mounts does he have","vesprystus animals","what does he fly"}},{q="How do you reach Darnassus from where Vesprystus stands?",a="You do not need a flight to reach Darnassus from Rut'theran Village. A shimmering pink-tinted portal stands just up the path from Vesprystus's roost, instantly transporting travelers up to the city canopy.",al={"how to get to darnassus from vesprystus","vesprystus to darnassus","path to darnassus"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elf adventurers leaving Teldrassil for the first time, Vesprystus is often the handler who sends them soaring toward their very first glimpse of mainland Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Vesprystus forms a vital transit link for any Alliance traveler arriving at Teldrassil's docks and needing swift transport to coastal Darkshore."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","flight master","hippogryph master","rut'theran village","teldrassil","vesprystus"},rel={"subzone:rut-theran-village","quest:6342","quest:6341","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Vesprystus"}}
E["npc:volcor"] = {t="npc",n="Volcor",z="darkshore",s="Volcor is an injured night elf scout stranded deep within Blackwood Den in northern Darkshore. Trapped by hostile Blackwood furbolgs, he relies on his faithful companion Grimclaw and the aid of Auberdine's defenders to escape.",h="Volcor is an injured night elf scout stranded deep within Blackwood Den in northern Darkshore.",sec={{t="Trapped in the Den",b="While tracking the corrupted Blackwood tribe in their subterranean lair, Volcor was ambushed and severely wounded. Unable to fight his way past the hostile furbolgs on his own, he sent his loyal bear companion, Grimclaw, out into the wilds of Darkshore to seek help from the settlement of Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="A Way to Freedom",b="Once contacted by scouts alerted by Terenthis, Volcor offers two avenues of escape depending on his savior's strengths. Those who favor direct action can carve a bloody path through the cave's defenders, while those adept at subterfuge can use cunning and quiet movement to slip past the sentries unnoticed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Volcor located?",a="Volcor is hidden deep inside Blackwood Den, a furbolg cave located in northern Darkshore, just east of the main road heading north from Auberdine.",al={"volcor location","where is volcor","find volcor"}},{q="Why is Volcor trapped in Blackwood Den?",a="He was scouting the Blackwood furbolgs when he was attacked and wounded. Cut off from the cave entrance, he could not bypass the hostile sentries without aid.",al={"why is volcor in a cave","what happened to volcor"}},{q="Who is Grimclaw?",a="Grimclaw is Volcor's loyal bear companion. When Volcor was trapped, he sent Grimclaw out to find help in Auberdine, which ultimately alerted the scout Terenthis.",al={"who is the bear","volcor bear","grimclaw lore"}},{q="How can you help Volcor escape?",a="Volcor allows you to choose your method of rescue: you can either fight your way out through the cave's furbolg guards in a frontal assault, or sneak past them using stealth.",al={"escape through force or stealth","volcor escort quest","rescue volcor"}},{q="Who sent you to find Volcor?",a="Terenthis, a night elf sentinel stationed in Auberdine, directs adventurers to look for Volcor after Grimclaw is found wandering without his master.",al={"who gave the volcor quest","terenthis connection"}},{q="What tribe of furbolgs attacked him?",a="The Blackwood tribe, a corrupted group of furbolgs native to northern Darkshore that has succumbed to madness and hostility.",al={"which furbolgs","blackwood furbolgs"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Volcor's plight illustrates the growing danger facing the Kaldorei in Darkshore as formerly peaceful furbolg allies fall to corruption.",["class:Druid"]="The bond between Volcor and Grimclaw mirrors the deep connection druids share with nature's beasts, making his rescue a matter of natural balance.",["class:Rogue"]="Volcor appreciates tactical finesse, offering rogues the chance to bypass the Blackwood guards quietly rather than relying on brute force."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood den","darkshore","escape through force","escape through stealth","furbolg","grimclaw","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"quest:986","subzone:blackwood-den","npc:terenthis","subzone:auberdine","quest:994","quest:995","zone:darkshore","topic:furbolg"},src={"Volcor"}}
E["npc:wizbang-cranktoggle"] = {t="npc",n="Wizbang Cranktoggle",z="darkshore",s="Wizbang Cranktoggle is an eccentric gnome engineer residing on the upper floor of the Auberdine inn. Despite being far from the cog-filled halls of Gnomeregan or Ironforge, he has turned his mechanical ingenuity toward setting up and maintaining automated communication devices known as buzzboxes across the wild coast of Darkshore.",h="Wizbang Cranktoggle is an eccentric gnome engineer residing on the upper floor of the Auberdine inn.",sec={{t="An Engineer in Auberdine",b="While the night elves of Auberdine prefer living in harmony with nature and leaning upon ancient customs, Wizbang Cranktoggle represents the curious, tinkering presence of the Alliance. Perched on the top floor of Auberdine's inn, surrounded by tools and spare components, Wizbang pays little mind to the solemn druidic traditions of Kalimdor, focusing instead on pragmatic mechanical challenges.",sp=0},{t="The Buzzbox Network",b="Wizbang's primary project along Darkshore is deploying and maintaining his peculiar invention: the buzzbox. Designed to establish automated reporting and long-distance communication across the rugged, sprawling coastline, these contraptions often suffer from coastal weathering and the hostility of local wildlife. Wizbang frequently recruits travelers to gather components, salvage tools like gaffer jacks, and recover electropellers to keep his mechanical surveillance functioning.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang is located on the upper floor of the inn in the seaside night elf settlement of Auberdine, in Darkshore.",al={"wizbang location","where is wizbang","auberdine gnome location"}},{q="What is Wizbang Cranktoggle doing in Darkshore?",a="He is an Alliance engineer working on establishing and maintaining a network of automated communication machines called buzzboxes throughout the Darkshore wilderness.",al={"why is wizbang in auberdine","wizbang purpose","what does wizbang do"}},{q="What are buzzboxes?",a="Buzzboxes are mechanical communication and monitoring devices invented by Wizbang Cranktoggle to relay information across Darkshore, though they frequently break down due to wildlife attacks and harsh weather.",al={"what is a buzzbox","buzzbox lore","buzzbox purpose"}},{q="Is Wizbang related to any other gnomes?",a="He shares a surname with Delber Cranktoggle, suggesting they may belong to the same family of tinkerers.",al={"cranktoggle family","who is delber cranktoggle","wizbang relatives"}},{q="Why do the night elves tolerate his tinkering in Auberdine?",a="As fellow members of the Grand Alliance, the night elves provide lodging and refuge to allied races in Auberdine, even if gnomish contraptions contrast sharply with traditional elven harmony.",al={"night elves and gnomes","why allow engineering in auberdine"}},{q="What tasks does Wizbang give to adventurers?",a="Wizbang asks adventurers to help repair and configure his buzzbox machines, which involves scouring the shoreline for specialized parts like electropellers and gaffer jacks.",al={"wizbang quests","what quests does wizbang offer"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Seeing a fellow gnome operating an experimental communication network along Kalimdor's rugged coast is a welcome reminder of Gnomeregan's relentless inventiveness.",["profession:Engineering"]="Wizbang's reliance on custom tools like gaffer jacks and electropellers highlights the classic gnomish mindset: mechanical answers to logistical problems in uncharted lands.",["race:NightElf"]="While elven sentinels and druids rely on whisps, messengers, and natural bonds, Wizbang brings loud, whirring gears and metal boxes into Darkshore's sacred woods."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox","cranktoggle","darkshore","electropellers","engineer","gaffer jacks","gnome","wizbang"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:983","quest:1579","quest:1580","topic:gnome","topic:alliance"},src={"Wizbang Cranktoggle"}}
E["quest:1001"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 411",z="darkshore",s="Buzzbox 411 is an Alliance quest found along the windswept coastline of Darkshore. Operating through an eccentric mechanical relay network, the intoxicated gnome inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle enlists travelers to gather coastal thresher eyes to bring his second research machine back online.",h="Buzzbox 411 is an Alliance quest found along the windswept coastline of Darkshore.",sec={{t="Voice Through the Static",b="After assisting with the repairs of Buzzbox 827 further south, the voice of the gnome inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle crackles over the mechanical transmitter once more. Stationed somewhere safely out of sight, Wizbang directs adventurers further north along Darkshore's mist-laden beach to locate another damaged terminal: Buzzbox 411. Between transmissions punctuated by hiccups and muttered praises of crawler wine, he reveals that local aquatic predators hold the components necessary to keep his coastal apparatus functional.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Beneath the Surf",b="Restoring Buzzbox 411 requires diving into the chilly, turbulent waters off the coast of Auberdine. Darkshore threshers prowl the shallows, aggressive marine beasts whose ocular organs contain precisely the properties Wizbang claims are needed to recalibrate the device. Feeding the requested thresher eyes into the waiting hatch of the machine jolts the apparatus back into operation, rewarding the courier and opening the line for another increasingly slurred assignment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Buzzbox 411?",a="Buzzbox 411 is a mechanical transmitter device situated north of Auberdine along the Darkshore shoreline. It serves as part of an experimental listening and research network maintained by the gnome engineer Wizbang Cranktoggle.",al={"buzzbox 411","what is buzzbox 411","buzzbox 411 purpose"}},{q="Who is Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is an eccentric gnome tinkerer who communicates remotely through the Buzzbox network. He spends his field research heavily enjoying crawler wine while relying on passing adventurers to do the hazardous fieldwork of collecting animal parts.",al={"wizbang","who is wizbang","who made buzzbox"}},{q="Why does a machine need Thresher Eyes?",a="Gnomish engineering frequently blends bizarre organic matter with mechanical components to perform unorthodox tasks. Whether Wizbang truly needs the eyes for optical sensors or is merely using them in biological research while drunk, he insists they are vital to repairing Buzzbox 411.",al={"why thresher eyes","thresher eyes for machine","buzzbox eyes"}},{q="Where is Buzzbox 411 located?",a="Buzzbox 411 is planted right on the beach in Darkshore, located north of the night elf settlement of Auberdine.",al={"where is buzzbox 411","buzzbox 411 location","find buzzbox 411"}},{q="Where do I find Darkshore Threshers?",a="Darkshore threshers swim in the coastal waters off Auberdine and along the nearby shores, easily found by swimming out past the surf line.",al={"where are threshers","thresher eye source","thresher location"}},{q="What happens after Buzzbox 411 is fixed?",a="Once Buzzbox 411 hums back to life, Wizbang Cranktoggle thanks you over the static, downs another drink, and immediately asks if you are willing to fix his next machine, Buzzbox 323.",al={"next buzzbox","what comes after buzzbox 411","buzzbox chain"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang Cranktoggle represents the quintessential gnomish approach to fieldwork: bold innovation, peculiar component choices, and delegating the dangerous swimming to whoever is passing by.",["profession:Engineering"]="Using organic thresher eyes to calibrate a mechanical transmitter demonstrates the eccentric, boundary-pushing methods favored by unconventional tinkerers.",["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine's sentinels keep a watchful eye on Darkshore's waters, though they typically leave peculiar gnomish contraptions on the shoreline to their own devices."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 411","crawler wine","darkshore","gnome","thresher eyes","tinkering","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","quest:983","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},m={start="Buzzbox 827",["end"]="Buzzbox 411",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=1001},src={"Buzzbox 411 (quest)"}}
E["quest:1002"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 323",z="darkshore",s="Buzzbox 323 is the second task in a field-research line along the coast of Darkshore, commissioned through a speaker device by the eccentric gnome engineer Wizbang Cranktoggle. Players must gather Moonstalker fangs from local predators and deposit them into the humming contraption situated north of Auberdine.",h="Buzzbox 323 is the second task in a field-research line along the coast of Darkshore, commissioned through a...",sec={{t="A Slurred Transmission",b="After operating Buzzbox 411 further south, the voice of the gnomish inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle crackles to life over the speaker. Interspersed with the sounds of heavy drinking and slurred directions, Wizbang directs adventurers north toward Auberdine, pointing them to Buzzbox 323 near a road bridge. His research requires six Moonstalker Fangs, harvested from the fierce feline hunters roaming the shrouded forests of Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Field Machinery",b="Approaching Buzzbox 323 reveals a machine that chatters with static and faint muttering even before repairs begin. Once the requested fangs are placed inside its intake hopper, the machine violently rattles to life, noisily pulverizing the teeth to dust. Wizbang's boozy voice promptly resumes over the transceiver, celebrating the delivery before prodding the traveler toward the next machine in his scattered network.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Buzzbox 323 located?",a="Buzzbox 323 stands alongside the main road north of Auberdine, just near the bridge crossing the local river in Darkshore.",al={"buzzbox 323 location","where is buzzbox 323","find buzzbox 323"}},{q="Who is speaking through the Buzzbox?",a="The voice belongs to Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome inventor stationed elsewhere in Darkshore who communicates through remote transmitters while heavily indulging in ale.",al={"who talks in buzzbox","buzzbox gnome","wizbang cranktoggle"}},{q="What does Buzzbox 323 do with the fangs?",a="Upon dropping the Moonstalker fangs inside, internal gears immediately grind them down into fine powder as part of Wizbang's automated biological sampling mechanism.",al={"what happens to the fangs","why moonstalker fangs","buzzbox grinding"}},{q="Where can I find Moonstalkers in Darkshore?",a="Moonstalkers and their runts prowl the shaded woodlands and hills bordering the road both north and south of Auberdine.",al={"where are moonstalkers","moonstalker fang farm","moonstalker location"}},{q="What quest comes before and after Buzzbox 323?",a="This assignment follows Buzzbox 411, which required crawler claws, and directly precedes Buzzbox 525, which sends you to harvest thresher eyes further along the coast.",al={"buzzbox quest chain","what follows buzzbox 323","buzzbox order"}},{q="Why does Wizbang sound so incoherent?",a="Wizbang is thoroughly intoxicated while giving instructions, pausing to search for his ale and taking loud gulps between sentences.",al={"why is wizbang drunk","buzzbox voice slurring"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang's remote acoustic communication network showcases typical gnomish engineering flair—even if his personal discipline leaves much to be desired.",["race:NightElf"]="While native night elves treat the fierce Moonstalkers with reverent caution, gnomish science reduces their lethal fangs to pulverized machine fuel.",["profession:Engineering"]="The Buzzbox series demonstrates automated material processing coupled with long-range voice relay, an impressive technical design despite its rough operation."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox","buzzbox 323","cranktoggle","darkshore","fangs","moonstalker","wizbang"},rel={"quest:1001","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},m={start="Buzzbox 411",["end"]="Buzzbox 323",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=1002},src={"Buzzbox 323 (quest)"}}
E["quest:1003"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 525",z="darkshore",s="Buzzbox 525 is the second stage in a series of communicative machines scattered along the coast of Darkshore. Created by the eccentric gnome tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle, the contraption demands animal remnants to function—while slowly unraveling the inventor's true, illicit ambitions.",h="Buzzbox 525 is the second stage in a series of communicative machines scattered along the coast of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Slurred Transmission",b="After servicing Buzzbox 323, travelers receive garbled instructions broadcast straight through the machine's rattling speakers. Wizbang Cranktoggle's speech grows increasingly slurred, filled with drunken chuckles and rambling directions leading far south along the main road of Darkshore. He directs his helpers to hunt down the local grizzled thistle bears and deliver four of their thick scalps into the compartment of Buzzbox 525, concealed carefully behind a fence in the roadside brush.",sp=0},{t="The Distiller's Secret",b="Upon arriving at the hidden machine, the curious hum of machinery is drowned out by raucous singing echoing from within the iron plating. As the grizzly bear scalps are deposited into the receptacle, Wizbang finally comes clean about his network. The contraptions are far more than mere communications equipment: they double as automated micro-breweries and distilleries. Disdainful of the night elves' strict and abstemious customs in Auberdine, the gnome built his contraptions to distill forbidden woodland spirits—using animal harvest like bear scalps to brew potent batches of 'thistle bear beer.'",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Buzzbox 525 located?",a="Buzzbox 525 sits far south down the main road from Auberdine. Wizbang tucked it away just off the path near a rustic fence line, partially concealed beneath bushes.",al={"buzzbox 525 location","where is buzzbox 525","buzzbox 525 find"}},{q="Why does Wizbang want grizzled scalps?",a="While Wizbang initially claims the scalps are required repairs or fuel for his network, they actually serve as bizarre brewing ingredients. He uses the organic material within the Buzzbox mechanism to distill what he calls thistle bear beer.",al={"why grizzled scalps","buzzbox bear scalps","what are scalps for"},sp=1},{q="Why does Wizbang hide the Buzzboxes out in the wilderness?",a="The night elves residing in Auberdine do not appreciate reckless moonshining or an illicit alcohol trade within their serene settlements. By scattering the machines along the desolate Darkshore road, Wizbang keeps his brewing network hidden from elven authorities.",al={"why are buzzboxes hidden","why hide buzzbox","wizbang secret"},sp=1},{q="Who is speaking through the Buzzbox?",a="The voice belongs to Wizbang Cranktoggle, an enterprising gnome tinkerer who installed voice transmitters inside his makeshift brewing apparatuses across Darkshore.",al={"who talks in buzzbox","buzzbox voice","wizbang identity"}},{q="Can Wizbang speak through the machine without the scalps?",a="Yes. Upon completing the task, Wizbang admits that the audio transceivers function regardless of whether materials are fed into the hatch. His request for ingredients was entirely to keep his automated distilling operation supplied.",al={"is the buzzbox broken","did wizbang lie"},sp=1},{q="What song does the Buzzbox sing?",a="Before you deposit the scalps, the speaker repeatedly chants a drunken limerick: 'Though crawler wine's sweet, and thresher ale fine, and moonstalker moonshine is grand. There's nothing so dear, as a thistle bear beer, and soon I shall have some on hand!'",al={"buzzbox singing","thistle bear beer song"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The strict stewardship of Darkshore leaves little patience for reckless gnomish tinkering, let alone a clandestine bootlegging network operating right under the sentinels' noses.",["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang's multi-purpose brewing transceivers showcase typical gnomish ambition, blending complex engineering with questionable practical priorities.",["profession:Engineering"]="The Buzzbox system cleverly combines two-way acoustic communications with automated distillation boilers in a single, compact chassis."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 525","darkshore","distillery","grizzled scalp","thistle bear","thistle bear beer","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1002","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine"},m={start="Buzzbox 323",["end"]="Buzzbox 525",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=1003},src={"Buzzbox 525 (quest)"}}
E["quest:1132"] = {t="quest",n="Fiora Longears",z="darkshore",s="This errand introduces Alliance adventurers from the Eastern Kingdoms to the untamed continent of Kalimdor. Directed by the enthusiastic recruiter Red Jack Flint in Menethil Harbor, travelers take ship across the Great Sea to report to his night elf contact, Fiora Longears, on the docks of Auberdine.",h="This errand introduces Alliance adventurers from the Eastern Kingdoms to the untamed continent of Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Call to the West",b="For many humans, dwarves, and gnomes, the Eastern Kingdoms feel fraught with old conflicts and scarred earth. In the bustling port of Menethil Harbor, the sailor Red Jack Flint spends his days urging adventurous travelers to board a vessel bound across the Great Sea. Describing Kalimdor as an uncharted realm of fortune and opportunity, Flint directs bold wanderers to Auberdine to meet his associate, an elf named Fiora Longears.",sp=0},{t="Arrival in Auberdine",b="Crossing the ocean brings travelers to Darkshore, a misty, storm-swept coast governed by the night elves. Waiting on the wooden docks of Auberdine, Fiora Longears receives arrivals recommended by Flint. Trusting Flint's eye for character, Fiora welcomes newly arrived Alliance heroes and prepares to direct them inland toward the ancient forests of Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fiora Longears?",a="Fiora Longears is a night elf stationed at the docks of Auberdine in Darkshore. She acts as a welcoming partner and contact for Red Jack Flint, greeting Alliance travelers arriving from the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"fiora longears","who is fiora"}},{q="Who starts this quest?",a="The quest is offered by Red Jack Flint, an energetic human sailor located in Menethil Harbor along the coast of the Wetlands.",al={"quest giver","where to get fiora longears quest","who gives quest"}},{q="How do I reach Fiora Longears from Menethil Harbor?",a="Board the passenger vessel docked at Menethil Harbor that sails westward across the Great Sea directly to the harbor town of Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"how to get to auberdine","ship to auberdine","boat from menethil"}},{q="What happens after meeting Fiora Longears?",a="Upon greeting you in Auberdine, Fiora commends Flint's recommendation and offers the next leg of your journey, sending you inland to Astranaar in Ashenvale.",al={"what comes next","follow up quest","journey to astranaar quest"}},{q="What is the relationship between Red Jack Flint and Fiora Longears?",a="Flint refers to Fiora as his partner across the sea. While Flint scouts eager adventurers in the Eastern Kingdoms, Fiora receives them in Kalimdor to facilitate Alliance operations and travel inland.",al={"are flint and fiora partners","red jack flint fiora connection"}},{q="Why is the Alliance recruiting travelers to Kalimdor?",a="Kalimdor represents vast new territory and resources for the Alliance, as well as a front where night elven allies need assistance protecting their ancestral lands from threats like the Horde and demonic remnants.",al={"why go to kalimdor","why darkshore"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This journey represents the bridge between the Eastern Kingdoms and the night elven territories of Kalimdor, uniting the Alliance's eastern and western frontiers.",["race:NightElf"]="Fiora Longears serves as an official welcoming presence for eastern allies arriving at Auberdine, preparing them for the ancient wilds of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","boat","darkshore","fiora longears","kalimdor","menethil harbor","red jack flint","wetlands"},rel={"npc:red-jack-flint","subzone:auberdine","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:darkshore","quest:1133","subzone:astranaar"},m={start="Red Jack Flint",["end"]="Fiora Longears",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1132},src={"Fiora Longears (quest)"}}
E["quest:1135"] = {t="quest",n="Highperch Venom",z="darkshore",s="Fiora Longears in Auberdine tasks Alliance adventurers with journeying far south to the canyons of Thousand Needles. There, atop the elevated bluffs of Highperch, roost dangerous wyverns prized for their exceptionally potent venom.",h="Fiora Longears in Auberdine tasks Alliance adventurers with journeying far south to the canyons of Thousand...",sec={{t="A Lucrative Expedition",b="While resting in the seaside port of Auberdine, travelers may cross paths with Fiora Longears. While orcs commonly capture and domesticate wyverns as aerial mounts, Fiora points out a far more clandestine trade: the creature's lethal venom. Certain buyers across Kalimdor value fresh venom sacs far more than the beasts themselves, prompting Fiora to recruit hunters willing to brave long distances and precarious heights.",sp=0},{t="The Crags of Highperch",b="The quarry nests far south of Darkshore, within the towering sandstone mesas of Thousand Needles. At a roost known as Highperch, the local wyverns possess an unusually concentrated toxin. Reaching their nests requires navigating hostile Horde territory and scaling treacherous terrain, where hunters must slay wyverns to extract intact venom sacs before hauling the prize back to Darkshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find the wyverns for this quest?",a="The wyverns inhabit Highperch, a tall mesa nestled in the western stretches of Thousand Needles, far south of Darkshore.",al={"highperch location","where is highperch","wyvern location"}},{q="Who is Fiora Longears?",a="Fiora Longears is an Alliance contact stationed in Auberdine on the Darkshore coast. She recruits daring adventurers to procure rare and valuable natural reagents from across Kalimdor.",al={"fiora longears","who gives highperch venom"}},{q="Why is wyvern venom so valuable?",a="Wyvern venom is extremely potent and prized in select underground circles, apothecaries, and trade networks. While the Horde primarily values wyverns as aerial mounts, their venom glands fetch a handsome price among alchemists and poison-makers.",al={"why wyvern venom","wyvern poison use"}},{q="Why is an Auberdine quest sending me so far south?",a="Fiora is an enterprising dealer seeking exotic specimens that cannot be found along the calm shores of Darkshore. Highperch in Thousand Needles harbors a distinct, concentrated breed of wyvern not found in the northern forests.",al={"why thousand needles","why send to thousand needles"}},{q="What happens when you return the venom sacs?",a="Fiora inspects the sacs and notes they are bursting with venom, remarking that such quality usually only comes from young wyverns or fertile females, congratulating you on the hunt.",al={"fiora reaction","quest completion highperch venom"}},{q="Is Highperch safe for Alliance travelers?",a="No. Thousand Needles contains heavy Horde presence, centering around nearby settlements like Freewind Post. Scaling Highperch means contending with both wild predators and hostile Horde scouts.",al={"is highperch dangerous","alliance in thousand needles"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Rogues naturally understand the dark allure of exotic toxins. Sourcing pure, unrefined wyvern venom gives an intimate appreciation for Kalimdor's deadliest biological agents.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, sending hunters deep into the arid barrens of Thousand Needles highlights how far trade interests and curious reagents reach outside Ashenvale and Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Venturing into Thousand Needles places Alliance adventurers deep behind enemy lines, right beneath the watchful eyes of the Horde's tauren and orc patrols."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","fiora","highperch","longears","thousand needles","venom","wyvern"},rel={"quest:1132","subzone:highperch","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Fiora Longears",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1135},src={"Highperch Venom"}}
E["quest:1138"] = {t="quest",n="Fruit of the Sea",z="darkshore",s="Fruit of the Sea is an Alliance quest offered by the fisherman Gubber Blump on the docks of Auberdine. Passionate about culinary crustacean dishes, Gubber asks travelers to scour the Darkshore coastline for fine crab chunks while he tends to his fishing lines.",h="Fruit of the Sea is an Alliance quest offered by the fisherman Gubber Blump on the docks of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Passion for Crustaceans",b="Gubber Blump, a fisherman casting his line off the long wooden piers of Auberdine, harbors an obsessive culinary devotion to crab meat. Viewing crabs as the true bounty of the ocean, Gubber envisions an endless repertoire of recipes ranging from baked, barbecued, and boiled preparations to elaborate local specialties like whipper root crab and Ironforge surprise crab.",sp=0},{t="Combing the Tidepools",b="Because Gubber cannot tear himself away from his fishing rod, he relies on passing adventurers to gather ingredients along Darkshore's mist-shrouded beaches. The coastline teems with reef crawlers and encrusted tide crawlers scuttling among the breakers, making them an accessible, if occasionally pinch-happy, source of meat for an aspiring coastal cook.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Fruit of the Sea?",a="The quest is given by Gubber Blump, an Alliance fisherman stationed on the docks of Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"fruit of the sea quest giver","who gives fruit of the sea","gubber blump quest"}},{q="What creatures drop the Fine Crab Chunks?",a="Fine Crab Chunks are harvested from reef crawlers and encrusted tide crawlers found walking the shores and shallow surf along the Darkshore coastline.",al={"where do fine crab chunks drop","what drops crab chunks","which crabs drop fine crab chunks"}},{q="Why doesn't Gubber gather the crab meat himself?",a="Gubber is fully occupied fishing from the piers of Auberdine and cannot abandon his line to hunt crawling crabs along the beach.",al={"why doesn't gubber get his own crab","why does gubber need help"}},{q="What dishes does Gubber want to make?",a="Gubber boasts about an enormous variety of preparation styles, including crab salad, soup, stew, pepper crab, lemon crab, whipper root crab, and a regional recipe he calls Ironforge surprise crab.",al={"gubber crab recipes","what recipes does gubber mention","crab dishes"}},{q="Is Gubber Blump's speech referencing something?",a="Yes. His monologue cataloging every conceivable method to cook crab is a clear homage to Benjamin Buford 'Bubba' Blue from the film Forrest Gump, who famously delivered an identical speech about shrimp.",al={"gubber blump pop culture reference","forrest gump bubba reference"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The quest begins and turns in at the port village of Auberdine, with the hunting taking place along the shores of Darkshore in northern Kalimdor.",al={"where is fruit of the sea","what zone is fruit of the sea in"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Gubber's enthusiastic breakdown of crab recipes serves as inspiration for any cook looking to make the most of local coastal catches.",["race:Dwarf"]="Hearing an outsider in northern Kalimdor dream about cooking an 'Ironforge surprise crab' is a quaint reminder of home for traveling Khaz Modan mountaineers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as a vital landing hub for Alliance explorers arriving in Kalimdor, offering small favors like helping local fishermen settle in."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","encrusted tide crawlers","fine crab chunks","fruit of the sea","gubber blump","reef crawlers"},rel={"npc:gubber-blump","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Gubber Blump",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=1138},src={"Fruit of the Sea"}}
E["quest:1140"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest represents the sixth chapter in the crusade against the cultists of the Tower of Althalaxx, directed by Delgren the Purifier from Maestra's Post. Delgren deciphers orcish writings recovered from the cult's emissaries to reveal that the warlock Athrikus Narassin has hidden two trapped Highborne soulgems inside demonic satyr strongholds deep in Ashenvale. Champions are dispatched to Night Run and Satyrnaar to shatter these vessels, freeing the tormented ancient spirits and shattering Athrikus's dark source of power.",h="This quest represents the sixth chapter in the crusade against the cultists of the Tower of Althalaxx...",sec={{t="Deciphering the Scribblings",b="After cutting down the orcish courier Ilkrud Magthrull, Delgren the Purifier puts his controversial studies of the Orcish tongue to good use. While his peers in the Holy Light often scoffed at learning the language of their adversaries, Delgren's pragmatic insight unravels the cult's clandestine trade. The notes reveal that Athrikus Narassin secured two potent soulgems containing the essences of ancient Highborne, hiding them far to the northeast within the defiled groves of Night Run and Satyrnaar.",sp=0},{t="Unholy Alliances",b="The presence of Highborne soulgems inside satyr encampments exposes a foul convergence between Athrikus's dark cabal and the demonic scions of the Burning Legion. Bound above ritual circles of imprisonment, these ancient spirits suffer endless torment to fuel dark spellcraft. Venturing into the blood-soaked altars of the satyr requires confronting not only wild demonic corruption, but the lurking daggers of hidden satyr stalkers sworn to guard these arcane conduits.",sp=1},{t="Weakening Athrikus",b="By smashing the crimson stones and liberating the Highborne souls from their circles of agony, adventurers strike a devastating blow to Athrikus's reservoir of mystic strength. Delgren notes that with these soulgems destroyed, the leader of the Althalaxx cult is severely weakened. The deed also leaves the holy crusader unsettled by the night elves' quiet unease regarding the satyrs, prompting him to resolve to bring the lingering demonic blight to the attention of Auberdine's leaders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Delgren know how to read Orcish?",a="Delgren took the initiative to study the language of the orcs, despite being ridiculed by others in his holy order. He believes that understanding an enemy's tongue is vital to gaining tactical insight, which directly allows him to translate the recovered notes from Ilkrud Magthrull.",al={"delgren reads orc","how does delgren know orcish","delgren translation"}},{q="What are the soulgems and why are they held by satyrs?",a="The soulgems are crimson focus stones binding the ancient spirits of Highborne elves, suspended over ritual circles of imprisonment. Athrikus Narassin bargained or placed them within satyr sanctuaries like Night Run and Satyrnaar, drawing upon their misery to fuel the cult's arcane power.",al={"althalaxx soulgems","why do satyrs have the gems","trapped highborne souls"}},{q="Where are Night Run and Satyrnaar located?",a="Both locations are demonic satyr strongholds nestled in the forested heights of northeastern Ashenvale, east of Maestra's Post.",al={"where is night run","where is satyrnaar","satyr camp locations"}},{q="Why are the night elves reluctant to talk about the satyrs?",a="Delgren notices that his elven hosts avoid discussing the satyrs because the creatures were once night elves themselves. The satyrs were warped into goat-legged fiends during the ancient War of the Ancients after surrendering to demonic corruption, making their existence an enduring source of grief and shame for the Kaldorei.",al={"why secretive about satyr","night elf satyr connection","satyr history elven"}},{q="How does freeing these souls help stop the Tower of Althalaxx cult?",a="Athrikus Narassin relies heavily on the stolen spiritual energy held within the Highborne soulgems. Shattering the floating gems and releasing the trapped ghosts starves his rituals of power, leaving him vulnerable to a direct assault at the tower.",al={"why shatter soulgems","athrikus power source","weakening athrikus"}},{q="Who is Elissa that Delgren mentions speaking to?",a="Elissa Starbreeze is a prominent night elf priestess stationed in Auberdine who coordinates local defenses in Darkshore. Delgren plans to confer with her regarding the entrenched satyr infestation threatening northern Kalimdor.",al={"elissa auberdine","who is elissa","delgren elissa"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Delgren the Purifier reflects a pragmatic brand of holy crusader, using the language of his foes to unearth demonic corruption and cleanse the tormented dead.",["race:NightElf"]="Liberating Highborne ancestors from satyr desecration is a solemn duty, confronting the tragic remnants of your people's ancient past.",["class:Priest"]="Shattering the circles of imprisonment brings peace to anguished spirits suffering centuries of demonic torment."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","athrikus","delgren","highborne","maestra's post","night run","satyrnaar","soulgems"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:night-run","subzone:satyrnaar","topic:highborne","topic:satyr","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1140},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (6)"}}
E["quest:1141"] = {t="quest",n="The Family and the Fishing Pole",z="darkshore",s="Gubber Blump, a dwarf dwelling on the docks of Auberdine, seeks assistance catching native Darkshore grouper. Hostile murlocs prowling the coast have disrupted the town's small fishing boats, leaving Gubber stranded on shore and offering an heirloom rod to anyone willing to cast their line.",h="Gubber Blump, a dwarf dwelling on the docks of Auberdine, seeks assistance catching native Darkshore grouper.",sec={{t="A Dwarf Far From Ironforge",b="Gubber Blump takes great pride in his lineage, declaring that the Blump name has long been synonymous with the art of angling. While night elves occupy most of Auberdine, dwarves and gnomes have settled into its docks and bustling port facilities. Rather than digging into stone, Gubber spends his days gazing out over the misty waters of the Veiled Sea, eager to haul in the local bounty.",sp=0},{t="Murloc Infestations and Darkshore Grouper",b="The Darkshore grouper is a prized coastal fish, versatile in cooking and famously spirited on the line. Normally, local fishermen would row small craft out into deeper waters to haul them in. However, the aggressive arrival of coastal murlocs has brought civilian boat traffic to a standstill. Fearing the creatures are devouring all the local fish stocks, Gubber recruits travelers willing to angle from the shoreline.",sp=0},{t="The Blump Legacy",b="To reward those who bring him a hearty catch, Gubber parts with a Blump Family Fishing Pole. By his estimation, anyone capable of hauling in a batch of feisty groupers measures up to the legendary anglers of his bloodline—including his bearded, sharp-scented cousin Graun Blump. To a dwarf of his eccentric tastes, handing over a family rod is the ultimate sign of respect.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gubber Blump?",a="Gubber Blump is a dwarf fisherman stationed on the docks of Auberdine in Darkshore. Hailing from a proud family of anglers, he teaches basic fishing techniques and passes down his family's signature rods to promising fishermen.",al={"who is gubber","gubber blump lore","auberdine dwarf fisherman"}},{q="Why aren't boats going out from Auberdine to fish?",a="Hostile murlocs have overrun large stretches of the Darkshore coastline. Their aggressive presence has made launching small personal fishing crafts far too dangerous, keeping local anglers pinned to the piers and shallows.",al={"why no boats","darkshore fishing boats","auberdine boat trouble"}},{q="What is a Darkshore grouper?",a="It is a native saltwater fish found off the misty coast of Darkshore. Anglers prize the grouper for both the challenge of landing one and its versatility in various hearty coastal recipes.",al={"darkshore grouper","grouper darkshore"}},{q="Who is Graun Blump?",a="Graun is Gubber Blump's cousin. According to Gubber, she possesses a full beard, smells rather pungent, and stands among the finest anglers their family has ever produced.",al={"graun blump","gubber cousin"}},{q="Why are there dwarves in a night elf town like Auberdine?",a="Following the Third War and the forging of the Alliance, Ironforge dwarves and gnomes traveled across the sea to Kalimdor to trade, establish maritime links, and assist their new night elf allies with harbor infrastructure.",al={"why dwarves in auberdine","dwarves in darkshore"}},{q="What is the Blump Family Fishing Pole?",a="It is a sturdy fishing rod crafted and used by the Blump clan. Gubber bestows these treasured poles upon travelers who prove they have genuine angling talent along Darkshore's waters.",al={"blump fishing pole","blump family rod","gubber reward pole"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Finding a fellow dwarf passionately dedicated to fishing rather than subterranean smithing or brewing is an eccentric reminder of your people's varied pursuits.",["profession:Cooking"]="Darkshore grouper makes for a reliable, nutritious catch along the northern Kalimdor coast, serving as a staple ingredient for frontier camp meals.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as a vital Alliance port on Kalimdor, where mainland races and night elves cooperate daily against coastal hazards like murlocs."},kw={"auberdine","blump family fishing pole","darkshore grouper","fishing","graun blump","gubber blump","murloc","veiled sea"},rel={"npc:gubber-blump","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc","quest:1579","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle"},m={start="Gubber Blump",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=1141},src={"The Family and the Fishing Pole"}}
E["quest:1143"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest marks the direct assault on Athrikus Narassin, the ancient dark sorcerer holding the pinnacle of the Tower of Althalaxx. Under the direction of Balthule Shadowstrike, an Alliance operative must breach the ruined keep and execute the cabal's master. Eliminating Athrikus strikes a devastating blow to the demonic worship corrupting northern Darkshore.",h="This quest marks the direct assault on Athrikus Narassin, the ancient dark sorcerer holding the pinnacle of...",sec={{t="Breaching the Summit",b="Perched upon the ruined heights of northern Darkshore, the Tower of Althalaxx has become a foul center of demonic summoning. Balthule Shadowstrike, monitoring the ruin from nearby, determines that the time to act is immediate. At the tower's peak dwells Athrikus Narassin, an ancient and formidable night elven warlock who orchestrates the dark rituals taking place beneath its shattered stone roof.",sp=0},{t="A Decisive Strike",b="Athrikus surrounds himself with loyal warlocks and dark magic far deadlier than the cultists patrolling the slopes below. Striking down the master cultist requires cutting through his inner circle and securing his severed head as proof. While Balthule notes that the demonic presence may one day seek to regroup, Athrikus's demise robs the cult of its commanding intellect and buys precious safety for Darkshore.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Athrikus Narassin?",a="Athrikus Narassin is an ancient night elf warlock commanding the cultists stationed at the Tower of Althalaxx. He directs the dark summonings and demonic rites infesting the ruins in northern Darkshore.",al={"athrikus","who is athrikus","boss of althalaxx"}},{q="Where can Athrikus Narassin be found?",a="Athrikus resides at the very top of the Tower of Althalaxx, guarded by a coterie of seasoned warlocks and summoned minions.",al={"where is athrikus","athrikus location","top of althalaxx"}},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike, an Alliance scout camped near the base of the Tower of Althalaxx, issues the mission to slay Athrikus.",al={"quest giver","balthule","balthule shadowstrike"}},{q="Who is Delgren mentioned in the quest?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance ally stationed nearby who sent you to coordinate with Balthule to eliminate the demonic cabal.",al={"delgren","delgren the purifier"}},{q="What happens after Athrikus is defeated?",a="Balthule confirms that Athrikus's death deals a critical blow to demonic operations in the area, though he warns that the dark forces will eventually regroup.",al={"after athrikus","tower of althalaxx ending"},sp=1},{q="Why is the Tower of Althalaxx dangerous to Darkshore?",a="The cultists and warlocks residing in the tower practice fel sorcery and summon demons into night elven lands, threatening the wilderness and the nearby settlements.",al={"why clean tower","althalaxx threat"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Confronting Athrikus Narassin represents a bitter reminder of the arcane and demonic corruption that once devastated night elven civilization.",["class:Warlock"]="Athrikus commands potent demonic magic from the summit of Althalaxx, serving as a lethal example of how unbound fel worship draws lethal attention.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing northern Darkshore from demonic cultists is vital to protecting Alliance travel corridors between Auberdine and the lands beyond."},kw={"althalaxx","athrikus","balthule","darkshore","demonic","narassin","shadowstrike","warlock"},rel={"npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","quest:494","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=1143},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (8)"}}
E["quest:1167"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest marks the tense pause before confronting Athrikus Narassin at the Tower of Althalaxx. Sent northward by Delgren the Purifier, adventurers reconvene with the scout Balthule Shadowstrike to gather intelligence on erratic, dark occurrences rocking the spire.",h="This quest marks the tense pause before confronting Athrikus Narassin at the Tower of Althalaxx.",sec={{t="A Scout's Report",b="After purifying corrupted relics and unraveling the cult's grip along Darkshore's border, Delgren the Purifier dispatches you back north to consult his sentinel partner, Balthule Shadowstrike. Before assaulting the sorcerer Athrikus directly, Delgren recognizes the necessity of fresh battlefield reconnaissance, trusting Balthule's tireless watch from the ruins overlooking the tower.",sp=0},{t="Disturbances in the Spire",b="Upon reaching Balthule's vigil, the scout describes an alarming escalation within the upper sanctum. Sudden flashes of blinding luminescence, agonizing screams cutting through the mist, and erratic strikes of lightning have begun to violently wrack the ancient elven tower, heralding an unstable and dangerous climax to Athrikus's dark work.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Delgren send me back to Balthule?",a="Delgren knows that charging blindly into Athrikus's lair is reckless. Balthule has been keeping constant eyes on the Tower of Althalaxx, making him the only one who knows what Athrikus and his cultists have been doing in recent moments.",al={"why see balthule","talk to balthule","delgren orders"}},{q="Where is Balthule Shadowstrike located?",a="Balthule maintains an observation campsite on the hills just south and east of the Tower of Althalaxx, watching the ruins in northern Darkshore.",al={"balthule location","find balthule","where is balthule"}},{q="What recent events did Balthule witness at the tower?",a="Balthule witnessed a blinding flash erupting from the tower's uppermost chamber, followed by wretched screams carrying across the coast and erratic bolts of lightning striking the ground.",al={"what happened at the tower","balthule screams","tower flash"}},{q="Who is Athrikus?",a="Athrikus Narassin is the dark sorcerer leading the cultists at the Tower of Althalaxx, whose fell rituals Delgren and Balthule are determined to stop.",al={"who is athrikus","athrikus narassin","tower boss"}},{q="Is Delgren the Purifier a local night elf?",a="No, Delgren is a human paladin and warrior of the Holy Light stationed on the border between Darkshore and Ashenvale, allied with night elf scouts to purge demonic corruption.",al={"who is delgren","delgren race","is delgren an elf"}},{q="What kind of ruin is the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="It is a highborne or ancient night elf spire along the craggy northern cliffs of Darkshore, long abandoned before fallen arcanists and demonic cultists claimed it for forbidden rites.",al={"althalaxx background","what is the tower","tower lore"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The coordination between Delgren and Balthule represents a practical wartime partnership between human paladins and night elf scouts to keep northern Kalimdor safe.",["class:Paladin"]="Delgren's calculated approach demonstrates the discipline expected of warriors of the Light, favoring vigilant intelligence before rushing into unholy sanctums.",["race:NightElf"]="Balthule Shadowstrike defends ancestral lands from sorcery that mirrors the reckless arcane excesses that ruined night elf civilization ten millennia ago."},kw={"althalaxx","athrikus","balthule","cultists","darkshore","delgren","tower"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",["end"]="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1167},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (7)"}}
E["quest:1442"] = {t="quest",n="Seeking the Kor Gem",z="darkshore",s="\"Seeking the Kor Gem\" is an Alliance paladin quest that sends an initiate deep into the ancient ruins of northern Kalimdor. Directed by the night elf Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine, paladins venture into Blackfathom Deeps to wrest a potent Kor gem from the naga who corrupt it. The retrieved stone serves as a key material in Jordan Stilwell's craft.",h="\"Seeking the Kor Gem\" is an Alliance paladin quest that sends an initiate deep into the ancient ruins of...",sec={{t="A Trusted Alliance",b="When paladins in training seek the materials needed by the human smith Jordan Stilwell, their journey crosses continental borders to Darkshore. There, at Auberdine, Thundris Windweaver remembers the blacksmith with respect. Despite the natural aloofness of the night elves and the transgressions of certain fallen human figures, Thundris holds faith in paladins pursuing a righteous path and willingly reveals where such ancient gems are found.",sp=0},{t="Into the Deeps",b="The search leads directly to the subterranean temple complex of Blackfathom Deeps along the foggy northwestern coast of Ashenvale. Inhabited by Twilight's Hammer cultists and treacherous sea-dwellers, the watery depths are also home to naga priestesses who channel foul magic through ancient Kor gems. A paladin must brave these dark halls, defeat the sorceresses, and secure a gem steeped in serpentine malice.",sp=0},{t="Cleansing the Stone",b="Returning a corrupted Kor gem to Thundris Windweaver reveals the true purpose of seeking out an elven mystic. While the naga imbue the gem with raw magical potency, their enchantments twist it toward evil. Before Jordan Stilwell can forge it into a holy weapon, Thundris must excise the darkness, ensuring its power remains pure and stable for the sacred smithing ritual ahead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find the Kor Gem?",a="The quest is given by Thundris Windweaver, a night elf located in the coastal port of Auberdine in Darkshore. He directs paladins on behalf of the weaponsmith Jordan Stilwell.",al={"quest giver seeking kor gem","who gives seeking the kor gem","thundris windweaver quest"}},{q="Where is the Kor Gem located?",a="The gem is found inside Blackfathom Deeps, an ancient subterranean dungeon located in northwestern Ashenvale along the coast. It is carried by the naga priestesses inhabiting the ruins.",al={"kor gem location","where to get kor gem","where is corrupted kor gem"}},{q="Why does Jordan Stilwell need a Kor Gem?",a="The gem contains potent magical energies required as a component for crafting Jordan's refined weapon during the paladin trial known as The Test of Righteousness.",al={"why kor gem","what is kor gem for","stilwell gem"}},{q="Why does Thundris have to purify the gem?",a="The naga imbue Kor gems with substantial arcane power, but their foul nature taints the magic. Thundris purifies the gem of this corruption so that its remaining strength can be safely channeled into a weapon of the Light.",al={"why purify kor gem","corrupted kor gem cleansed","cleansing the gem"}},{q="Why does Thundris mention a 'fallen kind'?",a="Thundris is likely alluding to high-profile human betrayals, such as Prince Arthas Menethil, whose descent into darkness tarnished the reputation of the Silver Hand across Azeroth. Despite this, Thundris chooses to judge individual paladins by their own merit.",al={"who is the fallen one","thundris fallen kind","fallen paladin reference"}},{q="Do I need a group to get the Kor Gem?",a="Thundris explicitly warns adventurers not to go alone. Because the gem drops from elite naga deep inside Blackfathom Deeps, entering with a dedicated adventuring party is strongly advised.",al={"is kor gem soloable","can you solo kor gem","blackfathom deeps group"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="This quest is an essential trial of character and endurance for an Alliance paladin, testing your willingness to travel into hostile Kalimdor depths to forge a consecrated arm of the Light.",["race:NightElf"]="Thundris Windweaver's cooperation highlights the fragile yet growing bridge between the ancient Kaldorei and the newly allied practitioners of the Holy Light from the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="The mission illustrates Alliance unity in action, as a human blacksmith relies on night elf wisdom and dwarven steel to craft armaments against rising darkness."},kw={"auberdine","blackfathom deeps","darkshore","jordan stilwell","kor gem","naga","paladin","test of righteousness","thundris windweaver"},rel={"quest:1653","zone:blackfathom","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:naga"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1442},src={"Seeking the Kor Gem"}}
E["quest:1579"] = {t="quest",n="Gaffer Jacks",z="darkshore",s="Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome inventor nursing a hangover in Auberdine, needs help retrieving a box of lost hardware he tossed into the sea. Having fled the clatter of Ironforge for the quiet shores of Kalimdor, he managed to drop his vital gaffer jacks overboard during the voyage. Anyone with a fishing rod and patience can dredge up these missing components along the coastline.",h="Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome inventor nursing a hangover in Auberdine, needs help retrieving a box of lost...",sec={{t="A Cluttered Mind in a Quiet Haven",b="Seeking peace and quiet away from the deafening clatter of Ironforge's Great Forge, the eccentric gnome inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle sailed across the Great Sea to Darkshore. Unfortunately, Wizbang indulged in a bit too much drink during the crossing. While leaning over the railing in an alcoholic haze, he managed to lose an entire crate of specialized metal components known as gaffer jacks into the coastal waters outside Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="Tuning the Stintle Pegs",b="Gaffer jacks might look like obscure bits of metallic scrap to ordinary passersby, but to Wizbang they are indispensable precision tools. Without them, he claims it is entirely impossible to properly calibrate his stintle pegs or proceed with any of his delicate tinkering. Reluctant to plunge into the cold ocean surf himself, the gnome relies on local anglers to cast their lines along the Darkshore surf and fish up the scattered hardware.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are gaffer jacks?",a="Gaffer jacks are small gnomish mechanical fasteners and components. According to Wizbang Cranktoggle, they are vital specialized tools used specifically for tuning stintle pegs in his tinkering projects.",al={"what is a gaffer jack","gaffer jack use","gaffer jacks item"}},{q="How did the gaffer jacks end up in the sea?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle had a bit too much to drink while traveling by ship from the Eastern Kingdoms to Kalimdor. While intoxicated aboard the vessel, he accidentally dropped his supply box overboard near the coast of Darkshore.",al={"how did he lose them","why are they in the water","why fish for gaffer jacks"}},{q="Why is Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine instead of Ironforge?",a="Wizbang sought out Auberdine specifically for its silence and tranquility. He found the constant clatter, ringing anvils, and noisy workshops of Ironforge unbearable, particularly while nursing the persistent hangovers from his heavy drinking.",al={"why is wizbang in auberdine","why did wizbang leave ironforge"}},{q="Where can the lost gaffer jacks be fished up?",a="They can be fished out of the open saltwater along the Darkshore coastline near Auberdine. Anglers reel them in from regular coastal water casts rather than distinct schools of fish.",al={"where do i fish gaffer jacks","gaffer jacks location"}},{q="What happens after recovering the gaffer jacks?",a="Once Wizbang has his gaffer jacks returned to tune his pegs, he reveals that he also managed to lose another critical set of equipment in the sea: his electropellers, which require further fishing or diving to retrieve.",al={"what next after gaffer jacks","quest after gaffer jacks"},sp=1},{q="Why does Wizbang need adventurers instead of retrieving them himself?",a="Between his throbbing hangover and lack of sea angling gear, Wizbang prefers to stay safely dry on the Auberdine docks, leaving the tedious dredging work to any passerby with a fishing rod.",al={"why cant wizbang get them","why doesnt wizbang fish"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang embodies the restless eccentricity of gnomish tinkerers, though even fellow gnomes might cringe at his reckless combination of high-precision components and heavy drinking.",["profession:Engineering"]="Any engineer knows the misery of missing one tiny, non-standard mechanical component needed to finish calibrating a delicate device.",["race:NightElf"]="The quiet, sacred woods of Darkshore make an odd destination for an abrasive, hungover gnome inventor, testing the legendary patience of Auberdine's night elf sentinels."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","electropellers","fishing","gaffer jacks","ironforge","stintle pegs","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","quest:1580","quest:1141","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Wizbang Cranktoggle",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=1579},src={"Gaffer Jacks"}}
E["quest:1580"] = {t="quest",n="Electropellers",z="darkshore",s="Electropellers is a lighthearted errand for the eccentric gnome tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine. After losing his bag of prototype components in Darkshore's freshwater streams during a misadventure with an explosive duck decoy, Wizbang asks passing anglers to fish them back out.",h="Electropellers is a lighthearted errand for the eccentric gnome tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Tipsy Invention",b="Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome tinkerer stationed in the quiet night elf port of Auberdine, spent an evening wandering inland Darkshore searching for testing grounds. His latest passion project was a self-propelled, exploding duck decoy. Unfortunately, a bit too much drink led to an untimely blackout. Wizbang woke hours later back in town with singed hair and a completely empty pack, having accidentally dropped his precious bag of electropellers into one of the coastal rivers.",sp=0},{t="Dredging the Waters",b="Rather than brave the wilds himself to retrieve his scattered mechanical parts, Wizbang calls upon local fishermen to dredge the freshwater streams of Darkshore. Anglers casting lines across waterways like the Wildbend River and Cliffspring River frequently snag these buoyant, metallic gizmos alongside the local fish. Recovering the components allows the oblivious gnome to resume his dangerously erratic waterfowl experiments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find the electropellers?",a="They must be fished out of Darkshore's freshwater rivers and lakes, such as the Cliffspring River or the Wildbend River. They will not appear in the ocean waters along the coast.",al={"where are electropellers","how to get electropellers","electropeller location"}},{q="Who is Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang is an eccentric gnomish engineer residing in Auberdine. Known for bizarre and explosive inventions, he relies on adventurous travelers to gather lost components and oddities for his experiments.",al={"who gives electropellers","wizbang cranktoggle"}},{q="What was Wizbang trying to build?",a="He was working on a self-propelled, exploding duck decoy. His testing went awry after he indulged in a bit too much drink and accidentally detonated an early prototype, scorching his hair and losing his bag of parts in the water.",al={"exploding duck decoy","wizbang project"}},{q="Can electropellers be found in fish schools?",a="No, electropellers are hauled up from open freshwater casts. Casting your line directly into special schools, such as Lesser Oily Blackmouth nodes, will not yield the mechanical parts.",al={"fish schools electropellers","can i fish schools"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="You must first complete Gaffer Jacks, an earlier fishing task Wizbang assigns to test your angling luck in the local waters.",al={"prereq for electropellers","electropellers prerequisite"}},{q="Are electropellers dropped by monsters?",a="No. They cannot be looted from enemies or found in ground containers; they must be retrieved from the rivers using a fishing pole.",al={"do mobs drop electropellers","who drops electropellers"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang's chaotic ambition to build exploding duck decoys is a familiar sight to any gnome, even if losing expensive parts in an elf-guarded river is slightly embarrassing.",["profession:Engineering"]="Electropellers are curious examples of miniaturized gnomish propulsion, designed to drive mechanical decoys before violently combusting.",["race:NightElf"]="Local night elves look upon Wizbang's loud, smoky inventions and river-littering mishaps with quiet disapproval, preferring Darkshore's streams remain natural."},kw={"auberdine","cliffspring river","darkshore","duck decoy","electropellers","fishing","wildbend river","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1579","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","subzone:auberdine","subzone:wildbend-river","quest:4762","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Wizbang Cranktoggle",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=1580},src={"Electropellers"}}
E["quest:2078"] = {t="quest",n="Gyromast's Revenge",z="darkshore",s="Gelkak Gyromast seeks payback against the local murlocs who wrecked his ship along the Darkshore coastline. To carry out his vendetta, the eccentric captain sends adventurers to reactivate his mechanical first mate, the Threshwackonator 4100.",h="Gelkak Gyromast seeks payback against the local murlocs who wrecked his ship along the Darkshore coastline.",sec={{t="A Captain's Vendetta",b="Stranded upon the misty strands of Darkshore, Gelkak Gyromast refuses to accept defeat at the hands of the shore-dwelling murlocs. Having salvaged the pieces needed to fuel his schemes, the eccentric captain sets his sights on complete retaliation against the tribe and their chief. Rather than wading into the surf with cutlass in hand, Gelkak relies on heavy engineering to exact his vengeance, entrusting a winding key to any landlubber brave enough to handle his mechanical subordinate.",sp=0},{t="The First Mate's Mutiny",b="Gelkak's trusted first mate is no salty dwarf or sailor, but the Threshwackonator 4100—a clanking mechanical golem abandoned in the shallows south of the wreck. While wind-up automation promises an easy slaughter of the murlocs, gnomish and dwarven contraptions are notorious for volatile behavior when exposed to salt water. Upon being wound up and led back to the captain, the construct suffers a catastrophic malfunction, mistaking its rescuer and creator for hostile targets and forcing a battle on the beach.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gelkak's first mate?",a="Gelkak's first mate is the Threshwackonator 4100, an automated mechanical golem resting on the coast south of the stranded captain's camp.",al={"first mate","gelkak first mate","who is the first mate"}},{q="Why does Gelkak want revenge?",a="Gelkak's vessel was shipwrecked along Darkshore, and the native Greymist murlocs scavenged his belongings and harassed his surviving crew. Gelkak intends to use his golem to crush the tribe and their chief.",al={"why revenge","murloc revenge","gelkak motivation"}},{q="What happens when you bring the Threshwackonator back?",a="Once wound up and led back to Gelkak's camp, the Threshwackonator 4100 suffers an operational malfunction and turns hostile, forcing you to destroy it to protect the area.",al={"threshwackonator attack","robot malfunction","why does the golem attack"},sp=1},{q="What do I do with Gyromast's Key after finishing the quest?",a="Gyromast's Key serves no further purpose once the Threshwackonator 4100 has been activated and defeated, and it can be safely discarded.",al={"gyromast key use","keep gyromast key","can i delete key"},sp=1},{q="Where did Gelkak get the Threshwackonator?",a="The golem is part of the cargo and equipment salvaged from Gelkak's ill-fated voyage along northern Kalimdor, designed as heavy mechanical muscle for his crew.",al={"who built threshwackonator","threshwackonator origin"}},{q="Does Gelkak give up after the golem is destroyed?",a="Despite the destruction of his mechanical first mate, Gelkak grudgingly commends your survival, jokingly offering a promotion to poop deck swabby while remaining stranded on the beach.",al={"what happens to gelkak","after gyromast revenge"},sp=1}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The Threshwackonator 4100 is a classic example of clockwork automation gone awry after exposure to sea spray and water damage, reinforcing the engineering maxim to always double-check gyro-stabilizers.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomes will immediately recognize the folly of trying to reboot sensitive mechanical automata with a simple winding key in the damp, briny environment of Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing out malfunctioning machinery and aggressive murlocs helps secure the coastline for Alliance travel between Auberdine and the lands to the south."},kw={"darkshore","gelkak","golem","gyromast","key","murloc","threshwackonator","threshwackonator 4100"},rel={"npc:gelkak-gyromast","quest:2098","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc"},m={start="Gelkak Gyromast",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=2078},src={"Gyromast's Revenge"}}
E["quest:2098"] = {t="quest",n="Gyromast's Retrieval",z="darkshore",s="Shipwrecked on the misty coast of Darkshore, the eccentric gnome pirate Gelkak Gyromast seeks aid to restore his mechanical first mate. His vital winding key was shattered upon the rocks and scavenged by the local wildlife and murlocs. Recovering the three pieces is the first step toward getting his crew back in working order.",h="Shipwrecked on the misty coast of Darkshore, the eccentric gnome pirate Gelkak Gyromast seeks aid to restore...",sec={{t="Castaway on Darkshore",b="Gelkak Gyromast is an odd sight along the gloomy sands of Darkshore: a gnome pirate stranded far from the typical sea routes of the South Seas. According to Gelkak, his vessel met an unfortunate end just off the coastline after being attacked and sunk by aggressive threshadons. Washing ashore amid the flotsam, he found himself utterly marooned and separated from his trusty crew.",sp=0},{t="The Scavenged Key",b="Gelkak's most pressing concern is not provisions or gold, but his first mate. Activating and operating this companion requires a specialized key, which shattered into three distinct fragments when Gelkak crashed onto the rocky shoals. Before he could gather the fragments, the indigenous wildlife—scuttling reef crawlers on the beach, towering foreststriders near the woods, and scavengers from the local Greymist murloc tribe—snatched the shiny metal pieces away.",sp=0},{t="A Peculiar Companion",b="Gelkak speaks of his first mate with the fierce loyalty of a sea captain, though references to needing to put the companion 'in workin' order' hint at an unorthodox crewmate. A gnome mariner stranded on foreign shores naturally relies on mechanical ingenuity, and reassembling the broken key proves vital to restarting whatever clockwork marvel Gelkak dragged from the depths.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gelkak Gyromast?",a="Gelkak Gyromast is an eccentric gnome pirate who was shipwrecked off the coast of Darkshore when predatory threshadons attacked and sank his vessel.",al={"gelkak gyromast","who is the gnome pirate","darkshore gnome pirate"}},{q="What is the key used for?",a="The key is required to reactivate and wind up Gelkak's first mate, a mechanical creation that was powered down during their disastrous shipwreck.",al={"why does gelkak need the key","gelkak key purpose","first mate key"}},{q="Where did the three pieces of the key go?",a="When the key broke on the shore, the pieces were scavenged by local creatures: the top piece was taken by foreststriders, the middle by Greymist murlocs, and the bottom by coastal reef crawlers.",al={"where are the key pieces","who stole the key","broken key darkshore"}},{q="Why was a gnome pirate sailing near Darkshore?",a="Gelkak was navigating the waters off northern Kalimdor in search of plunder, but hostile threshadons brought an abrupt end to his voyage.",al={"why is gelkak in darkshore","pirates in darkshore"}},{q="What happens after the key is reassembled?",a="Once Gelkak has all three pieces of his key, he can proceed with winding up his companion, leading directly into the quest 'Gyromast's Revenge'.",al={"what next after key","gyromast retrieval follow up"},sp=1},{q="Who are the murlocs holding the key piece?",a="The middle piece is scavenged by the Greymist tribe of murlocs, who have made their home among the wreckage of drowned ships along Darkshore's shoals.",al={"darkshore murlocs","greymist murloc key","shipwreck murlocs"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Gnomes will immediately recognize Gelkak's reliance on clockwork devices over flesh-and-blood shipmates, even if his pirate lifestyle is quite unusual for their kin.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate the challenge of keeping clockwork contraptions functional after enduring a violent shipwreck in saltwater."},kw={"darkshore","first mate","foreststrider","gelkak gyromast","greymist","gyromast's retrieval","pirate","reef crawler","threshadon"},rel={"npc:gelkak-gyromast","quest:2078","zone:darkshore","topic:pirate","topic:murloc","quest:938"},m={start="Gelkak Gyromast",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=2098},src={"Gyromast's Retrieval"}}
E["quest:2118"] = {t="quest",n="Plagued Lands",z="darkshore",s="Plagued Lands is an Alliance quest offered by Tharnariun Treetender in Darkshore. Driven to remedy the spreading corruption afflicting the native wildlife, Tharnariun tasks adventurers with trapping a rabid thistle bear alive using an enchanted relic to attempt a cure.",h="Plagued Lands is an Alliance quest offered by Tharnariun Treetender in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Blight on the Wilderness",b="A sinister affliction creeps through Darkshore's woods, twisting its beasts into maddened, aggressive shadows of their former selves. The native thistle bears have suffered the worst of this madness, succumbing to a rabid frenzy that threatens both passing travelers and the fragile ecological harmony of the coast. Where night elf sentinels often respond with steel, the druids seek to understand and heal the root cause.",sp=0},{t="Tharnariun's Hope",b="Refusing to slaughter the corrupted beasts without trying to save them, Tharnariun Treetender fashioned a specialized trap known as Tharnariun's Hope. Adventurers place the device on the forest floor, using its soothing light to temporarily calm a raging thistle bear's mind. Once pacified, the creature meekly follows the traveler back to Tharnariun's outpost for study.",sp=0},{t="Tragic Medicine",b="When an adventurer successfully guides an infected bear into camp, Tharnariun immediately attempts to purge the sickness with restorative magic. Sadly, his initial efforts prove catastrophic: the swirling cleansing energies overwhelm the creature's weakened constitution, causing the beast to collapse and die on the spot. The failure reveals just how deeply the dark plague has taken hold.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Plagued Lands?",a="The quest is given by Tharnariun Treetender, a night elf druid situated in northern Darkshore who seeks to cure the afflicted wildlife.",al={"quest giver plagued lands","tharnariun darkshore quest","who starts plagued lands"}},{q="What is the objective of Plagued Lands?",a="You must use the provided item, Tharnariun's Hope, to trap and pacify a Rabid Thistle Bear in Darkshore, then lead the subdued creature back to Tharnariun alive.",al={"plagued lands goal","what to do in plagued lands","how to catch bear darkshore"}},{q="What happens to the bear when you bring it back?",a="Tharnariun attempts to cleanse the animal with healing magic, but the sickness has progressed too deeply. The strain overwhelms the creature, and it dies immediately after the treatment.",al={"does the bear die","tharnariun bear cure result","bear death plagued lands"},sp=1},{q="What item do you use to capture the bear?",a="Tharnariun provides an enchanted trapping device named Tharnariun's Hope, which emits a calming light that pacifies the enraged bear so it will follow you.",al={"plagued lands trap","tharnariun's hope item","bear cage darkshore"}},{q="What quest follows Plagued Lands?",a="Plagued Lands is the first chapter of a three-part chain. Completing it unlocks the follow-up quest, Cleansing of the Infected, which eventually leads to the final quest, Tharnariun's Hope.",al={"next quest after plagued lands","plagued lands chain","tharnariun follow up"}},{q="Why are the thistle bears rabid?",a="A creeping, corruptive plague is spreading across Darkshore, poisoning the minds and bodies of the local wildlife and driving noble thistle bears into mindless aggression.",al={"why are bears sick in darkshore","darkshore plague bears","darkshore corruption"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, seeing Darkshore's native flora and fauna decay into rabid madness is an affront to Cenarius and the balance of nature they are sworn to protect.",["class:Druid"]="Druids share Tharnariun's grief upon witnessing nature corrupted, and the tragic loss of the bear underscores the insidious depth of the land's spreading disease.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance travelers journeying through northern Kalimdor must reckon with untamed corruption encroaching right on the borders of settled territories."},kw={"cleansing of the infected","darkshore","plagued lands","rabid thistle bear","tharnariun treetender","tharnariun's hope","thistle bear"},rel={"npc:tharnariun-treetender","quest:2138","quest:2139","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Tharnariun Treetender",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=2118},src={"Plagued Lands"}}
E["quest:2138"] = {t="quest",n="Cleansing of the Infected",z="darkshore",s="Cleansing of the Infected is an Alliance task in Darkshore given by Tharnariun Treetender in Auberdine. After attempted herbal cures fail to halt the woodland sickness, the caretaker reluctantly orders a cull of the rabid thistle bears roaming the misty wilderness. It represents a bitter turning point where preservation gives way to containment.",h="Cleansing of the Infected is an Alliance task in Darkshore given by Tharnariun Treetender in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Bitter Necessity",b="Tharnariun Treetender has spent long hours searching for a remedy to stem the creeping affliction corrupting Darkshore's wildlife. Despite the careful brewing of medicinal drafts from native roots and mosses, the thistle bears remain deeply diseased and violent. Having exhausted his gentler options, the night elf tender concludes that putting the beasts down is the only immediate way to prevent them from mauling other creatures and spreading their sickness further into the ancient woodlands.",sp=0},{t="Containing the Wilds",b="The culling of twenty rabid bears is an agonizing duty for any servant of nature. Tharnariun admits plainly that killing the beasts will not cure the underlying plague, but it purchases valuable time for the defenders of Auberdine. Until the primary source of the forest's corruption can be identified and severed, thinning the aggressive herds remains the settlement's only buffer against catastrophe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Tharnariun want the thistle bears killed instead of cured?",a="Tharnariun previously attempted to brew and test an herbal cure, but it utterly failed against the sickness. With the diseased bears turning violent and threatening other creatures, killing them is a last resort to slow the disease's spread.",al={"why kill the bears","why not cure bears","tharnariun bear quest"}},{q="Who is Tharnariun Treetender?",a="Tharnariun is a night elf caretaker stationed in Auberdine. He studies the ailments gripping Darkshore's flora and fauna, striving to preserve the natural balance against spreading corruption.",al={"tharnariun role","who gives cleansing of the infected"}},{q="Does slaying the rabid bears actually end the plague?",a="No. Tharnariun explicitly warns that killing the rabid bears will not stop the plague. It only buys the forest and the residents of Auberdine precious time by slowing the rate of infection and violence.",al={"does this fix darkshore","is the plague cured"}},{q="What comes after Cleansing of the Infected?",a="Once you report back to Tharnariun, he asks you to prepare your spirit for further bloodshed and offers the follow-up quest, Tharnariun's Hope, to continue addressing the blighted wildlife.",al={"next quest after cleansing","what follows cleasning infected"}},{q="Where are the rabid thistle bears found?",a="Rabid thistle bears wander the coastal and inland forest stretches of central Darkshore, often found roaming among the misty pines south and east of Auberdine.",al={"rabid thistle bear location","where are bears darkshore"}},{q="What caused the thistle bears to go rabid?",a="The bears are victims of a mysterious taint sweeping through northern Kalimdor's woodlands, corrupting peaceful wildlife into frenzied, aggressive beasts that defy standard herbal remedies.",al={"why are bears sick","bear sickness darkshore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, ordering the slaughter of corrupted beasts is a heavy burden, underscoring how deeply post-war corruption has penetrated their ancestral homeland.",["class:Druid"]="Druids who revere the wild bear spirits find Tharnariun's command especially poignant: it is an act of mercy and forest triage rather than routine hunting.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters understand that culling diseased predators is sometimes mandatory to protect the wider ecology, even when the underlying cause remains unsolved."},kw={"auberdine","cleansing","darkshore","infected","rabid thistle bear","tharnariun","treetender"},rel={"npc:tharnariun-treetender","quest:2118","quest:2139","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine"},m={start="Tharnariun Treetender",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=2138},src={"Cleansing of the Infected"}}
E["quest:2139"] = {t="quest",n="Tharnariun's Hope",z="darkshore",s="Tharnariun's Hope is the somber conclusion to Tharnariun Treetender's efforts to curb Darkshore's wildlife sickness. After mercy-killing numerous infected beasts across the woodlands, an Alliance champion is tasked with slaying the rabid Den Mother northeast of Auberdine.",h="Tharnariun's Hope is the somber conclusion to Tharnariun Treetender's efforts to curb Darkshore's wildlife...",sec={{t="A Tragic Necessity",b="Following the Third War, the wild creatures of Darkshore began succumbing to an unnatural, rabid sickness. Tharnariun Treetender, stationed in Auberdine, spent days tasking travelers with putting down infected beasts to ease the forest's agony. However, culling rabid thistle bears was merely treating the symptom. To halt the spread, he determined that the source within the local bears had to be excised: the matriarch known as the Den Mother.",sp=0},{t="The Den Mother",b="Lurking in a cavern northeast of Auberdine near the ancient ruins of Bashal'Aran, the Den Mother was once a vital guardian of the woodland fauna. Consumed by the maddening affliction spreading across northern Kalimdor, she continuously bore and raised litters of rabid cubs. By hunting down the matriarch within her den, Alliance heroes put an end to her torment and stemmed the tide of frenzied bears prowling the coastal highway.",sp=1},{t="The Grim Reality of Kalimdor",b="Upon the Den Mother's demise, Tharnariun expresses profound gratitude, albeit clouded by melancholy. For the kaldorei, raising weapons against woodland creatures is an agonizing duty. Yet as dark forces press against their new home and many despair or seek shelter, deeds like this prove that the defenders of Auberdine are willing to bear the heavy moral burden required to protect their wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tharnariun Treetender?",a="Tharnariun Treetender is a night elf caretaker stationed in Auberdine. Distraught over the blight and madness warping Darkshore's wildlife, he oversees efforts to study, track, and ultimately put suffering animals out of their misery.",al={"tharnariun","who gives tharnariun's hope","treetender auberdine"}},{q="Where is the Den Mother located?",a="She dwells inside a cave nestled into the hills northeast of Auberdine, just east of the ruins of Bashal'Aran.",al={"where is den mother","den mother cave location","find den mother"}},{q="Why must the Den Mother be killed instead of cured?",a="The affliction ravaging Darkshore's wildlife is deeply ingrained and actively driving the beasts into violent frenzies. With no immediate cure and the Den Mother actively raising rabid offspring, Tharnariun determined that putting her down was the only way to stop the sickness from proliferating further.",al={"can den mother be saved","why kill den mother","cure den mother"}},{q="What quests lead up to Tharnariun's Hope?",a="This quest is the final step in a three-part chain. It begins with 'Plagued Lands', continues through 'Cleansing of the Infected', and concludes with 'Tharnariun's Hope'.",al={"prerequisites for tharnariuns hope","quest chain tharnariun"}},{q="What is making the animals of Darkshore sick?",a="The woodlands of Darkshore suffer lingering corruption from demonic energies left behind after the Third War, compounded by twilight cultists, corrupted elemental remnants, and the lingering scars around Felwood and Mount Hyjal.",al={"why are bears rabid in darkshore","darkshore animal plague cause","what corrupted the bears"}},{q="Why does Tharnariun mention people escaping to fortified lands?",a="Auberdine is an exposed coastal outpost beset by ghosts, corrupted wildlife, and hostile creatures. With night elf civilization struggling to rebuild in the aftermath of the Burning Legion's invasion, some residents feel overwhelmed and choose to hide or retreat toward safer Alliance bastions.",al={"fleeing auberdine","fortified alliance lands"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, slaying woodland beasts—especially a matriarch bear—goes against their fundamental reverence for nature, making this duty a bitter and sorrowful necessity.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold bears in high spiritual esteem through the teachings of Ursoc. Executing a corrupted Den Mother serves as a solemn reminder of nature's delicate balance and the tragedies of corruption.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters understand the tragedy of an apex predator driven mad by disease, recognizing when culling an infected beast is the truest act of mercy.",["faction:Alliance"]="Protecting Auberdine strengthens the Alliance's foothold along northern Kalimdor's coast, proving their readiness to defend night elf lands from escalating wilderness threats."},kw={"auberdine","bashal'aran","cleansing of the infected","darkshore","den mother","rabid thistle bear","tharnariun treetender","tharnariun's hope"},rel={"npc:tharnariun-treetender","quest:2138","quest:2118","subzone:auberdine","quest:954","zone:darkshore","topic:alliance"},m={start="Tharnariun Treetender",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=2139},src={"Tharnariun's Hope (quest)"}}
E["quest:2178"] = {t="quest",n="Easy Strider Living",z="darkshore",s="Easy Strider Living is a local culinary task offered by Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine. She is eager to share her prized recipe for strider stew, provided an adventurer is willing to hunt down the fierce foreststriders wandering Darkshore and retrieve their meat.",h="Easy Strider Living is a local culinary task offered by Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Taste of the Wild",b="Auberdine might be a quiet port village, but survival along the coast requires making good use of the local wildlife. Alanndarian Nightsong has developed a secret recipe for hearty strider stew, a savory dish made from the tall, fleet-footed foreststriders that stalk the shadowy woods of Darkshore. Rather than simply handing out culinary secrets, she asks aspiring cooks and hunters to venture out and cull the birds themselves.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Foreststriders",b="Foreststriders are swift, sharp-beaked avian predators that roam the mist-shrouded woodlands and beaches north and south of Auberdine. While they can be temperamental and aggressive when provoked, their succulent meat makes an excellent base for a rich stew. Bringing back fresh meat satisfies Alanndarian's hungry pot and earns the hunter her cherished recipe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf resident of Auberdine in Darkshore. Known for her simmering pot of strider stew, she offers to teach her culinary craft to travelers who prove their hunting prowess.",al={"alanndarian","who is alanndarian nightsong","stew cook auberdine"}},{q="Where do I find the strider meat?",a="Strider meat is obtained by hunting foreststriders throughout Darkshore. These large, flightless birds roam both the sandy shorelines and the forested groves outside Auberdine.",al={"strider meat location","where are foreststriders","how to get strider meat"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The quest tasks you with hunting down foreststriders to bring back five cuts of meat for Alanndarian Nightsong, in exchange for learning how to prepare Strider Stew.",al={"why do easy strider living","quest purpose","easy strider living objective"}},{q="Are the foreststriders dangerous to hunt?",a="Foreststriders are territorial birds armed with sharp beaks and swift legs, making them aggressive when approached. However, a reasonably equipped adventurer can hunt them down without much peril.",al={"are striders hard to kill","foreststrider danger"}},{q="Does this quest unlock a cooking recipe?",a="Yes. Upon bringing Alanndarian her requested meat, she shares her culinary secrets, teaching adventurers the recipe for Strider Stew.",al={"do i get recipe","strider stew recipe","cooking reward"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The quest begins and ends in the settlement of Auberdine, with the hunting taking place in the wilderness of Darkshore.",al={"quest zone","where is easy strider living"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="This task is essential for culinarians traveling through Darkshore, rewarding the recipe to prepare nourishing Strider Stew from local wildlife.",["race:NightElf"]="Living harmoniously in Kalimdor often involves living off the land, and hearty strider stews have become a coastal staple for night elves in Auberdine.",["class:Hunter"]="Foreststriders are both swift game and potential animal companions, offering tracking and hunting practice along Darkshore's mist-laden paths."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cooking","darkshore","easy strider living","foreststrider","strider meat","strider stew"},rel={"npc:alanndarian-nightsong","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Alanndarian Nightsong",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=2178},src={"Easy Strider Living"}}
E["quest:3524"] = {t="quest",n="Washed Ashore",z="darkshore",s="Washed Ashore is an investigation initiated by Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine on behalf of the Temple of the Moon. Mass strandings of giant sea creatures along the Darkshore coastline have raised alarms among the night elf priesthood in Darnassus. Adventurers are tasked with driving back scavenging murlocs to secure skeletal specimens for study.",h="Washed Ashore is an investigation initiated by Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine on behalf of the Temple of...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Omen",b="Giant, majestic creatures of the deep have long been known to occasionally beach themselves on the foggy shoals of Darkshore. Recently, however, their deaths have ceased being tragic anomalies and become an escalating pattern. Beached leviathans are washing up along the coastline in alarming numbers. To the Priestesses of Elune residing in the Temple of the Moon, such unprompted mass strandings are treated not merely as natural oddities, but as potential ill omens threatening northern Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Scavengers of the Shallows",b="To decipher why these great beasts are hurling themselves onto the sands, scholar Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde was dispatched to the port town of Auberdine. Her task is to collect biological samples and send them by hippogryph to Darnassus for close examination. However, the Greymist murlocs infesting the surf line have swarmed the massive carcasses, aggressively scavenging the remains and preventing field researchers from reaching the bones without armed protection.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are giant sea creatures washing up on Darkshore?",a="The exact cause remains under active investigation by the Temple of the Moon. While occasional strandings are natural, the sudden surge in frequency has convinced night elf scholars that a deeper disturbance or ill omen lurks beneath the waves of the Great Sea.",al={"why beached creatures","sea creature strandings","dying sea beasts"}},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is an investigator sent from Darnassus by the Temple of the Moon. Stationed in Auberdine, she is responsible for cataloging coastal anomalies and collecting physical samples from beached leviathans to send back to the priesthood for analysis.",al={"gwennyth","who is gwennyth bly'leggonde"}},{q="Where does the creature south of Auberdine lie?",a="The skeletal remains lie on the shoreline just a short march south of the Auberdine docks. The massive carcass rests in the surf, surrounded and guarded by hostile Greymist murlocs.",al={"creature location","sea creature bones location","where is the beached beast"}},{q="What will Darnassus do with the sea creature bones?",a="The bones are dispatched via hippogryph directly to Darnassus. Scholars and priestesses at the Temple of the Moon study the marrow, structure, and signs of decay to uncover whether disease, foul magic, or unnatural predation drove the beast ashore.",al={"why collect bones","purpose of sea creature bones","darnassus bones"}},{q="Why are the Greymist murlocs gathered around the carcass?",a="The Greymist tribe exploits the stranded giants as an effortless source of food, tools, and bonecraft. Their territorial claim over the carcasses makes it impossible for unarmed scholars to approach without risking their lives.",al={"murlocs at whale","why murlocs around creature"}},{q="Does this investigation conclude after retrieving the first set of bones?",a="No. The carcass south of town is only the first site. Gwennyth continues her research with further inquiries into other stranded leviathans that have perished along Darkshore's expansive, mist-shrouded coast.",al={"is this a chain","washed ashore follow up"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The coastal strandings disturb the delicate balance of Darkshore, prompting the Sisterhood of Elune to intervene directly from Darnassus.",["class:Priest"]="Serving the Sisterhood of Elune means interpreting spiritual omens and natural imbalances, exactly what Gwennyth seeks to decipher from the sea creature's remains.",["class:Druid"]="The mass death of noble marine life is an alarming sign of ecological discord along the Kalimdor coast that demands watchful attention."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","darnassus","greymist murlocs","gwennyth bly'leggonde","sea creature bones","temple of the moon","washed ashore"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","topic:murloc","quest:4723","quest:2519"},m={start="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=3524},src={"Washed Ashore"}}
E["quest:4681"] = {t="quest",n="Washed Ashore",z="darkshore",s="Washed Ashore is an investigation initiated by Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine to examine deceased marine life along Darkshore's mist-shrouded coast. Acting on behalf of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, she sends adventurers to inspect the skeletal remains of a giant sea turtle submerged west of the village. The research seeks to explain why so many sea creatures are stranding themselves or dying off the shore.",h="Washed Ashore is an investigation initiated by Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine to examine deceased marine...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Tide",b="The misty beaches of Darkshore have become a graveyard for oceanic giants. Beached behemoths and drowned leviathans line the sands and shallows, baffling the night elves of Auberdine. Having already looked into a grounded sea creature along the strand, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde tasks travelers with diving into the waters west of the docks, near a sunken vessel, to examine the bones of a massive sea turtle and gather evidence for the Temple of the Moon.",sp=0},{t="Flight from the World Tree",b="Gwennyth's ultimate goal is gathering enough physical evidence to submit a formal report to the Priestesses of Elune in Darnassus. Her preliminary findings point toward a deeply unsettling hypothesis: these gentle marine animals may not be dying by accident, but deliberately fleeing something out in the open sea—potentially the waters encircling Teldrassil itself.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are sea creatures washing ashore in Darkshore?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde suspects these marine creatures are deliberately fleeing something disturbing in the surrounding ocean. Preliminary findings suggest they may be escaping the waters encircling the newly grown World Tree of Teldrassil.",al={"why turtles dying","beached creatures darkshore","why beached whales"}},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf researcher stationed in Auberdine who reports directly to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. She is documenting the wave of dead and beached sea creatures along Darkshore's coastline.",al={"gwennyth","auberdine researcher","quest giver washed ashore"}},{q="Where is the skeletal sea turtle located?",a="The skeletal sea turtle rests on the ocean floor due west of Auberdine's docks, lying close to the wreckage of a sunken vessel off the Darkshore coast.",al={"turtle remains location","where skeletal turtle","sea turtle bones"}},{q="What does the Temple of the Moon have to do with this?",a="The Temple of the Moon directs ecological and spiritual matters for night elf lands. Gwennyth requires concrete physical samples to present a formal report to the priestesses regarding the strange die-off.",al={"why darnassus care","temple of the moon role","priestesses of elune involvement"}},{q="Are there more beached creatures to find?",a="Yes. Gwennyth notes that beached creatures lie strewn all along the Darkshore coastline, encouraging adventurers to search the sands and recover remains from other stranded behemoths.",al={"other beached sea creatures","more sea creature quests","darkshore beached behemoth"}},{q="What is the difference between the two 'Washed Ashore' quests?",a="The first quest sends you to investigate a creature stranded on the beach nearby, while the follow-up asks you to swim west of the docks to inspect a submerged skeletal sea turtle.",al={"washed ashore part 1 vs part 2","two washed ashore quests","washed ashore chain"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The mass death and erratic flight of Darkshore's ancient marine beasts hints at a corruption or disruption in the balance of nature radiating from the waters around Teldrassil.",["class:Priest"]="Carrying out this inquiry supports the Priestesses of Elune at the Temple of the Moon, who oversee the spiritual and natural well-being of northern Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine serves as the gateway between Teldrassil and the mainland; evidence that ocean life is actively fleeing your new home is a troubling omen."},kw={"auberdine","beached creature","darkshore","darnassus","gwennyth bly'leggonde","sea turtle","sea turtle remains","teldrassil","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:3524","subzone:auberdine","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","quest:940","quest:2519","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4681},src={"Washed Ashore (2)"}}
E["quest:4722"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along the misty, surf-battered shores of Darkshore lies the carcass of a massive beached sea turtle, surrounded by scavenging murlocs. Though picked over, viable biological samples can still be recovered from the remains. Naturalists in Auberdine collect such specimens to ship back to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus for formal study.",h="Along the misty, surf-battered shores of Darkshore lies the carcass of a massive beached sea turtle...",sec={{t="A Stranded Leviathan",b="The long coastline of Darkshore frequently catches the casualties of the Great Sea, including massive ancient sea turtles that drift ashore after death or beach themselves in confusion. Once grounded, the carcasses quickly attract scavengers. Hostile Greymist murlocs have established crude camps around this turtle's skeletal frame, carving away flesh and shell. Despite their foraging, viable bone, shell, or tissue samples often remain intact within the wreckage.",sp=0},{t="Field Research for Darnassus",b="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, stationed in the settlement of Auberdine, serves as a field researcher documenting the unusual marine life and ecological disturbances along the coast. The night elves observe these stranded beasts with both reverence and scientific curiosity. Once recovered, suitable remains are carefully cataloged and prepared for shipment to scholars in Darnassus, who seek to understand why so many pelagic giants are washing ashore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there so many beached sea creatures in Darkshore?",a="Darkshore's turbulent waters and strong coastal currents naturally push drifting debris and dying sea beasts onto the sand. Night elf scholars suspect unnatural disturbances in the deep ocean are driving marine life toward the shallows, prompting local naturalists to study every corpse that washes up.",al={"why dead sea turtle","darkshore beached creatures","why stranded"}},{q="Who wants the sea turtle remains?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, a night elf researcher located in Auberdine, collects washed-up samples from adventurers on behalf of naturalists and scholars based in Darnassus.",al={"who do i turn this in to","gwennyth auberdine","where to turn in turtle remains"}},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the turtle?",a="The local Greymist murlocs are opportunists who scavenge whatever drifts onto the beaches. A beached giant sea turtle provides them with an abundant supply of meat, tough hide, and bone for tools and shelters.",al={"murlocs near turtle","greymist scavengers","murloc camp"}},{q="What happens to the samples once Gwennyth receives them?",a="Gwennyth packages the viable tissue and skeletal samples for transport across the sea to Darnassus, where scholars and priestesses examine them to monitor the health and behavior of the coastal ecosystem.",al={"what does darnassus do with remains","turtle sample research"}},{q="Is this the only beached creature along the coast?",a="No. Darkshore's long coastline holds multiple beached sea turtles as well as stranded sea behemoths, several of which yield research specimens for Auberdine's scholars.",al={"other beached animals","more dead turtles","washed ashore creatures"}},{q="Are sea turtles sacred to the night elves?",a="The night elves revere the native beasts of Kalimdor as part of the natural balance under Elune and the wild gods. While sea turtles are not solitary divine avatars, their unexpected deaths and beachings are treated as grave ecological warning signs.",al={"night elf turtles","druids and turtles"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The unexplained beaching of ancient sea creatures signals a deeper disruption in Kalimdor's waters, motivating the researchers of Auberdine and Darnassus to investigate every washed-up leviathan.",["class:Druid"]="Druids view the stranded sea life and the scavenging murlocs as symptoms of an ecological imbalance along Darkshore that demands close observation and healing."},kw={"auberdine","beached","darkshore","darnassus","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","remains","sea turtle"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:3524","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","zone:darnassus","topic:murloc"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=4722},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (1)"}}
E["quest:4723"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="Along the fog-draped strand of Mist's Edge lies the massive carcass of a sea thresher, far larger than any native to Darkshore's shallows. While local murlocs pick through the carrion, naturalists in Auberdine seek bone samples to understand why such colossal deep-sea beasts are beaching themselves along the coast.",h="Along the fog-draped strand of Mist's Edge lies the massive carcass of a sea thresher, far larger than any...",sec={{t="A Giant on the Shallows",b="The Mist's Edge coastline is no stranger to shipwrecks and tide-washed debris, but the sudden appearance of enormous thresher remains is troubling. The creature dwarfs typical local wildlife, pointing to depths far beyond the calm waters of the Veiled Sea. Although coastal murlocs eagerly swarm and feast on the corpse, they lack the strength or coordination to bring down a leviathan of this scale. The predator succumbed to something else entirely before washing ashore.",sp=0},{t="Studies in Darnassus",b="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine coordinates field efforts to salvage bones and biological samples from Darkshore's stranded megafauna. Night elf researchers in Darnassus hope that by examining skeletal remains and tissue samples, they can determine whether illness, deep-sea disturbances, or arcane corruption drives these ocean giants onto the killing sands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kind of beast washed up on the shore?",a="It is the remains of a giant thresher, an aquatic predator vastly larger than the threshers typically spotted close to Darkshore's beaches.",al={"what creature is this","what is the dead monster","what animal is dead on the beach"}},{q="Did the murlocs kill it?",a="No. Although murlocs swarm around the carcass to feed on the rotting meat, observers note they are far too weak, even in large groups, to hunt down a deep-water behemoth of that size.",al={"did murlocs kill the thresher","did murlocs kill the sea creature"}},{q="Why are sea creatures stranding themselves along Darkshore?",a="The exact cause remains unknown. Night elf researchers suspect unseen oceanic disturbances, disease, or ecological distress are forcing deep-sea fauna to swim into shallow surf where they beach and die.",al={"why are threshers dying","why do creatures beach themselves"}},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf researcher stationed in Auberdine. She collects skeletal specimens and biological samples from beached wildlife along Darkshore to send to Darnassus for detailed study.",al={"who is gwennyth","who takes the bones in auberdine"}},{q="Where are the collected bones sent?",a="After Gwennyth catalogs and preps the samples in Auberdine, they are dispatched to scholars and naturalists in the capital city of Darnassus for anatomical and magical investigation.",al={"where do bones go","what does auberdine do with bones"}},{q="Where is this carcass located?",a="The carcass rests directly on the sandy shores of Mist's Edge, along Darkshore's western coastline.",al={"carcass location","where is the beached sea creature"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The strandings along Darkshore are a distressing sign of imbalance in the surrounding waters, prompting naturalists in Auberdine and Darnassus to investigate before more marine life perishes.",["class:Druid"]="Druids committed to the preservation of natural harmony look upon the stranded leviathan as an alarming symptom of disturbance in the Veiled Sea's ecosystem."},kw={"auberdine","beached","bones","darkshore","gwennyth bly'leggonde","mist's edge","murloc","sea creature","thresher"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","subzone:mist-s-edge","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus","topic:murloc","quest:938"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=4723},src={"Beached Sea Creature (1)"}}
E["quest:4725"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along the surf of Darkshore lies the carcass of a massive sea turtle, fitted with a broken carriage and swarming with opportunistic Greymist murlocs. Unlike other dead leviathans on the coast, this creature was harnessed as a beast of burden by the serpent-like naga before dying on the sand.",h="Along the surf of Darkshore lies the carcass of a massive sea turtle, fitted with a broken carriage and...",sec={{t="A Beast in Harness",b="The mist-shrouded shores of Darkshore are troubled by an alarming number of stranded sea giants, but this particular sea turtle tells a far more sinister story. Strapped across the creature's colossal carapace sits a dilapidated carriage, abandoned and decaying in the tide. Rather than dying of sickness or natural exhaustion like other beached creatures, this giant was pressed into service and driven onto the coast by intelligent handlers.",sp=0},{t="Scavengers of the Shallows",b="The carcass did not remain quiet for long. Local Greymist murlocs quickly swarmed the remains, carving out a den amidst the rotting meat and scavenged timber. Amidst the murlocs' refuse and the broken chassis of the sea carriage rests an intact, curiously marked container, left behind by the beast's original masters.",sp=0},{t="Naga Supply Lines",b="Upon delivering the strangely marked container to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine, the grim reality comes into focus. The container bears naga markings, and the harness matches the supply carriages used by the serpent folk to ferry weapons and war material from the oceanic depths. The dead turtle is direct proof of the naga staging incursions into northern Darkshore, and the recovered artifact is hurried off to Darnassus for further study.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is there a carriage on the sea turtle's shell?",a="The carriage belonged to the naga, who harness giant sea turtles as pack animals and siege beasts. They use these carriages to transport supplies and weapons from the depths up onto the Darkshore coastline.",al={"turtle carriage","why carriage on turtle","harnessed turtle"}},{q="What is inside the carriage?",a="Within the ruins of the abandoned carriage lies a strangely marked box. Its runes identify it as naga property, prompting the scholars in Auberdine to send it along to Darnassus for official scrutiny.",al={"turtle box","strangely marked box","box in turtle carriage"}},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the turtle?",a="Greymist murlocs inhabit the coastline and regularly scavenge shipwrecks and beached carcasses. They have claimed the giant turtle's remains as a food source and nest.",al={"murlocs around turtle","greymist murlocs turtle","why murlocs eating turtle"}},{q="Who studies the beached creatures in Darkshore?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine oversees the investigation into the wave of beached sea creatures, cataloging relics and strange materials found upon their remains.",al={"who studies beached sea creatures","auberdine researcher","gwennyth bly'leggonde role"}},{q="How does this turtle differ from other beached creatures along Darkshore?",a="While many other creatures wash ashore due to illness, corruption, or oceanic distress, this turtle was clearly domesticated, saddled with heavy cargo gear, and driven to the beach deliberately by the naga.",al={"other beached turtles","why this turtle different","turtle mystery darkshore"}},{q="What happens to the marked box after Auberdine?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde logs the discovery in Auberdine and sends the naga box up to Darnassus, where elven leadership analyzes the growing threat along their northern borders.",al={"where does box go","box sent to darnassus","what does auberdine do with box"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The presence of naga supply beasts washing up on Darkshore confirms that the ancestral enemies of the kaldorei are actively reinforcing beachheads uncomfortably close to Darnassus.",["faction:Alliance"]="Investigating beached creatures provides crucial intelligence for Auberdine's sentinels, tracking both murloc infestations and the rise of organized naga raiding parties."},kw={"auberdine","beached","carriage","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","naga","sea turtle","strangely marked box"},rel={"quest:4722","npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:naga","topic:murloc","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4725},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (2)"}}
E["quest:4727"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along the northern shores of Darkshore lies the massive skeletal carcass of a beached sea turtle, curiously untouched by the local Greymist murlocs. A sample of its remains is gathered and delivered to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine on behalf of the Temple of the Moon. Naturalists and priestesses seek to uncover why these great oceanic creatures are washing ashore and why even scavengers seem reluctant to approach.",h="Along the northern shores of Darkshore lies the massive skeletal carcass of a beached sea turtle, curiously...",sec={{t="A Curious Absence",b="The northern coastline of Darkshore is thick with Greymist murlocs, creatures known to aggressively scavenge anything of nutritive value that washes up from the Veiled Sea. Yet this enormous turtle skeleton lies largely undisturbed. Whether the murlocs simply overlooked the bounty or actively avoided the remains for an unseen reason remains a troubling puzzle for those studying the beach's ecology.",sp=0},{t="Study of the Shoreline",b="In Auberdine, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde collects samples of these beached behemoths for the Temple of the Moon. The night elf priestesses seek to comprehend the disturbances troubling Darkshore's waters, using skeletal fragments to determine whether sickness, magical corruption, or foul marine predators are driving the sea's ancient dwellers to their deaths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the beached sea turtle?",a="It is the massive skeletal remains of an ancient sea turtle washed ashore in northern Darkshore. Its unusual presence and the lack of scavenger activity make it an object of study for the night elves.",al={"turtle carcass","sea turtle skeleton","what is this turtle"}},{q="Why are the murlocs avoiding the carcass?",a="The Greymist murlocs usually tear through any carcass on the beach, yet they have left these remains alone. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde and the Temple of the Moon suspect the scavengers may be shying away due to an unnatural taint or an unseen danger surrounding the creature's death.",al={"why aren't murlocs eating it","greymist murlocs turtle","why avoid carcass"}},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf researcher stationed in Auberdine who gathers field samples from Darkshore's beached marine life on behalf of the Temple of the Moon.",al={"gwennyth auberdine","who wants turtle remains","turtle quest turn in"}},{q="Why does the Temple of the Moon care about beached sea creatures?",a="The priestesses of Elune maintain balance and stewardship over the natural world in northern Kalimdor. With sea creatures dying in unusual numbers along Darkshore, the Temple is analyzing biological samples to diagnose the underlying affliction harming the seas.",al={"temple of the moon turtle","why study turtles","elune marine life"}},{q="Where is this particular sea turtle located?",a="This particular carcass rests on the sandy northern coastline of Darkshore, situated near territory inhabited by the Greymist murloc tribes.",al={"where is the turtle","beached sea turtle location","turtle darkshore"}},{q="Are there other beached creatures along Darkshore?",a="Yes. Multiple beached sea creatures and giant sea turtles litter the shores of Darkshore, each prompting an investigation by Auberdine's researchers into why the ocean's giants are perishing.",al={"other beached creatures","more sea turtles","beached sea creature quests"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The unexplained death and avoidance of majestic sea creatures along Darkshore highlights the growing imbalance threatening the ancestral lands of the kaldorei.",["class:Druid"]="Druids closely monitor the coastline, deeply troubled when scavenger species like murlocs refuse to touch the dead, signaling a possible unnatural taint in the waters.",["class:Priest"]="Serving the Temple of the Moon means extending Elune's compassionate stewardship to all living things, investigating deaths that disrupt nature's harmony."},kw={"auberdine","beached","carcass","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","remains","sea turtle","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:murloc","quest:4722","quest:2519","quest:938"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4727},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (3)"}}
E["quest:4728"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="Along the misty coast of Darkshore lies the massive carcass of a sea mammal, abandoned mid-excavation. Scattered tools and an idle wheelbarrow reveal an expedition cut short, leaving the specimen to opportunistic murlocs and the curious eyes of passing travelers.",h="Along the misty coast of Darkshore lies the massive carcass of a sea mammal, abandoned mid-excavation.",sec={{t="A Halted Excavation",b="The carcass resting upon the sands of Darkshore is that of an enormous marine mammal, partially gutted and heavily weathered by sea spray. Strewn about its decaying frame are a rusted wheelbarrow and discarded excavation tools, clearly showing that someone attempted an organized study of the beast before being driven off or abandoning the site in haste.",sp=0},{t="The League and the Murlocs",b="The abandoned equipment belonged to dwarven field researchers of the Explorer's League operating in Darkshore. Their examination of the massive carcass came to an abrupt halt when local murlocs swarmed the site, claiming the washed-up giant for scavenging. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine, acting on behalf of the Temple of the Moon, gladly accepts any salvaged bone samples to further study the unnatural wash-ups plaguing the coastline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is this creature lying on the beach?",a="It is the remains of a giant sea mammal that washed ashore on Darkshore's coast. The species is not definitively identified, but it is large enough to attract both scavenging murlocs and dwarven researchers.",al={"beached sea creature identity","what is this carcass","what died here"}},{q="Who left the tools and wheelbarrow behind?",a="The tools were left by members of the dwarven Explorer's League. They set up an excavation site to study the beached beast, but were attacked and driven off by hostile coastal murlocs before they could finish.",al={"who left the tools","abandoned wheelbarrow darkshore","who was digging here"}},{q="Why does Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde want these bones?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde collects samples on behalf of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. The night elves are actively investigating the strange and unsettling phenomenon of massive sea creatures washing up dead along Darkshore's shores.",al={"why does gwennyth want bones","temple of the moon sea creature","auberdine sea bones"}},{q="Why are murlocs prowling around the carcass?",a="The murlocs were drawn by the colossal feast of meat and blubber, subsequently chasing off the dwarven scholars to scavenge and defend the remains for themselves.",al={"murlocs around carcass","why are murlocs here","murloc scavengers"}},{q="Is the Explorer's League officially allied with Auberdine here?",a="Yes. As fellow members of the Alliance, the Explorer's League maintains a presence in Darkshore and collaborates with local night elf authorities, frequently sharing reports of their scientific discoveries and coastal investigations.",al={"explorers league auberdine","dwarves in darkshore","explorers league alliance darkshore"}},{q="Are there other beached creatures along the Darkshore coast?",a="Yes. Multiple enormous marine beasts and skeletal remains have washed up along the length of Darkshore's misty beaches, suggesting widespread disturbance in the waters off Kalimdor.",al={"more beached creatures","other carcasses darkshore","multiple beached sea creatures"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The abandoned tools around the carcass belong to your kin in the Explorer's League, who were chased from their dig site by native murlocs.",["race:NightElf"]="The Temple of the Moon is deeply concerned by the unnatural frequency of massive sea life dying and washing up on the sacred shores of Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="This discovery highlights the cooperative efforts between Darnassus and the Ironforge Explorer's League to catalog the mysteries of Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","beached","bones","darkshore","explorers league","gwennyth","murloc","sea creature"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","quest:4723","quest:2519"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4728},src={"Beached Sea Creature (2)"}}
E["quest:4730"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="Along the windswept coast of Darkshore, the half-devoured remains of a massive sea mammal have washed ashore, guarded by opportunistic murlocs. Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine seeks bone samples from these stranded giants to discern why normally docile ocean beasts are violently dying upon the sands.",h="Along the windswept coast of Darkshore, the half-devoured remains of a massive sea mammal have washed ashore...",sec={{t="A Gruesome Shoreline Discovery",b="North along the lonely beaches of Darkshore lies the rotting, half-eaten carcass of a gargantuan sea mammal. Waves crash against its exposed ribs while an unusually vicious tribe of murlocs picks the scavenged bones clean. The sight is both tragic and unnerving, signaling that the ocean's balance is tipping just as severely as the blighted forests inland.",sp=0},{t="Uncharacteristic Stranding",b="According to Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, the creatures washing up along the strand are typically gentle marine mammals native to the waters surrounding the base of Teldrassil. Unlike aggressive threshers, these gentle beasts have never been known to drive themselves violently onto the rocks. The Temple of the Moon is actively cataloging bone samples to uncover what foul corruption or hidden threat is driving them from the deep to perish on the coast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kind of creature washed up here?",a="The skeletal remains belong to a large, gentle sea mammal that usually inhabits the deep, tranquil waters around the base of Teldrassil. They are naturally peaceful giants and are not prone to aggressive behavior or beaching.",al={"what animal is this","what is the beached creature","sea monster bones"}},{q="Why did the sea creature beach itself?",a="The exact cause is unknown, but Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde notes that such strandings are completely unnatural for this species. Night elf researchers suspect an underlying disturbance or corruption in the surrounding seas is disorienting the creatures or forcing them to flee their native habitats.",al={"why did it beach","why are sea creatures dying","darkshore strandings"}},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a priestess representing the Temple of the Moon stationed in Auberdine. She is coordinating the ecological investigation into Darkshore's coastline, collecting skeletal remains to study the affliction plaguing the local marine fauna.",al={"who turns in this quest","who is gwennyth","auberdine priestess"}},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the corpse?",a="The murlocs are opportunists drawn to the beached giant as an easy, abundant food source. The band surrounding this particular carcass is notably stronger and more aggressive than the murlocs dwelling closer to Auberdine.",al={"why murlocs here","murlocs near bones","beach murlocs"}},{q="Where does this creature normally live?",a="These marine mammals make their home in the open waters encircling the giant boughs and roots of Teldrassil, rarely approaching the mainland shores under normal circumstances.",al={"where do these live","sea mammal habitat","teldrassil sea creatures"}},{q="How does this relate to other beachings in Darkshore?",a="Several marine species have washed ashore along Darkshore, including carnivorous threshers and giant sea turtles. While threshers are naturally turbulent, the beaching of peaceful mammals confirms that the maritime anomaly affects species across the entire coastal ecosystem.",al={"other beached sea creatures","beached thresher","beached sea turtle"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The strandings along Darkshore strike a painful chord for the Kaldorei, who revere natural harmony and watch with dread as the waters around their new home of Teldrassil grow troubled.",["class:Priest"]="The Temple of the Moon funds and oversees this inquiry, seeking divine insight into the corruption unsettling Kalimdor's waters.",["class:Druid"]="Any disruption in marine behavior is a dire omen for the Cenarion Circle, pointing toward an unnatural blight poisoning the coastal wildlife.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing the shores around Auberdine protects vital Alliance shipping lanes between Darkshore, Teldrassil, and the eastern kingdoms."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea creature","darkshore","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","sea creature bones","teldrassil","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:4723","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:940","topic:murloc","quest:2519","subzone:temple-of-the-moon"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=4730},src={"Beached Sea Creature (3)"}}
E["quest:4731"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="This beached sea turtle carcass along the Darkshore coastline carries a broken carriage and a box inscribed with strange runes. Unlike other naturally stranded marine life, this creature appears to have been slain while serving as a beast of burden.",h="This beached sea turtle carcass along the Darkshore coastline carries a broken carriage and a box inscribed...",sec={{t="A Beast of Burden",b="The Darkshore coast is littered with the bones of ancient sea creatures, but this turtle skeleton tells a distinctly artificial tale. Strapped across its massive shell are the splintered remnants of a buckled carriage. The creature did not die of sickness or disorientation like others washed ashore; it was driven onto the rocks while hauling cargo. In the wreckage of the carriage rests a container decorated with unfamiliar, serpent-like carvings, left behind amidst the scavengers who claimed the rotting shell.",sp=0},{t="The Naga Incursion",b="When Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde examines the salvaged box in Auberdine, she identifies the craftsmanship as belonging to the naga. The serpentine fiends frequently harness great sea beasts to ferry provisions and weapons ashore during their amphibious assaults. Given the location of the wreckage along the southern shores of Darkshore, Gwennyth suspects this supply transport met its end while ferrying gear toward Ashenvale, pointing toward expanding naga ambitions across northern Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does this sea turtle have a carriage on its back?",a="The carriage was fitted onto the creature by the naga, who use giant sea turtles as living pack animals to transport supplies, weapons, and war materiel from the ocean depths onto land.",al={"turtle carriage","why turtle has cart","sea turtle harness"}},{q="Who is currently inhabiting the remains?",a="A band of powerful Greymist murlocs took over the giant shell after the turtle died, using its massive hollowed-out carcass as a fortified seaside shelter.",al={"who lives in turtle","greymist murlocs turtle","what is guarding turtle"}},{q="Where does the Strangely Marked Box go?",a="The box should be brought to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, an emissary representing the Temple of the Moon stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine.",al={"where do i take the box","strangely marked box","turn in marked box"}},{q="What do the markings on the box mean?",a="The markings are naga script. They indicate that the box and its carriage were part of a naga supply convoy moving along the coast, likely heading south toward Ashenvale before disaster struck.",al={"turtle box lore","who made the marked box","naga box"},sp=1},{q="Why is the Temple of the Moon interested in beached turtles?",a="The priestesses of Elune are investigating the environmental and military threats afflicting the Darkshore coastline. Recovered artifacts like this box are sent to Darnassus so scholars can map out hostile movements.",al={"why temple wants turtles","gwennyth darkshore mission"}},{q="Where was the turtle traveling before it died?",a="Based on the location of the carcass along the coast, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde suspects the naga were directing the laden creature southward, potentially headed toward Ashenvale.",al={"turtle destination","where was turtle going"},sp=1}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of sea life for military transport by the naga is an outrage to the kaldorei, and discovering these tracks helps the Temple of the Moon track threats toward Ashenvale.",["class:Druid"]="Seeing a noble sea turtle enslaved to haul weapons of war and left to rot among scavengers illustrates the corrupting disregard the naga show toward wild beasts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Investigating this wreckage alerts Auberdine and Darnassus to naga logistical routes threatening northern Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","beached sea turtle","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","naga","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","topic:naga","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc","zone:ashenvale","zone:darnassus","quest:4722"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=4731},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (4)"}}
E["quest:4732"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along the wind-battered coast of Darkshore, the bleached bones of giant sea turtles wash ashore with unsettling frequency. Investigating these tragic strandings provides Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine with specimens to study why Kalimdor's marine life is dying out.",h="Along the wind-battered coast of Darkshore, the bleached bones of giant sea turtles wash ashore with...",sec={{t="A Strand of Bones",b="The mist-shrouded coast of Darkshore is strewn with the remains of great leviathans and majestic sea turtles. Many of these ancient reptiles have drifted onto the shoals or hauled themselves onto the sand to perish. Greymist murlocs frequently swarm the massive carcasses, picking the flesh down to the shell and bone while establishing crude camps around the carrion.",sp=0},{t="Vanishing Waters",b="Before the Third War, sea turtles were known to thrive in the sacred waters around Mount Hyjal and the roots of the World Tree, Nordrassil. Following Nordrassil's sacrifice to defeat the Burning Legion and the subsequent planting of Teldrassil off Kalimdor's northern shore, the population collapsed. Priestesses of Elune like Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde study these coastal remains on behalf of the Temple of the Moon, seeking to understand whether dark magic, the changing sea, or the loss of their ancient sanctuary is driving these gentle giants to their deaths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are sea turtles beaching themselves in Darkshore?",a="The exact reason remains a mystery to the night elves. Historically, sea turtles thrived in the waters beneath the World Tree Nordrassil. Following Nordrassil's destruction in the Third War and the raising of Teldrassil, their numbers have plummeted, and many seem to deliberately end their lives along the Darkshore shoals.",al={"why do turtles die here","darkshore turtle mystery","why beached"}},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf scholar and representative of the Temple of the Moon stationed in Auberdine. She is tasked with cataloging and studying the washed-up sea creatures along the coast to uncover why Darkshore's wildlife is suffering.",al={"who is gwennyth","where to turn in turtle remains","auberdine researcher"}},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the turtle remains?",a="The local Greymist murlocs are opportunists who scavenge the enormous carcasses for sustenance and materials. They often pitch their shoreline settlements right next to beached sea turtles and sea creatures to strip them clean.",al={"why murlocs on turtle","greymist scavengers","murloc camps on beach"}},{q="What connection do these turtles have to Nordrassil?",a="According to the night elves, sea turtles were once common and playful in the pristine waters around the base of Mount Hyjal and the World Tree Nordrassil. The violent destruction of Nordrassil deeply disrupted the natural balance, after which sightings of these creatures drastically declined.",al={"nordrassil connection","hyjal turtles","mount hyjal turtle link"}},{q="Does Teldrassil have anything to do with their decline?",a="The priesthood notes that since the growth of Teldrassil, sea turtles have been seen in ever-decreasing numbers. Whether the new World Tree has altered coastal currents, disrupted their migration, or carries an unnatural aura affecting ocean life is an active area of study for the Temple of the Moon.",al={"teldrassil effect on turtles","why did teldrassil change turtles"}},{q="Are there multiple beached creatures along Darkshore?",a="Yes. Darkshore's long coastline holds multiple beached sea creatures and sea turtles. Each carcass provides unique bone and tissue samples that Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde uses to piece together the broader ecological disaster unfolding along the shore.",al={"more beached quests","other beached turtles","beached sea creatures"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The tragic stranding of these ancient ocean dwellers is a stark sign of nature out of balance following the battle at Mount Hyjal and the sudden arrival of Teldrassil.",["race:NightElf"]="The Temple of the Moon seeks to honor and understand the fading creatures that once frolicked peacefully beneath Nordrassil's boughs.",["class:Priest"]="Serving the Temple of the Moon by retrieving these remains helps the Sisterhood of Elune diagnose the unseen spiritual sickness spreading through Kalimdor's waters."},kw={"auberdine","beached","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","nordrassil","sea turtle","teldrassil","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:nordrassil","quest:940","topic:murloc","quest:4722"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=4732},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (5)"}}
E["quest:4733"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="Along the rocky inlets of the Twilight Shore, the colossal carcass of a giant thresher lies stranded in the surf. Far larger than any known local specimens, its sudden death and stranding are part of a worrying trend of deep-sea anomalies troubling the night elves of Darkshore.",h="Along the rocky inlets of the Twilight Shore, the colossal carcass of a giant thresher lies stranded in the...",sec={{t="A Giant Cast Ashore",b="The Twilight Shore in southern Darkshore is often strewn with driftwood and sea debris, but this inlet holds something far more striking: the remains of an enormous thresher. Although scavengers and the tides have begun picking it apart, its massive skeleton dwarfs any ordinary predator found in these coastal shallows. It is clearly an outsider to these waters, driven onto the rocks either by unnatural sickness, disorientation, or some deeper disturbance out in the Veiled Sea.",sp=0},{t="The Temple's Vigil",b="In Auberdine, priestesses representing the Temple of the Moon have taken great interest in the dead giants washing ashore. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde oversees the collection of skeletal samples to determine what drives such deep-dwelling predators to their deaths. While colossal threshers were once sighted near the roots of Teldrassil, their numbers have steadily plummeted, leading the priestesses to fear that the fragile marine balance off Kalimdor's northern coast is unraveling.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What kind of beast is this beached carcass?",a="It is the skeleton of an immense thresher, a predatory marine beast. It is several times larger than the common threshers native to the Darkshore coastline, making its presence here deeply anomalous.",al={"what is the beached sea creature","giant thresher darkshore","beached monster carcass"}},{q="Where did this creature originally come from?",a="Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde notes that while specimens of this immense scale were once known to roam the waters near Teldrassil, their population has declined steadily. It is not native to the immediate shallows of Darkshore.",al={"where do giant threshers live","thresher origin"}},{q="Why is the Temple of the Moon studying these carcasses?",a="The Temple of the Moon seeks to understand the widespread beaching phenomena plaguing the Darkshore coast. By inspecting bones and remains, the priestesses hope to determine whether corruption, disease, or external forces are driving deep-sea beasts onto land.",al={"why does gwennyth want bones","temple of the moon sea creatures","why study beached animals"}},{q="Where should the bones be brought?",a="The Sea Creature Bones are brought to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, a night elf researcher located in the harbor town of Auberdine.",al={"where to turn in sea creature bones","who gets the thresher bones"}},{q="Where on the coast is this carcass located?",a="The carcass rests in a rocky inlet along the Twilight Shore, the southern coastal strip of Darkshore.",al={"where is the beached creature","thresher location darkshore","twilight shore skeleton"}},{q="Are there other creatures beaching themselves in Darkshore?",a="Yes. Multiple distinct sea beasts and behemoths have washed up along the length of Darkshore's coastline, prompting an ongoing investigation by the researchers in Auberdine.",al={"other beached animals","beached sea creature questline"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The unexplained decline and beaching of marine life close to Teldrassil strikes a nerve among the Kaldorei, who look to Elune and the Temple of the Moon to interpret such dark omens.",["class:Priest"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde conducts her study under the auspices of the Temple of the Moon, seeking balance and divine insight through tangible scientific inquiry into the sea's balance.",["class:Druid"]="The stranding of apex marine predators is a telltale sign of an ecosystem in distress, aligning closely with the Cenarion Circle's wider concerns throughout Darkshore."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea creature","darkshore","gwennyth bly'leggonde","sea creature bones","temple of the moon","thresher","twilight shore"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:twilight-shore-darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:4723","quest:3524","quest:940","topic:elune"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=4733},src={"Beached Sea Creature (4)"}}
E["quest:4740"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Murkdeep!",z="darkshore",s="WANTED: Murkdeep! is an Alliance bounty posted on the notice board outside the inn in Auberdine. The village council seeks the death of Murkdeep, a dangerous murloc chieftain blamed for slaying a night elf Sentinel and sinking merchant vessels off Darkshore. Adventurers must march south along the mist-shrouded coast to draw out the raider and deliver justice.",h="WANTED: Murkdeep!",sec={{t="A Threat on the Mist-Shrouded Shoals",b="The Greymist murlocs along the Darkshore coastline are usually considered a nuisance, but Murkdeep escalated matters into open warfare against Auberdine. According to the wanted poster pinned outside the town inn, the ferocious beast is directly responsible for killing at least one night elf Sentinel and is suspected of sabotaging or wrecking two cargo vessels in the waters offshore. Facing mounting maritime losses and coastal raids, the Auberdine Village Council authorized a public bounty to put an end to the rampaging murloc leader.",sp=0},{t="The Ambush at the Huts",b="Murkdeep does not idly wander the open shoreline. He lurks off the southern coast near a cluster of murloc huts centered around a bonfire. Anyone trespassing into the encampment triggers an organized defense: waves of Greymist coastrunners and shore-crawlers surge from the surf to protect their settlement before Murkdeep himself emerges alongside his vanguard to strike down intruders.",sp=0},{t="Justice for the Fallen",b="Returning to Auberdine with proof of Murkdeep's demise fulfills a grim necessity for the Sentinels. Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea handles the bounty payout on behalf of the council. By breaking the Greymist leadership, travelers and shipping lanes traveling through the Darkshore fog are granted a reprieve from coastal sabotage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I pick up the bounty on Murkdeep?",a="You can accept the quest from the wanted poster posted right outside the inn in the center of Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"where to start wanted murkdeep","murkdeep quest start","auberdine wanted poster"}},{q="Why is the Auberdine council offering a bounty on Murkdeep?",a="Murkdeep is a particularly violent murloc responsible for slaying at least one night elf Sentinel and suspected of sinking two cargo vessels off the coast of Darkshore.",al={"why kill murkdeep","what did murkdeep do","murkdeep crimes"}},{q="Where can I find Murkdeep?",a="Murkdeep is found far south of Auberdine along the beach, guarding a cluster of three murloc huts positioned around a central bonfire.",al={"murkdeep location","where is murkdeep","murkdeep camp"}},{q="Why isn't Murkdeep at the murloc camp when I arrive?",a="Murkdeep does not stand out in the open. Stepping between the huts near the bonfire triggers waves of Greymist murlocs emerging from the ocean. Murkdeep appears with the final wave once the initial defenders are slain.",al={"murkdeep not there","murkdeep spawn","how to summon murkdeep"}},{q="Who turns in the quest once Murkdeep is dead?",a="Report the death of Murkdeep to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea, who is stationed on duty in Auberdine.",al={"who to turn in murkdeep","murkdeep turn in","glynda nalshea location"}},{q="Are the murlocs at this camp different from other murlocs in Darkshore?",a="Murkdeep commands members of the Greymist murloc tribe, including coastal scouts and warriors that work in coordinated waves to defend their seaside encampment.",al={"greymist murlocs","murkdeep tribe","what murlocs are with murkdeep"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei defending Darkshore, slaying Murkdeep avenges a fallen sister of the Sentinels and safeguards the fragile lifeline Auberdine's docks provide.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as a vital northern trade hub, making the cargo ships Murkdeep sank a costly strike against Alliance logistics in Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","glynda nal'shea","greymist","murkdeep","murloc","sentinels","wanted poster"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc","topic:sentinels","quest:938"},m={start="WANTED: Murkdeep!",["end"]="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=4740},src={"WANTED: Murkdeep! (quest)"}}
E["quest:4761"] = {t="quest",n="Thundris Windweaver",z="darkshore",s="Thundris Windweaver is an Alliance quest connecting the ranger Terenthis's reconnaissance of the local furbolgs to the civic leadership of Auberdine. Having confirmed the growing aggression of the nearby Blackwood tribe, adventurers are directed to report directly to Elder Windweaver. The elder seeks to understand the root causes of the encroaching taint warping Darkshore's wilderness.",h="Thundris Windweaver is an Alliance quest connecting the ranger Terenthis's reconnaissance of the local...",sec={{t="A Report to the Elder",b="Following your scouting mission into the corrupted furbolg camps of Darkshore, the ranger Terenthis directs you to Auberdine's village elder, Thundris Windweaver. While Terenthis monitors martial threats along the woodland borders, Thundris oversees the daily welfare of the settlement and weighs the broader spiritual and environmental perils facing the kaldorei. The report provides leadership with clear evidence that the furbolgs are not simply territorial, but actively deteriorating under an unnatural malice.",sp=0},{t="Corruption Along the Coast",b="Upon receiving word of the furbolg encampment, Thundris confirms that Auberdine has been wrestling with mounting hostility from native forest dwellers for some time. More distressing than the aggression alone is the creeping corruption infecting Darkshore's soil, flora, and waters. Believing that healing the land requires discovering the wellspring of this blight, Thundris turns his focus toward tracing the taint upstream, enlisting capable allies to investigate the region's waterways.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver serves as the elder of Auberdine, acting as a sage steward over the town's governance and daily affairs. He works closely with sentinels and druids to understand and combat the strange corruption spreading through Darkshore.",al={"thundris windweaver","auberdine elder","who is thundris"}},{q="Why does Terenthis send you to Thundris?",a="After scouting the Blackwood furbolg camps, Terenthis determines that the town's civic leadership must be briefed. Thundris Windweaver holds theories on why the wildlife and furbolgs are falling to madness and requires firsthand intelligence to coordinate a response.",al={"why go to thundris","terenthis report","auberdine report"}},{q="What is happening to the furbolgs in Darkshore?",a="The native furbolgs of Darkshore have grown increasingly violent, succumbing to a dark corruption that is warping the forest itself. Rather than simple border disputes, their hostility stems from a sinister taint poisoning the land.",al={"corrupted furbolgs","furbolg hostility","why are furbolgs mad"}},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Elder Windweaver suspects that Darkshore's water sources may be carrying the source of the rot. He promptly directs adventurers to sample the Cliffspring River to determine where the contamination originates.",al={"next quest","what after thundris","cliffspring river quest"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine represents the kaldorei's primary port and foothold on the mainland coast; bringing intelligence to Elder Windweaver directly aids your people's effort to preserve their sacred wilderness.",["class:Druid"]="The rapid corruption of the local furbolgs and forest dwellers signals a severe ecological imbalance that Cenarion allies and village elders cannot afford to ignore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Auberdine from hostile woodland tribes is vital for ensuring the safety of Alliance supply lines and travelers crossing between Kalimdor and Teldrassil."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","cliffspring","darkshore","furbolg","terenthis","thundris windweaver"},rel={"npc:terenthis","quest:984","quest:4762","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:furbolg"},m={start="Terenthis",["end"]="Thundris Windweaver",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4761},src={"Thundris Windweaver (quest)"}}
E["quest:4762"] = {t="quest",n="The Cliffspring River",z="darkshore",s="The Cliffspring River is a major waterway in northern Darkshore that is rapidly turning foul and threatening the settlement of Auberdine. Thundris Windweaver tasks Alliance investigators with gathering a water sample from beneath a river bridge waterfall to confirm the creeping blight. The analysis points beyond the riverbanks to a much darker source of corruption festering in the eastern highlands.",h="The Cliffspring River is a major waterway in northern Darkshore that is rapidly turning foul and threatening...",sec={{t="A Tainted Waterway",b="Running down from the eastern highlands, the Cliffspring River empties into the coastal shoals along Mist's Edge, just north of Auberdine. Recently, its waters have begun to turn foul, carrying an unnatural rot toward the night elf settlement. Fearing that the wash will poison the surrounding shores and the town's supplies, Thundris Windweaver sends scouts upriver to draw samples from the waterfall pool beneath the road bridge.",sp=0},{t="The Root in Felwood",b="While the local Blackwood furbolgs have set up encampments along the river and show severe signs of agitation, Thundris suspects they are merely victims and conduits rather than the creators of the blight. Examining the drawn water confirms his fears: the taint trickles down directly from Felwood, the blighted forest to the east scarred during the Third War. Remedying the water will require confronting the corrupted furbolgs and purifying the land's ancient sources.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I collect the water sample?",a="Head north from Auberdine until you reach the mouth of the Cliffspring River along Mist's Edge. Follow the river inland to the first waterfall, located just beneath an overhead road bridge, and fill the sampling tube in the pool.",al={"where is the water sample","cliffspring river location","waterfall pool location"}},{q="Why is the Cliffspring River turning foul?",a="The foul runoff trickles down from the blighted heights of Felwood to the east, carrying demonic corruption into Darkshore's river system and driving the local Blackwood furbolg tribe mad.",al={"why is river corrupted","what is poisoning darkshore water","cliffspring taint source"},sp=1},{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver is a night elf scholar and investigator stationed in Auberdine. He studies the ecological decay spreading through Darkshore and works to divine the causes of regional corruption.",al={"thundris windweaver lore","who gives cliffspring river quest"}},{q="Are the furbolgs responsible for poisoning the river?",a="No. While the Blackwood furbolgs live along the river and spread violence in their mad state, they are merely victims of the taint washing down from Felwood rather than the true root of the plague.",al={"did furbolgs taint the water","blackwood furbolg corruption"},sp=1},{q="How does this river impact Auberdine?",a="The Cliffspring River empties out into Mist's Edge just north of town. The coastal currents threaten to carry the putrid runoff straight into Auberdine's shoreline, endangering their fisheries, flora, and freshwater supply.",al={"threat to auberdine","why does auberdine care about cliffspring"}},{q="What happens after testing the sample?",a="Testing confirms the corruption matches the blighted magic of Felwood, leading Thundris Windweaver to send adventurers further into Blackwood territory to investigate the tribe and seek a cure.",al={"quest after cliffspring river","what follows cliffspring river"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids of the Cenarion Circle, seeing clean woodland waters turn putrid with lingering demonic taint is a call to arms to cleanse Darkshore's wounded nature.",["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine relies on the balance of Darkshore's coastline, and allowing Felwood's rot to spill into Mist's Edge endangers the homes and livelihood of the Kaldorei."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","cliffspring","darkshore","felwood","river","taint","thundris","waterfall","windweaver"},rel={"quest:4761","quest:4763","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","subzone:mist-s-edge","zone:felwood","topic:furbolg","quest:938"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4762},src={"The Cliffspring River"}}
E["quest:4763"] = {t="quest",n="The Blackwood Corrupted",z="darkshore",s="Following evidence found in the tainted waters of Cliffspring River, Thundris Windweaver sends adventurers to sever the dark influence strangling the Blackwood tribe. By purifying their food supply with moonwell water, you provoke their demonic handler into the open to shatter his hold on the northern camp.",h="Following evidence found in the tainted waters of Cliffspring River, Thundris Windweaver sends adventurers to...",sec={{t="A Hidden Master",b="The night elves of Auberdine have long struggled to understand why the once-peaceful Blackwood furbolgs turned so viciously against their neighbors. Investigations along the Cliffspring River traced the rot to satyr meddling. These ancient servants of the Burning Legion have been actively manipulating the tribe, channeling fel magic through insidious talismans to twist the minds of the furbolgs and drive them into feral aggression.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Shackles",b="To lure the puppet master into the open, Thundris Windweaver concocts a simple yet potent remedy. By gathering common rations—grain, fruit, and nuts—from the northern Blackwood settlement and immersing them in holy waters drawn from Auberdine's moonwell, the tainted nourishment is purified. Offering this blessed food at the central bonfire grants nearby furbolgs a brief respite from their madness, directly exposing the meddling satyr corruptor, Xabraxxis, who emerges in fury to defend his twisted dominion.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the Blackwood furbolgs aggressive?",a="Their minds have been poisoned by demonic influence. Satyrs secretly planted themselves near the camps, channeling foul magic through enchanted talismans to corrupt the furbolgs' food supply and twist their natural instincts into rabid violence.",al={"why furbolgs mad","why are furbolgs hostile","blackwood aggression"}},{q="Who is Xabraxxis?",a="Xabraxxis is a satyr corruptor overseeing the northern Blackwood furbolg camp. He works from the shadows to ensure the tribe remains gripped by fel madness, relying on a Talisman of Corruption to sustain his control.",al={"xabraxxis lore","who is the satyr","satyr boss darkshore"}},{q="Does cleansing their food cure the furbolgs forever?",a="No. The moonwell-infused nourishment only breaks the demonic haze long enough for them to recognize peace and draw out Xabraxxis. Slaying the satyr and claiming his talisman is a significant victory, but Thundris Windweaver notes that discovering a permanent cure for the corrupted tribes will take further effort.",al={"is the cure permanent","did we save the furbolgs","are furbolgs cured"},sp=1},{q="Where did the idea to use moonwell water come from?",a="Moonwells are sacred pools blessed by the Goddess Elune, brimming with rejuvenating magic that counters fel and undeath. Thundris Windweaver provides a cleansing bowl so its sanctified waters can neutralize the demonic toxins woven into the furbolgs' foodstuffs.",al={"why moonwell water","moonwell cleansing bowl"}},{q="What happens when the food bowl is placed at the bonfire?",a="The nearby furbolgs briefly snap out of their bloodlust, gather peacefully around the blessed food, and cease attacking. Enraged that his puppets are breaking free of their torment, Xabraxxis immediately manifests to punish the meddlers.",al={"bowl near bonfire","cleansing the furbolgs"},sp=1},{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver is a night elf researcher and investigator stationed in Auberdine. He coordinates efforts to uncover the root causes behind Darkshore's creeping ecological decay and the madness gripping local wildlife.",al={"thundris windweaver lore","who gives the quest"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The furbolgs were ancient allies of the kaldorei during the War of the Ancients; watching them fall under the sway of their ancestral enemies, the satyrs, is a bitter tragedy night elves are eager to right.",["class:Druid"]="Restoring balance demands cutting out the rot at its root. Seeing a satyr use fel talismans to warp primal woodland creatures makes confronting Xabraxxis an urgent priority for the Cenarion Circle.",["class:Priest"]="Channeling the pure, restorative grace of Elune through moonwell waters provides a stark contrast to the corrupting shadow and fel magic deployed by the satyr."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","darkshore","furbolg","moonwell","satyr","talisman of corruption","thundris windweaver","xabraxxis"},rel={"quest:4762","quest:4761","topic:furbolg","topic:satyr","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=4763},src={"The Blackwood Corrupted"}}
E["quest:4811"] = {t="quest",n="The Red Crystal",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea of Auberdine tasks travelers with investigating rumors of a mysterious red crystal embedded along Darkshore's eastern mountains. With hostile moonkin multiplying nearby and appearing drawn to the formation, the Sentinels need to confirm whether the anomaly truly exists.",h="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea of Auberdine tasks travelers with investigating rumors of a mysterious red crystal...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Shift in the Wilds",b="For generations, the night elves of Kalimdor viewed moonkin as gentle, mystical creatures closely tied to the wilderness. In recent days, however, aggressive packs have multiplied rapidly along the slopes east of Auberdine. While some traditionalists maintain reverence for the moonkin, Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea prioritizes the town's safety and cannot ignore the rising danger. Reports suggest the beasts are flocking to a specific location along the eastern peaks.",sp=0},{t="The Eastern Mountain Anomaly",b="Scouts and wanderers brought whispers of an unnatural red crystal jutting from the rocky hillside high above Darkshore. Because wild rumors spread easily in the fog-bound coast, Glynda seeks boots on the ground to separate myth from fact. Finding the crimson monolith confirms that the anomaly is very real, leaving the Sentinels to puzzle out why the local moonkin are inexplicably drawn to it and whether its presence portends a sinister influence over the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the red crystal in Darkshore?",a="It is an enigmatic, glowing crimson formation embedded in the eastern mountain range above Darkshore. The Sentinels initially knew little about its origins, only that local wildlife—particularly moonkin—appear irresistibly drawn toward its location.",al={"what is red crystal","darkshore crystal","red rock auberdine"}},{q="Who sends you to look for the red crystal?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea, stationed in Auberdine, assigns the mission. She is responsible for defending the settlement and wants firsthand confirmation of the rumors surrounding the eastern mountains.",al={"who gives the red crystal quest","glynda nalshea quest","auberdine crystal quest giver"}},{q="Why are moonkin behaving aggressively around the crystal?",a="Historically regarded as gentle and mystical beings, the moonkin have become territorial and volatile. Sentinel Glynda suspects their sudden change in behavior and swelling numbers are linked directly to whatever power radiates from the mysterious red crystal.",al={"why are moonkin mad","angry moonkin darkshore","moonkin hostile"}},{q="Where is the red crystal located?",a="The crystal lies due east of Auberdine, nestled high up along the rugged eastern mountain ridge of Darkshore, surrounded by prowling moonkin.",al={"where to find red crystal","red crystal location","darkshore red crystal map"}},{q="Is the crystal considered dangerous by the night elves?",a="Sentinel Glynda is deeply cautious. While unsure whether the stone is benign or sinister, the fact that it agitates and congregates wild beasts makes it an immediate concern for the security of Auberdine.",al={"is the crystal bad","is red crystal evil"}},{q="What happens after you discover the crystal?",a="Reporting its existence back to Glynda proves the rumors true. She immediately seeks to uncover its true nature, leading to efforts to cleanse and sample it using water from the local falls.",al={"what is after red crystal","as water cascades follow up"},sp=1}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The agitation of the moonkin is a troubling sight for Kaldorei, who revere these creatures as sacred wards of Elune and nature.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold close spiritual ties to moonkin and the natural order of Darkshore, making the crystal's corruptive or disruptive pull an urgent ecological concern.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the Alliance's primary coastal port on northern Kalimdor; any unchecked threat gathering in the hills risks isolating the haven from the wilderness."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","glynda nal'shea","moonkin","red crystal","sentinels"},rel={"quest:4812","quest:4813","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4811},src={"The Red Crystal"}}
E["quest:4812"] = {t="quest",n="As Water Cascades",z="darkshore",s="As Water Cascades is an Alliance quest in Darkshore where players test the nature of the mysterious red crystal jutting from the eastern mountain wall. By pouring sacred moonwell water from Auberdine over its surface, players attempt to pierce its opaque exterior and uncover where it came from.",h="As Water Cascades is an Alliance quest in Darkshore where players test the nature of the mysterious red...",sec={{t="Purifying the Unknown",b="After the red crystal is first sighted high on the eastern cliffs of Darkshore, Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea devises a way to examine its composition safely. Moonwell waters carry potent divine and restorative magic, blessed by the night elves' devotion to Elune. Glynda reasons that dousing the alien monolith with water drawn from the moonwell in Auberdine will trigger a reaction, cutting through its strange, opaque shell without destroying it outright.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of Felwood",b="Nal'Shea's concern stems largely from geography. Darkshore's eastern ridge looms beneath the corrupted heights of Felwood, a forest twisted by demonic energies during the Third War. If the red spire is linked to Felwood's corruption, handling it carries immense risk. When the sacred water trickles down the crystal's lattice, the humming stone momentarily turns transparent, hinting that whatever lies trapped within requires a closer look.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I get the water for this quest?",a="You must draw the water from the moonwell located in the night elf settlement of Auberdine, using the empty vial provided by Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea.",al={"where is the moonwell","moonwell water location","fill empty water tube"}},{q="Why does moonwell water affect the crystal?",a="Moonwells hold consecrated, magic-rich water blessed by Elune. Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea anticipates that its purifying essence will react against the foreign energy of the stone and reveal its hidden composition.",al={"why moonwell water","moonwell magic on crystal"}},{q="Where is the red crystal located?",a="The mysterious red crystal rests along Darkshore's eastern mountain wall, nestled into the rocky foothills separating the shore from the highlands above.",al={"red crystal location","where is the crystal","red crystal darkshore"}},{q="Why is Sentinel Glynda worried about Felwood?",a="Felwood lies directly east and above Darkshore, ravaged by demonic corruption from the Third War. Because the crystal appeared near the boundary ridge, Glynda fears it may share that foul, demonic origin.",al={"glynda felwood","connection to felwood"}},{q="What happens when you pour the water on the crystal?",a="As the moonwell water cascades down the crystal's facets, the stone hums and its normally opaque outer shell briefly turns transparent, revealing deeper secrets sealed inside.",al={"pouring water result","what happens to the crystal"},sp=1},{q="Who gives the quest As Water Cascades?",a="The quest is given by Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine, immediately following the reconnaissance mission, The Red Crystal.",al={"quest giver","who starts as water cascades"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, moonwells are sacred fonts of life and solace. Using their consecrated waters as a tool of revelation highlights how central Elune's grace is to untangling threats along their borders.",["class:Druid"]="Druids watching over Darkshore's fragile ecosystem are naturally suspicious of unnatural foreign formations, especially along the ridge below corrupted Felwood.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts based in Auberdine must keep the coast secure from looming corruption creeping down from the eastern highlands."},kw={"as water cascades","auberdine","darkshore","empty water tube","felwood","glynda nal'shea","moonwell","red crystal"},rel={"quest:4811","quest:4813","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","zone:felwood"},m={start="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",["end"]="Mysterious Red Crystal",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4812},src={"As Water Cascades"}}
E["quest:4813"] = {t="quest",n="The Fragments Within",z="darkshore",s="\"The Fragments Within\" is the concluding task in the investigation of the mysterious red crystal jutting from the cliffs east of Auberdine. Equipped with purified moonwell water, you are sent back to the site to examine what lies within the strange formation and report back to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea.",h="\"The Fragments Within\" is the concluding task in the investigation of the mysterious red crystal jutting from...",sec={{t="A Grim Revelation",b="Pouring blessed moonwell water over the crimson crystal clears away the murky exterior, exposing what lies trapped beneath its polished surface. Suspended inside the dense mineral are several small bone fragments and half of a humanoid jawbone. The stone encasing them is extraordinarily tough—so durable that even formidable spells would struggle to crack it open. Whatever entity or artifact spawned these remains, it has been preserved in uncanny isolation above the Darkshore coastline.",sp=1},{t="Reporting to Auberdine",b="Returning to Auberdine, Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea takes note of your disturbing discovery. Rather than offering definitive answers, the revelation only raises more concerns among the local night elf leadership. Glynda promises to present the findings to the town council, though she takes solace in the fact that the strange crystal sits high in the eastern cliffs, far enough from town that it poses no immediate danger to the residents.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is trapped inside the red crystal?",a="Washing the crystal with sanctified moonwell water makes it transparent enough to spot several bone fragments and half of a humanoid jawbone embedded deep inside.",al={"what is in the crystal","what are the fragments","what bones are inside"},sp=1},{q="Can the crystal be broken open to inspect the bones?",a="No. The crystal is exceptionally resilient. Even the strongest forms of magic would find breaking through its structure nearly impossible, leaving the exact identity of the bones a mystery.",al={"can you break the crystal","opening the red crystal"},sp=1},{q="Who do you report the findings to?",a="You report your findings to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea, who is stationed in the port town of Auberdine.",al={"who turns in the fragments within","quest turn in","glynda nalshea"}},{q="What will the Sentinels do about the crystal?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea plans to inform the council in Auberdine so they can deliberate on potential actions. However, because the crystal rests high in the eastern cliffs, it is not viewed as an urgent threat.",al={"what happens next with the crystal","auberdine council crystal"},sp=1}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The discovery of humanoid bones suspended in strange crystal along the mountain borders of Ashenvale and Felwood warrants careful vigilance from the Sentinels guarding Darkshore.",["class:Druid"]="The mysterious mineral resists natural wear and high magic alike, serving as a curious anomaly against the traditional balance of the wild."},kw={"auberdine","bone fragments","darkshore","glynda nal'shea","jawbone","moonwell water","mysterious red crystal"},rel={"quest:4812","quest:4811","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:felwood"},m={start="Mysterious Red Crystal",["end"]="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4813},src={"The Fragments Within"}}
E["quest:5321"] = {t="quest",n="The Sleeper Has Awakened",z="darkshore",s="Kerlonian Evershade, a recently awakened Druid of the Claw, struggles to remain awake on his journey toward Maestra's Post in Ashenvale. Entrusted with his Horn of Awakening, travelers must shepherd the lethargic druid along the forested border, rousing him when he drifts into slumber and defending him against wild furbolgs and sinister cultists.",h="Kerlonian Evershade, a recently awakened Druid of the Claw, struggles to remain awake on his journey toward...",sec={{t="A Slumbering Mind",b="For millennia, the Druids of the Claw slept within barrows, communing with the wild spirits across the Emerald Dream. Though the Third War demanded their awakening, shaking off centuries of hibernation does not come easily to every mind. Kerlonian Evershade set out south from Darkshore toward Ashenvale to rendezvous with Liladris Moonriver, but exhaustion overtook him shortly into his trek. Finding himself helplessly prone to sudden naps along the wilds, he relies on a brass Horn of Awakening and passing allies to keep his feet moving.",sp=0},{t="Peril Along the Road",b="The path connecting Darkshore to Ashenvale is far from tranquil. As Kerlonian meanders southward, his vulnerable state invites aggression from the surrounding wilderness. In Twilight Vale, corrupted Blackwood furbolgs stalk the roadway, while farther south into Ashenvale, members of the shadowy Dark Strand cult lurk in ambush. Escorting the groggy druid requires a vigilant watch, as Kerlonian will simply lie down to sleep wherever he stands unless forcefully roused with the horn.",sp=0},{t="Arrival at the Outpost",b="Upon surviving the ambushes and reaching Maestra's Post, Kerlonian promptly slips away to find another comfortable patch of grass to continue his interrupted nap. His contact, Liladris Moonriver, expresses little surprise at his habitual daze, greeting his arrival with fond exasperation. Kerlonian's struggle reflects the lingering disorientation shared by many druids who find the waking world jarring compared to the timeless tranquility of the Dream.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Kerlonian keep falling asleep?",a="Kerlonian Evershade is a Druid of the Claw who only recently awoke from centuries of hibernation in the Emerald Dream. Returning to the waking world leaves many druids disoriented and profoundly lethargic, making it nearly impossible for him to stay awake without constant external stimulation.",al={"why is kerlonian sleeping","why is he so sleepy","druid falling asleep"}},{q="How do you wake Kerlonian up when he naps?",a="You must use the Horn of Awakening, which is retrieved from a chest beside Kerlonian when the journey begins. Whenever he collapses into slumber along the trail, blowing the horn will snap him back to his senses so he can continue following.",al={"how to wake kerlonian","kerlonian horn","horn of awakening use"}},{q="Who is waiting for Kerlonian at Maestra's Post?",a="He is traveling to meet Liladris Moonriver, an elf stationed at Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale. She is familiar with his chronic sleepiness and is simply relieved to see him arrive intact.",al={"who is liladris","who is kerlonian meeting"}},{q="What enemies attack along the way?",a="The road leads past Twilight Vale, where hostile Blackwood furbolgs ambush the party. Further south into Ashenvale, excavators, adepts, and cultists belonging to the secretive Dark Strand strike from the shadows.",al={"ambushes during escort","what attacks kerlonian","twilight vale ambush"}},{q="Where does the title 'The sleeper has awakened' come from?",a="It is the iconic greeting spoken by Druids of the Claw upon being called into service during the Third War, highlighting Kerlonian's nature as an awakened shapeshifter.",al={"sleeper has awakened quote","druid voiceline"}},{q="What happens to the horn if you take too long?",a="The Horn of Awakening carries a limited duration before it vanishes from your possessions. If the escort takes too long or must be restarted after a failure, a replacement must be gathered from the chest at Kerlonian's resting spot.",al={"horn expired","horn of awakening disappeared"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druids will recognize the heavy toll of deep communion with the Emerald Dream, as prolonged hibernation often leaves the waking mind slow to regain full consciousness.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Kerlonian is a familiar sight of their culture's recent upheaval, representing the thousands of druids who answered the call of the horn during the Third War and now adjust to daylight.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing the safe passage of travelers between Darkshore and northern Ashenvale helps maintain vital communication lines between Auberdine and outlying sentry posts."},kw={"ashenvale","dark strand","darkshore","druid of the claw","evershade","horn of awakening","kerlonian","liladris","maestra's post","twilight vale"},rel={"npc:kerlonian-evershade","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","subzone:twilight-vale","topic:emerald-dream","topic:druid","quest:2561"},m={start="Kerlonian Evershade",["end"]="Liladris Moonriver",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=5321},src={"The Sleeper Has Awakened (Classic)"}}
E["quest:5713"] = {t="quest",n="One Shot. One Kill.",z="darkshore",s="While carrying an urgent message toward Lor'danel, Sentinel Aynasha was ambushed and poisoned by a hostile furbolg named Marosh the Devious and his pack of trackers. Immobilized while mixing an antidote, she relies on nearby travelers to hold off incoming attackers so she can survive and see her duty through.",h="While carrying an urgent message toward Lor'danel, Sentinel Aynasha was ambushed and poisoned by a hostile...",sec={{t="Ambush on the Forest Road",b="The trails through northern Kalimdor have grown treacherous as corruption takes deeper root among the wild denizens. Sentinel Aynasha was journeying toward Lor'danel bearing important communications when she was intercepted by hostile furbolgs. Led by Marosh the Devious, the ambushers struck fast, inflicting a debilitating venom that left the scout unsteady and unable to complete her trek on foot.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Line",b="Though skilled with natural concoctions, concocting and administering an antidote under the canopy takes time Aynasha does not possess while hunted. As Marosh's trackers close in, Aynasha must rely on travelers to guard her position while she works. Despite her failing strength, she steadies her bow to rain covering fire into the brush, determined that neither she nor her missive will fall in the wilds.",sp=0},{t="Report to Maestra's Post",b="Once the assault is broken and Marosh is slain, the antidote restores Aynasha's strength enough for her to finish her journey to Lor'danel. To ensure the outpost south in Ashenvale is alerted to the aggressive furbolg activity threatening regional supply routes, she bids her protectors report directly to Sentinel Onaeya at Maestra's Post.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Aynasha?",a="Sentinel Aynasha is a night elf scout tasked with carrying critical messages across the borders of Darkshore and Ashenvale. Skilled with a bow and woodland survival, she was nearly undone by an unexpected poison ambush while on duty.",al={"sentinel aynasha","aynasha","who is aynasha"}},{q="Who attacked Sentinel Aynasha?",a="She was ambushed by a pack of hostile furbolg led by Marosh the Devious. They poisoned her during the initial clash, hoping to overwhelm the immobilized scout before she could recover.",al={"who attacked her","marosh the devious","marosh","who poisoned her"}},{q="Where was Sentinel Aynasha traveling?",a="Aynasha was bound for Lor'danel to deliver an important dispatch before being trapped on the road by Marosh and his trackers.",al={"where was aynasha going","aynasha destination","lor'danel"}},{q="Why must you report to Sentinel Onaeya?",a="Because Aynasha must press forward immediately to Lor'danel to deliver her message, she asks you to travel south to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale to inform Sentinel Onaeya about the furbolg hostility.",al={"sentinel onaeya","why maestra's post","onaeya"}},{q="Why are the furbolgs in the area hostile?",a="Across Darkshore and Ashenvale, many furbolg tribes have succumbed to demonic taint and madness stemming from the Third War, driving them to attack traveling Sentinels and wayside travelers indiscriminately.",al={"why are furbolgs attacking","furbolg hostility","corrupted furbolg"}},{q="Does Aynasha fight during the ambush?",a="Yes. Even though the venom leaves her barely able to stand, she supports her defender by providing covering fire with her bow while preparing the antidote.",al={"does aynasha help","aynasha bow","does she fight"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Defending Aynasha preserves both a sister of the Sentinels and critical communications moving between outposts in Ashenvale and northern Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping the woodland paths clear of aggressive furbolg packs ensures safe passage between Ashenvale and the Alliance strongholds to the north.",["class:Hunter"]="Aynasha demonstrates the unwavering resolve of a marksman, continuing to loose deadly shots into the brush even while succumbing to potent venom."},kw={"ambush","antidote","aynasha","darkshore","furbolg","lor'danel","maestra's post","marosh","onaeya","sentinel"},rel={"npc:sentinel-aynasha","npc:sentinel-onaeya","subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:lor-danel","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:furbolg","topic:elune"},m={start="Sentinel Aynasha",["end"]="Sentinel Onaeya",faction="Alliance",id=5713},src={"One Shot. One Kill."}}
E["quest:6122"] = {t="quest",n="The Principal Source",z="darkshore",s="The Principal Source is an essential rite of passage for young night elf druids learning to understand and mend the natural world. Dispatched from Moonglade by Dendrite Starblaze, initiates must collect corrupted water from Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore to help Auberdine naturalist Alanndarian Nightsong halt a spreading sickness among the forest deer.",h="The Principal Source is an essential rite of passage for young night elf druids learning to understand and...",sec={{t="A Vital Waterway Corrupted",b="Cliffspring Falls provides the primary freshwater supply for the northern reaches of Darkshore. When wildlife—particularly the local deer populations—began succumbing to an unnatural, lingering malady, the Cenarion Circle turned their attention to the river. Suspecting that the aquifer itself was compromised, Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade entrusts novice druids with the crucial task of traveling to the mouth of the cavern beneath the falls to gather an untouched sample of the tainted water.",sp=0},{t="Shadows at the Falls",b="Sampling the water is not without peril. Vicious naga have established a presence inside Cliffspring River Cave, nesting near the very headwaters of the falls. Their presence around the subterranean spring poses a direct threat to anyone investigating the blight. Despite the danger, securing an uncontaminated sample from the cave mouth is the only way for the Cenarion Circle to study the agent sickening the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="A Deeper Malady",b="Upon delivering the sample to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine, the foulness of the water confirms the worst fears of the Circle. Yet examining the foul liquid reveals an unsettling truth: while the corrupted waterfall is indeed the main conduit poisoning the riverbanks, afflicted deer have been spotted far beyond its direct path. The water serves as a vital reagent to begin crafting an antidote, but Alanndarian suspects a deeper, broader corruption is spreading across Darkshore's entire water table.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Cliffspring Falls so important to Darkshore?",a="Cliffspring Falls acts as the principal natural source of drinking water for northern Darkshore. Because its flows supply local streams, rivers, and the surrounding flora and fauna, any contaminant introduced at its headwaters quickly spreads throughout the entire regional biome.",al={"why cliffspring falls matters","cliffspring river importance","darkshore water source"}},{q="Why are the deer in Darkshore falling ill?",a="The local deer drink directly from Cliffspring Falls and the streams it feeds. A virulent pollutant has tainted the water table at the source, causing the woodland creatures to suffer from a crippling, debilitating illness.",al={"why are deer sick","darkshore sick deer","what poisoned the deer"}},{q="Who is Dendrite Starblaze?",a="Dendrite Starblaze is an elder druid trainer residing in the sacred haven of Moonglade. Acting as a guide for ascending druids, he monitors disturbances across Kalimdor and coordinates the Cenarion Circle's response to natural crises.",al={"dendrite starblaze lore","who gave me this quest","starblaze moonglade"}},{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf naturalist stationed in Auberdine. Distressed by the spreading corruption and suffering fauna across Darkshore, she petitioned the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade for experienced aid to study the affliction and formulate a cure.",al={"who is alanndarian nightsong","nightsong auberdine"}},{q="Why are naga at Cliffspring Falls?",a="Naga from the Darkshore coast have pushed inland and occupied the cave system behind Cliffspring Falls. Their encroaching presence creates extreme hazard for anyone attempting to access the headwaters to investigate the water supply.",al={"naga in cliffspring cave","why are naga here","cliffspring falls naga"}},{q="What ability does this quest help druids learn?",a="This investigation is part of the 'Power over Poison' trial. By diagnosing this wildlife plague and synthesizing an antidote alongside Alanndarian Nightsong, druid initiates learn the vital magical art of curing poisons.",al={"what spell does this give","druid poison quest","cure poison chain"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="This task is part of a foundational druidic trial. By confronting ecological decay at Cliffspring Falls and compounding remedies, you awaken the spiritual and botanical knowledge required to cure poisons in the wild.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, the corruption of Cliffspring Falls represents a direct desecration of their ancestral forests, demanding immediate intervention to preserve the land's innocent creatures."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cenarion circle","cliffspring falls","cure poison","darkshore","dendrite starblaze","naga","power over poison"},rel={"quest:6125","npc:dendrite-starblaze","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","subzone:cliffspring-falls","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:cenarion-circle","quest:947"},m={start="Dendrite Starblaze",["end"]="Alanndarian Nightsong",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=6122},src={"The Principal Source (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:6123"] = {t="quest",n="Gathering the Cure",z="darkshore",s="Gathering the Cure is an essential trial for young night elf druids learning to master nature's healing powers in Darkshore. Guided by Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine, the druid collects vital natural reagents to brew a restorative salve for the region's ailing wildlife. This task lays the practical foundation for understanding how herbal remedies combat venom and disease.",h="Gathering the Cure is an essential trial for young night elf druids learning to master nature's healing...",sec={{t="A Remedy for Darkshore's Wildlife",b="Following the discovery of a contaminated water source plaguing the local wildlife, Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine sets out to concoct an effective curative salve. While pure water forms the base of the mixture, genuine healing requires potent natural catalysts. The afflicted forest deer cannot recover on their own, making the gathering of wholesome remedies a matter of urgency for the Cenarion Circle.",sp=0},{t="Roots and Lunar Blooms",b="The restorative salve demands two crucial flora: Earthroot and Lunar Fungus. Earthroot provides pure curative properties, requiring the practiced eye of an herbalist to harvest from the rocky soil. To lend the mixture potency, Alanndarian sends the druid into the nearby eastern caves to gather fungal blooms that flourish in the dark, nestled among increasingly territorial and agitated moonkin.",sp=0},{t="The Path to Poison Cleansing",b="Synthesizing a specific antidote for every toxin is a meticulous and demanding task. By walking the initiate through the delicate gathering and brewing of physical ingredients, Alanndarian demonstrates the sheer effort conventional medicine requires. This hands-on brewing serves as a stepping stone toward mastering the innate druidic art of purging toxins purely through nature magic.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Gathering the Cure?",a="The quest tasks a druid initiate with gathering Earthroot and Lunar Fungus for Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine. These reagents are used to craft a curative salve to treat the sick deer of Darkshore, serving as an instructional step in learning to neutralize poisons.",al={"why do this quest","gathering the cure goal","what is gathering the cure for"}},{q="Where does the Lunar Fungus grow?",a="Lunar Fungus grows inside the caves situated in the hills directly east of Auberdine. Druids must navigate these dens carefully, as the resident wild moonkin have grown territorial and aggressive.",al={"where is lunar fungus","lunar fungus location","how to find lunar fungus"}},{q="Do I need to be an herbalist to get Earthroot?",a="You do not need Herbalism yourself, though Earthroot is harvested from wild herb nodes. If you do not practice the trade, you must trade with an herbalist or acquire it from others to complete Alanndarian's recipe.",al={"need herbalism for earthroot","can non herbalists get earthroot","earthroot without profession"}},{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong is a Cenarion Circle druid stationed in Auberdine. She monitors the health of Darkshore's flora and fauna, guiding young druids through their initial trials to cleanse and preserve the wilderness.",al={"who is alanndarian","alanndarian nightsong lore"}},{q="Why are the deer in Darkshore sick?",a="The deer have consumed water tainted by a contaminated spring in the wilderness. The resulting poison leaves them incapacitated and suffering, requiring an active curative salve to relieve their symptoms.",al={"why are deer poisoned","sick deer darkshore","what poisoned the deer"}},{q="How does this quest help me learn Cure Poison?",a="This quest is part of the larger 'Power over Poison' training. By showing initiates how painstaking it is to prepare herbal antidotes for individual toxins, the Cenarion Circle prepares them to channel raw nature magic that can neutralize poisons effortlessly.",al={"cure poison quest druid","learn cure poison","power over poison chain"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="This rite of passage teaches young druids how mortal medicine interacts with natural toxins, laying the groundwork for channeling raw curative energy without mundane tools.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Alanndarian specifically notes the value of herbalists, who possess the trained eye needed to harvest Earthroot directly from the earth.",["race:NightElf"]="Protecting the sacred groves and fauna of Darkshore is a sacred duty for the kaldorei, who revere Elune and the spirits of the wild."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cure poison","darkshore","druid quest","earthroot","gathering the cure","lunar fungus","moonkin caves"},rel={"npc:alanndarian-nightsong","quest:6125","topic:druid","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Alanndarian Nightsong",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=6123},src={"Gathering the Cure (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:6124"] = {t="quest",n="Curing the Sick",z="darkshore",s="Curing the Sick is an essential trial for young Alliance druids, tasking them with using a prepared salve to heal the poisoned wildlife wandering Darkshore. By directly relieving the afflicted deer, initiates address the encroaching malaise troubling northern Kalimdor before reporting back to the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade.",h="Curing the Sick is an essential trial for young Alliance druids, tasking them with using a prepared salve to...",sec={{t="A Plague in the Woodlands",b="Across the shadowed forests of Darkshore, from the waters of the Cliffspring River south to the borders of Ashenvale, the local wildlife suffers from a persistent sickness. Sickly deer wander aimlessly through the mist, weakened by unnatural toxins seeped into the soil and streams. Having gathered the necessary reagents, the herbalist Alanndarian Nightsong entrusts an aspiring druid with a freshly brewed curative animal salve to treat the afflicted creatures in the field.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Unveiled in Moonglade",b="Once ten deer have been treated, the initiate is sent to report to Dendrite Starblaze in the sacred haven of Moonglade. While Auberdine breathes a small sigh of relief, Dendrite views the sickly herds as a harbinger of a far more sinister corruption sweeping northern Kalimdor. He warns that while leaders in Darnassus debate and overlook the creeping rot, the Cenarion Circle must remain vigilant against the true scale of the ecological rot taking root across the continent.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the deer in Darkshore sick?",a="The deer are suffering from a spreading ecological corruption that has begun seeping into the waters and soil of Darkshore, stretching from the Cliffspring River all the way south to Ashenvale. As wild grazers, the deer inadvertently consume the tainted flora and river water, becoming weak and diseased.",al={"why are deer sick","darkshore sickly deer","what poisoned the deer"}},{q="Who prepares the curative salve used on the deer?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong, an herbalist stationed in the night elf town of Auberdine, crafts the Curative Animal Salve from rare reagents gathered by the druid initiate. Her batch provides ten doses to immediately treat suffering animals while she attempts to produce more with the townsfolk.",al={"who makes the cure","alanndarian salve","curative animal salve maker"}},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze care about the deer?",a="Dendrite Starblaze oversees druidic training on behalf of the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade. For him, tending to the wildlife is both a practical test of a druid's duty and a stark confirmation that a wider, dangerous corruption is overtaking Kalimdor's wilderness.",al={"why dendrite moonglade","cenarion circle interest in deer","dendrite starblaze role"}},{q="What political tension does Dendrite Starblaze hint at?",a="Upon completing the task, Dendrite notes that while some night elf authorities in Darnassus acknowledge the growing environmental rot, others stubbornly ignore the warning signs. He urges the initiate never to place blinders over the uncomfortable truths facing the natural world.",al={"darnassus tension","who ignores the corruption","darnassus blinders"}},{q="Where can the sickly deer be found?",a="The sickly deer wander across almost the entirety of Darkshore. They can be found starting south of the Cliffspring River just north of Auberdine and roam throughout the coastal forests southward all the way to the border of Ashenvale.",al={"sickly deer location","where are the deer","darkshore deer location"}},{q="What does a druid learn from completing this task?",a="The quest forms the practical culmination of druidic poison-cleansing studies. By witnessing the suffering of forest animals and applying a physical cure, the druid bridges the gap between botanical remedies and spiritual mastery over poison.",al={"what does this teach druids","cure poison training druid","lesson of curing the sick"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="This rite of passage tests an initiate's commitment to preserving balance, serving as the bridge to earning the innate ability to purge poisons with druidic magic.",["race:NightElf"]="Darkshore represents the ancestral perimeter of modern night elf settlement, making the sudden blight among the deer an ominous omen for the kaldorei."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cenarion circle","cliffspring river","curative animal salve","curing the sick","darkshore","dendrite starblaze","poison","sickly deer"},rel={"npc:alanndarian-nightsong","npc:dendrite-starblaze","quest:6125","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:5921","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid"},m={start="Alanndarian Nightsong",["end"]="Dendrite Starblaze",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=6124},src={"Curing the Sick (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:6341"] = {t="quest",n="The Bounty of Teldrassil",z="darkshore",s="The Bounty of Teldrassil is an introductory errand given by Nessa Shadowsong in Rut'theran Village. Seeking to compare the unusual size and abundance of island fish with those caught along the mainland, she prepares a collection of bones and scales to be shipped across the strait to Darkshore. Delivering this package to the local hippogryph handler marks the first step in crossing the sea to Auberdine.",h="The Bounty of Teldrassil is an introductory errand given by Nessa Shadowsong in Rut'theran Village.",sec={{t="A Fisherman's Study",b="Beneath the massive boughs of the World Tree, the sheltered waters surrounding Rut'theran Village teem with remarkably large and plentiful marine life. Nessa Shadowsong, observing the remarkable yields hauled in by local fishermen, seeks to discover whether this vitality extends to the ancient mainland coast or remains unique to the waters nourished by Teldrassil. To test her theory, she prepares a collection of scales and bones to be examined by Laird, a fellow fishmonger based across the water in Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="Arranging Passage",b="Transporting cargo and travelers across the open sound between the island bough and mainland Kalimdor requires reliable wings. Rather than sending the parcel by small skiff, Nessa directs travelers directly to Vesprystus, the village hippogryph master. By handing the collection to him, travelers arrange the logistics needed to mount a trained beast and deliver the samples directly to the docks of Darkshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Nessa trying to investigate?",a="Nessa Shadowsong notices that the fish drawn from the waters around Rut'theran Village are extraordinarily large and abundant. She wants to send samples of bones and scales across the water to compare Teldrassil's harvest with the fish found along the mainland coast of Darkshore.",al={"nessa goal","why compare fish","bounty of teldrassil purpose"}},{q="Who is receiving the fish samples in Auberdine?",a="The collection is addressed to Laird, a fish vendor stationed in the coastal village of Auberdine on the mainland shore of Darkshore.",al={"who gets nessa collection","laird darkshore","auberdine fish vendor"}},{q="Why take the parcel to Vesprystus instead of traveling directly to Auberdine?",a="Vesprystus is the hippogryph master in Rut'theran Village. Handing the collection to him arranges for direct aerial transport, allowing you to secure passage on a hippogryph across the sea to Darkshore.",al={"why vesprystus","who is vesprystus","hippogryph master ruttheran"}},{q="Where is Rut'theran Village located in relation to Teldrassil?",a="Rut'theran Village sits at the southern base of Teldrassil at sea level, connected to Darnassus through an emerald portal. It serves as the primary coastal haven and harbor for ships and hippogryphs traveling to and from the great tree.",al={"rut'theran location","where is nessa shadowsong","how to reach ruttheran"}},{q="What happens after giving the collection to Vesprystus?",a="Vesprystus accepts the collection and offers the follow-up task, Flight to Auberdine, which sends you soaring across the strait on the back of a hippogryph directly to Darkshore.",al={"flight to auberdine next","after bounty of teldrassil","what does vesprystus do"}},{q="Is this part of leaving the starting zone for Night Elves?",a="Yes. This chain introduces young night elf adventurers to flight paths and guides them out of the island canopy down toward mainland Kalimdor to continue their journeys in Darkshore.",al={"leaving teldrassil","level 10 night elf quest","moving to darkshore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elf travelers, this journey marks the traditional passage from the safe heights of Teldrassil down to the shadowed mainland shores of Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="The route between Rut'theran and Auberdine serves as a crucial transit artery linking the night elf capital with the rest of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","bounty of teldrassil","darkshore","hippogryph","laird","nessa shadowsong","rut'theran village","vesprystus"},rel={"quest:6344","quest:6342","npc:vesprystus","npc:laird","subzone:rut-theran-village","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Nessa Shadowsong",["end"]="Vesprystus",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6341},src={"The Bounty of Teldrassil"}}
E["quest:6342"] = {t="quest",n="Flight to Auberdine",z="darkshore",s="This errand introduces adventurers leaving Teldrassil to the night elves' aerial transit network. Tasked by the hippogryph master Vesprystus at Rut'theran Village, travellers take wing across the sea to deliver a bundle of oversized marine specimens to Laird in Auberdine.",h="This errand introduces adventurers leaving Teldrassil to the night elves' aerial transit network.",sec={{t="Taking Wing to Darkshore",b="For many young adventurers departing the boughs of Teldrassil, Rut'theran Village marks the threshold between sanctuary and the wider world. While a mundane ferry plies the strait between the island haven and mainland Kalimdor, the night elves rely equally on their bonded hippogryphs. Entrusted with a parcel of rare fish parts from Nessa Shadowsong, travellers mount one of these winged beasts to establish their very first flight path onto the shores of Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="Curious Catches",b="The delivery itself is of keen interest to the fishermen of Darkshore. Laird, awaiting Nessa's findings at the docks of Auberdine, inspects the catch to find enormous scales the size of fists and a jawbone nearly twice the size of mainland specimens. The island waters around the base of the World Tree seem to produce altered or abnormally large life, a curiosity that hints at the potent, restless nature of Teldrassil itself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this flight?",a="The journey serves as a practical lesson in connecting flight paths between settlements while also delivering research samples of unusual fish caught around Rut'theran Village to Laird in Auberdine.",al={"why do i fly to auberdine","flight to auberdine quest goal","why fly"}},{q="Who sends the parcel, and what is inside it?",a="The package comes from the fisherwoman Nessa Shadowsong. It contains fish specimens from the waters surrounding Rut'theran Village, including massive scales and an oversized jawbone.",al={"nessa's collection","what is in the package","who sent package"}},{q="Why are the fish from Teldrassil so large?",a="Laird notes that the jawbone is nearly twice normal size and the scales are as big as a fist. The waters encircling the World Tree of Teldrassil foster strangely magnified wildlife compared to the mainland shores of Darkshore.",al={"why are fish big","rut'theran fish size","huge scales"}},{q="Who is Vesprystus?",a="Vesprystus is the hippogryph master stationed at Rut'theran Village. He tends the night elven mounts and coordinates aerial travel across the water to mainland Kalimdor.",al={"vesprystus lore","who is the hippogryph master"}},{q="Who is Laird?",a="Laird is a night elf fisherman based in Auberdine on the coast of Darkshore. He studies local aquatic life and compares mainland catches against those caught near Teldrassil.",al={"laird lore","who is laird","laird darkshore"}},{q="Can you travel between Rut'theran and Auberdine without flying?",a="Yes. A regular ferry boat runs between the docks at Rut'theran Village and the pier at Auberdine, offering an alternative to the hippogryph flight.",al={"boat to auberdine","ferry to darkshore","other way to auberdine"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Taking flight on a hippogryph to Auberdine marks an iconic rite of passage for young kaldorei stepping forth from Teldrassil onto the ancestral mainland.",["faction:Alliance"]="Hippogryphs serve as the Alliance's primary aerial network throughout northern Kalimdor, linking coastal outposts directly to the capital."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","flight path","flight to auberdine","hippogryph","laird","nessa shadowsong","rut'theran village","teldrassil","vesprystus"},rel={"npc:vesprystus","npc:laird","subzone:rut-theran-village","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:6341","quest:6343","quest:940"},m={start="Vesprystus",["end"]="Laird",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6342},src={"Flight to Auberdine"}}
E["quest:6343"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Nessa",z="darkshore",s="This quest sends young travelers from Auberdine back to Rut'theran Village to deliver Laird's findings to Nessa Shadowsong. It concludes an introductory errand teaching adventurers how to navigate transit between the mainland of Kalimdor and Teldrassil.",h="This quest sends young travelers from Auberdine back to Rut'theran Village to deliver Laird's findings to...",sec={{t="A Messenger Across the Sea",b="Having delivered Nessa Shadowsong's initial inquiries to Laird in Auberdine, travelers are charged with carrying his written observations back across the water. Laird notes stark differences in the fish catches between Darkshore and Teldrassil's shores, suspecting that the great World Tree itself alters local marine life. To make the journey back to Rut'theran Village, adventurers can either hire a flight from the hippogryph master Caylais Moonfeather or board the regular ferry running from the Auberdine pier.",sp=0},{t="Curious Bounties",b="Upon receiving Laird's reply at Rut'theran Village, Nessa expresses fascination with the pronounced disparity in marine life. While the massive size of the fish near the World Tree provides an immediate boon to local fishermen, the underlying cause remains an open question among the Kaldorei. Nessa resolves to share the findings with her fellow villagers, content for now to harvest the abundant sea life while keeping a watchful eye on what forces might truly be responsible.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts and completes this quest?",a="The quest is offered by the fisherman Laird in Auberdine on the Darkshore coast. It is turned in to Nessa Shadowsong at Rut'theran Village, at the base of Teldrassil.",al={"quest giver","where to turn in","who gives quest"}},{q="What is the fastest way back to Rut'theran Village?",a="You can either take a swift hippogryph flight by speaking with Caylais Moonfeather in Auberdine, or walk out onto the long pier to catch the regular passenger ferry back to the docks of Rut'theran Village.",al={"how to get back","travel to ruttheran","ferry or hippogryph"}},{q="Why is Laird studying the fish?",a="Laird notices that marine catches along Darkshore differ dramatically from those harvested around Teldrassil. He suspects that the burgeoning growth and unique energies of the World Tree are directly altering the surrounding wildlife.",al={"why study fish","fish difference","laird response lore"}},{q="Does Nessa find out why the fish are so strange?",a="Not immediately. Nessa notes the remarkable difference and agrees it warrants further investigation, but she is content to share the report with the local villagers and enjoy the bountiful catches in the meantime.",al={"why are fish big","teldrassil fish mystery"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="This quest directly follows 'Flight to Auberdine,' which sends travelers from Rut'theran Village over to Darkshore with Nessa's original letter to Laird.",al={"prerequisite","previous quest","flight to auberdine"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest chain?",a="Beyond introducing the mysterious ecological influence of Teldrassil on local wildlife, this two-part delivery serves as a rite of passage teaching young night elf adventurers how to commute between their island home and the Kalimdor mainland via ship and flight master.",al={"why do this quest","travel quest"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves venturing away from the boughs of Teldrassil for the first time, this exchange marks their first official errand connecting the new island haven to the ancient mainland of Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine and Rut'theran Village form the vital maritime gateway linking northern Kalimdor's night elf settlements to broader Alliance interests across Azeroth."},kw={"auberdine","caylais moonfeather","darkshore","laird","nessa shadowsong","return to nessa","rut'theran village","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:6342","npc:laird","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:940"},m={start="Laird",["end"]="Nessa Shadowsong",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6343},src={"Return to Nessa"}}
E["quest:729"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="Archaeologist Hollee has fled to Auberdine after an excavation site in southern Darkshore was overrun by hostile stone golems. Terrified for her senior colleague, she asks travelers to rush south and rescue Prospector Remtravel, an esteemed dwarven scholar who is notoriously blind to mortal danger when engrossed in his research.",h="Archaeologist Hollee has fled to Auberdine after an excavation site in southern Darkshore was overrun by...",sec={{t="A Perilous Dig",b="Dispatched across the sea by the Explorers' League under orders from Master Greywhisker, Archaeologist Hollee was thrilled to apprentice under Prospector Remtravel. Renowned among Ironforge's academic circles for his groundbreaking discoveries, Remtravel was sent to investigate ancient ruins along the untamed coast of Darkshore. However, during an excavation into what appeared to be the remnants of an ancient, great civilization, violent stone golems burst forth from the earth, rapidly overrunning the dig site.",sp=0},{t="Oblivious to Doom",b="While Hollee fled in panic to seek help in the night elven port of Auberdine, Remtravel barely batted an eye. Wholly consumed by the relics he uncovered, the elderly prospector remained knee-deep in rubble, completely unbothered by the lumbering constructs surrounding his camp. Anyone who reaches him south of Auberdine finds him not cowering in fear, but grumbling about missing stone brushes and misplaced fossils.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="Prospector Remtravel is a celebrated dwarven researcher belonging to the Explorers' League of Ironforge. Famous in the dwarven academies for his monumental discoveries, he is equally infamous for an extreme lack of situational awareness whenever valuable relics are nearby.",al={"remtravel","prospector remtravel lore","who is the prospector"}},{q="Why is Archaeologist Hollee in Auberdine?",a="Hollee was assigned as an assistant to Remtravel by Master Greywhisker. When dangerous golems emerged from the ground at their dig site, she fled northward to Auberdine seeking reinforcements to mount a rescue.",al={"archaeologist hollee","hollee auberdine","why did hollee run"}},{q="What were the dwarves excavating in Darkshore?",a="The expedition had uncovered evidence of an ancient, advanced society buried beneath Darkshore. Remtravel discovered a mysterious fossil and various stone artifacts before the site was overtaken by subterranean constructs.",al={"what was remtravel digging","darkshore dig site","remtravel fossil"}},{q="Where can Prospector Remtravel be found?",a="Remtravel is located in southern Darkshore, perched among ancient ruins south of Auberdine, surrounded by dangerous golems while obsessively looking for his stone brush and fossil.",al={"where is remtravel","remtravel location","find prospector remtravel"}},{q="Who sent this expedition to Darkshore?",a="The expedition was organized by the Explorers' League in Ironforge and directly assigned by Master Greywhisker, who tasked Hollee with assisting Remtravel in cataloging the region's ancient wonders.",al={"who sent hollee","master greywhisker","explorers league darkshore"}},{q="Is Remtravel in actual danger?",a="Yes. Hostile golems prowl the ruins directly around him. Remtravel is oblivious to the imminent threat, focusing entirely on cataloging his findings and wondering where his tools and assistant have wandered off to.",al={"is remtravel dead","remtravel alive","help remtravel"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Remtravel embodies the obsessive curiosity and tunnel vision of the Explorers' League, willing to risk limb and life over an uncatalogued fossil.",["faction:Alliance"]="This mission highlights the cooperative presence of Ironforge researchers attempting to study the unfamiliar, ancient lands of their night elf allies in Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","explorers league","fossil","golems","greywhisker","hollee","remtravel"},rel={"npc:prospector-remtravel","npc:archaeologist-hollee","quest:730","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Archaeologist Hollee",["end"]="Prospector Remtravel",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=729},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector"}}
E["quest:731"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="Deep in the southern ruins of Darkshore, Prospector Remtravel refuses to abandon his dig site without a prize to show the Explorers' League. Despite his severe forgetfulness and an infestation of hostile troggs, he insists on uncovering a mysterious fossil before retreating. Ensuring the dwarven researcher survives his erratic search allows word of his safety to reach his assistant back in Auberdine.",h="Deep in the southern ruins of Darkshore, Prospector Remtravel refuses to abandon his dig site without a prize...",sec={{t="A Perilous Excavation",b="Remtravel's Dig lies far to the south of Darkshore, nestled among ancient ruins that were supposed to hold forgotten secrets. Instead, the dwarven excavators struck into pockets of savage troggs, driving out the workers and leaving the camp under siege. While most would flee for Auberdine immediately, Prospector Remtravel became fixated on salvaging his findings. Refusing to leave empty-handed, he wanders right into the teeth of danger to recover an elusive fossil to justify the expedition's costs to the Explorers' League.",sp=0},{t="Muddled Memories and Trogg Ambushes",b="Protecting Remtravel proves as frustrating as it is dangerous. His scatterbrained nature leads him in circles across the excavation site, mistaking brushes for fossils and blundering past scaffolding and abandoned tents. Each stop draws the attention of aggressive troggs lurking in the shadowed recesses of the quarry. Only by clearing wave after wave of subterranean brutes can an escort coax the scholar into finally locating his prize and securing his passage home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="Prospector Remtravel is a senior field researcher for the dwarven Explorers' League. Stationed in Darkshore, he was tasked with excavating ancient ruins along the coast, though his extreme absent-mindedness frequently lands him in life-threatening situations.",al={"remtravel","who is the prospector","absent minded prospector guy"}},{q="Why is Remtravel still at the dig site?",a="Despite the dig being overrun by troggs, Remtravel refuses to return to Darnassus without tangible proof of his work. He insists on recovering a mysterious fossil to present to the Explorers' League before he will consider abandoning the camp.",al={"why stay at dig","why is remtravel there","why hasn't he fled"}},{q="Where did the troggs come from?",a="Like many dwarven excavations, Remtravel's team dug deep into the earth and unwittingly breached subterranean pockets inhabited by troggs. The primitive creatures surfaced in droves, violently overrunning the machinery, tents, and workers.",al={"why are there troggs in darkshore","darkshore troggs","dig site troggs"}},{q="Who is Archaeologist Hollee?",a="Archaeologist Hollee is Remtravel's colleague and assistant, based in the coastal town of Auberdine. Distraught over her mentor's prolonged absence and well aware of his forgetful habits, she recruits travelers to track him down and ensure his safe return.",al={"hollee","archaeologist hollee","remtravel assistant"}},{q="What happens after finding the fossil?",a="Once Remtravel recovers the fossil and reaches safety, you report back to Archaeologist Hollee in Auberdine. She is relieved by the news and prepares for the prospector's eventual trek across the sea to present his findings in Darnassus.",al={"quest continuation","what next","after remtravel escort"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Remtravel embodies both the relentless passion and perilous stubbornness of the Explorers' League, showing how dedication to ancient titan-lore can blind a scholar to immediate danger.",["race:NightElf"]="The kaldorei generally view dwarven excavations in Darkshore with wariness; Remtravel unearthing a horde of violent troggs confirms their fears about digging too deep into sacred ground.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Remtravel and his findings maintains vital diplomatic and scholarly cooperation between the dwarven Explorers' League and the night elves of Teldrassil."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","escort","excavation","explorers' league","fossil","hollee","remtravel","troggs"},rel={"npc:prospector-remtravel","npc:archaeologist-hollee","quest:729","topic:explorers-league","topic:trogg","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Prospector Remtravel",["end"]="Archaeologist Hollee",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=731},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (2)"}}
E["quest:741"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="This errand delivers a strange petrified specimen recovered from the wild beaches of Darkshore to the Explorers' League outpost in Darnassus. Archaeologist Hollee refuses to abandon her distracted colleague in the field, entrusting the specimen's transport to a passing adventurer instead. The fossil's arrival in the night elven capital immediately captures the keen interest of Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker.",h="This errand delivers a strange petrified specimen recovered from the wild beaches of Darkshore to the...",sec={{t="A Courier to the Capital",b="Prospector Remtravel's excavations along the misty coast of Darkshore have unearthed a curious fossil, but digging deeper matters more to him than protocol. Archaeologist Hollee, unwilling to leave the wandering prospector alone amidst the shore's dangerous beasts and hostile cultists, remains behind to watch over him. In order to get the discovery documented, she requires an Alliance traveler to ferry the specimen up to Darnassus, where the dwarven guild maintains a scholarly delegation.",sp=0},{t="The Dwarven Stake in Kalimdor",b="Dwarves from Ironforge have crossed the Great Sea in force under the banner of the Explorers' League, eager to unearth ancient relics and lost history beneath the soil of Kalimdor. Receiving the artifact in the elven capital, Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker wastes no time in marveling over Remtravel's knack for uncovering ancient treasures. While night elves view their forests as living sanctuaries, the League views the ancient lands as an expansive archaeological dig waiting to be deciphered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the mysterious fossil?",a="It is an unidentified petrified specimen unearthed along the coast of Darkshore by Prospector Remtravel. Its antiquity and strange nature make it a prize finding for the Explorers' League scholars stationed in Darnassus.",al={"mysterious fossil","what fossil is this","remtravel fossil"}},{q="Why does Hollee stay behind in Darkshore?",a="Archaeologist Hollee feels obligated to watch over Prospector Remtravel. He has a habit of wandering off and ignoring danger while excavating, so she refuses to leave him alone in the wilds while delivering his discoveries to Darnassus.",al={"why doesn't hollee go","hollee staying","why hollee stays"}},{q="Who is Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker?",a="Greywhisker is a senior representative of Ironforge's Explorers' League overseeing archaeological ventures in northern Kalimdor. He operates out of Darnassus, studying relics brought back from the field by dwarven diggers.",al={"greywhisker","who is greywhisker","chief greywhisker"}},{q="Why is the Explorers' League operating in Darnassus?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard chartered the Explorers' League to unearth the origins of the dwarven race and ancient history across Azeroth. Having friendly diplomatic ties with the night elves allows dwarven scholars to base expeditions out of Darnassus to study Kalimdor's forgotten lands.",al={"dwarves in darnassus","explorers league darnassus","why are dwarves here"}},{q="Where does this fossil end up after Darnassus?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker inspects the find in Darnassus, but discoveries of this scale are meant to be cataloged or routed further into League channels and back toward the great museum in Ironforge.",al={"where does fossil go","fossil next step"}},{q="Where did Remtravel find the specimen?",a="Remtravel uncovered the specimen along the wild coast of Darkshore, an area laden with shipwrecks, ancient ruins, and fossilized sea life dating back before the Great Sundering.",al={"where was fossil found","remtravel dig site"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Carrying Remtravel's fossil fulfills the primary mission of the Explorers' League: unearthing the world's deepest past and proving the boundless value of dwarven perseverance.",["race:NightElf"]="Watching dwarven excavators bring ancient remnants out of Darkshore's sacred soil can be jarring, but cooperating with the League preserves Alliance bonds.",["faction:Alliance"]="This task demonstrates the logistical reliance Alliance members have on each other, as dwarven researchers rely on traveling adventurers to safely bridge the remote shores of Darkshore and the heights of Darnassus."},kw={"archaeologist","darkshore","darnassus","explorers league","fossil","greywhisker","hollee","remtravel"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-hollee","npc:chief-archaeologist-greywhisker","npc:prospector-remtravel","topic:explorers-league","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Archaeologist Hollee",["end"]="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=741},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (3)"}}
E["quest:8721"] = {t="quest",n="Starweave the Elder",z="darkshore",s="Starweave the Elder is a Lunar Festival quest encountered in Darkshore. Adventurers seek out Elder Starweave in the settlement of Auberdine to pay their respects to the ancestral spirits of Kalimdor. In exchange for honoring ancient traditions, she offers celestial wisdom and her blessing.",h="Starweave the Elder is a Lunar Festival quest encountered in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Auberdine",b="During the Lunar Festival, spirits of venerated ancestors manifest across the continents of Azeroth, battened in pillars of radiant celestial radiance. Elder Starweave takes her place among the night elves of Auberdine, a critical harbor town situated along the mist-shrouded coast of Darkshore. Travelers honoring the festival make pilgrimage to her side, seeking the timeless guidance of ages past.",sp=0},{t="Whispers of the Heavens",b="Elder Starweave contemplates the cosmic tapestry above Kalimdor, reminding all who approach that the stars carry answers to mortal doubts and worldly riddles. Those who take the time to seek her council are urged to look skyward for truth and receive ancestral favor alongside tidings of other wandering spirits across the wild frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Elder Starweave?",a="Elder Starweave is located in the coastal night elf town of Auberdine in Darkshore. She stands illuminated by a brilliant beam of moonlight descending directly from the heavens.",al={"starweave location","where is elder starweave","elder starweave darkshore"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The quest is part of the yearly Lunar Festival celebration. Visiting and honoring the ancestral elders scattered across Azeroth awards recognition, festive currency, and ancestral goodwill.",al={"why do elder starweave","starweave the elder purpose","what does starweave do"}},{q="Who is Elder Starweave?",a="She is an ancient night elven spirit honoring the Lunar Festival. Bathed in starlight, she offers philosophical wisdom regarding the constellations and points pilgrims toward other revered elders, such as Elder Bladeswift.",al={"who is starweave","starweave lore","elder starweave backstory"}},{q="Can Horde players visit Elder Starweave?",a="Yes. Festival elders remain neutral and welcome respectful travelers of both factions. However, because Elder Starweave resides within the Alliance harbor of Auberdine, Horde adventurers must be cautious around the town's local night elven guards.",al={"can horde talk to starweave","horde elder starweave","starweave hostile horde"}},{q="What does Elder Starweave tell travelers?",a="Upon greeting visitors, she reminds them that the infinite stars above hold answers to mortal riddles, asking if the wise and fortunate might gaze upward to unveil truth.",al={"starweave dialogue","what does elder starweave say"}},{q="Which elder does Starweave point to?",a="Elder Starweave shares the location and tidings of Elder Bladeswift, guiding travelers onward across their festive journey through northern Kalimdor.",al={"who does starweave mention","elder after starweave","next elder darkshore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Honoring Elder Starweave in Auberdine connects night elves directly to the ancient spirits of their forebears and the revered mysteries of Elune and the stars.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold ancestral spirits and the celestial balance in deep reverence, making communion with Elder Starweave a natural reflection of their beliefs.",["faction:Horde"]="Reaching Elder Starweave requires Horde wanderers to carefully infiltrate the Alliance-held docks of Auberdine to pay their respects without provoking the local sentinels."},kw={"ancestor","auberdine","darkshore","elder bladeswift","elder starweave","lunar festival","starweave"},rel={"npc:elder-starweave","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Starweave",id=8721},src={"Starweave the Elder"}}
E["quest:942"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="This quest bridges an excavation mystery from Darkshore across the Great Sea to the Wetlands. Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker entrusts you with a strange Kalimdor fossil, directing you to Archaeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor to unlock its secrets.",h="This quest bridges an excavation mystery from Darkshore across the Great Sea to the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Curious Discovery",b="While examining the strange fossil uncovered in Darkshore, Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker notices a striking resemblance to a relic shown at an Explorers' League conference back in Ironforge. That earlier piece was presented by Archaeologist Flagongut, who was convinced that such fossils held latent powers waiting to be unlocked. Greywhisker believes Flagongut is the only dwarf capable of discerning what makes this Kalimdor find so extraordinary.",sp=0},{t="A Voyage Across the Sea",b="Carrying the mysterious relic means undertaking a long journey out of Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms. Flagongut was last seen waiting for an armed escort to the Whelgar Excavation Site while lodging at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. Delivering the fossil into his hands marks the turning point where a local Darkshore survey ties into a continent-spanning archaeological inquiry.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Greywhisker send me all the way to Menethil Harbor?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker recalls that Archaeologist Flagongut displayed an identical relic at an annual Explorers' League conference in Ironforge. Believing Flagongut holds the expertise to unlock its hidden power, Greywhisker dispatches you to find him at his last known location in Menethil Harbor.",al={"why go to menethil","greywhisker fossil errand","why wetlands"}},{q="Who is Archaeologist Flagongut?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut is an Explorers' League researcher stationed in the Wetlands. Waiting out delays at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor, he is preparing for an expedition to the perilous Whelgar Excavation Site.",al={"who is flagongut","archaeologist flagongut lore"}},{q="What is the mysterious fossil?",a="It is an ancient, curious specimen retrieved from Darkshore. Flagongut previously claimed that a twin specimen he studied possessed latent magical or historical power waiting to be unlocked.",al={"what is the fossil","mysterious fossil origin","remtravel fossil"}},{q="What does Flagongut say when you deliver the fossil?",a="Flagongut is astonished to discover that a relic identical to his own research sample originated from the distant continent of Kalimdor, verifying that ancient history links the two landmasses together.",al={"flagongut reaction","handing in the fossil"}},{q="Where does Flagongut want to go next?",a="Flagongut has been waiting in Menethil Harbor for an escort to travel inland toward the Whelgar Excavation Site, a major dig location situated in the Wetlands.",al={"where is flagongut going","flagongut excavation"}},{q="How does this quest fit into the Absent Minded Prospector storyline?",a="It serves as the transit leg of the questline. After escorting and rescuing Prospector Remtravel in Darkshore and analyzing his excavated relic with Greywhisker, the inquiry shifts from northern Kalimdor directly to League experts in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"absent minded prospector part 4","quest chain context"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven adventurers, this errand demonstrates the reach of the Explorers' League, connecting fieldwork in remote Kalimdor back to fellow scholars based in Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="This task requires utilizing Alliance shipping routes, taking sea voyages from Kalimdor over to Menethil Harbor to keep League branches connected."},kw={"absent minded prospector","archaeologist flagongut","chief archaeologist greywhisker","darkshore","deepwater tavern","explorers' league","menethil harbor","mysterious fossil"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-flagongut","npc:chief-archaeologist-greywhisker","subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:deepwater-tavern","topic:explorers-league","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker",["end"]="Archaeologist Flagongut",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=942},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (4)"}}
E["quest:943"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="This quest marks the final chapter in the search sparked by Prospector Remtravel's excavations in Darkshore. Archaeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor seeks to combine Remtravel's finds with his own fossil and the lost Stone of Relu to unlock the ancient titan relics' hidden powers.",h="This quest marks the final chapter in the search sparked by Prospector Remtravel's excavations in Darkshore.",sec={{t="Cross-Continental Archaeology",b="What began as an escort mission aiding the distracted Prospector Remtravel in the northern reaches of Darkshore leads across the Great Sea to the marshlands of the Wetlands. Remtravel's fossil had been entrusted to Prospector Whelgar, stationed at an excavation site near Menethil Harbor. Archaeologist Flagongut, reviewing the collected finds, realizes that unlocking the mysterious powers within the fossils requires a key artifact: the Stone of Relu.",sp=0},{t="Lost to the Marshes",b="Before Flagongut could rendezvous with Whelgar, a pack of mottled raptors ambushed his caravan along the road, devouring the Stone of Relu. To piece the mystery together, Flagongut requires an adventurer to hunt down the predatory beasts, recover the ingested stone, and retrieve the original fossil from Whelgar's camp. With both fossils and the key assembled, the dwarven researchers hope to uncover the relics' true origin and power.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is a Darkshore quest ending in the Wetlands?",a="The Explorers' League maintains active operations across both Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Prospector Remtravel sent his archaeological discoveries from Darkshore across the sea to colleagues stationed in the Wetlands, connecting the two dig sites through shared research.",al={"why wetlands darkshore quest","menethil harbor connection","why send to wetlands"}},{q="What is the Stone of Relu?",a="The Stone of Relu is an ancient relic recovered by Archaeologist Flagongut. He believes it acts as a cipher or catalyst capable of unlocking the dormant magical secrets preserved inside the fossils excavated in Darkshore and the Wetlands.",al={"stone of relu","what is relu stone","relu artifact"}},{q="Who is Archaeologist Flagongut?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut is an operative of the dwarven Explorers' League based in Menethil Harbor. He studies ancient relics recovered from surrounding excavations and works closely with Prospectors Remtravel and Whelgar to decipher titan remnants.",al={"flagongut","who is flagongut"}},{q="Who has the original fossil?",a="The fossil discovered by Remtravel in Darkshore was transported to Prospector Whelgar, who keeps camp at an excavation site in the southern hills of the Wetlands.",al={"where is the fossil","who has remtravel fossil","whelgar fossil"}},{q="Why do raptors have the Stone of Relu?",a="While traveling the Wetlands road to consult with Prospector Whelgar, Flagongut was ambushed by mottled raptors. In the chaos of the attack, one of the predatory beasts swallowed the stone whole.",al={"raptor swallowed relic","why raptors have stone"}},{q="What do the dwarves expect the fossils to do?",a="The Explorers' League believes ancient fossils from the dawn of Azeroth hold latent titan energies and forgotten history, which can be awakened and translated using specialized relic stones like the Stone of Relu.",al={"fossil power","what does the fossil do"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The quest chain exemplifies the core mission of the Explorers' League, linking remote dig sites across continents to piece together dwarven heritage and the mysteries of the Titans.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance couriers and adventurers frequently bridge the maritime divide between the night elven lands of Darkshore and the dwarven settlements around Menethil Harbor."},kw={"darkshore","explorers league","flagongut","fossil","menethil","remtravel","stone of relu","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-flagongut","npc:prospector-whelgar","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Archaeologist Flagongut",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=943},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (5)"}}
E["quest:944"] = {t="quest",n="The Master's Glaive",z="darkshore",s="This quest sends Alliance adventurers south across Darkshore to scout the eerie Master's Glaive on behalf of the ancient of lore, Onu. The goal is to investigate whether the sinister Twilight's Hammer cult has infiltrated the remains of the fallen ancient horror.",h="This quest sends Alliance adventurers south across Darkshore to scout the eerie Master's Glaive on behalf of...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Presence",b="While investigating the lingering corruption and displaced wildlife along Darkshore, the ancient of lore Onu notices alarming clues. The naga along the coast are troubled enough, but the presence of the Twilight's Hammer cult is far more ominous. This fanatic sect does not worship ordinary dark powers; they venerate the ancient, primal lords of the world who were overthrown in ages past.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Lord",b="Southward lies the Master's Glaive, a grim excavation centered around a colossal creature impaled by an immense stone weapon. Onu provides a Phial of Scrying and tasks scouts with entering the pit to confirm if the cultists have gathered there. As Onu warns, even though the impaled behemoth has been dead for eons, slivers of its ancient, corruptive power still linger within its bones—a prize the Twilight's Hammer cannot resist.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this mission?",a="The quest is given by Onu, a venerable ancient of lore stationed along the road in southern Darkshore near the Grove of the Ancients.",al={"quest giver","who gives the masters glaive quest","start npc"}},{q="What is the Master's Glaive?",a="The Master's Glaive is an ancient site in southern Darkshore where a monstrous ancient lord fell eons ago, impaled through its skull by a titanic stone glaive. Its massive petrified skeleton remains embedded in the earth.",al={"what is masters glaive","lore of masters glaive","giant skull in darkshore"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer cult interested in the site?",a="The Twilight's Hammer worships the old, dark powers of ancient Azeroth. Even though the titanic creature impaled at the glaive is long dead, dormant traces and slivers of its primeval power remain within its remains, which the cultists desperately seek to harness.",al={"twilight cult darkshore","why are twilight cultists here","twilights hammer masters glaive"}},{q="How do I report back to Onu?",a="You do not need to walk all the way back to Onu's physical location. Once you explore the excavation pit of the Master's Glaive, use the Phial of Scrying in your bags to conjure a Scrying Bowl on the ground, allowing you to speak directly with Onu via magic.",al={"where to turn in quest","how to use scrying phial","scrying bowl"}},{q="What follows this scout mission?",a="After you use the Scrying Bowl to confirm the cultists' presence, Onu immediately directs you toward their encampment in the quest 'The Twilight Camp' to uncover further details about their activities.",al={"next quest","followup to masters glaive"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the Master's Glaive is a stark reminder of primeval terrors that predated their civilization, and seeing mad cultists trespass upon Darkshore's sacred soil is an intolerable defilement.",["class:Druid"]="Druids answer Onu's call to understand how the ancient, dormant taint buried deep within the earth is disturbing the surrounding land and its wildlife.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance forces in Darkshore must keep the Twilight's Hammer from awakening ancient horrors that could overrun the struggling settlements of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"darkshore","master's glaive","old lord","onu","phial of scrying","scrying bowl","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:master-s-glaive","quest:948","quest:949","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:darkshore","topic:naga"},m={start="Onu",["end"]="Scrying Bowl",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=944},src={"The Master's Glaive (quest)"}}
E["quest:947"] = {t="quest",n="Cave Mushrooms",z="darkshore",s="Cave Mushrooms is an Alliance assignment offered by the night elf Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine. While formulating a specialized potion, Barithras tasks an adventurer with venturing into a hidden cavern behind Cliffspring Falls to harvest rare fungi and verify disturbing premonitions felt by the Grove of the Ancients.",h="Cave Mushrooms is an Alliance assignment offered by the night elf Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Recipe Behind the Falls",b="Barithras Moonshade requires specific ingredients for a potent mixture: scaber stalks and an elusive death cap. These particular fungi thrive in the damp, shadowy cavern concealed directly behind Cliffspring Falls in northeastern Darkshore. While the alchemy itself is delicate, gathering these specimens is far more hazardous than harvesting typical woodland herbs.",sp=0},{t="The Ancients' Warning",b="Barithras did not avoid the cavern out of mere idleness. The venerable tree guardians at the Grove of the Ancients issued stern warnings, sensing that a foul presence had begun nesting inside the mountain caves. By sending a hardy explorer rather than investigating himself, Moonshade seeks to confirm whether the elders' dire intuitions about a creeping evil in northern Darkshore are indeed well founded.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this task begin?",a="You receive this assignment from Barithras Moonshade, who resides in the night elf coastal settlement of Auberdine in central Darkshore.",al={"where to pick up cave mushrooms","barithras moonshade location","cave mushrooms quest start"}},{q="Where are the mushrooms located?",a="They grow inside a cavern hidden behind Cliffspring Falls, situated along the mountain face to the northeast of Auberdine.",al={"where are scaber stalks","death cap location","cave behind waterfall darkshore"}},{q="Why won't Barithras Moonshade retrieve the mushrooms himself?",a="Barithras was specifically advised by the Grove of the Ancients to stay clear of the falls. The great ancients sensed that an unnatural, rising evil has taken refuge inside that cave.",al={"why barithras won't go","why barithras stays in auberdine"}},{q="What specific mushrooms are needed?",a="Moonshade needs five scaber stalks along with a single, highly dangerous death cap mushroom to complete his potion.",al={"required mushrooms","which fungi for moonshade"}},{q="What does this errand lead to next?",a="Once the presence in the cave is verified and the fungi delivered, the journey turns south toward the ancient protector Onu at the Grove of the Ancients.",al={"next quest after cave mushrooms","onu follow up"}},{q="Are the Ancients' fears proven correct?",a="Yes. Upon returning the specimens, the adventurer confirms the dark foreboding of the elders, proving that a sinister force has indeed claimed the mountain cavern.",al={"is the cave actually evil","what is in cliffspring falls cave"},sp=1}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Foragers and herbalists will appreciate the hunt for the death cap and scaber stalks, though these specific specimens dwell in darkened caverns rather than lush woodland soil.",["race:NightElf"]="The Grove of the Ancients remains deeply attuned to the natural balance of Darkshore, making any disturbance they detect beneath the falls a matter of urgent concern to the Kaldorei.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the Alliance's primary bastion on the Kalimdor coast, and creeping evils in the eastern mountains directly endanger the stability of the entire shore."},kw={"auberdine","barithras moonshade","cave mushrooms","cliffspring falls","darkshore","death cap","grove of the ancients","onu","scaber stalks"},rel={"npc:barithras-moonshade","subzone:cliffspring-falls","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:952"},m={start="Barithras Moonshade",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=947},src={"Cave Mushrooms"}}
E["quest:948"] = {t="quest",n="Onu",z="darkshore",s="This errand directs travelers from Auberdine south toward the Grove of the Ancients to consult with Onu. Having investigated the strange fungal growth deep within Cliffwater Falls, your findings have drawn the urgent attention of one of Darkshore's oldest guardians.",h="This errand directs travelers from Auberdine south toward the Grove of the Ancients to consult with Onu.",sec={{t="A Summons from the Ancients",b="After returning to Auberdine with fungal samples from the depths of Cliffwater Falls, Barithras Moonshade realizes that the implications stretch far beyond mere botanical curiosity. Word of the tainted caverns travels quickly to Onu, an Ancient of Lore rooted in the tranquil sanctuary of the Grove of the Ancients south of town. Patient and ponderous though the ancient treants are by nature, Onu's immediate desire for counsel signals that the corruption running through Darkshore's waterways may touch upon ancient, unsettling powers.",sp=0},{t="Journey to the Grove",b="Following the southern road out of Auberdine leads away from the coastal ruins and inland toward the mountain slopes. The Grove of the Ancients serves as an ancestral redoubt of nature, largely sheltered from the creeping decay that plagues the shoreline. Here, Onu waits among towering stone barrows and kindred spirits, preparing to direct allies toward deeper, more terrifying blights stirring at the edge of the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Onu?",a="Onu is an Ancient of Lore, a colossal, sapient tree-guardian dedicated to gathering and preserving knowledge. He presides over the Grove of the Ancients nestled in southern Darkshore, offering wisdom and guidance to defenders of the land.",al={"who is onu","onu identity","what is onu"}},{q="Why does Onu want to speak with me?",a="You recently ventured into the caverns beneath Cliffwater Falls to gather fungal samples for Barithras Moonshade. The peculiar nature of what was uncovered there alarmed the naturalists, prompting Onu to request an audience to address the growing corruption.",al={"why onu summons","reason for talk","why go to onu"}},{q="Where is the Grove of the Ancients?",a="The Grove of the Ancients lies south of Auberdine, nestled along the foothills of the eastern mountain range. Follow the main road south through Darkshore and head east toward the mountain slopes to find Onu.",al={"onu location","where is grove of the ancients","how to find onu"}},{q="What kind of creature is an Ancient of Lore?",a="Ancients of Lore are ancient treant beings allied with the night elves and the Cenarion Circle. Revered for their deep wisdom and memory, they serve as living repositories of nature magic and historical secrets.",al={"ancient of lore","what creature is onu","treant vs ancient"}},{q="Why is Onu's summons considered urgent?",a="Ancients are known for their deliberate, unhurried demeanor, rarely acting in haste. As Barithras Moonshade notes, if a being as patient and methodical as Onu actively calls for your counsel, the threat to Darkshore must be severe.",al={"why urgent","is onu worried","barithras warning"}},{q="What comes after meeting with Onu?",a="Upon greeting you at the Grove of the Ancients, Onu enlists your aid in investigating a far darker threat situated further south along the coast: the ominous excavation taking place around the Master's Glaive.",al={"next quest after onu","what happens next","where does onu send you"},sp=1}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Ancients of Lore are sacred partners to the Kaldorei, having guided your people since before the Sundering. Answering Onu's call is a solemn duty to preserve the sanctity of Darkshore.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold the Ancients in deep reverence as manifestations of nature's wisdom. Investigating strange cavern growths at Onu's behest aligns directly with the duties of the Cenarion Circle.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers helping secure Darkshore, gaining the trust and insight of the regional ancients is crucial to navigating Kalimdor's mysterious northern wilderness."},kw={"ancient of lore","auberdine","barithras moonshade","cliffwater falls","darkshore","grove of the ancients","onu"},rel={"npc:barithras-moonshade","quest:947","zone:darkshore","quest:952"},m={start="Barithras Moonshade",["end"]="Onu",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=948},src={"Onu (quest)"}}
E["quest:949"] = {t="quest",n="The Twilight Camp",z="darkshore",s="The Twilight Camp is an Alliance reconnaissance mission directed at the secretive cultists encamped around the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore. Having caught a glimpse of their ritual site through a scrying bowl, investigators must infiltrate the excavation to uncover what the Twilight's Hammer seeks to unearth.",h="The Twilight Camp is an Alliance reconnaissance mission directed at the secretive cultists encamped around...",sec={{t="Probing the Dig",b="The Master's Glaive has long stood as an ominous, petrified mystery along the craggy hills of southern Darkshore, but the sudden arrival of the Twilight's Hammer cult transformed an ancient curiosity into an active threat. After using a scrying bowl to peer into their fortifications, scouts are sent into the thick of their camp to determine their true designs before defensive measures can be enacted.",sp=0},{t="The Illustrated Tome",b="Scouring the encampment reveals that the cultists are not mere scavengers or bandits; their operation is guided by deep, occult study. Deep within their northern camp rests an ancient, meticulously hand-printed tome illustrated with masterful yet unsettling artwork. This text serves as proof that the Twilight's Hammer is deliberately investigating the colossal entity buried beneath the earth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the goal of The Twilight Camp quest?",a="You must infiltrate the Twilight's Hammer encampment near the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore and recover a clue detailing their motives—specifically a hand-printed ritual book resting within their camp.",al={"twilight camp quest objective","what do i do twilight camp"}},{q="Who sends you to investigate the camp?",a="The quest is received directly from the Scrying Bowl at the overlook above the Master's Glaive, continuing the investigation initiated on behalf of the ancient protector Onu.",al={"who gives twilight camp","twilight camp quest giver"}},{q="Where is the clue found in the camp?",a="The valid clue is the Twilight Tome situated in the northern part of the encampment. Other tomes in the camp can be dangerous decoys that unleash warding magic against intruders.",al={"where is the book","twilight tome location","find clue twilight camp"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer at the Master's Glaive?",a="The cultists are obsessed with ancient, dark powers of the Old Gods and their servants. They are excavating the massive petrified carcass pinned by the giant stone blade to study or awaken whatever ancient evil remains there.",al={"why are cultists at masters glaive","twilights hammer darkshore purpose"}},{q="What happens after finding the tome?",a="Recovering the tome leads to the quest Return to Onu, instructing you to carry the discovered writings north to the ancient treant in the Grove of the Ancients.",al={"next quest after twilight camp","where to go after twilight tome"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Twilight's Hammer defiles sacred Kalimdor lands with dark sorceries right beneath the boughs of Darkshore's ancient groves.",["class:Druid"]="Uncovering the cult's research is critical for Cenarion wardens seeking to keep corrupting ancient entities safely buried.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stopping the cult's strange excavations prevents a gathering threat from destabilizing northern Kalimdor."},kw={"darkshore","master's glaive","onu","scrying bowl","twilight camp","twilight tome","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:944","quest:950","subzone:master-s-glaive","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Scrying Bowl",["end"]="Twilight Tome",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=949},src={"The Twilight Camp"}}
E["quest:950"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Onu",z="darkshore",s="Return to Onu is an Alliance quest concluding an initial investigation into the cultists encamped along the coast of Darkshore. After raiding the cultists' encampment and attempting to read the Twilight Tome, an adventurer recovers a single page of maddening scribbles to deliver to the ancient treant Onu in the Grove of the Ancients.",h="Return to Onu is an Alliance quest concluding an initial investigation into the cultists encamped along the...",sec={{t="A Glimpse into Madness",b="Upon discovering the Twilight Tome within the Twilight's Hammer encampment, anyone peering into its leaves suffers an immediate assault on the senses. The written text swims and dances across the parchment, and once-ornate scrollwork morphs into grotesque figures. The mental strain is so overwhelming that ripping free a single page of scribbled notes is all a mortal mind can endure before succumbing to vertigo.",sp=0},{t="Ancient Suspicions",b="When delivered to Onu, the towering treant recognizes the unnatural aura suffusing the scrap. The parchment radiates a chaotic, primal magic that Onu attributes directly to the work of the ancient, shadowy forces buried beneath the earth. While the scribblings are difficult to decipher, they confirm that the presence of the Twilight's Hammer in Darkshore is not mere banditry, but part of a deeper, blasphemous design.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the page taken from the Twilight Tome?",a="The page, known simply as Insane Scribbles, is a torn leaf from the cult's sacred book. Looking upon it causes severe mental distress, as the script twists into grotesque, shifting patterns tied to primeval void magic.",al={"insane scribbles","what are the scribbles","twilight tome page"}},{q="Who is Onu?",a="Onu is an Ancient of Lore rooted in the Grove of the Ancients in southern Darkshore. He acts as an elder guardian and scholar, guiding night elves and Alliance allies against emerging corruptions in the forest.",al={"who is onu","onu darkshore","treant onu"}},{q="What does Onu learn from the scribbles?",a="Onu senses chaotic, primal energies emanating from the page, identifying the influence of ancient, malevolent entities. The writings suggest the Twilight's Hammer cultists are actively pursuing relic sites and buried powers across Darkshore.",al={"what did onu find","meaning of scribbles"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer in Darkshore?",a="The cult is drawn to Darkshore to excavate ruined elven sites and uncover vestiges of ancient power linked to primeval darkness and the Old Gods, using the chaos of the land to mask their rites.",al={"cultists in darkshore","why twilight hammer here"}},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Following the discovery of the cult's presence, Onu turns attention toward the ancient elven ruins of Mathystra to the north, directing adventurers to secure ancient relics before the cultists can seize them.",al={"what quest is next","next after return to onu"},sp=1},{q="Why does reading the tome cause dizziness?",a="The Twilight Tome is inscribed with dark, maddening magic of void and chaos. The glyphs actively bewilder mortal minds, causing hallucinations and swoons to prevent outsiders from unraveling their secrets.",al={"why dizziness tome","twilight tome effects"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of Darkshore's shores by dark cultists threatens the balance guarded by the Ancients of Lore, making Onu's warnings deeply personal for the kaldorei.",["class:Druid"]="The chaotic, unnatural resonance of the scribbles represents an affront to the natural order that druids serve to preserve alongside treants like Onu.",["faction:Alliance"]="Investigating cult activity along Darkshore's coastline ensures that night elf settlements like Auberdine remain secure against hidden threats."},kw={"darkshore","grove of the ancients","insane scribbles","old ones","onu","twilight tome","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:949","quest:948","quest:951","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Twilight Tome",["end"]="Onu",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=950},src={"Return to Onu"}}
E["quest:951"] = {t="quest",n="Mathystra Relics",z="darkshore",s="This quest sends Alliance adventurers north along the coast of Darkshore to sift through the overgrown Ruins of Mathystra. Onu, an Ancient of Lore rooted in the Grove of the Ancients, seeks these ancient kaldorei artifacts to understand how the Twilight's Hammer cult is manipulating night elven sorcery for their sinister rites.",h="This quest sends Alliance adventurers north along the coast of Darkshore to sift through the overgrown Ruins...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Discovery",b="After adventurers recovered a tainted parchment from the cultists lurking around the colossal monument known as the Master's Glaive, Onu deciphered a disturbing revelation. The text was not native cult scripture, but a cursed fragment of ancient night elven writing. Tainted by the Twilight's Hammer, the parchment revealed that these apocalyptic zealots are harnessing forgotten elven magic to awaken or summon their ancient masters back into the mortal world.",sp=1},{t="The Fallen Bastion",b="To counteract this dark endeavor, Onu directs heroes to the Ruins of Mathystra, located along the northeastern shores of Darkshore. Long ago, Mathystra was a shining bastion of highborne civilization before it shattered during the Sundering. Though the city has collapsed into rubble, weeds, and naga infestation, powerful remnants of its original arcane and spiritual enchantments linger in shattered urns and ancient relics scattered across the stone foundations.",sp=0},{t="Divining Dark Designs",b="By collecting surviving artifacts from the ruin's grassy debris, defenders of Darkshore hope to unravel the specific techniques the cultists intend to exploit. Onu studies the residual magic imbued within the relics, racing against time to decipher the cult's plans before the Twilight's Hammer can fully bend ancient kaldorei sorcery toward freeing their subterranean masters.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the Mathystra Relics?",a="They are fragments of enchanted pottery, urns, and artifacts left behind in the Ruins of Mathystra. Created during the height of ancient night elven civilization prior to the Great Sundering, they still hum with lingering magical energy.",al={"what are the relics","mathystra relic lore","elven relics mathystra"}},{q="Why does Onu want these relics?",a="Onu discovered that the Twilight's Hammer cult is using ancient elven magic to try and bring their dark masters back into the world. By studying intact relics from Mathystra, Onu hopes to understand how the cult intends to manipulate that ancient power.",al={"why does onu want relics","purpose of mathystra relics"}},{q="Where were the Ruins of Mathystra located?",a="The ruins sit along the northeastern coastline of Darkshore, just north of the Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran ruins, and south of the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"where is mathystra","mathystra location"}},{q="Who is the Twilight's Hammer trying to bring back?",a="The cult is dedicated to ancient, malevolent entities deep beneath the earth and sea—often associated with the giant slain monstrosity buried at the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore.",al={"who are twilight hammer masters","cult masters darkshore"}},{q="What was Mathystra before it became a ruin?",a="Mathystra was once a great bastion and city of the night elves thousands of years ago. It fell into ruin during the Great Sundering and has since been overrun by wilderness, ghosts, and vile beach-dwelling creatures like the naga.",al={"history of mathystra","what was mathystra"}},{q="Who gives the quest 'Mathystra Relics'?",a="The quest is provided by Onu, an ancient treant rooted at the Grove of the Ancients in south-central Darkshore, following the investigation of the Master's Glaive.",al={"who starts mathystra relics","quest giver mathystra relics"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, seeing relics of their pre-Sundering glory dug out of the dirt is a somber reminder of their civilization's fall—and an alarming warning that their ancestors' potent arts are being exploited by apocalyptic madmen.",["class:Druid"]="Aiding Onu allows druids to serve one of nature's greatest elder sentinels, safeguarding the ancient history of Darkshore from being twisted by dark cultists.",["faction:Alliance"]="Preventing the Twilight's Hammer from weaponizing ancient magic is essential to securing northern Kalimdor against dark, subterranean forces."},kw={"darkshore","grove of the ancients","master's glaive","mathystra","onu","relics","ruins of mathystra","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","quest:948","quest:952","subzone:master-s-glaive","quest:944","topic:twilight-s-hammer","quest:950","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Onu",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=951},src={"Mathystra Relics"}}
E["quest:953"] = {t="quest",n="The Fall of Ameth'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade tasks adventurers with exploring the haunting ruins of Ameth'Aran in Darkshore to decipher ancient stone tablets. These inscriptions record the tragedy and ruin that struck the Highborne city during the Sundering. The gathered knowledge is intended for the Circle of Ancients in Auberdine, recovering history largely lost during the War of the Ancients.",h="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade tasks adventurers with exploring the haunting ruins of Ameth'Aran in Darkshore to...",sec={{t="Echoes of the Highborne",b="Long before the coast fractured into the misty expanse of Darkshore, Ameth'Aran stood as a flourishing settlement where Queen Azshara's elite sorcerers practiced powerful arcane magic. Following the cataclysmic destruction of the Well of Eternity ten thousand years ago, the city was reduced to broken marble and cracked pillars. Today, it remains haunted by the restless, anguished spirits of the Highborne who died when their golden age tore apart.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering Lost Chronicles",b="Because the War of the Ancients plunged the night elf civilization into chaotic survival, remarkably few written accounts survived the Great Sundering intact. Sentinel Tysha Moonblade attempted to survey the ruins herself, discovering two large engraved tablets—the Lay of Ameth'Aran and the Fall of Ameth'Aran—before ghostly Highborne specters forced her to retreat. Retrieving these readings ensures that the historical truths of the ancient disaster reach the scholars of the Circle of Ancients in Auberdine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Ameth'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran is an ancient night elf ruin located in central Darkshore. Ten thousand years ago, it was a city where Queen Azshara's Highborne nobility openly wielded and studied grand arcane magic before it fell during the Great Sundering.",al={"ametharan lore","what was ameth aran","who lived in ameth aran"}},{q="Why are there ghosts in Ameth'Aran?",a="The restless ghosts haunting the ruins are the spirits of the Highborne who lived and died there. Caught in the sudden, violent catastrophe that shattered the Well of Eternity and fragmented Kalimdor, their spirits remain bound to the ruins in eternal torment.",al={"why are there spirits in ameth aran","ameth aran ghosts","restless highborne"}},{q="Who is Sentinel Tysha Moonblade?",a="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade is a night elf sentinel stationed along the road in Darkshore. She was tasked with scouting ancient sites and recovering lost historical records for the Circle of Ancients in Auberdine.",al={"tysha moonblade","who gives fall of ameth aran"}},{q="Why does the Circle of Ancients want these tablets read?",a="The destruction of the Well of Eternity plunged Kalimdor into immense upheaval, obliterating countless libraries and monuments. Because so few written records survived the War of the Ancients, the tablets provide rare firsthand accounts of the Sundering from the perspective of the Highborne.",al={"why read the tablets","circle of ancients tablets","lay of ameth aran meaning"}},{q="Where are the tablets located?",a="The two large tablets—the Lay of Ameth'Aran and the Fall of Ameth'Aran—are etched into standing stone monuments nestled among the ruined courtyards of Ameth'Aran, surrounded by the wandering ghosts of the city's former residents.",al={"where are the ameth aran tablets","tablet locations","how to read ameth aran"}},{q="What happened to the Highborne of Ameth'Aran during the Sundering?",a="When the Well of Eternity imploded at the climax of the War of the Ancients, massive tremors and arcane backlash tore Kalimdor apart. Ameth'Aran collapsed in the ruin, burying its citizens and leaving their ghosts lingering in the rubble.",al={"how did ameth aran fall","ameth aran destruction"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The ruins of Ameth'Aran are a grim reminder of your ancestors' hubris under Queen Azshara and the catastrophic consequences of unregulated arcane sorcery.",["class:Mage"]="The tablets offer a sobering glimpse into the heights of pre-Sundering elven spellcraft and the terrible ruin brought on when that power spiraled out of control.",["faction:Alliance"]="Aiding the Sentinels in securing the history of Darkshore helps preserve crucial lore for the night elf leaders guiding the Alliance on Kalimdor."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","azshara","circle of ancients","darkshore","highborne","sundering","tablets","tysha moonblade"},rel={"subzone:ameth-aran","npc:sentinel-tysha-moonblade","zone:darkshore","topic:highborne","topic:war-of-the-ancients","subzone:auberdine"},m={start="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=953},src={"The Fall of Ameth'Aran (quest)"}}
E["quest:954"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Perched upon a bluff in the overrun ruins of Bashal'Aran, an unearthly blue aura repels the demonic satyrs and vicious grells that infest the ancient night elven city. The Sentinel scout Thundris Windweaver sends adventurers to investigate the source of this untouched sanctuary. Reaching the site reveals the lingering spirit of Asterion, an ancient highborne presence yearning for civil company.",h="Perched upon a bluff in the overrun ruins of Bashal'Aran, an unearthly blue aura repels the demonic satyrs...",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Ruins",b="Bashal'Aran once stood as a glorious settlement of the ancient Kaldorei Empire, but its broken marble and overgrown arches now teem with demonic taint. Twisted satyrs and corrupt grells feed greedily upon the lingering magical energies of the ruins, their malice swelling with every passing day. Yet despite their predatory dominion, Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine spotted a curious curiosity: atop a western bluff in the ruins, an ethereal blue aura burns pure, keeping every demon and sprite at bay.",sp=0},{t="The Wounded Shade",b="Braving the demonic patrols to reach the elevated shrine reveals that the warding light is no natural phenomenon. It emanates from Asterion, an ancient spirit whose vigil has persisted through centuries of solitude. Surrounded by howling beasts and vile fiends, the weary shade views even a traveling stranger as a welcome respite from decades of isolation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the blue aura located?",a="The blue aura shines atop a small raised bluff on the western edge of the ruins of Bashal'Aran, just east of Auberdine in Darkshore. It sits slightly elevated above the surrounding crumbling walls.",al={"find blue aura","where is asterion","bashal'aran shrine location"}},{q="Why do the satyrs avoid the shrine?",a="The shrine is protected by a warding blue aura projected by the ancient spirit Asterion, whose lingering magic repels the demonic satyrs and corrupt grells that otherwise infest the ruins.",al={"why demons afraid","why satyrs stay away"}},{q="Who sends you on this quest?",a="Thundris Windweaver, an elven scout stationed in Auberdine, provides the quest after observing the unnatural demonic movements within the eastern ruins.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver","thundris windweaver location"}},{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is an ancient night elf shade bound to a shrine in Bashal'Aran. Long separated from civilized society, he endures surrounded by hostile demonic beasts while maintaining the site's protective barrier.",al={"who is the ghost","asterion lore"}},{q="What is Bashal'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran is an ancient kaldorei ruin nestled in the forests of Darkshore. Sacked during the ancient Sundering, it has become infested with magical parasites, grells, and satyrs seeking to feast on its dormant ley powers.",al={"what happened to bashal'aran","history of bashal'aran"}},{q="Does this quest chain continue?",a="Yes. Upon speaking to Asterion, he enlists your help to strike back against the surrounding satyrs and grells to aid his lingering spirit.",al={"next quest","what comes after bashal'aran"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Bashal'Aran is a somber reminder of what was lost during the Sundering, where your ancient kin's lingering shades still hold lonely vigils against encroaching demonic corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine's scouts rely on Alliance wanderers to push into Darkshore's contested ruins and neutralize demonic threats before they reach the coast."},kw={"asterion","bashal'aran","blue aura","darkshore","grell","kaldorei ruins","satyr","thundris windweaver"},rel={"npc:asterion","quest:4761","topic:satyr","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",["end"]="Asterion",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=954},src={"Bashal'Aran (quest)"}}
E["quest:955"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Asterion, a sorrowful highborne ghost haunting the ancient ruins of Bashal'Aran, seeks a way to undo the binding magic that tethers his spectral form. Believing the mischievous local grells have touched the seal holding him, he tasks travelers with gathering their earrings to trace its lingering magical resonance.",h="Asterion, a sorrowful highborne ghost haunting the ancient ruins of Bashal'Aran, seeks a way to undo the...",sec={{t="A Centuries-Old Torment",b="Amid the shattered marble of Bashal'Aran lingers Asterion, an ancient night elf spirit who has endured centuries of confinement. Trapped between life and true death, his existence has dwindled into an agonizing wait under the canopy of Darkshore. Bound directly to the ruined settlement by arcane craft, Asterion lacks the means to dispel his shackles alone, his mind worn thin by uncounted years of solitude and despair.",sp=0},{t="Traces in the Wild",b="Asterion suspects that the key to his release is an ancient seal hidden somewhere in the ruins. While he cannot physically scour the brush and collapsed stones himself, the feral grells infesting Bashal'Aran constantly forage and steal small baubles. Asterion asks travelers to collect the earrings worn by these creatures, intending to read the residual magical impressions on the trinkets and locate the seal that holds his soul in torment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is an ancient night elf ghost bound to the ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore. Trapped for centuries by a mystical seal, he has watched the ages pass in torment while longing for release from his spectral state.",al={"asterion lore","who is the ghost in bashal'aran","asterion quest giver"}},{q="Why does Asterion want grell earrings?",a="Grells are notorious scavengers that hoard shiny trinkets and jewelry. Asterion believes the creatures have handled the magical seal that binds him, meaning their worn earrings may carry enough magical residue to help him locate it.",al={"why grell earrings","grell earring purpose","earrings quest darkshore"}},{q="What is Bashal'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran is an ancient night elf ruin located along the forested coast of Darkshore, dating back to before the Great Sundering. It is overrun by wild grells, satyrs, and spectral remnants of its long-fallen inhabitants.",al={"what is bashal'aran","bashal'aran history","ruins of bashal'aran"}},{q="What happens after collecting the earrings?",a="Asterion examines the earrings and senses that while the grells do not carry the seal itself, they have brushed against it in what he considers relatively recent times. This trace allows him to narrow down its location within the ruins.",al={"what do the earrings show","did the grells have the seal","grell earring result"},sp=1},{q="Why is Asterion trapped here?",a="Asterion was bound to Bashal'Aran by an ancient magical seal created centuries ago. The binding anchors his spirit to the physical site of the ruins, preventing him from moving on to a peaceful rest.",al={"who bound asterion","how is asterion bound","asterion's seal"}},{q="What are grells?",a="Grells are small, malicious woodland creatures native to Kalimdor's forests. Known for their mischievous nature, sharp claws, and love of trinkets, they frequently infest old ruins and attack passing travelers.",al={"what is a grell","grells lore","darkshore grells"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, encountering Asterion is a sobering reminder of the ancient civilization that fell during the Sundering, leaving tortured souls bound in ruin for millennia.",["class:Mage"]="Asterion's method of using enchanted trinkets to trace residual magical emanations reflects ancient Highborne practices of arcane divination.",["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing out the chaotic grells around Bashal'Aran helps pacify the treacherous northern reaches of Darkshore for the Alliance."},kw={"asterion","bashal'aran","binding","darkshore","ghost","grell","grell earring","seal"},rel={"npc:asterion","zone:darkshore","quest:954","quest:99141"},m={start="Asterion",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=955},src={"Bashal'Aran (2)"}}
E["quest:956"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Asterion, a night elf spirit trapped amidst the ruined pillars of Bashal'Aran, seeks the relic holding him bound to this world. Having sensed the corruption of his prison among the local grells, he directs travelers to hunt the satyrs who command them and recover the Ancient Moonstone Seal.",h="Asterion, a night elf spirit trapped amidst the ruined pillars of Bashal'Aran, seeks the relic holding him...",sec={{t="A Prison of Ancient Stone",b="For well over a thousand years, the spirit Asterion has remained tethered to the fallen ruins of Bashal'Aran. The surrounding marble pillars serve as an unyielding cage that neither his fading spiritual strength nor his ancient magic can crack. Bound by a cursed relic, he has spent centuries staring out at Darkshore's mist-shrouded canopy, wondering whether even the erosion of the stone around him would grant him release.",sp=0},{t="Satyrs and the Moonstone Seal",b="After discovering that nearby grells bore traces of the magic maintaining his captivity, Asterion deduced that the source of the enchantment had fallen into the hands of the satyrs who direct the chaotic creatures. Wandering through the ancient groves, these demonic night elves keep a watchful grip on the Ancient Moonstone Seal. Reclaiming this talisman is the critical step toward shattering the invisible bars that anchor Asterion to his shrine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is an ancient night elf ghost trapped within the ruins of Bashal'Aran. Bound by ancient magic, he has spent more than a thousand years confined to the shrine's standing pillars, unable to pass on or wander beyond his stony prison.",al={"who is asterion","asterion lore","ghost in bashal aran"}},{q="Why do the satyrs have the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="Satyrs lead and influence the wild grells infesting northern Darkshore. Because the grells carried traces of the binding magic, Asterion realized that their wicked satyr masters had seized the Ancient Moonstone Seal to keep the local spirits tormented and tethered.",al={"why do satyrs have seal","satyr moonstone seal","ancient moonstone seal"}},{q="What happens once the seal is recovered?",a="Asterion takes hold of the very relic that has bound him for centuries. Recovering the Ancient Moonstone Seal is the penultimate step in his liberation, allowing the seal to be broken so he may finally walk the forests freely again.",al={"what does seal do","recovering the seal"},sp=1},{q="What is Bashal'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran is an ancient night elf ruin located along the mist-draped shores of northern Darkshore. Once a magnificent settlement or holy enclave, it now lies broken, plagued by grells, satyrs, and trapped spirits from an earlier age.",al={"bashal aran lore","what is bashal aran"}},{q="How long has Asterion been trapped here?",a="Asterion has been imprisoned for more than a thousand years. Without physical means or magic to dismantle the boundary, he was forced to wait through the centuries, wondering if he would ever be freed.",al={"how old is asterion","how long trapped"}},{q="Can Asterion simply walk away from the shrine?",a="No. The Ancient Moonstone Seal maintains a metaphysical barrier around the shrine. The stone pillars act as an impenetrable cage that prevents his spectral form from crossing beyond them.",al={"can asterion leave","why is ghost trapped"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Bashal'Aran is a somber reminder of your people's ancient past, where lingering ancestors remain chained to the earth by satyrs who embody the demonic betrayal of the Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="The twisted influence of the satyrs continues to corrupt Darkshore's wildlife and disturb ancient spirits who should be resting peacefully in the cycle of nature.",["faction:Alliance"]="Cleansing the ruins of Darkshore from satyr corruption secures Kalimdor's northern coast and aids the Kaldorei in laying their tragic past to rest."},kw={"ancient moonstone seal","asterion","bashal'aran","darkshore","grell","kaldorei","night elf ghost","satyr"},rel={"npc:asterion","quest:954","topic:satyr","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Asterion",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=956},src={"Bashal'Aran (3)"}}
E["quest:957"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="This quest tasks adventurers with helping the trapped spirit of Asterion in the ruins of Bashal'Aran. By carrying his binding seal south to the sister ruins of Ameth'Aran, adventurers seek a way to shatter his ancient bonds.",h="This quest tasks adventurers with helping the trapped spirit of Asterion in the ruins of Bashal'Aran.",sec={{t="A Prison of Ancient Sorcery",b="The spirit Asterion has lingered in Bashal'Aran for millennia, chained in death by an Ancient Moonstone Seal. Forged through the mighty sorceries of the Highborne caste before the Great Sundering, the seal cannot be shattered by mundane strength. Its destruction requires the specific magic of an ancient flame that still smolders amid the fallen stonework of Ameth'Aran to the south.",sp=0},{t="Twin Ruins of Darkshore",b="Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran were once vibrant sister settlements of the kaldorei civilization, back when Queen Azshara reigned and the Well of Eternity still anchored their empire. Today, both sites are overgrown, haunted ruins filled with lingering ghosts and volatile arcane energies. Within a stone gazebo in Ameth'Aran, a mystical brazier holding a cyan-hued fire offers the only power capable of consuming Asterion's binding relic.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance Awakens",b="With the seal destroyed, Asterion is finally unburdened, gazing upon a shattered Kalimdor vastly altered from the golden age he remembers. Yet his freedom does not bring him peace. Sensing that his former master and jailor, the Highborne Athrikus, still endures, Asterion's ancient despair quickly turns into a cold, burning hunger for revenge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is a night elf spirit trapped within the ruins of Bashal'Aran. He dates back ten thousand years to the reign of Queen Azshara, having been bound to the ruined city by his former Highborne master.",al={"asterion","who is the ghost","npc asterion"}},{q="Where do I destroy the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="The seal must be taken south to Ameth'Aran, the twin ruin of Bashal'Aran. Look for a stone gazebo sheltering a large cubical brazier that burns with an ancient, greenish-blue magical fire.",al={"where is the flame","ancient flame location","destroy seal"}},{q="What is the relationship between Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran?",a="They were sister cities of the ancient night elf empire before the Sundering. Both fell to devastation ten thousand years ago, leaving behind haunted stone pillars, residual arcane energies, and restless spirits.",al={"twin ruins","ametharan connection","bashalaran ametharan"}},{q="Who imprisoned Asterion?",a="Asterion was imprisoned by his former master, a powerful Highborne sorcerer named Athrikus. Upon being freed, Asterion senses that Athrikus somehow still survives in the world.",al={"who imprisoned asterion","who is athrikus","asterion master"},sp=1},{q="What era does Asterion remember?",a="Asterion last walked the world when the original Well of Eternity still existed, Queen Azshara ruled the empire, and the Highborne nobility held their majestic courts before the Sundering.",al={"asterion past","well of eternity era","how old is asterion"}},{q="Does freeing Asterion lay his spirit to rest?",a="No. Rather than crossing into peaceful rest, Asterion's sorrow turns toward retribution when he senses that Athrikus still lingers, prompting him to seek vengeance against his ancient captor.",al={"does asterion pass on","what happens to asterion","asterion after free"},sp=1}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of modern Kalimdor, freeing Asterion is a sober encounter with their people's pre-Sundering past and the lingering corruption of Queen Azshara's Highborne nobility.",["class:Mage"]="The durable enchantments binding Asterion and the surviving flames of Ameth'Aran offer a glimpse into the raw arcane power wielded by ancient Highborne sorcerers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing the ancient curses in Darkshore secures the borders for new night elf settlements pushing out from Auberdine."},kw={"ameth'aran","asterion","athrikus","azshara","bashal'aran","darkshore","highborne","moonstone seal"},rel={"npc:asterion","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:highborne","quest:954","zone:darkshore","zone:azshara"},m={start="Asterion",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=957},src={"Bashal'Aran (4)"}}
E["quest:960"] = {t="quest",n="Onu is meditating",z="darkshore",s="While investigating the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, the ancient of lore Onu enters a deep trance to contemplate the growing threat. Players who lose their mystical scrying phial can speak to the meditating ancient to receive a replacement. His thoughts center on the sinister alliance and motivations of the Twilight's Hammer cult and the serpentine naga.",h="While investigating the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, the ancient of lore Onu enters a deep trance...",sec={{t="A Mind in Deep Contemplation",b="Onu is an Ancient of Lore rooted in Darkshore's Grove of the Ancients, standing as a living repository of Kalimdor's history. When ominous reports surface concerning dark excavations at the Master's Glaive, Onu turns his immense consciousness inward. He meditates heavily on what could draw both the fanatic Twilight's Hammer cultists and the insidious naga to the petrified remains of an ancient behemoth. For adventurers carrying out his reconnaissance, he remains an accessible anchor, offering replacement scrying phials should theirs be misplaced in the wild.",sp=0},{t="Scrying the Depths",b="To monitor the ruins without risking the ancient's physical presence, Onu relies on nature-attuned divination. Adventurers are entrusted with a phial of scrying, meant to conjure a scrying bowl directly within the excavation site so Onu can commune from afar. Because the journey south through Darkshore is perilous and fraught with hostile wildlife and cultist patrols, Onu anticipates mishaps. His trance is not unbroken slumber, but an attentive vigil; he readily provides another vial of sacred waters to ensure the investigation of the Master's Glaive continues without delay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Onu meditating?",a="Onu is an ancient of lore pondering the disturbing presence of both the Twilight's Hammer cult and the naga at the Master's Glaive. He uses this meditation to perceive their motives and guide adventurers investigating the site.",al={"why is onu meditating","onu trance","what is onu doing"}},{q="What is the purpose of this interaction?",a="It serves as a safety mechanism for players on the quest 'The Master's Glaive'. If you lose, destroy, or prematurely use your Phial of Scrying, speaking to the meditating Onu provides you with a replacement phial so you can complete the ritual.",al={"lost phial of scrying","get another phial","onu replacement quest"}},{q="Where is Onu located?",a="Onu is rooted in the Grove of the Ancients, located in central-southern Darkshore, just off the main road.",al={"onu location","where to find onu"}},{q="What do I do with the Phial of Scrying?",a="You carry the phial south to the Master's Glaive and use it near the scrying bowl at the site. This allows Onu to magically communicate with you and observe the dark activities taking place around the ancient remains.",al={"how to use phial of scrying","scrying bowl darkshore","phial of scrying purpose"}},{q="What is the Master's Glaive?",a="The Master's Glaive is a massive, ancient excavation site in southern Darkshore where the colossal, petrified skull of a forgotten entity lies pierced by a gargantuan blade. Cultists and naga have converged there for unknown, malevolent purposes.",al={"what is masters glaive","monument in south darkshore"}},{q="Can Horde players interact with Onu here?",a="No. Onu is allied strictly with the night elves and the Alliance. Horde adventurers trespassing near the Grove of the Ancients will find Onu and his protectors hostile or uncooperative.",al={"is onu alliance only","horde onu meditating"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As stewards of Kalimdor's balance, night elves revere ancients of lore like Onu, relying on their ageless wisdom to interpret disturbances in the wilds of Darkshore.",["class:Druid"]="Druids share a profound natural bond with ancients of lore. Maintaining communication via scrying rituals reflects the Cenarion Circle's method of surveying tainted ground from a distance.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Darkshore from cultists and aquatic invaders is critical for Alliance travelers journeying between Teldrassil and Ashenvale."},kw={"darkshore","grove of the ancients","master's glaive","meditating","onu","phial of scrying","scrying bowl","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:944","quest:950","quest:948","subzone:master-s-glaive","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Onu",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=960},src={"Onu is meditating"}}
E["quest:963"] = {t="quest",n="For Love Eternal",z="darkshore",s="\"For Love Eternal\" is a tragic quest given by Cerellean Whiteclaw in Auberdine. Haunted by memories of his lost lover, Anaya Dawnrunner, Cerellean asks an adventurer to travel to the shattered ruins of Ameth'Aran to release her restless spirit from an eternity of torment.",h="\"For Love Eternal\" is a tragic quest given by Cerellean Whiteclaw in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Slumber Full of Grief",b="Ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients, the catastrophe surrounding the Well of Eternity tore ancient Kalimdor apart. Among the casualties was the city of Ameth'Aran, where Cerellean Whiteclaw lost his beloved, Anaya Dawnrunner. Stricken with despair, Cerellean followed Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage into the long hibernation of the druids, hoping the millennia spent walking the Emerald Dream would quiet his aching heart. Instead, his sorrow only lingered, following him through the ages.",sp=0},{t="The Ghost of Ameth'Aran",b="Upon awakening in recent times, Cerellean wandered through Darkshore in a stupor until his feet brought him back to the melancholy ruins of Ameth'Aran. There, wandering among the ancient stones, he beheld the tortured ghost of Anaya. Unable to bear raising a weapon against the woman he loved, he pleads with passing travelers to destroy her tormented manifestation, retrieve her pendant, and finally grant her troubled soul peace.",sp=0},{t="Parting Across the Veil",b="When Anaya's pendant is returned to Auberdine, a spectral remnant of Anaya appears before Cerellean one last time. Freed from the lingering anguish that bound her to the ruins, she shares a brief, silent goodbye before fading away into the ether, leaving the grieving druid to weep in bittersweet solace by the seaside.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Cerellean Whiteclaw?",a="Cerellean Whiteclaw is a night elf druid resting in Auberdine. After losing his beloved Anaya during the Sundering ten thousand years ago, he entered the long druidic hibernation alongside Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage, carrying his unhealed sorrow across millennia.",al={"cerellean whiteclaw","who gives for love eternal","cerellean lore"}},{q="Who was Anaya Dawnrunner?",a="Anaya Dawnrunner was a night elf who lived in the city of Ameth'Aran prior to the Great Sundering. She was killed when the city fell during the aftermath of the War of the Ancients, and her ghost has remained trapped in the ruins ever since.",al={"anaya dawnrunner","who is anaya","anaya darkshore"}},{q="Where is Anaya's spirit located?",a="Her spirit wanders among the ancient, ghost-infested ruins of Ameth'Aran, located in southern Darkshore east of the main road.",al={"anaya location","where is anaya dawnrunner","anaya's pendant location"}},{q="Why couldn't Cerellean free Anaya himself?",a="Despite the passage of ten thousand years, Cerellean's love for Anaya was so profound that he could not bear the heartbreak of raising his own hand or casting a spell against her apparition, even to end her suffering.",al={"why doesn't cerellean kill anaya","why cerellean asks for help"}},{q="What happened to Ameth'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran was an ancient night elven settlement destroyed ten millennia ago during the Sundering that followed the War of the Ancients. Its ruins in Darkshore remain thick with lingering ghosts and lingering arcane echoes.",al={"ameth'aran history","fall of ameth'aran","what is ameth'aran"}},{q="What happens when you return Anaya's pendant?",a="Returning Anaya's pendant to Cerellean in Auberdine causes Anaya's ghost to appear briefly before him. She shares a final, silent moment of closure before dissolving, leaving Cerellean alone by the shore with his grief.",al={"quest turn in anaya","cerellean ending","for love eternal ending"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Cerellean's fate reflects the personal cost paid by the druids who entered thousands of years of slumber at Shan'do Stormrage's side, only to find the waking world still marked by their ancient losses.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Darkshore, this tragic reunion is a poignant reminder of the enduring scars left behind by the Great Sundering and the fall of their ancient cities.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping Cerellean offers Alliance heroes a glimpse into the tragic, millennia-spanning lives of their night elven allies as they adjust to the waking world."},kw={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","anaya's pendant","auberdine","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","for love eternal","sundering"},rel={"npc:cerellean-whiteclaw","subzone:ameth-aran","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:shan-do"},m={start="Cerellean Whiteclaw",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=963},src={"For Love Eternal"}}
E["quest:9633"] = {t="quest",n="The Way to Auberdine",z="darkshore",s="The Way to Auberdine marks an essential diplomatic bridge connecting the remote western islands to Kalimdor's mainland. Carrying a letter of introduction from Huntress Kella Nightbow, travelers journey by vessel across the sea to deliver word of distant perils to Thundris Windweaver in Darkshore. This simple crossing formalizes a growing pact of mutual defense between the night elves and newfound allies.",h="The Way to Auberdine marks an essential diplomatic bridge connecting the remote western islands to Kalimdor's...",sec={{t="Crossing the Sea",b="For travelers emerging from the trials of the northern isles, the journey across the waters represents an entry into the broader Alliance theater. Huntress Kella Nightbow arranges passage from the island docks aboard the ferry bound for Darkshore. Carrying a sealed Letter of Introduction, the voyager is tasked with establishing contact with Thundris Windweaver, a respected night elf citizen of Auberdine. The voyage serves as both a diplomatic mission and an invitation to delve into the troubled wilderness of northern Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="A Legacy of Ancient Grounds",b="Upon receiving the letter, Thundris Windweaver reflects on the shared history binding the regions together. The islands of Azuremyst and Bloodmyst were long ago inhabited by the night elves, and the encroaching dangers faced by settlements there are no novelty to his people. Recognizing ancient adversaries, Thundris pledges that the community of Auberdine and the local Sentinels will offer whatever aid they can muster, ensuring that the isolated islanders do not stand alone against gathering threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the journey to Auberdine?",a="The journey begins with Huntress Kella Nightbow, a night elf sentinel stationed near the docks on Bloodmyst Isle. She entrusts travelers with a letter of introduction intended for her trusted friend across the water.",al={"who gives the way to auberdine","where do i get the quest","quest giver"}},{q="Who receives the letter in Auberdine?",a="The letter must be handed to Thundris Windweaver, a respected resident of Auberdine. He can be found in the town on the mainland coast of Darkshore, typically inside the large cross-shaped building situated just north of the town's primary docks.",al={"where do i turn this in","thundris windweaver location","turn in npc"}},{q="Why is this letter being sent to Auberdine?",a="The letter alerts the night elf leadership in Darkshore to the situation unfolding on the islands. It formalizes requests for aid on behalf of Anchorite Paetheus and appeals to historical ties, inviting mainland support against ancient shared foes.",al={"why send letter","purpose of the quest","what is the letter for"}},{q="How do you reach Darkshore from the docks?",a="Travelers wait on the dock near Huntress Kella Nightbow for the transport vessel sailing between the islands and Auberdine. Once boarded, the ship carries passengers directly across the sea into the harbor of Darkshore.",al={"how to get to auberdine","where is the boat","how do i cross the sea"}},{q="What connection do the night elves have to the western isles?",a="As Thundris Windweaver notes, the isles known as Azuremyst and Bloodmyst were ancient night elf territories long before the recent arrival of new allies. The threats currently menacing those shores are longstanding enemies the kaldorei have contested for generations.",al={"night elf connection to bloodmyst","azuremyst history","why do night elves care"}},{q="What happens after the letter is delivered?",a="Thundris Windweaver promises to confer with the local townspeople and the Sentinels to coordinate relief efforts and send word back to Anchorite Paetheus, opening up further journeys and duties throughout Darkshore for the adventurer.",al={"what comes next","follow up","after turn in"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This voyage cements early diplomatic and military cooperation, integrating newly arrived refugees and island outposts firmly into the fold of the Alliance.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the quest is a reminder of forgotten ancestral outposts in the misty western seas, now re-emerging with ancient evils that demand kaldorei vigilance."},kw={"anchorite paetheus","auberdine","boat","darkshore","dock","kella nightbow","letter of introduction","thundris windweaver"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","npc:huntress-kella-nightbow","quest:4761","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Huntress Kella Nightbow",["end"]="Thundris Windweaver",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=9633},src={"The Way to Auberdine"}}
E["quest:965"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="Charged with the defense of Auberdine, Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze suspects foul dealings at the ancient ruins to the north. She tasks adventurers with finding Balthule Shadowstrike, a scout dispatched to watch the enigmatic Tower of Althalaxx who has failed to report back on schedule.",h="Charged with the defense of Auberdine, Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze suspects foul dealings at the ancient ruins...",sec={{t="A Scout Unaccounted For",b="Auberdine's sentinels must remain ever watchful over Darkshore's creeping perils. Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze noticed suspicious activity stirring around the Tower of Althalaxx in the northern reaches of the forest. Unwilling to leave the town unprotected without clearer intelligence, she sent Balthule Shadowstrike to survey the ancient ruin. Days have passed without word from the scout, prompting Elissa to seek a willing traveler to journey north, locate Balthule, and ensure he has not met an untimely end.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Upon the Ruin",b="The road north from Auberdine crosses past ancient Kaldorei ruins and over the Cliffspring River before reaching the shadowy sprawl of the tower. Though cut off from sending word back to Auberdine, Balthule survived his initial surveillance. Upon being located in the surrounding woods, he confirms that Elissa's instincts were correct: dark and troubling developments are actively underway within the crumbling stone spire.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze?",a="Elissa Starbreeze is a night elf Sentinel stationed in Auberdine. She is charged with safeguarding the settlement from external threats across Darkshore and monitors regional dangers like the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"elissa starbreeze","who gives quest","auberdine questgiver"}},{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is a scout dispatched by Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze to spy on the mysterious activity surrounding the Tower of Althalaxx. He maintains a vigil outside the ruin to keep track of hostile forces.",al={"balthule","who is the scout","shadowstrike"}},{q="Where is the Tower of Althalaxx located?",a="The tower sits in northeastern Darkshore. Travelers can reach it by heading east out of Auberdine, following the northern road past Bashal'Aran, and crossing the bridge over the Cliffspring River until the spire comes into view.",al={"tower of althalaxx location","where is the tower","how to find althalaxx"}},{q="Why was a scout sent to the tower in the first place?",a="Strange and threatening activity was detected around the ruins. Rather than committing Auberdine's garrison blindly, Sentinel Elissa sent Balthule ahead to investigate the nature of the disturbance.",al={"why watch the tower","what is wrong at althalaxx","why sent balthule"}},{q="Why hasn't Balthule returned to Auberdine?",a="Balthule observed grave, troubling developments at the tower and lacked safe means to deliver his findings back to Auberdine without abandoning his vigil or risking interception.",al={"why balthule missing","is balthule trapped","why did balthule stay"}},{q="Does this quest chain continue?",a="Yes. Locating Balthule Shadowstrike begins a multi-part investigation into the dark forces occupying the Tower of Althalaxx and their sinister ambitions in Darkshore.",al={"is this a chain","what quest comes next","althalaxx chain"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The ruins of Althalaxx stand as a reminder of ancient Kalimdor's fallen highborne past, and preserving Auberdine from the corruption festering in those stones is a vital duty for night elf sentinels.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the Alliance's primary gateway into northern Kalimdor, making the defense of its surrounding roads and borders essential for all visiting allies."},kw={"althalaxx","auberdine","balthule shadowstrike","darkshore","elissa starbreeze","scout","sentinel","tower"},rel={"npc:sentinel-elissa-starbreeze","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:954"},m={start="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze",["end"]="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=965},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}}
E["quest:966"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="Investigating suspicious activity around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, the scout Balthule Shadowstrike enlists aid to gather intelligence from the gathering warlocks. By recovering discarded parchment scraps from the fanatics encamped outside the ruins, he attempts to uncover the cultists' identity and sinister purpose.",h="Investigating suspicious activity around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, the scout Balthule...",sec={{t="Eyes in the Shallows",b="Balthule Shadowstrike stands watch along the misty shoreline of northern Darkshore, keeping a vigilant eye on the ancient ruin known as the Tower of Althalaxx. Sent to monitor the site for Auberdine and warn Delgren the Purifier of any rising danger, Balthule hesitated to leave his post to report. Fearing he would miss crucial movements by the dark spellcasters occupying the stones, he instead relies on passing travelers to scout the perimeter camps.",sp=0},{t="Deciphering the Cult",b="The lesser followers haunting the ruined grounds carry fragmented scrolls and notes. By piecing together several worn parchments recovered from these outer cultists, Balthule discovers a disturbing name: the Cult of the Dark Strand. Entirely unfamiliar with this shadowy sect, the scout realizes the peril is more organized than a simple band of rogue warlocks, demanding an immediate warning to Delgren.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is an Alliance scout stationed on the road near the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. He was dispatched to monitor suspicious gatherings at the tower on behalf of Auberdine's leadership and the paladin Delgren the Purifier.",al={"balthule shadowstrike lore","who is balthule","balthule darkshore"}},{q="What is the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient elven ruin in northern Darkshore. Recently, sinister warlocks and their cultist thralls have occupied the surrounding grounds and the interior of the tower, conducting dark rituals far from the watch of Auberdine.",al={"tower of althalaxx","what is althalaxx","darkshore ruined tower"}},{q="Who are the cultists surrounding the tower?",a="They belong to the Cult of the Dark Strand, a secretive organization of warlocks and zealots who have gathered at the ancient elven ruins to pursue dark summoning rituals.",al={"who are the warlocks","cult of the dark strand","dark strand fanatics"}},{q="Why does Balthule warn against entering the tower?",a="Balthule notes that the warlocks residing inside the upper tower are far more powerful and dangerous than the fanatics camping outside among the ruins. He advises gathering intelligence from the perimeter before attempting to storm the stronghold.",al={"can i go into the tower","tower warlocks dangerous","inside the tower"}},{q="What do the worn parchments reveal?",a="Piecemeal scraps carried by the cult's fanatics provide the first clear confirmation of the group's name—the Cult of the Dark Strand—revealing to Balthule that the occupants are an organized sect whose presence poses an immediate threat to the region.",al={"what is on the parchments","worn parchment lore","cult notes"}},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance paladin stationed in Darkshore who works to cleanse demonic and corrupt influences. He suspected malicious activity was taking root at the Tower of Althalaxx and depends on scouts like Balthule for intelligence.",al={"delgren","who is delgren","delgren the purifier"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The discovery of a cohesive dark cult operating in northern Darkshore directly aids the crusade of Delgren the Purifier, an ally dedicated to purging fel and demonic corruption.",["class:Warlock"]="The Cult of the Dark Strand demonstrates that unaligned covens will seize ancient ruins to perform their summonings far away from the prying eyes of Alliance and Horde authorities alike.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of the Tower of Althalaxx by human and demonic cultists represents yet another defilement of ancient elven heritage across the shores of Kalimdor."},kw={"althalaxx","auberdine","balthule","dark strand","darkshore","delgren","fanatics","parchment","purifier","shadowstrike","warlocks"},rel={"npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=966},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (2)"}}
E["quest:967"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest bridges the investigation of the Dark Strand cult in northern Darkshore with the broader defense of northern Kalimdor. Balthule Shadowstrike dispatches an Alliance courier south to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale to alert his mentor, Delgren the Purifier, of the cult's sinister gathering at the Tower of Althalaxx.",h="This quest bridges the investigation of the Dark Strand cult in northern Darkshore with the broader defense...",sec={{t="A Plea for Reinforcements",b="Following initial clashes with the Dark Strand cultists around the Tower of Althalaxx, the night elf scout Balthule Shadowstrike recognizes that the threat surpasses his solitary vigil. To mount a decisive response, he writes a detailed report and entrusts it to an Alliance messenger bound for his master, Delgren the Purifier. Because the cult's summoners are growing bolder by the hour, word must reach seasoned leadership capable of directing an eradication effort.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Ashenvale",b="Carrying Balthule's dispatch requires a trek across the full length of Darkshore, following the long coastal highway south out of the mist and over the forested border into Ashenvale. Stationed at Maestra's Post along the western road, Delgren the Purifier has dedicated himself to cleansing demons and undead lingering in the woodland. Though initially unfamiliar with night elven customs, the human paladin has forged a deep mutual respect with the Sentinels as an indispensable ally.",sp=0},{t="A Holy Warrior Awakened",b="Delgren receives Balthule's urgent letter with grim resolve. As a warrior devoted to the Holy Light, he views the presence of dark cultists, soul corruption, and demonic fiends in these ancient woods as an intolerable blight. Reading of the Dark Strand's entrenched foothold at the ruined highborne tower, Delgren immediately prepares to take charge of the operation and strike back.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale. Devoted to the Holy Light, he offers his martial and spiritual expertise to the night elf Sentinels to cleanse demons and undead encroaching upon their ancestral forests.",al={"delgren the purifier","who is delgren","delgren lore"}},{q="Why is Balthule Shadowstrike sending a messenger to Ashenvale?",a="Balthule is a scout stationed outside the Tower of Althalaxx who has been studying the Dark Strand cult. Recognizing that the cult's dark rituals and numbers are escalating rapidly, he sends his findings to his mentor Delgren so an organized strike can be mounted.",al={"why send letter to delgren","balthule letter reason"}},{q="What is the relationship between Balthule and Delgren?",a="Delgren is Balthule's master. The human paladin has instructed the night elf in the art of battle and introduced him to the teachings of the Holy Light, fostering an unusually close bond across their cultural divides.",al={"balthule and delgren","how do balthule and delgren know each other"}},{q="Where is Maestra's Post?",a="Maestra's Post is an Alliance outpost situated in western Ashenvale along the main road leading south from Darkshore. It serves as an early sentry point for travelers moving between Darkshore and the depths of the forest.",al={"maestras post location","where is maestras post"}},{q="What is the Dark Strand cult doing at the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The Dark Strand is a cult operating out of the ruined highborne Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. They practice dark arts, consort with demonic powers, and threaten to unleash corrupting forces across the shoreline.",al={"dark strand cult althalaxx","tower of althalaxx cultists"}},{q="How does Delgren view his alliance with the night elves?",a="Delgren admitted that he was initially unaccustomed to night elven manners and lifestyle when he first arrived in Kalimdor. Over time, however, standing alongside them against common evils has led him to develop immense respect for the Sentinels.",al={"delgren night elves","human paladin night elves"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Meeting Delgren offers paladins an inspiring example of their holy calling in unfamiliar lands: a human crusader wielding the Light to earn the deep trust of Kalimdor's reclusive night elves.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, this mission highlights the growing, practical partnership between their Sentinels and the eastern races who have come to help purge demonic remnants from their woods.",["faction:Alliance"]="The cooperation between Balthule in Darkshore and Delgren in Ashenvale shows the vital communication lines binding northern Kalimdor's scattered Alliance garrisons together."},kw={"ashenvale","balthule shadowstrike","dark strand","darkshore","delgren the purifier","holy light","maestra's post","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:light","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",["end"]="Delgren the Purifier",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=967},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (3)"}}
E["quest:968"] = {t="quest",n="Tools of the Highborne",z="darkshore",s="Tools of the Highborne is an Alliance quest offered by Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine. Travelers are dispatched south into the shattered ruins of Ameth'Aran to pry lingering magical relics from the hands of restless Highborne apparitions. The goal is simple: recover these ancient artifacts before their latent sorcery can unleash further harm upon Kalimdor.",h="Tools of the Highborne is an Alliance quest offered by Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine.",sec={{t="Echoes in the Ruins",b="South of Auberdine, east of the coastal highway, lie the overgrown stone foundations of Ameth'Aran. Ten thousand years ago, this settlement served as a bastion for the Highborne—the privileged aristocracy of the ancient night elven empire. When their unchecked arcane dabbling culminated in the Sundering of the world, Ameth'Aran was shattered. Yet its inhabitants never truly departed. Sentinels patrolling Darkshore report that the ghosts of these aristocrats still haunt the sunken plazas, clutching the enchanted tools and trinkets they possessed in life.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Arcane Past",b="For modern kaldorei society, the arcane is not merely forbidden knowledge; it is an existential danger that nearly obliterated life on Azeroth. Thundris Windweaver recognizes that leaving these Highborne implements in ghostly hands leaves the doorway open to corruption. By dispatching adventurers to wrench these relics away from the restless spirits, Thundris intends to see them thoroughly destroyed, ensuring the dormant, tainted sorcery can never again fuel another disaster.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find the Highborne relics?",a="The relics are found within the ruins of Ameth'Aran, located south of Auberdine on the eastern side of the main path through Darkshore. Wandering spirits throughout the ruined stone courtyards carry these ancient implements.",al={"where are the relics","ameth'aran location","where to find relics"}},{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver is a night elf scholar and elder residing in the port town of Auberdine. Working closely with the local Sentinels, he coordinates efforts to protect Darkshore from lingering magical taints and ancient curses left behind by the Sundering.",al={"thundris windweaver","who gives tools of the highborne"}},{q="Why does Thundris want these relics destroyed?",a="Night elf society strictly rejects arcane magic due to the devastating Great Sundering caused by Highborne reckless sorcery. Thundris fears that the lingering arcane power inside these items could reawaken dormant evils if left unchecked.",al={"why destroy the relics","purpose of tools of the highborne"}},{q="What kind of spirits haunt Ameth'Aran?",a="The spirits are the spectral remains of the Highborne elite who perished during the War of the Ancients. Even in death, they cling to their former pride, power, and magical artifacts, reenacting their faded lives among the ruined stone.",al={"ghosts in ameth aran","what are the spirits"}},{q="Why are the Highborne still bound to the ruins?",a="The sudden, cataclysmic destruction during the Sundering ripped through the empire with such magical violence that many souls remained trapped, bound by trauma and arcane resonance to the ruins of their former homes.",al={"why are they ghosts","highborne curse"}},{q="What happens to the relics after you turn them in?",a="Thundris Windweaver takes custody of the collected relics with the explicit plan to have them permanently dismantled and destroyed so their dormant arcane taint can never be harnessed or released again.",al={"what does thundris do with relics","relic fate"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, confronting the ghosts of Ameth'Aran is a somber reminder of their ancestors' hubris and the catastrophic sundering of their ancestral empire.",["class:Mage"]="While kaldorei society seeks to smash these artifacts out of fear, arcane scholars recognize them as rare, pristine examples of pre-Sundering Highborne craftsmanship.",["class:Druid"]="Clearing the corrupted arcane remnants from Ameth'Aran helps heal the spiritual wounds that disrupt the natural tranquility of the Darkshore wilderness.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting the night elves in securing their haunted territories cements the Alliance's presence and solidarity in the ancient forests of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","darkshore","highborne","relics","sundering","thundris windweaver"},rel={"subzone:ameth-aran","quest:4761","subzone:auberdine","topic:highborne","zone:darkshore","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=968},src={"Tools of the Highborne"}}
E["quest:970"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest marks a critical turn in the investigation of the sinister Cult of the Dark Strand, shifting the pursuit from the ruined Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore across the border to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale. Delgren the Purifier dispatches adventurers into nearby cultist camps to secure a potent Glowing Soul Gem. Unlocking this artifact reveals the grim sorcery that fuels the cult's influence over the northern forests.",h="This quest marks a critical turn in the investigation of the sinister Cult of the Dark Strand, shifting the...",sec={{t="A Plea Across the Border",b="After uncovering the ominous activities around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, reports led directly south into Ashenvale to Delgren the Purifier. Stationed at Maestra's Post, Delgren has long contended with the Cult of the Dark Strand encroaching on the ancient elven woods. Recognizing that the cult's threat spans across both territories, Delgren resolves to strike at the heart of their vile sorcery.",sp=0},{t="The Secrets of Ordil'Aran",b="Northeast of Maestra's Post lies the ruins of Ordil'Aran, now overrun by fanatical Dark Strand cultists. Delgren identifies that their operatives carry glowing soul gems—dark vessels enchanted with sinister magic that sustain the cult's power. By hunting down the cultists among the ruins and reclaiming one of these gems, Delgren intends to shatter their enchantment and expose the true source behind their malevolent rite.",sp=0},{t="A Spirit Trapped",b="Upon deciphering the foul enchantments bound to the glowing soul gem, Delgren does not merely unearth dark incantations; he unravels a vessel of torment. Breaking the gem's wards releases the captive spirit of a victim murdered by the cult. This spectral apparition provides harrowing insight into the Dark Strand's broader rituals and the grim fate awaiting anyone caught within their grasp.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I find the Glowing Soul Gem?",a="The Glowing Soul Gem is held by members of the Cult of the Dark Strand located northeast of Maestra's Post at the ruins of Ordil'Aran in Ashenvale. Various cultists lurking within the ruins carry it, though it can take some persistence to recover one.",al={"soul gem location","where does soul gem drop","dark strand soul gem"}},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance champion stationed at Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale. He actively fights the sinister forces invading the forest, with a particular focus on hunting down and destroying the Cult of the Dark Strand.",al={"delgren","who is delgren"}},{q="What is the Cult of the Dark Strand?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand is a malevolent sect operating out of the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore and ancient elven ruins like Ordil'Aran in Ashenvale. They practice dark sorcery, soul binding, and necromantic rituals.",al={"dark strand cult","who are dark strand"}},{q="Why is a Darkshore quest sending me to Ashenvale?",a="While the investigation begins at the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore, the cult's network extends south across the border into Ashenvale. Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post holds the expertise needed to counter the cult's soul-binding magic.",al={"why maestra's post","why go to ashenvale"}},{q="What happens when the soul gem is deciphered?",a="When Delgren unravels the dark enchantments binding the soul gem, he releases a tormented ghost imprisoned within the stone. The freed spirit reveals key information about the cult's sinister workings.",al={"what is in the soul gem","soul gem ghost"},sp=1},{q="Where is Ordil'Aran located?",a="Ordil'Aran is an ancient elven ruin situated just northeast of Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale, currently infested by the Cult of the Dark Strand.",al={"ordil'aran location","where is ordilaran"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Purifying dark soul vessels and putting twisted cultists to the sword aligns closely with the paladin's duty to purge unholy corruption from the world.",["class:Priest"]="The release of a bound spirit from dark torment echoes the priest's calling to bring redemption and solace to tormented souls.",["race:NightElf"]="Watching vile cultists defile ancient ruins like Ordil'Aran and corrupt the northern woods makes eliminating the Cult of the Dark Strand an urgent priority for any night elf.",["faction:Alliance"]="Coordinating between outposts in Darkshore and Ashenvale secures the northern frontier against dark practitioners threatening Alliance travelers."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","dark strand","darkshore","delgren","delgren the purifier","glowing soul gem","maestra's post","ordil'aran"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=970},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (4)"}}
E["quest:973"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest is the fifth chapter in the investigation of the Tower of Althalaxx, leading Alliance adventurers south from Darkshore into Ashenvale. Delgren the Purifier dispatches you to strike down Ilkrud Magthrull, an orc warlock residing at the corrupted Fire Scar Shrine, and retrieve his esoteric tome.",h="This quest is the fifth chapter in the investigation of the Tower of Althalaxx, leading Alliance adventurers...",sec={{t="A Hunt Into Ashenvale",b="Following the trail of dark cultist activity uncovered at the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore, the holy warrior Delgren the Purifier recognizes the signature of a dangerous practitioner: the orc warlock Ilkrud Magthrull. Operating out of the demonic blight known as Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale, Ilkrud's shadowy dealings threaten to spread foul magic across the pristine elven woodlands. Delgren tasks you with slaying the warlock and seizing his grimoire to expose his master's designs.",sp=0},{t="The Warlock's Lair",b="Fire Scar Shrine is a fel-scarred ruin swarming with demonic thralls. Marked by ominous red pillars along its rocky ascent, the shrine houses Ilkrud alongside a summoned succubus and guardian felslayers. Defeating the orc in the heart of his fel domain allows Delgren to scour Ilkrud's tome for the dark knowledge and commands tying back to the sinister rituals unfolding at Althalaxx.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance champion stationed at Maestra's Post, a night elf outpost on the border between Darkshore and Ashenvale. He directs operations against demonic corruption and cultists operating in the region.",al={"delgren","delgren lore","who starts quest"}},{q="Who is Ilkrud Magthrull?",a="Ilkrud Magthrull is a formidable orc warlock making his lair at the Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale. Though initially deemed a minor annoyance by Delgren, his connection to the dark rites at the Tower of Althalaxx makes him a critical target.",al={"ilkrud","who is ilkrud magthrull","orc warlock ashenvale"}},{q="Where is the Fire Scar Shrine located?",a="The shrine is situated in southwestern Ashenvale, south of the Shrine of Aessina and west of Astranaar. It is a corrupted, demon-infested enclave flanked by two distinct red pillars leading up to Ilkrud's altar.",al={"fire scar shrine location","where is ilkrud","how to reach ilkrud"}},{q="Why does Delgren need Ilkrud Magthrull's tome?",a="Ilkrud's tome contains his dark rituals and communications. Delgren aims to decipher the writings to uncover what sinister plot links the orc warlock to the cultists lingering around the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"why tome","what is in ilkrud's tome","purpose of tome"}},{q="How does this quest connect Darkshore to Ashenvale?",a="The storyline begins with investigations at the Tower of Althalaxx on the northern coast of Darkshore. As the mystery deepens, the cultists' network leads adventurers down through Darkshore into the contested forests of Ashenvale.",al={"darkshore to ashenvale quest","althalaxx chain connection"}},{q="What happens after recovering the tome?",a="Delgren examines the text to deduce the deeper schemes behind the cultist presence at the Tower of Althalaxx, leading into the final confrontations of the quest chain.",al={"next quest","what follows althalaxx 5"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This task takes Alliance adventurers out of the safety of Darkshore and deep into the demon-tainted corners of Ashenvale to cleanse a growing dark menace.",["class:Paladin"]="Working alongside Delgren the Purifier to strike down fel summoners and confiscate corrupt tomes reflects the classic calling of the Holy Light against demonic corruption.",["class:Warlock"]="Confronting Ilkrud Magthrull pits you against a fellow practitioner of the dark arts who uses summoned succubi and voidwalkers to guard his unholy texts.",["race:NightElf"]="The Fire Scar Shrine represents a vile defilement of Ashenvale's ancient forests, making the elimination of Ilkrud a matter of defending sacred ancestral lands."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","delgren","fire scar shrine","ilkrud","maestra","magthrull","tome","warlock"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:fire-scar-shrine","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore","subzone:shrine-of-aessina","subzone:astranaar","npc:lars"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=973},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (5)"}}
E["quest:981"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This errand marks the triumphant conclusion of the campaign against the Cult of the Dark Strand at the Tower of Althalaxx. Having eliminated the cult's leadership within the sinister ruins of Darkshore, an adventurer carries word south into Ashenvale to Delgren the Purifier. It represents a vital victory for the Alliance in purging demonic corruption from the ancient night elven borders.",h="This errand marks the triumphant conclusion of the campaign against the Cult of the Dark Strand at the Tower...",sec={{t="A Threat Severed",b="The Tower of Althalaxx stood for weeks as a festering wound in northern Darkshore, occupied by the fanatical Cult of the Dark Strand and their shadowy masters. Through relentless tracking, intelligence gathering, and violent skirmishes, the cult's operations were systematically dismantled. With their sorcerers slain and their dark rituals broken, the immediate danger of demonic infiltration in Darkshore has finally been stayed.",sp=0},{t="Report to Maestra's Post",b="Following the cult leader's death, Balthule Shadowstrike directs the victor south to Maestra's Post in the Ashenvale canopy. There waits Delgren the Purifier, a devoted warrior of the Holy Light who oversaw the crusade against Althalaxx's wicked occupants. Delivering news of the cult's collapse brings peace of mind to the regional defenders, earning the champion Delgren's lasting blessing and well-earned gratitude.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the goal of this quest?",a="This quest serves as the final turn-in for the long Tower of Althalaxx storyline. You simply need to journey from the tower's vicinity down to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale and report your decisive victory to Delgren the Purifier.",al={"tower of althalaxx objective","turn in tower of althalaxx","where to turn in quest 981"}},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance champion stationed at Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale. Wielding the Holy Light, he is dedicated to purging corruption and combating demonic threats like the Cult of the Dark Strand across northern Kalimdor.",al={"who is delgren","delgren lore","delgren the purifier"}},{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is an Alliance operative positioned near the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore. Working closely with Delgren, he monitors the cult's movements and guides adventurers through dismantling the dark cabal from within.",al={"balthule","balthule lore","who is balthule shadowstrike"}},{q="What was the Cult of the Dark Strand doing at the tower?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand occupied the ancient ruins of the Tower of Althalaxx to perform dark rituals, summon demonic entities, and expand their sinister influence across the coastal lands of Darkshore.",al={"cult of the dark strand","what happened at althalaxx","tower of althalaxx lore"}},{q="Where is Maestra's Post located?",a="Maestra's Post is an Alliance outpost situated in northwestern Ashenvale, just south of the border crossing from Darkshore along the main road.",al={"maestra's post location","where is maestras post","delgren location"}},{q="Is the Cult of the Dark Strand completely destroyed?",a="While their leadership at the Tower of Althalaxx has been executed and their primary ritual broken, scattered cultists and remnants still haunt isolated corners of Kalimdor. However, their organized threat in Darkshore has been shattered.",al={"is the cult gone","dark strand destroyed","did we kill the cult"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Reporting to Delgren the Purifier carries special resonance for paladins, who share his holy mission to cleanse demonic corruption and wicked cults from the world.",["faction:Alliance"]="Eliminating the cult protects the overland road connecting Darkshore and Ashenvale, ensuring Alliance scouts and travelers remain safe from demonic ambushes.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, cleansing the Tower of Althalaxx removes a foul blight from the ancient Highborne ruins that litter their sacred coastal forests."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","balthule","cult","dark strand","darkshore","delgren","maestra's post"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",["end"]="Delgren the Purifier",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=981},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (9)"}}
E["quest:982"] = {t="quest",n="Deep Ocean, Vast Sea",z="darkshore",s="Deep Ocean, Vast Sea is an Alliance quest offered by Gorbold Steelhand in Auberdine. Players are tasked with diving into the waters north of the village to recover personal lockboxes from two sunken night elf vessels, the Silver Dawning and the Mist Veil. Both ships were ambushed by coastal murlocs, leaving their surviving crew members in search of closure.",h="Deep Ocean, Vast Sea is an Alliance quest offered by Gorbold Steelhand in Auberdine.",sec={{t="Tragedy off the Coast",b="The waters off Darkshore have grown increasingly hazardous, not just from treacherous currents and natural reefs, but from aggressive coastal tribes. The vessels Silver Dawning and Mist Veil were making their way into port at Auberdine when they were overwhelmed by swarming murlocs. Neither ship survived the encounter, and both sank into the shallows north of the settlement. The surviving crew made it ashore, but the loss of their ships and captains cast a heavy shadow over the port.",sp=0},{t="Recovering Lost Memories",b="Gorbold Steelhand, a dwarf stationed in Auberdine, takes up the cause of honoring the fallen night elf captains. Although the vessels are now underwater ruins claimed as trophies and nests by the local murlocs, the captains' lockboxes remain locked in the flooded holds. Recovering the logs and personal effects inside allows the surviving sailors in Auberdine to properly mourn their commanders and lay their spirits to rest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the sunken ships located?",a="The wrecks of both the Silver Dawning and the Mist Veil lie submerged off the coast of Darkshore, directly to the north of the Auberdine docks.",al={"where are the shipwrecks","wreck location","where to find silver dawning"}},{q="What happened to the Silver Dawning and the Mist Veil?",a="Both vessels were ambushed by murlocs as they sailed toward Auberdine across the sea. The crews were overrun, both captains died, and the ships foundered and settled on the ocean floor.",al={"how did ships sink","why did ships wreck","what sank mist veil"}},{q="Who is Gorbold Steelhand?",a="Gorbold Steelhand is a dwarf residing in the night elf port of Auberdine. He looks out for the surviving sailors around town and tasks adventurers with recovering the lost captains' belongings.",al={"who gives deep ocean vast sea","gorbold steelhand lore"}},{q="What is inside the lockboxes?",a="The lockboxes contain the personal effects and logs belonging to the fallen night elf captains, items cherished by the surviving crew members who escaped the wreck.",al={"what are in the lockboxes","captains lockbox contents"}},{q="Why do the survivors care so much about these effects?",a="The captains were respected night elf mariners. Recovering their logs and possessions provides closure to their surviving crew and is believed to help put their spirits to rest.",al={"why recover lockboxes","why help the captains"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the shipwrecks now?",a="The ruins have been overtaken by murlocs, who treat the wrecked hulls as trophies and prowl the surrounding waters.",al={"what is guarding the ships","mobs at the shipwrecks"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The fallen captains were night elf mariners serving Auberdine's maritime trade, making the recovery of their belongings a matter of ancestral honor.",["race:Dwarf"]="Gorbold Steelhand shows the typical dwarven instinct to honor fallen comrades and support his fellow sailors in foreign ports.",["faction:Alliance"]="The shared grief of the crew in Auberdine demonstrates the close maritime cooperation between dwarfs and night elves along the Kalimdor coast."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","deep ocean vast sea","gorbold steelhand","lockbox","mist veil","murloc","shipwreck","silver dawning"},rel={"npc:gorbold-steelhand","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc","quest:938"},m={start="Gorbold Steelhand",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=982},src={"Deep Ocean, Vast Sea"}}
E["quest:983"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 827",z="darkshore",s="Buzzbox 827 is the first in an experimental communication relay built by the gnome Wizbang Cranktoggle along the coastline of Darkshore. Plagued by breakdowns, these curious mechanical contraptions rely on an eccentric design that uses local wildlife parts for field repairs. Restoring the silent machine allows Wizbang to test his long-distance voice network directly from Auberdine.",h="Buzzbox 827 is the first in an experimental communication relay built by the gnome Wizbang Cranktoggle along...",sec={{t="Gnomish Innovation on Ancient Shores",b="While visiting Auberdine, the eccentric gnomish engineer Wizbang Cranktoggle sought to bridge the long distances of the wild coast with a series of long-range acoustic relays called Buzzboxes. Designed to transmit voice over great distances, these lever-laden devices stand out starkly against the ancient ruins and somber forests of Darkshore. However, like many ambitious gnomish inventions, they suffer from chronic instability and require near-constant upkeep to keep their internal gears churning.",sp=0},{t="Ecological Maintenance",b="Rather than hauling refined iron gears and copper pins across the wilderness, Wizbang adopted an unconventional solution: he built each Buzzbox to be serviced using components harvested from nearby native fauna. Buzzbox 827, stationed just south of Auberdine along the misty shoreline, was engineered to function with the sturdy, jointed legs of local tide and reef crawlers. Depositing the legs into the receiver hopper prompts the machine to self-assemble and jump back to life, broadcasting Wizbang's distant voice through its speakers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Buzzbox?",a="A Buzzbox is a long-distance voice communication machine invented by the gnome Wizbang Cranktoggle. Equipped with levers and internal machinery, it is designed to transmit voices across the untamed expanse of Darkshore, allowing people to speak across miles.",al={"what does a buzzbox do","buzzbox purpose","gnome box darkshore"}},{q="Why does a metal machine need crab legs to run?",a="Wizbang purposefully designed each Buzzbox to use organic components from surrounding wildlife as improvised replacement parts. By placing Buzzbox 827 near the beach where crawlers dwell, he ensured travelers could make emergency mechanical repairs using chitinous limbs instead of rare machined metal.",al={"why crawler legs","crawler leg repair","why feed it legs"}},{q="Where is Buzzbox 827 located?",a="Buzzbox 827 is situated along the shoreline of Darkshore, just a short trek south of the coastal settlement of Auberdine.",al={"buzzbox 827 location","where is buzzbox 827","find buzzbox 827"}},{q="Who is Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is a gnome tinkerer staying on the upper floor of the Auberdine inn. Ambitious and enterprising, he is attempting to construct an interconnected communication network across Darkshore despite the constant malfunctions of his prototypes.",al={"wizbang cranktoggle","who made buzzbox","auberdine gnome"}},{q="Where can I find Crawler Legs for the repair?",a="Crawler Legs can be gathered from Pygmy Tide Crawlers and Young Reef Crawlers scuttling along the sands and shallows of the Darkshore beach just south of Auberdine.",al={"crawler leg location","how to get crawler legs","pygmy tide crawler"}},{q="What happens once Buzzbox 827 is repaired?",a="Once the Crawler Legs are fed into the hopper, the machine churns them into place, hums back to life, and relays Wizbang's voice from Auberdine. Pleased with the success, he immediately asks you to travel further down the coast to repair the next unit in the chain, Buzzbox 411.",al={"after buzzbox 827","buzzbox questline next","buzzbox 827 completion"},sp=1}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Using organic chitin and arthropod limbs in place of forged brass gears is quintessential gnomish improvisation, trading durability for readily scavenged local materials.",["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang's device represents classic gnomish ambition, attempting to bring technological connectivity to an ancient, untamed land that has never seen a telephone or radio.",["race:NightElf"]="The clanking, smoking Buzzboxes are a bizarre eyesore on the sacred, somber shores of Kalimdor, though the night elves of Auberdine tolerate the tinkerer's experiments."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 827","crawler legs","darkshore","gnomish engineering","reef crawler","tide crawler","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},m={start="Wizbang Cranktoggle",["end"]="Buzzbox 827",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=983},src={"Buzzbox 827 (quest)"}}
E["quest:984"] = {t="quest",n="How Big a Threat?",z="darkshore",s="How Big a Threat? is an Alliance quest given by Terenthis in Auberdine. Having witnessed furbolg madness taking root across Teldrassil, the night elf sentinel directs scouts to investigate local furbolg settlements in Darkshore to confirm whether the same dark taint has crossed the sea.",h="How Big a Threat?",sec={{t="Shadows Across the Sea",b="The night elves of northern Kalimdor have long maintained cordial or peaceful relations with indigenous furbolg tribes. However, following the Third War, strange corruptions began unhinging furbolg minds in Teldrassil, resulting in violent kidnappings and feral attacks against their former allies. Stationed in Auberdine, the sentinel Terenthis fears that this sinister affliction is not isolated to the World Tree, but is actively spreading among the mainland tribes along the misty coasts of Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="A Gathering Storm",b="Reconnaissance of a furbolg encampment nestled near the ruins of Ameth'Aran confirms Terenthis's worst suspicions. The furbolgs there display erratic, hostile aggression, bearing the clear marks of the same corruption plaguing the north. Their close proximity to Auberdine elevates them from a peaceful wilderness neighbor to an urgent defensive hazard for the Alliance settlement.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Terenthis?",a="Terenthis is a night elf sentinel stationed in the coastal haven of Auberdine. Haunted by accounts of night elves assaulted and captured by maddened furbolgs across Teldrassil, he works to monitor and suppress emerging threats throughout Darkshore.",al={"terenthis questgiver","who gives how big a threat","terenthis auberdine"}},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Darkshore turning hostile?",a="Historically friendly or neutral toward the night elves, many furbolg clans have fallen victim to a spreading supernatural taint following the Third War. This unseen corruption drives them into frantic, territorial madness, causing them to attack travelers and former allies alike.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","corrupt furbolgs darkshore","furbolg corruption"}},{q="Where is the corrupt furbolg camp located?",a="The encampment lies inland in central Darkshore, situated just north of the ancient highborne ruins of Ameth'Aran and southeast of Auberdine.",al={"camp location","where is the furbolg camp","how big a threat location"}},{q="How does this relate to events on Teldrassil?",a="In Teldrassil, several corrupted furbolgs kidnapped and injured night elf sentinels and civilians. Terenthis references those recent rescues when seeking to verify if mainland Darkshore faces the exact same crisis.",al={"teldrassil connection","teldrassil furbolgs","why does terenthis mention teldrassil"}},{q="What happens after reporting back to Terenthis?",a="Confirming the corruption prompts Terenthis to prepare defensive measures for Auberdine, continuing a quest chain focused on investigating the root source and countering the aggressive furbolgs nearby.",al={"next quest","what follows how big a threat","quest continuation"}},{q="Why are night elves so concerned about furbolg camps near Auberdine?",a="Auberdine serves as the principal Alliance port and supply lifeline on the mainland. Having deeply corrupted, hostile tribes nesting within striking distance leaves trade roads, scouting parties, and the town itself vulnerable to sudden assaults.",al={"threat to auberdine","why care about furbolgs"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, watching ancient allies like the furbolgs succumb to irrational darkness so soon after the Third War is both a bitter tragedy and an immediate danger to sacred lands.",["class:Druid"]="Furbolgs share deep bonds with nature and ancient wilderness spirits, making their sudden descent into corruption a grave concern for druids tasked with healing Kalimdor's balance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As the Alliance's primary gateway to mainland northern Kalimdor, safeguarding Auberdine from wilderness threats is essential for regional security and logistics."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","corruption","darkshore","furbolg","teldrassil","terenthis","threat"},rel={"npc:terenthis","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:furbolg","quest:940"},m={start="Terenthis",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=984},src={"How Big a Threat?"}}
E["quest:985"] = {t="quest",n="How Big a Threat?",z="darkshore",s="How Big a Threat? is an Alliance quest offered by the night elf Terenthis in Auberdine. Having already scouted the hostile Blackwood furbolg camp south of town, adventurers are sent to cull the corrupted pathfinders and windtalkers before their frenzy threatens the settlement.",h="How Big a Threat?",sec={{t="A Necessary Cull",b="Following initial scouting south of Auberdine, the Sentinels have determined that the Blackwood furbolgs pose an immediate danger to Darkshore's refugees and defenders. Terenthis tasks combat-capable travelers with striking directly at their camp, eliminating Blackwood Pathfinders and Windtalkers to break their offensive momentum.",sp=0},{t="Tragedy of the Corrupted",b="Night elves traditionally view furbolgs as spiritual kin and historic allies of the wilderness. However, the malignant spread of fel moss and demonic taint across northern Kalimdor has driven the Blackwood tribe mad. With no known remedy to restore the furbolgs' minds, the defenders of Auberdine view violence as a grim necessity to prevent innocent deaths.",sp=0},{t="Grimclaw's Arrival",b="Upon reporting the cull back to Terenthis, a white bear named Grimclaw rushes into Auberdine toward the night elf. The arrival signals urgent new developments regarding the wildlife and corruption ravaging the coastline, setting off the next stage in Auberdine's defensive efforts.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Terenthis want the Blackwood furbolgs killed?",a="The Blackwood tribe south of Auberdine has fallen to corruption, turning violent and irrational. Because their camp poses an imminent threat to the settlement and no cure exists for their madness, Terenthis orders a preemptive strike to keep Auberdine safe.",al={"why kill blackwood furbolgs","reason for furbolg cull","terenthis furbolg quest"}},{q="Where is the Blackwood furbolg camp located?",a="The camp lies just south of Auberdine along the coastal forest of Darkshore, nestled among the corrupted trees where the Blackwood tribe has gathered.",al={"blackwood furbolg location","where are pathfinders and windtalkers","furbolg camp darkshore"}},{q="Who is Grimclaw?",a="Grimclaw is a white bear companion tied to the wilderness investigations in Darkshore. When you complete the cull of the Blackwood furbolgs, Grimclaw sprints into Auberdine to alert Terenthis of further troubles in the wild.",al={"white bear auberdine","who is the bear running to terenthis","grimclaw the bear"},sp=1},{q="What is causing the furbolgs to go mad?",a="The furbolgs have been poisoned by fel moss and lingering demonic corruption left behind after the Third War. The dark energies ravaging Darkshore warp both mind and body, driving peaceful tribes into uncontrollable aggression.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","darkshore furbolg corruption","what corrupted blackwood"}},{q="Why are night elves reluctant to kill furbolgs?",a="The furbolgs and night elves have shared a bond of friendship and reverence for nature for thousands of years. Putting them down feels to the night elves like slaughtering their own brothers of the wild, but the corruption leaves them no alternative.",al={"night elves and furbolgs","why mourn furbolgs"}},{q="What is the difference between the first and second 'How Big a Threat?' quests?",a="The first quest tests scouting ability by requiring you to locate and observe the Blackwood camp. The second quest is a direct combat assignment to thin out the camp's pathfinders and windtalkers once the threat is confirmed.",al={"how big a threat parts","how big a threat difference"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, culling the Blackwood is a bitter grief; centuries of kinship with the furbolgs have been shattered by the lingering demonic blight of the Third War.",["class:Druid"]="Druids feel the tragedy keenly, as the furbolgs' plight reflects the ongoing suffering of Cenarius's creations beneath the taint of fel moss.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the vital port anchor for the Alliance in Darkshore, making the elimination of nearby hostile encampments crucial to securing the region."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","darkshore","fel moss","furbolg","grimclaw","pathfinder","terenthis","windtalker"},rel={"npc:terenthis","quest:984","subzone:auberdine","topic:furbolg","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Terenthis",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=985},src={"How Big a Threat? (2)"}}
E["quest:986"] = {t="quest",n="A Lost Master",z="darkshore",s="A Lost Master tasks an Alliance adventurer with gathering materials to aid in the search for Volcor, a night elf lost in the wilderness of Darkshore. Terenthis in Auberdine offers to weave an enchanted camouflage cloak to protect the rescuer, requiring pelts from the coast's fiercest moonstalkers.",h="A Lost Master tasks an Alliance adventurer with gathering materials to aid in the search for Volcor, a night...",sec={{t="A Search into the Wilds",b="While tracking threats along the coast of Darkshore, Terenthis in Auberdine becomes concerned for the fate of Volcor and his companion, Grimclaw. Venturing deep into the southern reaches of the region is notoriously dangerous due to aggressive predators and corrupted wildlife. Rather than sending a scout unprotected, Terenthis devises a plan to craft a protective cloak imbued with wild illusions.",sp=0},{t="Pelts of the Pride",b="To weave a cloak capable of confounding Darkshore's beasts, standard hides are insufficient. Terenthis requires fine moonstalker pelts taken specifically from mature moonstalker sires or matriarchs. These formidable great cats prowl the woodlands south of Auberdine near the Wildbend River and extend toward the forested border of Ashenvale.",sp=0},{t="Delicate Magic",b="The finished garment uses moonstalker fur and nature enchantments to let the wearer pass unhindered through hostile territory while searching for Volcor. However, Terenthis warns that the illusion is delicate: engaging in strenuous activity or combat breaks the enchantment, leaving the searcher exposed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout or tracker who went missing in the wilds of southern Darkshore. His companion Grimclaw and Terenthis in Auberdine seek his whereabouts, prompting the search.",al={"who is volcor","volcor lore","lost master volcor"}},{q="Who offers this task?",a="Terenthis, a night elf stationed in the settlement of Auberdine in Darkshore, provides the quest after adventurers assist him with earlier local concerns.",al={"quest giver","where to get a lost master","terenthis location"}},{q="Where are moonstalker sires and matriarchs found?",a="These mature moonstalkers roam southern Darkshore, particularly near the banks of the Wildbend River and farther south approaching the border with Ashenvale.",al={"fine moonstalker pelt locations","where to find moonstalkers","wildbend river cats"}},{q="What is the cloak meant to do?",a="Terenthis intends to craft an enchanted cloak that conceals the wearer from the hostile beasts of Darkshore, allowing them to search for Volcor without constantly drawing attacks.",al={"what does the cloak do","terenthis cloak","cloak enchantment"}},{q="Why does Terenthis need specific pelts?",a="Ordinary pelts lack the strength and natural presence required to channel the camouflage illusion. Only the thick, resilient hides of sires and matriarchs can carry the enchantment.",al={"why sires and matriarchs","why fine pelts"}},{q="Does the camouflage cloak have limitations?",a="Yes. Terenthis warns that the enchantment is fragile. Speaking to others is permitted, but strenuous interactions or combat will quickly dispel the illusion.",al={"does the illusion break","cloak restrictions"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Locating Volcor reflects the night elves' duty to safeguard their kindred and wild companions across the untamed reaches of Darkshore.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters will recognize the bond between Volcor and Grimclaw, as well as the skill demanded to track and hunt Darkshore's matriarchs and sires.",["class:Druid"]="Druids can appreciate Terenthis's respect for the natural stealth of moonstalkers, turning their wild essence into protective camouflage."},kw={"a lost master","auberdine","darkshore","fine moonstalker pelt","grimclaw","moonstalker","terenthis","volcor","wildbend river"},rel={"npc:terenthis","npc:volcor","subzone:auberdine","subzone:wildbend-river","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Terenthis",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=986},src={"A Lost Master"}}
E["quest:993"] = {t="quest",n="A Lost Master",z="darkshore",s="Having gathered pelts and fine thread, you carry the completed Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak into the wilds of Darkshore to find the missing night elf, Volcor. Guided by his loyal nightsaber Grimclaw, you must track down the wounded scout before hostile furbolgs finish him off.",h="Having gathered pelts and fine thread, you carry the completed Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak into the wilds of...",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Woods",b="After Terenthis in Auberdine weaves the Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak, the search for the missing scout Volcor begins in earnest. His nightsaber companion, Grimclaw, has returned to the road south of the settlement, standing watch for any ally sent by Terenthis. By offering a familiar greeting to the loyal beast, travelers are led directly off the beaten track toward the cave where Volcor lies in hiding.",sp=0},{t="Hiding in the Dark",b="Volcor sought refuge within a cavern after suffering severe injuries at the hands of the local corrupted furbolgs. Trapped and bleeding, he has had to rely entirely on stealth and Grimclaw's wits to avoid being overrun. The enchanted cloak provides him with the concealment and hope necessary to plan his extraction, though his wounds leave him in precarious condition for the return trek to Auberdine.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout based out of Darkshore who went missing while venturing near hostile furbolg encampments. He was badly wounded during a confrontation and managed to crawl into a nearby cave, sending his companion nightsaber Grimclaw to seek aid.",al={"volcor lore","who is the lost master"}},{q="How do you find Volcor's hiding spot?",a="Grimclaw waits alongside the road south of Auberdine. Waving to the beast lets him know you are the helper sent by Terenthis, prompting Grimclaw to run directly toward the secluded cave where Volcor is nursing his injuries.",al={"where is volcor","find volcor cave","how to follow grimclaw"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak?",a="Terenthis enchanted the cloak crafted from fine thread and moonstalker pelts to grant brief, potent magical stealth. It is intended to shield the severely wounded Volcor from predatory eyes long enough to slip past dangerous wilderness threats.",al={"moonstalker cloak","cloak magic"}},{q="Who attacked Volcor?",a="Volcor was ambushed and wounded by the corrupted furbolg tribes roaming Darkshore. Though he managed to evade immediate slaughter, his injuries prevented him from making the journey back to Auberdine unassisted.",al={"who hurt volcor","why is volcor bleeding"}},{q="What happens after finding Volcor?",a="Once Volcor receives the enchanted cloak, he catches his breath and asks for your assistance in escaping the wilderness, offering you a choice between guiding him out through careful stealth or cutting a path through the furbolgs by raw force.",al={"volcor next quest","after a lost master"},sp=1}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The bond between night elf scouts and their nightsabers is demonstrated here by Grimclaw's steadfast loyalty in seeking aid for his master Volcor.",["class:Hunter"]="Seeing Grimclaw navigate the road to locate help for Volcor highlights the remarkable intelligence and devotion of well-trained Kalimdor beasts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine depends on scouts like Volcor to monitor the rising corruption of Darkshore's furbolg tribes, making his rescue a vital priority for the outpost."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","furbolg","grimclaw","moonstalker cloak","nightsaber","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"npc:volcor","npc:terenthis","quest:986","topic:furbolg","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Terenthis",["end"]="Volcor",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=993},src={"A Lost Master (2)"}}
E["quest:994"] = {t="quest",n="Escape Through Force",z="darkshore",s="Escape Through Force is an Alliance quest in Darkshore where the adventurer helps Volcor break through surrounding threats by direct combat. After fighting past the perils of the wild to reach the road and reunite with his faithful companion Grimclaw, the player reports Volcor's safe escape back to Terenthis in Auberdine.",h="Escape Through Force is an Alliance quest in Darkshore where the adventurer helps Volcor break through...",sec={{t="A Direct Way Out",b="When stranded in the perilous wilderness of Darkshore, subtle movement is not always the chosen path. Faced with danger, the night elf Volcor accepts a blunt strategy: cutting directly through the surrounding hostile creatures to reach safety. Rather than attempting to slip away unseen, Volcor relies on martial prowess to carve a corridor straight down to the main road.",sp=0},{t="Reunion on the Road",b="Reaching the thoroughfare safely allows Volcor to reunite with Grimclaw, his stalwart bear companion who has been waiting by the path. With their escape secured, Volcor prepares for his next journey while urging the adventurer to report directly to Terenthis in Auberdine. Delivering news of Volcor's safety reassures the night elf leadership and immediately draws the attention of Sentinel Selarin, pointing toward deeper troubles brewing southward in Ashenvale.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout or woodsman in Darkshore who went missing along with his companion Grimclaw. After being located by adventurers searching on behalf of Terenthis, he requires assistance escaping hostile wildlife and dangerous terrain.",al={"volcor identity","who is volcor","volcor darkshore"}},{q="Who is Grimclaw?",a="Grimclaw is Volcor's loyal companion bear. During Volcor's entrapment, Grimclaw remained separated near the road, serving as the landmark rendezvous point for Volcor's escape.",al={"grimclaw","volcor bear","volcor pet"}},{q="Why does Terenthis care about Volcor's return?",a="Terenthis coordinates scout movements and local defense efforts out of Auberdine. Tracking down lost allies and assessing threats along the coastline is critical to maintaining night elf control across a rapidly destabilizing Darkshore.",al={"terenthis volcor","why help volcor","terenthis quest"}},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="Upon returning to Terenthis in Auberdine, Sentinel Selarin rushes into the outpost with urgent news, opening the path for the adventurer to take on the trek south into Ashenvale.",al={"after escape through force","what comes next","next quest after volcor"},sp=1},{q="Is there an alternate way to finish Volcor's escort?",a="Yes. When rescuing Volcor, adventurers are offered a choice in approach: fighting their way out head-on via Escape Through Force, or guiding him quietly past danger using stealth.",al={"escape through force alternate","escape through stealth","volcor choices"}},{q="Where does this quest lead in the broader storyline?",a="Securing Volcor's survival serves as a bridge between the local conflicts of Darkshore and the larger regional defense of the night elf lands, directly opening up assignments in Ashenvale.",al={"volcor storyline","darkshore to ashenvale questline"},sp=1}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Rescuing scouts like Volcor is vital to the Kaldorei's tenuous grip on Darkshore, where wild beasts, corruption, and outside invaders threaten their ancestral woodlands.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting local scouts deepens the bond between the young Alliance and the Night Elves, proving the faction's value in securing Kalimdor's northern frontier."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","escort","grimclaw","selarin","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"npc:volcor","npc:terenthis","npc:sentinel-selarin","quest:990","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Volcor",["end"]="Terenthis",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=994},src={"Escape Through Force"}}
E["quest:995"] = {t="quest",n="Escape Through Stealth",z="darkshore",s="Escape Through Stealth is an Alliance escort quest set in Darkshore. After locating the trapped night elf scout Volcor deep within a furbolg den, the player helps guide him safely past hostile beasts to freedom before reporting back to Terenthis in Auberdine.",h="Escape Through Stealth is an Alliance escort quest set in Darkshore.",sec={{t="The Trapped Scout",b="Volcor, an operative sent into the depths of Darkshore to investigate the region's mounting threats, ended up cornered inside a furbolg cave. Outnumbered and cut off from the main roads, he relies on a passing ally to coordinate an exit before the hostile furbolgs realize he is slipping away.",sp=0},{t="A Careful Flight",b="Rather than attempting a suicidal frontal charge, Volcor chooses caution. Relying on shadows and deliberate maneuvering, he slips past the corrupted denizens of the cavern. Knowing that speed and quiet are paramount, Volcor separates from his rescuer once outside the mouth of the cave, racing ahead on foot while instructing his savior to meet him at the settlement of Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Auberdine",b="Upon returning to Auberdine, the player delivers news of the rescue to Terenthis, a night elf leader coordinating efforts to protect the troubled coastline. Terenthis views Volcor's safe return as proof that the encroaching darkness throughout Darkshore and the wilderness beyond can be resisted with discipline and teamwork.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout who ventured deep into Darkshore's wilderness on a mission for his superiors. He became trapped inside a hostile furbolg cavern until rescued by an Alliance adventurer.",al={"volcor lore","who is volcor","volcor darkshore"}},{q="Why does Volcor run off alone once outside the cave?",a="Volcor notes that he can travel faster on his own once clear of the cavern's confined passages. He instructs the adventurer to reconvene in Auberdine rather than stick together along the open roads.",al={"why does volcor leave","volcor splits up"}},{q="Who is Terenthis?",a="Terenthis is a prominent night elf coordinator stationed in Auberdine. He oversees local scouting efforts and organizes responses to the corruption and hostile denizens threatening Darkshore.",al={"terenthis auberdine","who is terenthis"}},{q="Where does this rescue take place?",a="The rescue begins deep inside a furbolg cave located within the wilder, contested forests of Darkshore, far from the safety of Auberdine.",al={"volcor cave location","where is volcor cave"}},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="After Volcor is safely accounted for and Terenthis is debriefed, players are directed toward the next stage of their journey south toward Ashenvale in the quest Trek to Ashenvale.",al={"what comes after escape through stealth","next quest after volcor"}},{q="What is the alternative to stealth in this rescue?",a="Volcor offers an alternative approach: instead of sneaking out through stealth, adventurers can choose to fight their way out through sheer force in a separate, combat-focused escort option.",al={"escape through force","volcor other quest","stealth vs force"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, aiding Volcor reinforces the vital network of scouts watching over Kalimdor's troubled forests while corruption spreads outward from corrupted barrows and dens.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues appreciate Volcor's tactical instinct to bypass an entrenched enemy rather than waste time and blood in a reckless frontal brawl.",["faction:Alliance"]="Successfully securing Volcor's escape proves to the night elf leadership in Auberdine that non-kaldorei Alliance allies can be trusted with delicate wilderness operations."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","darkshore","escort","furbolg","stealth","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"npc:volcor","npc:terenthis","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:990","topic:furbolg"},m={start="Volcor",["end"]="Terenthis",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=995},src={"Escape Through Stealth"}}
E["subzone:ameth-aran"] = {t="subzone",n="Ameth'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Ameth'Aran is an ancient ruin in southern Darkshore, once a thriving city where Queen Azshara's Highborne practiced arcane sorcery. When the Great Sundering shattered the ancient world, the city collapsed and its citizens were deceived and bound into eternal torment. Today, its broken colonnades are haunted by the vengeful ghosts of the elves who died there.",h="Ameth'Aran is an ancient ruin in southern Darkshore, once a thriving city where Queen Azshara's Highborne...",sec={{t="A City of Sorcerers",b="Before the Great Sundering, Ameth'Aran and its sister settlement, Bashal'Aran, stood as twin centers of Highborne influence along the ancient coastline. Under the favor of Queen Azshara, the city boasted bustling bazaars and graceful shrines to Elune, though its ruling nobility dedicated themselves to unrestrained arcane experimentation. Governed from afar by the sorcerer Athrikus Narassin in the Tower of Althalaxx, the city thrived until the catastrophic collapse of the Well of Eternity tore the Kaldorei Empire apart.",sp=0},{t="Betrayal and Eternal Torment",b="As the world began to tear itself apart, Athrikus Narassin returned to Ameth'Aran, promising his panicked subjects salvation through powerful shielding magic. Instead of shielding them, the sorcerer enacted a horrific betrayal, stealing their life force to feed his own soul gems under the cruel guise of giving them eternal preservation. Shattered by cataclysm and dark magic, Ameth'Aran fell. Today, its grounds are stalked by anguished Highborne specters, unable to find rest ten thousand years after their murder.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Ameth'Aran?",a="During the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, the sorcerer Athrikus Narassin promised to protect the citizens of Ameth'Aran from destruction. Instead, he betrayed them, trapping their spirits within soul gems as the city collapsed. The ruins remain haunted by those murdered souls to this day.",al={"why is ametharan ruined","ameth aran history","fall of ametharan"}},{q="Who are the ghosts wandering the ruins?",a="They are the restless spirits of the Highborne elves who lived and practiced arcane magic in the city before the Great Sundering. Trapped between life and death by Athrikus Narassin's deceitful magic, they wander the broken stones in perpetual agony and fury.",al={"ghosts in ameth aran","ametharan specters","highborne ghosts darkshore"}},{q="Who was Anaya Dawnrunner?",a="Anaya Dawnrunner was a resident of Ameth'Aran and the beloved of Cerellean Whiteclaw. She perished when the city fell during the Sundering, and her ghost remained bound to the ruins until Cerellean sought outside aid to finally grant her soul release.",al={"anaya dawnrunner","cerellean lover","ameth aran lost love"},sp=1},{q="What are the stone tablets found in the ruins?",a="The ruins contain ancient stone tablets inscribed with the history of Ameth'Aran and the account of its fall. Sentinel Tysha Moonblade attempted to decipher them to deliver a historical report to the Cenarion Circle, but hostile ghosts forced her to rely on passing travelers.",al={"ametharan tablets","runestones in ameth aran","fall of ametharan tablets"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Ameth'Aran is a grim monument to the hubris and treachery of the Highborne caste that brought about the Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="Druids view the ruins as an unhealed scar upon Darkshore, where tormented spirits linger and disrupt the natural balance of the wilds."},kw={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","athrikus narassin","bashal'aran","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","highborne","tysha moonblade"},rel={"quest:953","quest:963","quest:954","zone:darkshore","npc:cerellean-whiteclaw","npc:sentinel-tysha-moonblade","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","topic:highborne"},src={"Ameth'Aran"}}
E["subzone:apothecary-darkshore"] = {t="subzone",n="Apothecary (Darkshore)",z="darkshore",s="Tucked along the misty northern coast of Darkshore, this Forsaken apothecary camp stands out starkly against the ancient kaldorei woods. Equipped with alchemical vats and plague cauldrons, the outpost marks a sinister Undercity foothold on northern Kalimdor. Its presence so far from Lordaeron poses a silent, toxic threat to the local woodland and sea life.",h="Tucked along the misty northern coast of Darkshore, this Forsaken apothecary camp stands out starkly against...",sec={{t="A Chemical Encampment",b="The Apothecary setup on the Gloomtide Strand brings the bleak industry of the Royal Apothecary Society straight to ancient elven shores. Centered around bubbling alchemy vats and makeshift tents, Forsaken researchers have established a working lab far from the Undercity. Their goal remains shrouded in secrecy, but the apparatus present mirrors the tools used across Tirisfal Glades to brew volatile concotions and experimental blights.",sp=0},{t="Intruders on Kaldorei Soil",b="Darkshore's delicate coastal ecosystem already buckles under the corrupting influence of beached behemoths, lingering ghosts, and vile cultists. The intrusion of Forsaken apothecaries introduces a direct alchemical menace to the strand. Night elf sentinels and druids view this unauthorized lab as a foul desecration of their ancestral home, watching warily for whatever foul brew the Society intends to unleash upon the shore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Forsaken Apothecary doing in Darkshore?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society frequently sends forward researchers across Kalimdor to study local reagents, test strange chemicals, and brew alchemical compounds away from prying eyes. Their encampment along the coast gives them a quiet staging point to conduct experiments far from the watchful gaze of the Alliance capitals.",al={"forsaken darkshore tent","why are undead in darkshore","apothecary camp gloomtide"}},{q="Where is this apothecary camp located?",a="It lies along the Gloomtide Strand and the northern reaches of Mist's Edge in Darkshore, pitched directly against the cold, gray sands near the surf.",al={"where is apothecary darkshore","darkshore apothecary location"}},{q="What equipment is kept at the site?",a="The camp is marked by Forsaken-style leather canopies housing bubbling alchemy vats, chemical jars, and testing equipment identical to those used by the Royal Apothecary Society in Lordaeron.",al={"alchemy vat darkshore","apothecary tent tools"}},{q="How do the local night elves react to this camp?",a="The kaldorei consider any Forsaken alchemical presence an utter blasphemy against nature. Sentinel scouts and druids from Auberdine treat chemical testing on their coastline as an immediate ecological and territorial threat.",al={"do night elves know about apothecary","alliance reaction apothecary"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The stench of Forsaken chemicals upon sacred kaldorei shores is an outrage to Elune and nature alike, demanding immediate cleansing before the land is poisoned.",["race:Undead"]="Establishing remote testing vats allows the Royal Apothecary Society to research rare coastal reagents without interference from the Living or meddling Horde allies."},kw={"alchemy vat","apothecary","darkshore","forsaken","gloomtide strand","mist's edge","undercity"},rel={"subzone:gloomtide-strand","subzone:mist-s-edge","zone:darkshore","topic:forsaken","topic:druid","topic:alliance"},src={"Apothecary (Darkshore)"}}
E["subzone:ashwood-depot"] = {t="subzone",n="Ashwood Depot",z="darkshore",s="Ashwood Depot does not exist in present-day Darkshore. In the current era of 25 ADP, the wooded coasts of northern Darkshore remain an undisturbed wilderness under the watchful eye of the night elves.",h="Ashwood Depot does not exist in present-day Darkshore.",sec={{t="Unbroken Wilderness",b="Travelers trekking through northern Darkshore will find no fortified encampments, military supply lines, or deforested clearings under the name of Ashwood Depot. In this year, the kaldorei maintain quiet vigil over their ancestral woodlands, and neither the Horde nor foreign armies have established logging or munitions outposts along this desolate shoreline. The ancient trees stand undisturbed by the machines and blight of distant wars.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Ashwood Depot located in Darkshore?",a="Ashwood Depot does not exist in the world today. The northern reaches of Darkshore consist purely of misty forests, wildlife, and ancient kaldorei ruins untouched by any such military installation.",al={"find ashwood depot","ashwood depot location","where is ashwood depot"}},{q="Is Ashwood Depot a Horde settlement?",a="No. There is no Horde camp or depot established here. The Horde holds no foothold along the northern shores of Darkshore in the present era, leaving the territory firmly under the dominion of the night elves and the Alliance.",al={"horde base darkshore","is ashwood horde","who controls ashwood depot"}},{q="Are there Forsaken or goblin forces stationed here?",a="There are no Forsaken armies or goblin engineers operating in northern Darkshore. The shoreline remains wild, home only to native beasts and wandering spirits of the forest.",al={"forsaken in darkshore","goblin camp darkshore","ashwood npcs"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The northern forests of Darkshore remain sacred and untainted by foreign siege engines or timber operations, standing as a tranquil domain under the protection of the kaldorei.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde has established no major supply depots or outposts along the misty northern coast of Darkshore, making these territories dangerous and untamed ground for any wayward scout."},kw={"ashwood depot","darkshore","forsaken","goblin","horde","kaldorei"},rel={"zone:darkshore","topic:alliance","topic:horde","topic:forsaken","topic:goblin"},src={"Ashwood Depot"}}
E["subzone:auberdine"] = {t="subzone",n="Auberdine",z="darkshore",s="Auberdine is a coastal night elven port town on the gloomy shores of Darkshore, serving as the Alliance's primary maritime gateway to northern Kalimdor. Sheltered beneath overcast skies and pine-covered bluffs, it connects the island home of Teldrassil to the Eastern Kingdoms while serving as an administrative haven against the encroaching wilderness.",h="Auberdine is a coastal night elven port town on the gloomy shores of Darkshore, serving as the Alliance's...",sec={{t="Gateway to Northern Kalimdor",b="Resting along the shores of the Veiled Sea, Auberdine is the only major settlement to successfully endure in modern Darkshore. Unlike the secluded treetop cities of Teldrassil, Auberdine looks outward, serving as the Alliance's busiest port in the north. Regular ships sail between here and Menethil Harbor in the Eastern Kingdoms, while local ferries run to Rut'theran Village at the boughs of the World Tree. Because of its trade role, Auberdine embraces a more cosmopolitan air than traditional elven enclaves; visitors find lamps illuminating stone-laid streets, bilingual signs in Darnassian and Common, and outland merchants including dwarves and gnomes mingling among the low-slung, arched timber houses.",sp=0},{t="A Beleaguered Haven",b="Governed by elder Thundris Windweaver and the Auberdine Village Council, the town coordinates the defence of Darkshore alongside the local Sentinels. Despite its role as a vital trade hub, highborn denizens of Darnassus often look askance at Auberdine, viewing its population of traders, fishermen, and outsiders as misfits. The town endures relentless regional perils: aggressive murlocs raid the fishing boats along the strand, corrupted Blackwood furbolgs press from the south, and foul magic seeping down from Felwood agitates the local wildlife.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the ships in Auberdine go?",a="The docks connect northern Kalimdor to the wider Alliance world. One pier hosts the ferry to Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil, while another berths large ocean-going vessels that sail across the Great Sea directly to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"auberdine boats","where do boats go","auberdine travel"}},{q="Who rules Auberdine?",a="Auberdine is stewarded by elder Thundris Windweaver alongside the Auberdine Village Council. The settlement's defense is overseen by the Sentinels, led locally by Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea.",al={"auberdine leader","who is in charge","village council"}},{q="Why are there dwarves and humans living in a night elf town?",a="Because Auberdine serves as the Alliance's chief port on northern Kalimdor, foreign traders, craftsmen, and travelers arrive here first. Dwarves have set up a local smithy to service visiting ships and travellers, making the town unusually diverse and welcoming compared to traditional night elf settlements.",al={"non elves in auberdine","why dwarves here"}},{q="Why do night elves from Darnassus look down on Auberdine?",a="Traditionalists and isolationists in Darnassus often regard Auberdine as tainted by worldly commerce and outland influences. Some orthodox elves consider its people to be misfits, and the bustling trade hub is viewed as poorly suited to strictly traditional druidic lifestyles.",al={"darnassus auberdine rivalry","auberdine outcasts"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For kaldorei venturing out from Teldrassil, Auberdine is the first true mainland hub where ancient tradition meets the strange ways and bustling industry of younger Alliance allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="This port is the lifeblood of Alliance travel and supply lines into northern Kalimdor, ensuring steady logistics between Stormwind, Ironforge, and Darnassus."},kw={"auberdine","boat","darkshore","docks","kaldorei","lighthouse","port","sentinels","thundris windweaver"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:rut-theran-village","subzone:menethil-harbor","quest:4761","zone:darnassus","topic:sentinels","quest:4740","topic:alliance"},src={"Auberdine"}}
E["subzone:auberdine-coast"] = {t="subzone",n="Auberdine Coast",z="darkshore",s="The Auberdine Coast stretches along the western shoreline of Darkshore, bordering the night elven port town of Auberdine. Its docks serve as the primary maritime lifeline connecting northern Kalimdor to Teldrassil and the Eastern Kingdoms. Travellers and fishermen walk its sands beneath misty, shadowed skies.",h="The Auberdine Coast stretches along the western shoreline of Darkshore, bordering the night elven port town...",sec={{t="A Lifeline on the Veiled Sea",b="Running along the edge of Darkshore, the Auberdine Coast hosts the sprawling timber piers of Auberdine. Through these docks, night elven vessels transport supplies and pilgrims between Rut'theran Village at the foot of Teldrassil and mainland Kalimdor, alongside Alliance ships sailing west from Menethil Harbor. Away from the bustle of the harbor, the cold waters wash ashore driftage, beached sea creatures, and wreckage brought in by the treacherous tides of the Veiled Sea.",sp=0},{t="Washed Ashore",b="The shoreline is rarely peaceful. Beached thresher carcasses and giant sea turtles attract scavengers, while murlocs and naga prowl the shoals. Local night elves regularly scout the sandbars to investigate strange strandings, salvage nautical supplies, and keep the trade lane secure from sea monsters lurking just beneath the surf.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Auberdine Coast?",a="It is the seaside strip of Darkshore surrounding the night elf settlement of Auberdine. Its most prominent features are the long wooden docks handling ferry traffic to Teldrassil and the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"auberdine coast info","darkshore coastline","where is auberdine coast"}},{q="Where do the ships at the coast lead?",a="The ships departing from the Auberdine piers connect travelers north to Rut'theran Village at the roots of Teldrassil, and east across the Great Sea to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"auberdine boat destination","where do boats go","auberdine ferries"}},{q="Why are there beached sea creatures along the shore?",a="The waters off Darkshore have grown increasingly disturbed, casting dead threshers, turtles, and other deep-sea beasts onto the beaches. Night elf scholars and hunters frequently investigate the strandings to understand what is afflicting the sea life.",al={"dead sea beasts darkshore","beached sea creatures","sea creature carcasses"}},{q="What threats wander these beaches?",a="Aside from aggressive crab and crawler species, the shoreline frequently sees incursions by Greymist murlocs and prowling naga, as well as hostile water elementals and reef predators.",al={"auberdine coast enemies","shore dangers","beach mobs"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The coast houses the primary Alliance naval foothold in northern Kalimdor, making it an essential hub for travelers crossing the sea from Wetlands or Teldrassil.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, this shoreline is a crucial gateway linking their sacred home on Teldrassil with the ancestral lands of mainland Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","auberdine coast","beached creatures","darkshore","docks","piers","veiled sea"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:alliance"},src={"Auberdine Coast"}}
E["subzone:auberdine-refugee-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Auberdine Refugee Camp",z="darkshore",s="Auberdine Refugee Camp is a makeshift settlement established on the forested outskirts of Auberdine in Darkshore. As darkness and corruption creep along the coast, displaced kaldorei and travelers gather here under the watchful eyes of Sentinel scouts. It serves as a precarious sanctuary for those forced from their homes along the wild shore.",h="Auberdine Refugee Camp is a makeshift settlement established on the forested outskirts of Auberdine in...",sec={{t="Haven on the Coast",b="Perched near the coastal paths of Darkshore, this refugee camp offers a fragile safe haven amidst mounting turmoil. Displaced night elves and wandering refugees shelter under canvas tents and ancient trees, relying on Kaldorei Sentinels and vigilant archers to keep hostile wildlife and coastal threats at bay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there refugees in Darkshore?",a="With creeping corruption, aggressive wildlife, and coastal hazards unsettling northern Kalimdor, local travelers and night elves displaced from threatened homesteads seek safety near established defenses.",al={"why a refugee camp","who are these refugees","darkshore refugees"}},{q="Who guards the refugee camp?",a="Kaldorei Sentinels and archers maintain a perimeter around the settlement, keeping aggressive beasts and encroaching perils from overrunning the makeshift camp.",al={"who protects the camp","auberdine camp guards","camp defenders"}},{q="Is the camp safe for travelers?",a="The camp is firmly under night elf stewardship and aligned with the Alliance, offering friendly harbor to allies, while remaining deeply cautious of outsiders.",al={"is it safe here","alliance friendly"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Seeing your kin huddled under makeshift awnings is a sober reminder that even the ancient forests of northern Kalimdor are under siege by unseen corruptions.",["faction:Alliance"]="A vital bastion of hospitality, this camp offers safety for Alliance adventurers traveling the windswept and dangerous shores of Darkshore."},kw={"auberdine","camp","darkshore","kaldorei","night elf","refugee","sentinels"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:sentinels"},src={"Auberdine Refugee Camp"}}
E["subzone:bashal-aran"] = {t="subzone",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Bashal'Aran is an ancient Highborne ruin situated in northern Darkshore, just east of Auberdine. Once a flourishing sister city to Ameth'Aran before the Great Sundering, the site now crawls with demonic satyrs and grells feeding on lingering arcane magic, while a solitary elven ghost remains trapped by a centuries-old curse.",h="Bashal'Aran is an ancient Highborne ruin situated in northern Darkshore, just east of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Shattered Twin City",b="Before the Great Sundering broke ancient Kalimdor ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara settled favored Highborne subjects in the twin towns of Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran. Governed by the powerful mage Athrikus Narassin, the cities boasted splendid markets and temples dedicated to Elune. When the Well of Eternity collapsed, the cataclysm laid both settlements to waste. For reasons lost to time, Athrikus used his arcane mastery to bind his own second-in-command, the mage Asterion, into a moonstone seal within Bashal'Aran. Even after his physical body perished, Asterion's ghost remained shackled to the ruined shrine.",sp=0},{t="Demonic Infestation",b="In the modern day, the crumbled stones of Bashal'Aran have been claimed by vile squatters: the Deth'ryll satyrs and mischievous grells. Drawn by residual magic clinging to the ancient masonry, these corrupted beings drink in the lingering energy to bolster their foul arts. Though they swarm the broken courtyards and terrorize travelers along Darkshore's forest paths, the demons give a wide berth to the central shrine where Asterion endures his endless vigil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Bashal'Aran before it was destroyed?",a="Bashal'Aran was a magnificent Kaldorei city established by Queen Azshara for favored Highborne aristocrats before the Great Sundering. Along with its twin city of Ameth'Aran, it was governed by the mage-lord Athrikus Narassin.",al={"bashal'aran history","who built bashal'aran","what was this ruin"}},{q="Who is the ghost wandering the shrine?",a="The spirit is Asterion, a respected Highborne warrior-mage who once oversaw both Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran. He was mysteriously betrayed and bound to the site with a moonstone seal by his governor, Athrikus Narassin, enduring imprisonment even beyond mortal death.",al={"who is asterion","bashal'aran ghost","why is there a ghost"}},{q="Why are satyrs inhabiting the ruins?",a="Satyrs and grells were lured to Bashal'Aran by the remnants of powerful arcane energy left behind by the ancient Highborne. They feast on these lingering magical emanations to empower their dark demonic magic.",al={"why are there satyrs here","deth'ryll satyr lore","grells at bashal'aran"}},{q="How does Bashal'Aran relate to Ameth'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran were sister cities governed together under Queen Azshara's reign. Asterion made frequent journeys between both settlements to tend to the people's needs before both were shattered by the Sundering.",al={"ameth'aran connection","twin cities darkshore","ameth'aran bashal'aran"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Bashal'Aran serves as a tragic reminder of the reckless arcane hubris that doomed the ancient Kaldorei Empire and paved the way for demonic corruption.",["class:Mage"]="The moonstone ward binding Asterion showcases the terrifying permanence and potency of pre-Sundering Highborne spellcraft."},kw={"ameth'aran","asterion","athrikus narassin","bashal'aran","darkshore","deth'ryll","grell","highborne","satyr"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","npc:asterion","quest:954","topic:highborne","topic:satyr","topic:elune","topic:alliance"},src={"Bashal'Aran"}}
E["subzone:bashal-aran-collapse"] = {t="subzone",n="Bashal'Aran Collapse",z="darkshore",s="The Bashal'Aran Collapse is a subterranean cavern system lying beneath the fractured ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore. Positioned far below the surface within the Maw of the Void, it shelters ancient Highborne spirits and the lingering remnants of an empire torn apart by cataclysmic ruin.",h="The Bashal'Aran Collapse is a subterranean cavern system lying beneath the fractured ruins of Bashal'Aran in...",sec={{t="Sunken Splendor",b="When the great Sundering tore ancient Kalimdor asunder ten thousand years ago, the grand city of Bashal'Aran was shattered and swallowed into the earth. The deepest fragment of these ruins came to rest within the subterranean chasm known as the Maw of the Void. Here, submerged stone corridors and isolated ledges echo with the quiet torment of the past. Cenarion druids, including Bielara Ivyshroud, cautiously observe this sunken cavern, bearing witness to restless Forlorn Highborne phantoms who still wander the damp stonework, hopelessly bound to the memories of their fallen kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Shadows of the Void",b="Deep within the spiraling path of the collapse stands Telarius Voidstrider, a renegade demon hunter entrenched on the cliffs above. Telarius occupies the shattered foundation performing dark, solitary rituals. Those who breach his subterranean redoubt find him clutching the Writings of the Dark Herald, ominous texts pointing to foul designs festering beneath Darkshore's fractured soil. While the Cenarion Circle maintains a tenuous watch over the subterranean pool below, the dread magics woven in the depths remain an active menace to the coast.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Bashal'Aran Collapse?",a="It is a subterranean subzone located beneath the Maw of the Void in Darkshore. It consists of the sunken, shattered remnants of ancient Bashal'Aran that fell deep into the earth during the Great Sundering.",al={"bashal aran collapse","what is this place","sunken ruins darkshore"}},{q="How do you leave the cavern?",a="Bielara Ivyshroud, a member of the Cenarion Circle stationed near the subterranean pool of water, assists travelers trapped in the depths by teleporting them back to the surface of Darkshore.",al={"how to get out","teleport out","bielara ivyshroud"}},{q="Who is Telarius Voidstrider?",a="Telarius Voidstrider is a demon hunter perched on a rocky cliff along the spiraling cavern path. He enacts mysterious and sinister rituals amidst the ancient ruins while carrying the Writings of the Dark Herald.",al={"demon hunter darkshore","telarius voidstrider","who is the demon hunter"}},{q="Why are there ghosts haunting the collapse?",a="The ghostly apparitions are Forlorn Highborne whose lives were abruptly ended when Bashal'Aran collapsed ten thousand years ago. Their souls remain tethered to the ruins, doomed to re-enact their final moments in the dark.",al={"forlorn highborne","why are there ghosts here","spirits in darkshore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the collapse is a painful reminder of the Hubris of Queen Azshara's court, where the shattered remains of their ancestral home now lie buried beneath the earth.",["class:Druid"]="Druids of the Cenarion Circle venture into these sunken hollows to observe the corrupted lingering spirits and assist those who stumble into the chasm."},kw={"bashal'aran","bielara ivyshroud","collapse","darkshore","highborne","maw of the void","telarius voidstrider"},rel={"subzone:maw-of-the-void","quest:954","zone:darkshore","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:highborne"},src={"Bashal'Aran Collapse"}}
E["subzone:bitterstone-quarry"] = {t="subzone",n="Bitterstone Quarry",z="darkshore",s="Bitterstone Quarry is an excavation site located in central Darkshore, lying in the hills east of Auberdine. Tucked between coastal cliffs and ancient forest slopes, the rocky pit serves as a rugged landmark amid the misty wilderness.",h="Bitterstone Quarry is an excavation site located in central Darkshore, lying in the hills east of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Carved Hollow in the Mist",b="Carved into the rugged terrain of Darkshore east of Auberdine, Bitterstone Quarry represents an uncharacteristic gouge in lands otherwise jealously guarded by the night elves. The quarry cuts into the stony hillside, nestled north of the rocky coastline and the churning currents of the shore. Travelers moving through the misty expanse often have to navigate the jagged rock faces and hazardous ridges surrounding the excavation.",sp=0},{t="Wilds and Strife",b="The quarry sits amid a precarious landscape where encroaching perils constantly brush against night elf territory. The rugged ridges nearby are stalked by territorial wildlife, including the ferocious wildkin Madfeather roaming between the quarry and the turbulent shore. As conflicts ripple across northern Kalimdor, such mineral-rich hollows stand as contested ground caught between natural predators and outside eyes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Bitterstone Quarry located?",a="Bitterstone Quarry is located in central Darkshore, set inland into the rocky hills east of Auberdine and north of the coastal vortex waters.",al={"bitterstone quarry location","where is bitterstone quarry","how to find bitterstone quarry"}},{q="What threats wander around the quarry?",a="The rugged wilderness bordering the quarry is home to fierce local wildlife, notably the enraged wildkin known as Madfeather, who prowls the rocky trails between the quarry and the nearby shoreline.",al={"bitterstone quarry monsters","who is in bitterstone quarry","madfeather location"}},{q="Why do the night elves care about this site?",a="The night elves are deeply protective of Darkshore's pristine wilderness. Any quarrying or intrusion into the natural stone disrupts the balance of the ancient coastal woodlands.",al={"why night elves care bitterstone","kaldorei in bitterstone quarry"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Sentinels of Darkshore, rocky scars like Bitterstone Quarry represent an ongoing challenge to preserve the wild coast against foreign intrusion and rampaging beasts.",["profession:Mining"]="The exposed rock faces of the quarry cut deep into Darkshore's coastal bedrock, providing visible mineral veins amidst the thick moss and roots."},kw={"auberdine","bitterstone quarry","darkshore","kaldorei","madfeather","quarry"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Bitterstone Quarry"}}
E["subzone:blackwood-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackwood Camp",z="darkshore",s="Blackwood Camp is a small furbolg settlement nestled along the coast of Darkshore south of Auberdine. Once peaceful allies of the night elves, the Blackwood tribe residing here has fallen into violent madness under a sinister demonic taint.",h="Blackwood Camp is a small furbolg settlement nestled along the coast of Darkshore south of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Tribe in Madness",b="The Blackwood furbolgs long coexisted peacefully with the night elves of Auberdine, sharing reverence for nature and guarding the coastal woodlands. In recent times, however, an unnatural corruption seeped into their settlement, twisting their minds and turning them fiercely aggressive toward all outsiders. Driven to desperation and rage, the tribe attacked travelers and severed all ties of kinship. Night elf sentinels and druids watch the settlement with deep grief, searching for a way to break the dark hold gripping their former friends.",sp=0},{t="The Satyr's Shadow",b="The true cause of the tribe's downfall is not natural madness, but the malevolent scheming of a satyr hiding in the shadows of Darkshore. Through foul demonic magic, the creature poisoned the furbolgs' minds, binding them in misery and hostility. Night elf ritualists seek to slay the offending satyr and enact ancient purification rites, hoping to cleanse the Blackwood tribe before their corruption becomes irreversible.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the furbolgs at Blackwood Camp hostile?",a="The Blackwood furbolgs are suffering from a dark demonic curse cast by a local satyr. This foul magic warped their minds, driving them to blind aggression against anyone who approaches.",al={"why are blackwood furbolgs attacking","are blackwoods evil","blackwood camp hostile"}},{q="Can the Blackwood furbolgs be saved?",a="Yes. Night elf allies in Darkshore provide rituals to confront and slay the corrupting satyr, allowing sacred purifications to cleanse the furbolgs of their madness.",al={"can you cure blackwood furbolgs","saving the blackwood tribe"},sp=1},{q="Where is Blackwood Camp located?",a="The camp lies along the coast of Darkshore, situated south of the port town of Auberdine.",al={"blackwood camp location","where is blackwood camp"}},{q="What was the tribe's historical relationship with the night elves?",a="Before the Third War and the recent wave of demonic taint, furbolg tribes such as the Blackwood maintained peaceful and cooperative relations with the night elves, sharing mutual respect for the natural world.",al={"were furbolgs friendly","night elf furbolg history"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, the madness at Blackwood Camp is a tragedy hitting close to home, as former allies of the wilderness have fallen victim to lingering demonic corruption.",["class:Druid"]="Druids view the affliction of the Blackwood tribe as a spiritual infection demanding both decisive martial action against demonic manipulators and compassionate cleansing rites."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood camp","blackwood furbolg","corruption","darkshore","satyr"},rel={"quest:4763","zone:darkshore","topic:furbolg","topic:satyr","subzone:auberdine","topic:night-elf"},src={"Blackwood Camp"}}
E["subzone:blackwood-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackwood Den",z="darkshore",s="Blackwood Den is a corrupted furbolg encampment nestled in the southern reaches of Darkshore near the border of Ashenvale. Once a peaceful dwelling, the cave and surrounding camps have fallen into madness alongside the rest of the Blackwood tribe. A lone night elf scout named Volcor sits trapped within the cavern, awaiting aid from Auberdine.",h="Blackwood Den is a corrupted furbolg encampment nestled in the southern reaches of Darkshore near the border...",sec={{t="A Corrupted Stronghold",b="Situated near the southern border where Darkshore meets Ashenvale, Blackwood Den consists of a winding network of crude camps and a rocky cave. The Blackwood furbolgs who dwell here have succumbed to the pervasive corruption gripping the region, turning violently hostile toward outsiders. Deep inside the den's cave, the night elf Volcor remains pinned down and endangered by the aggressive tribe, desperately needing assistance from scouts and travelers dispatched from Auberdine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Blackwood Den?",a="Blackwood Den is a furbolg settlement and cave complex located in far southern Darkshore, close to the border of Ashenvale. It serves as a base for the corrupted Blackwood furbolg tribe.",al={"what is blackwood den","blackwood hold","where is blackwood den"}},{q="Who is inside the cave at Blackwood Den?",a="Inside the cave sits Volcor, a night elf who has become trapped behind enemy lines. Travelers who encounter him must coordinate with allies in Auberdine to stage an escape and guide him safely out of the den.",al={"who is trapped in the cave","who is volcor","elf in blackwood den"}},{q="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?",a="The Blackwood furbolgs have fallen victim to the dark corruption spreading across Darkshore and Kalimdor following the Third War. The affliction has driven them into a maddened frenzy, causing them to attack any outsiders on sight.",al={"why are blackwood furbolgs aggressive","are blackwood furbolgs evil","corrupted furbolgs darkshore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Auberdine, the loss of the Blackwood tribe to corruption is a tragic development, and rescuing Volcor from their clutches is an urgent duty to keep their people safe along the southern road.",["class:Druid"]="Druids mourn the fall of the furbolgs, who were once steadfast protectors of the wilderness, and view the madness at Blackwood Den as another painful symptom of Kalimdor's tainted nature."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","blackwood den","blackwood hold","darkshore","furbolg","volcor"},rel={"zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","subzone:auberdine","npc:volcor","topic:furbolg","topic:night-elf"},src={"Blackwood Den"}}
E["subzone:blazing-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Blazing Strand",z="darkshore",s="The Blazing Strand is a scorched stretch of coastline along western Darkshore, situated just west of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran. In the current era, the misty shore stands desolate against the waves of the Veiled Sea.",h="The Blazing Strand is a scorched stretch of coastline along western Darkshore, situated just west of the...",sec={{t="A Mist-Shrouded Shore",b="Running along the gloomy coast of Darkshore down from the heights of Ameth'Aran, this beach sits quiet beneath the perpetual coastal gloom. While Darkshore struggles under the corrupting influence of twisted wildlife and restless kaldorei spirits, the strand remains an open border between the haunted ancient ruins inland and the chilly waters of the Veiled Sea.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Blazing Strand located?",a="The Blazing Strand borders the western coast of Darkshore, lying directly west of the ancient highborne ruins of Ameth'Aran.",al={"blazing strand location","where is blazing strand","find blazing strand"}},{q="Is the Blazing Strand dangerous?",a="While the shoreline itself is quiet compared to the haunted ruins of Ameth'Aran, travelers should still watch out for wandering shoreline wildlife and the hostile spirits that drift out from the nearby ruins.",al={"dangers at blazing strand","enemies on blazing strand"}},{q="Why is it named the Blazing Strand?",a="In ancient times, coastal navigation and fiery beacons often marked the jagged kaldorei shorelines. Though quiet today under Darkshore's perpetual overcast gloom, it retains its historic name alongside the nearby ruins.",al={"blazing strand name origin","why called blazing strand"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Auberdine, the coastline is a quiet perimeter just below the mournful spirits haunting Ameth'Aran."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","beach","blazing strand","coast","darkshore"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran"},src={"Blazing Strand"}}
E["subzone:cinderfall-grove"] = {t="subzone",n="Cinderfall Grove",z="darkshore",s="Cinderfall Grove is a wooded area situated along the rugged coastline of Darkshore, nestled north of the ancient ruins of Bashal'Aran. In the present era, the grove stands quiet beneath the misty canopy, though the shifting tensions along northern Kalimdor leave the woodlands perpetually vulnerable. It remains an untamed stretch of wilderness watching over the shadowy shores.",h="Cinderfall Grove is a wooded area situated along the rugged coastline of Darkshore, nestled north of the...",sec={{t="A Misty Coastal Wilderness",b="Positioned just north of the ancient highborne grounds of Bashal'Aran, Cinderfall Grove rests amidst the perpetual gloom of Darkshore. Tall, mist-draped pines define the landscape, their roots digging deep into soil saturated with age-old kaldorei history and coastal dampness. While tranquil compared to the blighted ruins and corrupted dens scattered across the shore, travelers passing along the coastal road must remain wary, as the wild beasts of the forest and roving threats constantly test the boundaries of civilization.",sp=0},{t="Frontier of Kalimdor",b="Darkshore as a whole serves as the front doorstep of night elven territory on mainland Kalimdor. With settlements like Auberdine managing fragile coastal trade and defense, woodlands like Cinderfall Grove stand on the periphery of that vigilance. The surrounding lands are continually harassed by lingering demonic corruption, furbolg unrest, and the encroaching interests of foreign powers seeking timber and foothold in the north.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Cinderfall Grove located?",a="Cinderfall Grove lies in the misty coastal region of Darkshore, situated just north of the ruins of Bashal'Aran and east of the main road heading toward northern reaches.",al={"cinderfall location","where is cinderfall","cinderfall grove map"}},{q="Who controls Cinderfall Grove?",a="In 25 ADP, the territory falls under the broader ancestral domain of the night elves of Darkshore, though the wilderness itself is largely untamed and wild rather than formally fortified.",al={"who owns cinderfall","cinderfall grove faction"}},{q="What nearby landmarks should I look out for?",a="Just south of the grove lies the tragic highborne ruin of Bashal'Aran, haunted by ancient spirits and twisted satyrs, while Auberdine rests further down the coast to the southwest.",al={"cinderfall landmarks","what is near cinderfall"}},{q="Is Cinderfall Grove dangerous to wander through?",a="Yes. Darkshore's native wildlife, including prowling moonstalkers and bears, can be perilous to unwary explorers, and ancient curses linger heavily across the surrounding lands.",al={"is cinderfall grove safe","cinderfall dangers"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, protecting these ancient coastal forests from corruption, deforestation, and outside encroachment is a matter of natural duty and sacred guardianship.",["class:Druid"]="The damp groves of Darkshore are deeply connected to the natural balance, where druids constantly work to soothe agitated spirits and forest creatures."},kw={"auberdine","bashal'aran","cinderfall grove","darkshore","grove","kaldorei","kalimdor","woods"},rel={"zone:darkshore","quest:954","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},src={"Cinderfall Grove"}}
E["subzone:cliffspring-falls"] = {t="subzone",n="Cliffspring Falls",z="darkshore",s="Cliffspring Falls marks the dramatic origin of Darkshore's vital Cliffspring River, tumbling down from the eastern cliffs into the coastal forest. Long celebrated as the principal source of clean drinking water for the region, its waters have recently fallen victim to a foul, spreading taint. The subterranean cavern feeding the waterfall has become infested with hostile naga and shadowy Twilight's Hammer cultists.",h="Cliffspring Falls marks the dramatic origin of Darkshore's vital Cliffspring River, tumbling down from the...",sec={{t="A Tainted Source",b="Pouring out from caverns perched high in the rocky bluffs along Darkshore's eastern border, Cliffspring Falls feeds the Cliffspring River, which winds westward across the woods to empty into the sea. Traditionally, this cascade provided the purest drinking water for local night elf settlements. In recent times, however, the waters have turned foul and murky, spreading sickness and ecological decay throughout the river basin. Investigating naturalists have discovered that the cave network at the falls' headwaters is overrun by vile naga and dark cultists, who plot in the shadows while demonic corruption from neighboring Felwood threatens to seep through the highland bedrock.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Cliffspring Falls?",a="Cliffspring Falls is a major waterfall in eastern Darkshore that forms the headwaters of the Cliffspring River. It historically supplied the primary fresh drinking water for the surrounding forest.",al={"cliffspring falls","cliffwater falls","what is cliffspring falls"}},{q="Why is the water coming from the falls corrupted?",a="Two sinister influences are suspected: demonic taint seeping through the mountains from corrupted Felwood, and the active presence of Twilight's Hammer cultists and hostile naga lurking inside the caverns feeding the cascade.",al={"why is water tainted","cliffspring river corruption","corrupted water"}},{q="Who occupies the caverns behind the falls?",a="The caverns above and behind the waterfall are infested with hostile naga slithering through the flooded chambers, alongside cultists belonging to the apocalyptic Twilight's Hammer.",al={"who is in the caves","cliffspring cave mobs","who lives in cliffspring falls"}},{q="Why is Cliffspring Falls so important to Darkshore?",a="The Cliffspring River cuts through the center of northern Darkshore. Because it serves as the principal source of fresh water, its poisoning directly endangers wildlife, ancient groves, and local night elf habitations.",al={"why does darkshore care","cliffspring importance"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, the corruption of Cliffspring Falls is an environmental and spiritual crisis, polluting the vital waters that nourish Darkshore's ancient forests.",["class:Druid"]="Druids of the Cenarion Circle monitor the river closely, striving to diagnose and cleanse the unnatural rot that threatens to choke the wilderness."},kw={"auberdine","cliffspring falls","cliffspring river","cliffwater falls","darkshore","felwood","naga","twilight's hammer","water corruption"},rel={"quest:6122","quest:4762","zone:darkshore","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga","zone:felwood","topic:alliance"},src={"Cliffspring Falls"}}
E["subzone:delaryn-s-demise"] = {t="subzone",n="Delaryn's Demise",z="darkshore",s="Delaryn's Demise is a somber stretch along the windswept coastline of Mist's Edge in Darkshore. In the early days of 25 ADP, this quiet western shore remains largely untouched, known primarily to local Sentinels and fishermen walking the foggy sands. To those walking Darkshore's coastline today, it is merely another parcel of the mist-shrouded frontier.",h="Delaryn's Demise is a somber stretch along the windswept coastline of Mist's Edge in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Quiet Coastline",b="Situated west of the beachheads near Mist's Edge, this shore sits under the shadow of ancient Kalimdor's fog. In the current era, the coastline is dominated by stranded sea creatures, encroaching murlocs, and the vigil of the night elven Sentinels who patrol south from Auberdine. While later legends speak of tragic confrontations on this very soil, travelers today find only the relentless crashing of the western tides against cold stones.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Delaryn's Demise?",a="It refers to a specific stretch of shoreline along Mist's Edge in northern Darkshore. In the era of 25 ADP, it is simply an unassuming coastal expanse watched over by local night elf sentries and scavenged by coastal wildlife.",al={"what is this place","delaryns demise location","where is delaryn's demise"}},{q="Who is Delaryn?",a="Delaryn Summermoon is a night elf Sentinel officer whose fate becomes tied to the shoreline in later historical accounts. Currently, the shore shows none of the grim aftermath tied to her name.",al={"who is delaryn","delaryn summermoon","delaryn lore"}},{q="Why is the area named this way if nothing has happened yet?",a="Cartographers and chroniclers occasionally mark landmarks in advance of or reflecting tragic conflicts. For an adventurer in the current year, the sands are merely part of the untamed coastline of Darkshore.",al={"why is it named delaryns demise","why called demise","delaryns demise name origin"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The wild, mist-covered beaches of Darkshore remain sacred sovereign territory of the kaldorei, guarded fiercely against hostile intruders from the sea.",["faction:Alliance"]="Controlling the coastal waters and keeping communication open between Auberdine and neighboring territories is vital for maintaining Darnassus's security."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","delaryn","delaryn's demise","kaldorei","lor'danel","mist's edge","sentinels"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:mist-s-edge","topic:sentinels","quest:940"},src={"Delaryn's Demise"}}
E["subzone:dredge"] = {t="subzone",n="Dredge",z="darkshore",s="The Dredge refers to coastal dredging rigs and mechanical barges operated in northern Kalimdor's waters. These industrial operations, typical of enterprising goblin engineering outfits like the Venture Company, focus on dredging seabeds and extracting materials from the coast.",h="The Dredge refers to coastal dredging rigs and mechanical barges operated in northern Kalimdor's waters.",sec={{t="Industrial Encroachment",b="Along the shores of Kalimdor, goblin-built dredges and harvesting platforms occasionally appear off the wild coasts. Utilizing crude pumps, heavy mechanical scaffolding, and industrial extraction tools, outfits such as the Venture Company deploy these rigs to sift coastal sands and extract raw materials. To the night elves guarding their ancestral forests, such machinery represents an invasive, polluting intrusion into nature's pristine waters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Dredge?",a="It is a floating industrial platform or barge constructed with heavy goblin mechanics, designed to dredge coastal waters and extract resources from the seabed.",al={"what is dredge","dredge darkshore","goblin dredge"}},{q="Who operates these dredges?",a="They are typical of goblin operations, notably unregulated commercial cartels like the Venture Company, who exploit natural waters without regard for local wilderness.",al={"who runs dredge","who built dredge","goblin platform"}},{q="Why do the night elves oppose them?",a="The night elves view industrial machinery and offshore drilling rigs as unnatural polluters that blight the pristine coastline and disrupt sacred waters.",al={"night elf dredge","darkshore dredge lore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The mechanical clamor and polluting run-off of coastal dredging are an insult to the pristine waters of northern Kalimdor.",["profession:Engineering"]="The massive iron framework and specialized pumping apparatus reflect heavy-duty goblin marine engineering."},kw={"darkshore","dredge","goblin","platform","veiled sea","venture company"},rel={"zone:darkshore","topic:goblin","topic:venture-company","topic:alliance"},src={"Dredge"}}
E["subzone:eye-of-the-vortex"] = {t="subzone",n="Eye of the Vortex",z="darkshore",s="Located near the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran, the Eye of the Vortex is a turbulent convergence point where elemental air whips into violent tempests along the Darkshore coastline. The wild squalls and churning winds here pose an ongoing hazard to travelers and mark a place where the primal forces of nature remain unstable.",h="Located near the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran, the Eye of the Vortex is a turbulent convergence point where...",sec={{t="A Tempest Unleashed",b="Situated near the haunted elven ruins of Ameth'Aran, the Eye of the Vortex sits amidst the battered landscape of Darkshore. Here, raging winds and restless air elementals swirl into an unrelenting squall. The volatile currents threaten any who stray too close, howling through the twisted pines and battering the crags with unrestrained natural fury.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Eye of the Vortex?",a="It is a turbulent area in central Darkshore near the ruins of Ameth'Aran, characterized by violent, swirling winds and hostile air elementals.",al={"eye of the vortex lore","what is this vortex","darkshore vortex"}},{q="Where is the Eye of the Vortex located?",a="It lies in the wilderness of central Darkshore, situated just near the ancient night elven ruins of Ameth'Aran.",al={"vortex location","where is eye of the vortex","darkshore eye location"}},{q="Why are there air elementals here?",a="The elemental spirits of wind and weather are drawn to areas of severe turbulence and unrest, feeding into the squall that churns along Darkshore's craggy hills.",al={"elementals in darkshore","why air elementals","wind elementals here"}},{q="Is the vortex dangerous to travel through?",a="Yes. The swirling gales and hostile elemental denizens make traversing the immediate area treacherous for unwary travelers and couriers heading through Darkshore.",al={"is the vortex safe","can i walk into the vortex","vortex danger"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The wild, uncontrolled winds here are a reminder of how easily nature can slip out of balance when primal forces churn unchecked.",["class:Shaman"]="The agitation of the elemental wind spirits at this site offers a clear sign of elemental discord disturbing the coast."},kw={"ameth'aran","cyclarus","darkshore","elementals","eye of the vortex","tornado","vortex"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran"},src={"Eye of the Vortex"}}
E["subzone:forlorn-crossing"] = {t="subzone",n="Forlorn Crossing",z="darkshore",s="Forlorn Crossing is a lonely junction of paths nestled in northern Darkshore. Flanked by ancient ruins and shadowed coastlines, this road intersection serves as a transit point and staging ground for night elf defenders watching the wilderness.",h="Forlorn Crossing is a lonely junction of paths nestled in northern Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Waystation in the Mist",b="Situated between the haunted ruins of Bashal'Aran, the mist-choked Gloomtide Strand, and the encroaching forest wilds, Forlorn Crossing earns its grim name from the sorrowful atmosphere perpetual in Darkshore. As travelers and patrols journey between the coast and the inland groves, the intersection marks a rare clear waypoint amidst overgrown ancient lands.",sp=0},{t="Defenders of the Wilds",b="Because Darkshore faces corruption, aggressive wildlife, and ancient ghosts lingering in nearby ruins, vital path junctions require steady vigilance. Kaldorei Sentinels, archers, and allied druids frequently monitor such waypoints to maintain safe passage between night elven settlements and threatened ritual grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Forlorn Crossing located?",a="Forlorn Crossing is an intersection of roads in Darkshore, located in the vicinity of the ancient ruins of Bashal'Aran and near routes leading toward the Gloomtide Strand.",al={"forlorn crossing location","where is forlorn crossing","find forlorn crossing"}},{q="Why is it named Forlorn Crossing?",a="Like much of Darkshore, the region carries the weight of ancient tragedy dating back to the Great Sundering. Positioned near sorrowful ruins haunted by highborne spirits, the lonely road junction reflects the somber mood of the northern coast.",al={"forlorn crossing name meaning","why forlorn crossing"}},{q="Who guards or patrols Forlorn Crossing?",a="The area is watched over by night elven forces, including Sentinels, archers, huntresses, and druidic caretakers guarding against local threats and keeping travel routes viable.",al={"who protects forlorn crossing","forlorn crossing guards"}},{q="What nearby landmarks connect to this crossroads?",a="Paths from the crossroads connect travelers between the ruined settlement of Bashal'Aran, coastal shores like Gloomtide Strand, and nearby forest groves.",al={"paths near forlorn crossing","landmarks near forlorn crossing"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Every path through Darkshore cuts across sacred ground scarred by the Sundering, making regular surveillance by Sentinels and druids essential to preserving balance.",["faction:Alliance"]="Controlling and securing crossroad junctions ensures that Alliance supply lines and couriers can travel safely between northern coastal outposts."},kw={"bashal'aran","crossroads","darkshore","forlorn crossing","gloomtide strand","kaldorei","sentinels"},rel={"zone:darkshore","quest:954","subzone:gloomtide-strand","subzone:cinderfall-grove","subzone:ashwood-depot","topic:sentinels","topic:druid","topic:alliance"},src={"Forlorn Crossing"}}
E["subzone:gloomtide-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Gloomtide Strand",z="darkshore",s="Gloomtide Strand is a stretch of western Darkshore coastline facing the Veiled Sea. In these tranquil yet somber years, it remains a quiet coastal shore under the ancient guardianship of the night elves, undisturbed by large military encroachments.",h="Gloomtide Strand is a stretch of western Darkshore coastline facing the Veiled Sea.",sec={{t="A Fog-Shrouded Shore",b="Stretching along the misty perimeter of Darkshore, this coastal strand looks out across cold tides and wind-battered sands. Like much of the surrounding territory, it sits under the quiet watch of the night elves, who dwell among the brooding woodlands and misty beaches of northern Kalimdor. Though remote, the shoreline shares in Darkshore's characteristic gloom, washed by cold waters and framed by ancient coastal pines.",sp=0},{t="Winds of the Veiled Sea",b="Darkshore's beaches are frequently buffeted by squalls and littered with flotsam carried ashore from shipwrecks and ancient ruins. The strand remains an isolated and wild stretch of coastline, untouched by the larger military encampments that dominate more contested frontiers of the world.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Gloomtide Strand?",a="Gloomtide Strand is a coastal area along western Darkshore, characterized by cold ocean tides, overcast skies, and the wild, untamed nature of northern Kalimdor's shoreline.",al={"gloomtide strand info","what is this beach","where is gloomtide strand"}},{q="Who controls Gloomtide Strand?",a="The strand lies within the traditional ancestral lands of the night elves, who hold domain over Darkshore as part of the Alliance.",al={"who owns gloomtide strand","is gloomtide alliance","night elf territory"}},{q="Is there a settlement or camp here?",a="No permanent settlement exists along this open shore. It remains a wild stretch of coastal wilderness typical of Darkshore's fog-laden beaches.",al={"camp at gloomtide","town at gloomtide strand","inns near gloomtide"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The shores of Darkshore are part of your ancestral lands, watched over by the Sentinels and the druids who seek balance with Kalimdor's wilderness.",["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshore represents a vital night elf stronghold along northern Kalimdor's coast, securing the waterways below Teldrassil."},kw={"beach","coast","darkshore","gloomtide strand","kalimdor","strand","veiled sea"},rel={"zone:darkshore","topic:sentinels","topic:druid","topic:alliance"},src={"Gloomtide Strand"}}
E["subzone:grove-of-the-ancients"] = {t="subzone",n="Grove of the Ancients",z="darkshore",s="The Grove of the Ancients is a sacred night elven sanctuary set amidst old temple ruins in southeastern Darkshore. Nestled beside the Wildbend River, this serene haven serves as a gathering ground for nature spirits and is watched over by the venerable Ancient of Lore, Onu.",h="The Grove of the Ancients is a sacred night elven sanctuary set amidst old temple ruins in southeastern...",sec={{t="Sanctuary of the Wildbend",b="Tucked away near the southeastern mountains of Darkshore, the Grove of the Ancients stands as a peaceful haven surrounded by aged temple stones. Through its heart flows the surging Wildbend River, providing a quiet refuge amidst a coastline increasingly plagued by corruption and restless wildlife. The grove serves as a meeting place for the Circle of Ancients, where nature spirits and kaldorei tend to the delicate balance of the forest.",sp=0},{t="Keepers and Watchers",b="The focal presence within the grove is Onu, a towering Ancient of Lore who observes the land's shifting fortunes and offers ancient wisdom to passing travelers. Alongside Onu, wandering merchants and slumbering druids find rest beneath the boughs. Though quiet, the grove lies close to territorial furbolg camps to the southeast, making it an essential frontier outpost for Alliance sentinels and druids monitoring southern Darkshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Grove of the Ancients?",a="The grove is located in the southeastern region of Darkshore, nestled against the mountain foothills near the banks of the Wildbend River.",al={"grove of ancients location","where is grove of the ancients","onu location"}},{q="Who is Onu?",a="Onu is a wise Ancient of Lore residing in the grove. He acts as an elder guide, watching over the southeastern woods and advising druids and travelers attempting to mend the balance of Darkshore.",al={"who is onu","ancient in grove of ancients","tree guy darkshore"}},{q="What is the Circle of Ancients?",a="The Circle of Ancients is an assembly of great nature spirits and ancient treants who gather at the grove to commune, share knowledge, and discuss the welfare of the wild lands.",al={"circle of ancients","ancients meeting darkshore"}},{q="Are there dangers near the grove?",a="While the grove itself is a safe sanctuary with friendly guardians and merchants, hostile wildlife and territorial furbolg encampments lie just across the river and to the southeast.",al={"grove threats","is grove safe","monsters near grove"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The grove is a revered natural sanctuary, offering druids a direct connection to the wisdom of the Ancient of Lore Onu and the spirits of the forest.",["race:NightElf"]="Surrounded by ancient temple ruins and tended by nature spirits, the grove serves as a solemn reminder of long-standing kaldorei harmony with the land."},kw={"ancient of lore","circle of ancients","darkshore","grove of the ancients","onu","wildbend river"},rel={"quest:952","zone:darkshore","subzone:wildbend-river","topic:druid","subzone:auberdine","topic:furbolg"},src={"Grove of the Ancients"}}
E["subzone:kor-gar"] = {t="subzone",n="Kor'gar",z="darkshore",s="Kor'gar is a Horde encampment established within Darkshore, claiming ground formerly known as Blackwood Den. It serves as a fortified forward foothold for orcish forces in the ancient night elf territory.",h="Kor'gar is a Horde encampment established within Darkshore, claiming ground formerly known as Blackwood Den.",sec={{t="A Horde Foothold in Darkshore",b="Carved out of the territory historically held by the Blackwood furbolgs, Kor'gar stands as a fortified encampment for the Horde in northern Kalimdor. Where furbolgs once inhabited Blackwood Den, orcish grunts, shamans, and wolfriders now guard palisades and patrol the surrounding woods, asserting their presence in the shadowed reaches of Darkshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Kor'gar before it became an outpost?",a="Kor'gar was originally known as Blackwood Den, a settlement and burrow belonging to the local Blackwood tribe of furbolgs before Horde forces occupied and fortified the position.",al={"what was kor'gar","kor'gar origin","blackwood den kor'gar"}},{q="Who controls Kor'gar?",a="The outpost is manned by Horde forces under the command of Commander Drald, defended by Kor'gar grunts, wolfriders, and shamans.",al={"who leads kor'gar","kor'gar commander","horde outpost leader darkshore"}},{q="Are the Blackwood furbolgs still around the area?",a="Yes. Blackwood warriors and skirmishers, led by figures like Elder Brownpaw, remain active in the wilderness directly outside the outpost's boundaries.",al={"blackwood furbolgs kor'gar","furbolgs near kor'gar","elder brownpaw"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Kor'gar represents a vital strategic foothold carved straight out of hostile wilderness along the Darkshore coastline.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance forces and night elves view the presence of Kor'gar as an intrusion upon native lands and a direct threat to the region's delicate balance."},kw={"blackwood den","commander drald","darkshore","elder brownpaw","furbolg","kor'gar","korgar"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:blackwood-den","topic:furbolg","topic:horde"},src={"Kor'gar"}}
E["subzone:long-wash"] = {t="subzone",n="Long Wash",z="darkshore",s="The Long Wash is a bleak, windswept stretch of beach in Darkshore running just south of Auberdine toward the ruins of Ameth'Aran. Gloomy and scattered with marine carcasses and flotsam, the shoreline has recently grown dangerous due to an increasing presence of hostile murlocs.",h="The Long Wash is a bleak, windswept stretch of beach in Darkshore running just south of Auberdine toward the...",sec={{t="A Gloomy Shoreline",b="Despite its name, the Long Wash is actually the shortest distinct stretch of coastline in Darkshore. It sits under the region's perpetual overcast skies, an expanse of damp sand littered with flotsam, beached driftwood, and the carcasses of sea creatures washed up by the Veiled Sea. While local crabs and snails comb through the surf, travelers southward from Auberdine must tread cautiously: murloc tribes have established camps along the water's edge, aggressively attacking anyone encroaching on their scavenged territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Long Wash located?",a="The Long Wash stretches along the coastline of Darkshore immediately south of Auberdine, extending down until it lies roughly west of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran.",al={"long wash location","where is long wash","how to find long wash"}},{q="Why is it called the Long Wash?",a="A 'wash' is an archaic term referring to the portion of a shore swept and washed over by ocean waves. Ironically, despite being named the Long Wash, it is actually the shortest distinct stretch of beach in Darkshore.",al={"why long wash","long wash meaning","what does wash mean"}},{q="What threats can be found along the Long Wash?",a="The main danger along the Long Wash comes from aggressive murloc clans that have begun gathering in greater numbers along the coastline, alongside territorial tide crawlers and other beach wildlife.",al={"dangers in long wash","long wash mobs","what lives in long wash"}},{q="Why are there so many dead creatures on the beach?",a="The rough surf of the Veiled Sea and the encroaching corruption affecting the coastal waters of Darkshore regularly wash up debris, ship drift, and dying marine life onto the damp sands of the shore.",al={"dead animals long wash","beached creatures darkshore beach","flotsam on the shore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, the encroaching murlocs along the Long Wash represent another sign of unsettling imbalance creeping right up to the doorstep of their main port."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","darkshore","long wash","murloc","tide crawler","veiled sea"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:murloc"},src={"Long Wash"}}
E["subzone:lor-danel"] = {t="subzone",n="Lor'danel",z="darkshore",s="Lor'danel is a quiet night elf settlement nestled in the far northern reaches of Darkshore. Unlike the shadowy, storm-grey gloom that covers much of the coast, this coastal haven is framed by vibrant green trees and nourished by a sacred moonwell. Connected directly to Rut'theran Village and the broader Kaldorei lands by hippogryph routes, it stands as a peaceful outpost of Darnassus.",h="Lor'danel is a quiet night elf settlement nestled in the far northern reaches of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Verdant Outpost on the Foggy Coast",b="Situated at the northern edge of Darkshore, Lor'danel offers an abrupt and welcoming contrast to the somber coastline to the south. Where the rest of Darkshore lies draped in coastal gloom and mist-drenched grey beaches, the earth and flora surrounding Lor'danel flourish in bright, verdant greens. The settlement serves as an essential vantage along the sea, featuring an inn for wayfarers, a moonwell blessed by Elune, and a well-traveled flight roost connecting mainland Darkshore directly to Rut'theran Village and the world tree Teldrassil above.",sp=0},{t="Sentinels of the Shore",b="Though Lor'danel borders the open sea, it lacks maritime piers or heavy harbor works, relying instead on vigilant sentinels, glaive throwers, and roosting hippogryphs for its safety and transit. Darnassian huntresses and Sentinels patrol its perimeter, monitoring the rugged coastline for any threats drifting southward from the open waters or emerging from the troubled wilderness of northern Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Lor'danel located?",a="Lor'danel is located on the northern coast of Darkshore, resting along the seaside just south across the water from Teldrassil.",al={"lordanel location","where is lordanel","how to get to lordanel"}},{q="Why does Lor'danel look different from the rest of Darkshore?",a="While most of Darkshore is choked with perpetual sea haze, grey sands, and ancient gnarled forests, the grove around Lor'danel remains rich, vibrant, and lushly green, sheltered beneath sacred boughs and cared for around a dedicated moonwell.",al={"why is lordanel green","lordanel trees green","darkshore vs lordanel"}},{q="Does Lor'danel have a dock for ships?",a="No. Despite being nestled on the shoreline, Lor'danel has no harbor or docks. Instead, all travel across the sea to Rut'theran Village and other outposts is conducted through its hippogryph roost.",al={"lordanel harbor","is there a boat in lordanel","lordanel docks"}},{q="How is Lor'danel defended?",a="The settlement is protected by Darnassian Sentinels, vigilant protectors, archers, and heavy glaive throwers stationed to repel coastal beasts or hostile intruders.",al={"who defends lordanel","lordanel sentinels","guards at lordanel"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves traversing the coast of Darkshore, Lor'danel is a familiar refuge, maintaining direct hippogryph connections back to Rut'theran Village beneath Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="The moonwell resting within Lor'danel offers druids and followers of the Cenarion Circle a serene sanctuary to replenish their spirits and commune with nature."},kw={"darkshore","lor'danel","lordanel","moonwell","rut'theran","sentinels","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:rut-theran-village","zone:darnassus","subzone:auberdine","subzone:astranaar","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},src={"Lor'danel"}}
E["subzone:lor-danel-landing"] = {t="subzone",n="Lor'danel Landing",z="darkshore",s="Lor'danel Landing designates a stretch of northern Darkshore's coastline along Mist's Edge, sitting just west of the night elven settlement of Lor'danel. In this era, it remains an untamed northern shore of the Veiled Sea under the watchful watch of the local night elves.",h="Lor'danel Landing designates a stretch of northern Darkshore's coastline along Mist's Edge, sitting just west...",sec={{t="The Northern Shoreline",b="Situated at the northern limits of Darkshore, the strand known as Lor'danel Landing borders the misty waters of the Veiled Sea along Mist's Edge. The surrounding territory is ancient night elf land, closely situated to the small haven of Lor'danel and shielded by the wild, fog-draped forests of northern Kalimdor. Travelers wandering these reaches find cold sand, crashing waves, and the ever-vigilant presence of Sentinel scouts keeping watch against outside intrusion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Lor'danel Landing located?",a="Lor'danel Landing is located in far northern Darkshore, running along the coastline of Mist's Edge directly west of the settlement of Lor'danel on the Veiled Sea.",al={"lordanel landing location","where is lordanel landing","finding lordanel landing"}},{q="Who controls this stretch of coast?",a="The land falls firmly within night elven territory. The Sentinels of Darnassus watch over northern Darkshore, and the nearby settlement of Lor'danel serves as a haven for the kaldorei and the Alliance.",al={"who owns lordanel landing","is lordanel landing horde or alliance","who controls mist's edge"}},{q="What threats can be found near Lor'danel Landing?",a="Beyond natural coastland wildlife and stray sea creatures washed ashore by the tides of the Veiled Sea, northern Darkshore is regularly menaced by aggressive reef scavengers, furbolgs, and coastal beasts.",al={"threats near lordanel","dangers at lordanel landing"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The strand safeguards the approaches to northern Darkshore and stands as a peaceful threshold of ancient kaldorei coastal domain.",["faction:Alliance"]="Positioned just across the water from Teldrassil, this coastal shore helps secure the perimeter around Lor'danel and the northern sea routes."},kw={"darkshore","kaldorei","lor'danel landing","lordanel","mist's edge","sentinels","veiled sea"},rel={"subzone:lor-danel","subzone:mist-s-edge","zone:darkshore","topic:sentinels","topic:alliance"},src={"Lor'danel Landing"}}
E["subzone:master-s-glaive"] = {t="subzone",n="Master's Glaive",z="darkshore",s="The Master's Glaive is an ancient, unsettling landmark tucked into southwestern Darkshore where a colossal adamantine weapon stands impaled in a massive petrified skull. Long revered by local night elves as a sacred mystery, the site now swarms with Twilight's Hammer cultists drawn to the lingering malevolence of an ancient entity.",h="The Master's Glaive is an ancient, unsettling landmark tucked into southwestern Darkshore where a colossal...",sec={{t="A Monument of an Ancient Clash",b="Rising out of the Darkshore earth, the Master's Glaive is a massive blade buried deep into the horned skull of Soggoth the Slitherer, a herald of the Old Gods. According to ancient tablets uncovered by the dwarven Explorers' League nearby, the site preserves the climax of a primordial battle between Soggoth and twenty titan-forged stone giants. The largest giant, Kronn, allowed Soggoth's thrashing tendrils to snare him so he could pull himself close enough to drive his titanic blade directly into the monster's skull. Today, the impaled monolith stands as a stark, petrified monument to that titanic struggle.",sp=0},{t="Dark Excavations",b="Though the site was held in solemn reverence by night elves for generations, sinister forces have recently seized the grounds. Fanatics of the Twilight's Hammer cult have established a camp around the sunken carcass, carving out trenches and uncovering petrified ribs. Drawn by whispers beneath the stone, the cultists obsessively study the remains and commune with the malevolent power that still clings to the ancient herald, seeking to revive or harness whatever fell essence slumbers within the earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the massive weapon stuck in the skull?",a="The blade is the colossal sword of Kronn, the greatest of twenty titan-forged stone giants sent to destroy Soggoth the Slitherer. Kronn permitted himself to be seized by the herald's tendrils to draw close enough to plunge the massive adamantine weapon into the monster's skull, ending the battle.",al={"what is the sword","masters glaive sword","who put the sword there"}},{q="What creature's skull is buried here?",a="The enormous skull belongs to Soggoth the Slitherer, a herald of the Old Gods who waged war against the titans and their stone giant servants in primordial times before being struck down and petrified.",al={"what died here","soggoth skull","who is buried at masters glaive"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer cult gathered here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cult worships the Old Gods and their ancient servants. They have overrun the Master's Glaive to excavate Soggoth's petrified remains, drawn by the lingering dark power and hoping to revive the fallen herald.",al={"why are cultists here","twilight hammer darkshore","what are cultists digging"}},{q="Who knows about the history of this site?",a="Onu, the Ancient of Lore residing in Darkshore, recognizes the site as the resting place of an ancient lord of the earth and bids investigators to look into it. Meanwhile, dwarven archaeologists of the Explorers' League at Remtravel's Excavation uncovered stone tablets detailing the battle between Soggoth and the titan giants.",al={"who studies the glaive","how do we know about soggoth"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For generations, night elves treated the strange petrified monument as a solemn holy place, making the recent intrusion of the Twilight's Hammer cult an intolerable defilement of Darkshore's sacred grounds.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarven members of the Explorers' League at nearby Remtravel's Excavation take keen interest in the site, as the tablets they uncovered link the monument directly to the works and constructs of the ancient Titans."},kw={"darkshore","kronn","master's glaive","old god","remtravel","slitherer","soggoth","stone giant","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:944","zone:darkshore","subzone:remtravel-s-excavation","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","topic:titan","topic:explorers-league","topic:night-elf"},src={"Master's Glaive"}}
E["subzone:maw-of-the-void"] = {t="subzone",n="Maw of the Void",z="darkshore",s="The Maw of the Void is a violent, churning whirlpool located in Darkshore that swallows draining waters from across the region. Plunging into its roaring vortex pulls travelers deep beneath the earth into the cavernous Bashal'Aran Collapse. In recent days, the site has drawn dangerous attention from water elementals and sinister cultists.",h="The Maw of the Void is a violent, churning whirlpool located in Darkshore that swallows draining waters from...",sec={{t="The Churning Abyss",b="Situated southeast of Lor'danel, the Maw of the Void is a terrifying natural maelstrom where regional runoff, including the torrents of the Cliffspring River, empties into an abyss. Rather than battering swimmers against rocks, the vortex acts as a subterranean siphon, plunging anyone brave or foolish enough to leap inside safely down into the subterranean ruins of the Bashal'Aran Collapse. However, unrest has surrounded the vortex as violent water elementals stir, drawing dark opportunists from the Twilight's Hammer who seek to harness the chaotic aquatic forces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happens if I jump into the Maw of the Void?",a="Plunging into the center of the vortex sucks you downward in a fierce rush of water, depositing you safely at the bottom of the cavernous Bashal'Aran Collapse without suffering fall damage.",al={"jump in whirlpool","survive maw of the void","fall into whirlpool"}},{q="Where does the water draining into the whirlpool come from?",a="Much of the zone's drainage flows directly into the abyss, most notably the runoff carrying down from the Cliffspring River.",al={"water source","where does water come from"}},{q="Who is occupying the area around the vortex?",a="The whirlpool is swarming with agitated water elementals, including the powerful Hydrath, alongside Twilight's Hammer cultists like Twilight Enforcers and Wavebreakers who have claimed the surrounding shores.",al={"enemies at whirlpool","who is at maw of the void","cultists at maw"}},{q="Where does the Maw lead once you fall through?",a="The whirlpool washes you directly into the subterranean depths known as the Bashal'Aran Collapse, an ancient cavern buried beneath the ruins of the surface.",al={"maw exit","where do you land"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The chaotic water elementals gathering around the Maw indicate grave unrest among the spirits of Darkshore, particularly with cultists bending the elements to their will.",["race:NightElf"]="The corruption and disruption around ancient ruins like Bashal'Aran and its draining waters threaten the fragile balance of Darkshore."},kw={"bashal'aran collapse","darkshore","hydrath","maw of the void","twilight's hammer","vortex","whirlpool"},rel={"subzone:bashal-aran-collapse","zone:darkshore","topic:twilight-s-hammer","quest:4762","quest:954","subzone:lor-danel"},src={"Maw of the Void"}}
E["subzone:mist-s-edge"] = {t="subzone",n="Mist's Edge",z="darkshore",s="Mist's Edge is the long, windswept coastline spanning the western border of Darkshore. Shrouded in damp ocean fog, these gray beaches are littered with shipwrecks, colossal sea creature remains, and roving packs of crabs and murlocs.",h="Mist's Edge is the long, windswept coastline spanning the western border of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Fog-Shrouded Shore",b="Running along the western edge of Darkshore, Mist's Edge is defined by damp sands, rocky tidepools, and perpetual coastal fog. The beach is a graveyard of the sea, littered with decaying sea behemoths, drift timber, and the shattered ribs of wrecked vessels. While seemingly barren, the coastline teems with shoreline scavengers, notably aggressive crabs and territorial murloc tribes that nest in the surf.",sp=0},{t="Wrecks and Scavengers",b="The treacherous waters off the coast of Darkshore have claimed countless vessels, depositing shattered hulls and discarded cargo all along the sands. Night elf sentinels and local scavengers keep a wary eye on the coastline, where opportunistic murloc encampments frequently menace travelers heading up and down the coast from Auberdine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Mist's Edge?",a="Mist's Edge is the expansive stretch of coastline that forms the entire western shore of Darkshore, known for its cold ocean fog, shipwrecks, and beached sea creatures.",al={"mists edge","darkshore beach","what is mists edge"}},{q="What threats wander this coast?",a="The shoreline is heavily populated by hostile coastal crabs and aggressive murloc packs that dwell in primitive camps along the water's edge.",al={"mists edge monsters","what attacks you on the beach","darkshore coast dangers"}},{q="Why are there so many shipwrecks and skeletons here?",a="The harsh currents, hidden reefs, and heavy mist off Darkshore make navigation hazardous, driving ships onto the rocks. Similarly, ocean currents often wash the remains of massive leviathans and sea creatures ashore.",al={"darkshore beached whales","shipwrecks mists edge","giant bones darkshore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Auberdine, Mist's Edge represents both a vital maritime boundary and an untamed border plagued by invading murlocs and foul scavengers."},kw={"auberdine","beach","coast","crabs","darkshore","mist's edge","murloc","shipwreck"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc"},src={"Mist's Edge"}}
E["subzone:moonspray"] = {t="subzone",n="Moonspray",z="darkshore",s="The Moonspray is an Alliance transport vessel belonging to the Kaldorei Fleet. It provides essential maritime passage across the waters separating mainland Kalimdor from the great World Tree, Teldrassil.",h="The Moonspray is an Alliance transport vessel belonging to the Kaldorei Fleet.",sec={{t="A Vital Island Ferry",b="Graceful in design like all night elven ships, the Moonspray serves as an indispensable lifeline between the docks of Auberdine on Darkshore's coast and Rut'theran Village at the root of Teldrassil. Traversing the Veiled Sea, the transport carries adventurers, couriers, and vital provisions between the isolated night elf sanctuary in the crown of the World Tree and the ancient mainland of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Moonspray travel?",a="The Moonspray sails between the harbor town of Auberdine in Darkshore and Rut'theran Village, which sits at the oceanic base of Teldrassil.",al={"moonspray route","where does moonspray go","moonspray destination"}},{q="Who owns and operates this ship?",a="The Moonspray is a night elven vessel operating as part of the Kaldorei Fleet, sailing under the banner of the Alliance.",al={"who sails the moonspray","kaldorei fleet moonspray","is moonspray alliance"}},{q="Why is this ferry route important?",a="Teldrassil is an island perched high in the sea off the northwestern coast of Kalimdor. Ships like the Moonspray are the primary means of transferring troops, provisions, and travelers across the water to the mainland.",al={"why take moonspray","teldrassil boat"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves leaving Teldrassil to explore the wider world, the Moonspray is often the very vessel that carries them from their secluded home to the mainland for the first time.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Moonspray forms a key transport link connecting the Alliance's primary coastal hub in northern Kalimdor with the isolated capital of Darnassus."},kw={"auberdine","boat","darkshore","ferry","kaldorei fleet","moonspray","rut'theran village","teldrassil","transport"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","subzone:rut-theran-village","zone:darkshore","quest:940"},src={"Moonspray"}}
E["subzone:moontouched-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Moontouched Den",z="darkshore",s="Moontouched Den is a sheltered wildkin hollow tucked into the misty forest slopes of Darkshore, east of Auberdine. Blessed by Elune, the sanctuary is home to sacred wildkin who guard ancient nests and mystical fetishes. However, like much of the coastline, dark and troubling forces have begun disturbing the tranquility of the grove.",h="Moontouched Den is a sheltered wildkin hollow tucked into the misty forest slopes of Darkshore, east of...",sec={{t="Sanctuary of the Wildkin",b="Moontouched Den serves as a woodland sanctuary for wildkin, the feathered and antlered guardians tied intimately to the moon goddess Elune. Tucked into the forested ridges east of Auberdine, the enclave features scattered wildkin nests, carved natural fetishes, and secluded burrows. Druids and priests of Elune revere these creatures as embodiment of nature's balance, but travelers must exercise caution, as wildkin aggressively defend their nests from all outside encroachment.",sp=0},{t="Fading Balance",b="Across Darkshore, lingering corruption from the Third War and the sundering of Felwood has cast long shadows over the indigenous wildlife. While Moontouched Den remains a dedicated home for these majestic beast-kin, the growing agitation of the woodlands has put the wildkin on edge, leaving local night elves watchful of any shifts that might further corrupt or disturb this sacred ground.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Moontouched Den?",a="Moontouched Den is a wildkin hollow located in the hills east of Auberdine in Darkshore. It is recognized by the numerous nests, fetishes, and winding pathways carved out by resident wildkin.",al={"moontouched den","where is moontouched den","darkshore owlkin cave"}},{q="What creatures live here?",a="The den is populated by wildkin, also known as owlbeasts or moonkin. These feathered protectors are sacred to the night elves and the goddess Elune, fiercely guarding their nests against intruders.",al={"what lives in moontouched den","owlkin in darkshore","wildkin darkshore"}},{q="Why are the wildkin sacred to night elves?",a="Wildkin are believed to have been created or blessed directly by Elune to safeguard pristine natural groves. Night elves and druids regard them with reverence as living manifestations of lunar and natural balance.",al={"why do night elves like wildkin","elune owlkin","sacred wildkin"}},{q="Are the wildkin in the den friendly to travelers?",a="No. Despite their sacred connection to Elune, wildkin are extremely territorial and will attack anyone who wanders too close to their young, nests, or sacred grounds.",al={"are owlkin hostile","can i visit moontouched den","wildkin aggro"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druids view wildkin as sacred kinsfolk created by Elune, making any corruption or disruption within Moontouched Den a solemn matter for the Cenarion Circle.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves hold the wildkin of Darkshore in deep reverence, respecting their isolated enclaves while warily monitoring them for signs of the corruption spreading along the coast."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","elune","moontouched den","owlbeast","owlkin","wildkin"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine"},src={"Moontouched Den"}}
E["subzone:nazj-vel"] = {t="subzone",n="Nazj'vel",z="darkshore",s="Nazj'vel is a coastal cavern and settlement carved into the shoreline far south along Darkshore's Twilight Shore. Inhabited by the serpentine naga, the rocky outcropping serves as a base for their incursions along the misty Kalimdor coast.",h="Nazj'vel is a coastal cavern and settlement carved into the shoreline far south along Darkshore's Twilight...",sec={{t="A Serpent Enclave",b="Situated off the far southern reaches of Darkshore along the Twilight Shore, Nazj'vel is a coastal sanctuary established by the naga. Emerging from the deep ocean trenches, these serpentine descendants of the ancient Highborne have claimed the caverns and shoreline ruins for themselves, threatening any travelers or night elf sentinels who venture south toward the border with Ashenvale. The damp caves echo with the chanting of their priestesses, making it one of the most perilous points along the western coast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Nazj'vel located?",a="Nazj'vel lies far to the south along Darkshore's coastline, situated just off the edge of the Twilight Shore before reaching the southern borders of the region.",al={"nazj'vel location","where is nazjvel","how to find nazjvel"}},{q="Who controls Nazj'vel?",a="The caverns and surrounding waters of Nazj'vel are firmly in the hands of the naga, who defend their outpost against any land-dwellers who stray too close.",al={"who lives in nazjvel","nazjvel enemies","what mobs are at nazjvel"}},{q="Why are the naga here in Darkshore?",a="The naga have established strongholds along various coasts of Kalimdor, scavenging sunken ruins, recovering ancient relics of their former empire, and harassing night elf settlements.",al={"why are naga in darkshore","naga darkshore lore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Darkshore, Nazj'vel is a bitter reminder of the Highborne's tragic descent and an active menace along the region's southern borders."},kw={"coastal cave","darkshore","kalimdor","naga","nazj'vel","nazjvel","twilight shore"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:twilight-shore-darkshore","topic:naga","topic:night-elf"},src={"Nazj'vel"}}
E["subzone:remtravel-s-excavation"] = {t="subzone",n="Remtravel's Excavation",z="darkshore",s="Remtravel's Excavation is an archaeological dig site located in the southern reaches of Darkshore. Established by the dwarven Prospector Remtravel, the expedition recently struck ancient subterranean ruins, inadvertently unearthing hostile troggs and stone golems that quickly overran the quarry.",h="Remtravel's Excavation is an archaeological dig site located in the southern reaches of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Quarry Overrun",b="Prospector Remtravel came to Darkshore in search of relics of the distant past, establishing an ambitious dig far from the safety of Auberdine. While excavating ancient strata, his team unearthed a swarm of subterranean Gravelflint troggs alongside hulking stone golems buried beneath the earth. The site was instantly transformed from a scholarly quarry into a hazard zone, scattering the miners and leaving Remtravel scrambling to retrieve his most promising findings.",sp=0},{t="The Missing Fossil",b="Before the excavation descended into chaos, Remtravel had uncovered a rare fossil radiating curious mystic properties. In the panic of the trogg onslaught—and hindered by his notorious absent-mindedness—the prospector misplaced the valuable relic amid the sprawling dirt pits. Venturing down into the dig to recover it means braving both the vicious troggs and the ancient automatons awakened by the pickaxes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Remtravel's Excavation?",a="It is an archaeological dig site in southern Darkshore founded by Prospector Remtravel, an explorer searching for ancient fossils and subterranean relics.",al={"what is this place","darkshore dig site","remtravel site"}},{q="Why are there troggs here?",a="Dwarven miners dug too deeply into the earth and breached subterranean caverns, awakening a local tribe known as the Gravelflint troggs alongside dormant stone golems.",al={"why troggs in darkshore","gravelflint troggs","where did troggs come from"}},{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="He is a dwarven archaeologist leading the excavation. Known for his keen eye for artifacts as well as his absent-minded nature, he lost track of a key fossil when his dig was attacked.",al={"who is remtravel","prospector remtravel lore"}},{q="What kind of relic was discovered here?",a="Remtravel discovered an unusual fossil imbued with strange, mystic properties shortly before the troggs surged from the lower depths.",al={"what did they find","remtravel fossil","mystic fossil"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarven explorers of the Explorers' League are well known for seeking the secrets of the past, though unearthing dangerous troggs in foreign lands often leads to familiar headaches.",["race:NightElf"]="The kaldorei generally observe the deep meddling of Alliance dwarven picks with skepticism, especially when careless delving awakens wild troggs on Darkshore's ancient soil."},kw={"darkshore","excavation","fossil","golem","gravelflint","prospector","remtravel","trogg"},rel={"npc:prospector-remtravel","zone:darkshore","topic:trogg"},src={"Remtravel's Excavation"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-auberdine"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Auberdine",z="darkshore",s="Auberdine is the bustling coastal port town of Darkshore, serving as the primary maritime link between Kalimdor's northern forests and the outside world. Though distant tales speak of ominous portents, the settlement remains whole and vital under the stewardship of the night elves.",h="Auberdine is the bustling coastal port town of Darkshore, serving as the primary maritime link between...",sec={{t="The Northern Haven",b="In Darkshore, Auberdine stands as the central haven for travelers, druids, and sentinels safeguarding northern Kalimdor. Its docks provide steady passage across the waters to Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil and south to the wetlands of the Eastern Kingdoms. The town's moonwell provides spiritual solace to all who venerate Elune, and its craftsmen supply travelers braving the haunted shoreline.",sp=0},{t="Whispers of Ruin",b="While ominous seers speak in hushed tones of terrible calamities that could one day shatter the port to ash and sunken timbers, no such devastation has befallen the town. Auberdine stands proud against the misty gloom of Darkshore, its towers intact, its docks alive with cargo, and its community resolute.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Is Auberdine in ruins?",a="No. Auberdine is completely intact and serves as the primary quest hub and harbor for the Alliance along the coast of Darkshore.",al={"auberdine ruined","ruins of auberdine classic","destroyed auberdine"}},{q="What services are available in Auberdine?",a="The town features an inn, hippogryph roost, blacksmithing forge, profession trainers, and a moonwell. Ferries run regularly from its long wooden piers.",al={"auberdine vendors","auberdine trainers","what is in auberdine"}},{q="Where do the ships in Auberdine sail?",a="Vessels dock here carrying passengers to and from Rut'theran Village beneath Teldrassil, as well as Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"auberdine boat","auberdine docks destination","where does auberdine boat go"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine is the first major mainland settlement welcoming young night elves after they leave the boughs of Teldrassil.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine acts as the vital strategic bridgehead connecting Alliance territories across the seas to northern Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","docks","ferry","kaldorei","moonwell","port"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ruins of Auberdine"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-lornesta"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Lornesta",z="darkshore",s="The Ruins of Lornesta are the submerged remains of an ancient kaldorei settlement resting along the fog-laden coast of Darkshore. Long swallowed by the tides, the site is now infested by serpentine Darkscale naga led by Lady Janira.",h="The Ruins of Lornesta are the submerged remains of an ancient kaldorei settlement resting along the fog-laden...",sec={{t="Sunken Remnants",b="Situated along the Darkshore coastline, the Ruins of Lornesta stand as another tragic casualty of the ancient Sundering. Once an exquisite night elf settlement, its marble pillars and foundations have succumbed to the relentless saltwater surf. Today, the flooded arches and shallow pools harbor hazardous vegetation like fuming toadstools, making the drowned enclave as treacherous underfoot as it is bleak to behold.",sp=0},{t="The Darkscale Threat",b="Rather than lying peaceful in decay, Lornesta has been occupied by a forward contingent of Darkscale naga scouts commanded by Lady Janira. Slithering out from the coastal depths, these serpentine abominations utilize the drowned stonework as an entrenched staging ground, posing a direct threat to travelers and night elf scouts traversing the coastal paths of Darkshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Ruins of Lornesta?",a="The Ruins of Lornesta are the half-submerged remains of an ancient night elf settlement located on the coast of Darkshore, swallowed by the ocean thousands of years ago.",al={"lornesta history","what is lornesta","ruins of lornesta"}},{q="Who controls the ruins right now?",a="The ruins are currently occupied by Darkscale naga scouts who answer to their local commander, Lady Janira.",al={"who lives at lornesta","enemies at ruins of lornesta","naga darkshore"}},{q="Who is Lady Janira?",a="Lady Janira is the leader of the Darkscale naga warband entrenched among the sunken pillars and waters of the Ruins of Lornesta.",al={"janira","lady janira darkshore"}},{q="What dangerous flora grows in the ruins?",a="Fuming toadstools grow wild throughout the brackish waters and damp stones of the flooded ruins.",al={"plants in lornesta","fuming toadstool"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Seeing the ancestral halls of Lornesta half-drowned and crawling with the vile naga makes the ongoing defense of Darkshore all the more urgent.",["faction:Alliance"]="The naga encamped at Lornesta represent a constant threat of flanking raids against nearby Alliance trade routes along the misty Darkshore coast."},kw={"darkscale","darkshore","fuming toadstools","lady janira","lornesta","naga","ruins of lornesta"},rel={"zone:darkshore","topic:naga","topic:sentinels","topic:alliance"},src={"Ruins of Lornesta"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-mathystra"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Mathystra",z="darkshore",s="The Ruins of Mathystra are the crumbled remnants of an ancient night elven city sitting along the northern coast of Darkshore. Shattered during the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, the coastal ruins are now overrun by hostile Stormscale naga and prowled by elusive Ghost Sabers.",h="The Ruins of Mathystra are the crumbled remnants of an ancient night elven city sitting along the northern...",sec={{t="A City Cast into the Sea",b="Ten millennia ago, Mathystra stood as a bustling night elven settlement, home to high-ranking Highborne nobility. When the Well of Eternity collapsed during the Great Sundering, cataclysmic waves shattered the coastal city, toppling its grand marble arches and washing much of its stonework into the sea. The surviving night elves abandoned the ruined city in favor of smaller woodland villages further south, leaving Mathystra's sunken courtyards and cracked foundations to the relentless coastal elements.",sp=0},{t="The Stormscale Vipers and Ghost Sabers",b="In the modern era, Mathystra has become a dangerous domain ruled by the Stormscale naga. Creeping up from the dark depths, these serpentine abominations guard the broken halls fiercely, driving away any travelers who venture north past the Tower of Althalaxx. Among the shattered flagstones, ancient Highborne relics still lie half-buried in sand and seafoam. Daring young night elves sometimes brave the naga vipers hoping to recover remnants of their lost heritage, often contending not only with serpent blades but also with the spectral Ghost Sabers that stalk the broken streets.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What used to be here before the ruins?",a="Mathystra was a thriving night elven city built during the height of the ancient Highborne empire. It was shattered and largely drowned ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering, when the Well of Eternity exploded and cleaved Kalimdor apart.",al={"mathystra history","who built mathystra","what was mathystra"}},{q="Who controls the Ruins of Mathystra right now?",a="The ruins are currently occupied by the Stormscale naga, who have emerged from the sea to claim the sunken pavilions and coastlines. They aggressively attack any land-dwellers who intrude upon their territory.",al={"who lives in mathystra","mathystra mobs","who is at mathystra"}},{q="What are Ghost Sabers?",a="Ghost Sabers are ethereal, translucent felines that haunt the ruined stonework of Mathystra. Hunters often seek them out along the coast, though disturbing the ancient figurines in the area is known to draw these spirits out from the shadows.",al={"ghost saber mathystra","glowing cat darkshore","ghost sabers"}},{q="Why do night elves visit these ruins today?",a="Young night elves and scholars occasionally venture into the ruins to recover ancient Highborne relics left behind after the Sundering. However, the presence of fierce Stormscale naga makes recovering these historical treasures extremely perilous.",al={"mathystra relics","why go to mathystra"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Mathystra stands as a somber monument to the hubris of the ancient Highborne, whose reckless sorcery brought cataclysm down upon their own grand coastal settlements.",["class:Hunter"]="The translucent Ghost Sabers prowling among the rubble of Mathystra are renowned beasts for beastmasters seeking a striking companion with ties to the spirit world."},kw={"darkshore","ghost saber","great sundering","highborne","mathystra","naga","ruins of mathystra","stormscale"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","topic:naga","topic:highborne","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ruins of Mathystra"}}
E["subzone:shatterspear-pass"] = {t="subzone",n="Shatterspear Pass",z="darkshore",s="Shatterspear Pass is a rugged, hidden mountain corridor tucked away along the eastern ridges of Darkshore. Long concealed and largely inaccessible to standard travelers, it serves as the secluded gateway leading into the isolated enclave of Shatterspear Vale.",h="Shatterspear Pass is a rugged, hidden mountain corridor tucked away along the eastern ridges of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Hidden Mountain Thoroughfare",b="Tucked away high in the towering mountain range separating northern Darkshore from Mount Hyjal, Shatterspear Pass is an inhospitable, perilous path. In this quiet era, the passage remains heavily isolated and sealed off from the broader lands of Kalimdor, guarded by sheer cliffs and treacherous crags. Few travelers from Auberdine ever dare scramble along these jagged heights, leaving the path quiet, secretive, and veiled behind natural barriers.",sp=0},{t="The Way to the Vale",b="Beyond this steep, rugged approach lies Shatterspear Vale, home to an enigmatic settlement of jungle trolls known as the Shatterspear. Because the night elves keep a watchful eye across Darkshore, the pass functions as a vital threshold, maintaining the tribe's complete seclusion from the outside world. To reach the secluded vale, one must brave the jagged rocks and hidden ways where few outsiders are ever permitted to walk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Shatterspear Pass lead?",a="The pass cuts directly through the high mountains on the eastern edge of Darkshore, leading inward toward the remote, hidden settlement within Shatterspear Vale.",al={"where does pass go","pass destination","shatterspear pass path"}},{q="Who controls Shatterspear Pass right now?",a="At present, the pass is essentially wild, sealed, and untouched. It sits quietly within the mountainous perimeter claimed by the Shatterspear tribe, well away from active night elf or Horde encampments.",al={"who owns shatterspear pass","who lives in pass","pass guards"}},{q="Can ordinary travelers simply walk through the pass?",a="No. The passage is largely impassable and sealed off behind steep, unpaved terrain and perilous cliffs. Reaching it requires navigating extreme wilderness that keeps the valley beyond isolated from typical travelers.",al={"can i walk to shatterspear vale","is the pass open","pass entrance"}},{q="Are the night elves aware of the pass?",a="The Sentinels patrol Darkshore diligently, but their focus remains on local coastal threats and corruption. The high mountain crags of the pass remain remote, neglected, and obscure to everyday patrols.",al={"do night elves know about pass","sentinels at pass","darkshore elves pass"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei defending Darkshore, the jagged eastern peaks represent a quiet boundary that keeps strange, isolated threats locked far away from their woodland sanctuaries.",["race:Troll"]="To trolls who know Kalimdor's secrets, the hidden passage represents an enigmatic refuge where distant kin dwell far removed from the rest of the world."},kw={"darkshore","mountain","pass","passage","shatterspear","troll","vale"},rel={"subzone:shatterspear-vale","zone:darkshore","topic:troll","topic:sentinels","topic:horde"},src={"Shatterspear Pass"}}
E["subzone:shatterspear-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Shatterspear Vale",z="darkshore",s="Shatterspear Vale is a hidden valley tucked deep in the jagged mountains between Darkshore, Moonglade, and Felwood. It houses an isolated village of the Shatterspear troll tribe, living quietly around a secluded mountain lake. Largely sealed off from the wider world by sheer cliffs, it remains one of the most enigmatic settlements in northern Kalimdor.",h="Shatterspear Vale is a hidden valley tucked deep in the jagged mountains between Darkshore, Moonglade, and...",sec={{t="A Secluded Sanctuary",b="Ringed completely by steep mountain cliffs, Shatterspear Vale was carved over millennia by a towering waterfall that cascades into a wide, gray-blue lake. Scattered around the shoreline are simple wooden huts, fishing tents, and carved tribal dwellings. Split into two halves by a tumbling mountain river crossed by a rope bridge, the settlement feels entirely isolated from the tumultuous politics of modern Kalimdor. Flight paths connecting northern Kalimdor to Nighthaven in Moonglade occasionally offer passing travelers a fleeting aerial glimpse of the vibrant, dancing villagers far below.",sp=0},{t="An Uneasy Truce",b="The Shatterspear tribe originally split from the ancient Gurubashi Empire following the fall of Hakkar the Soulflayer, wandering far north until settling in this verdant basin. To survive in lands claimed by the night elves, the tribe struck an ancient pact: they were permitted to dwell unmolested so long as they remained strictly within their hidden vale. Should they leave, or should disaster strike them, the elves pledged no aid. To this day, the Shatterspear maintain their insular existence, friendly toward emissaries of the Horde yet wary of outsiders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Shatterspear Vale located?",a="The vale is nestled high in the mountain ridge bordering Darkshore, Moonglade, Felwood, and Winterspring. It is virtually enclosed by sheer cliffs and has no established road connecting it to the lowlands of Darkshore.",al={"shatterspear village location","where is the troll village in darkshore","how to get to shatterspear vale"}},{q="Who lives in Shatterspear Vale?",a="It is home to the Shatterspear tribe, a splinter group of jungle trolls who migrated north centuries ago following the defeat of Hakkar the Soulflayer in the ancient Gurubashi Empire.",al={"who lives here","what tribe is this","shatterspear tribe"}},{q="Why don't the night elves attack them?",a="The Shatterspear trolls established a historic pact with the local night elves. They agreed to remain entirely confined to their isolated valley and mind their own affairs; in exchange, the Kaldorei left them in peace, neither aiding nor harassing them.",al={"why night elves allow trolls here","night elf troll truce"}},{q="How can you view the village?",a="Adventurers traveling on flight paths to or from Nighthaven in Moonglade can often look down into the gorge and spot the village huts, the waterfall, and dancing trolls below.",al={"see troll village flight path","flight path view of village"}},{q="Are the Shatterspear trolls hostile?",a="The Shatterspear villagers are friendly toward members of the Horde, though they remain neutral and cautious toward the Alliance, defending their valley fiercely if provoked.",al={"are shatterspear trolls friendly","can horde visit shatterspear"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="The Shatterspear demonstrate that jungle trolls migrated far beyond Stranglethorn Vale, having managed to survive surrounded on all sides by suspicious night elves.",["race:NightElf"]="While your people generally harbor an ancient enmity toward all trolls, an exception was made for the Shatterspear, bound by a strict agreement that they never stray from their valley."},kw={"darkshore","jungle trolls","kaldorei pact","moonglade","shatterspear vale","shatterspear village","trolls","waterfall"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:nighthaven","zone:felwood","zone:winterspring","topic:troll","topic:night-elf","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Shatterspear Vale"}}
E["subzone:shatterspear-war-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Shatterspear War Camp",z="darkshore",s="The Shatterspear War Camp is a fortified encampment situated along the northern coastline of Darkshore, just north of the Ruins of Mathystra. Built and manned by the Shatterspear trolls alongside allied Horde Enforcers, the outpost serves as an aggressive staging ground encroaching deep into night elf territory. Equipped with coastal docks and holding pens for night elf prisoners, it poses a direct military threat to the surrounding region.",h="The Shatterspear War Camp is a fortified encampment situated along the northern coastline of Darkshore, just...",sec={{t="Frontier Encroachment",b="Perched on the northern bluffs and shorelines of Darkshore, the Shatterspear War Camp represents an overt military thrust by the Shatterspear tribe from their secluded home in Shatterspear Vale. Supported by veteran orc and tauren Horde Enforcers, the camp bristles with axe-throwers, mystics, and laborers fortifying the perimeter. Down by the water, a bustling dock allows the garrison to receive supplies and reinforce their beachfront hold, placing a hostile force directly on the doorstep of ancient kaldorei holdings.",sp=0},{t="Captives of the Shore",b="Beyond acting as a forward base of operations, the war camp serves a grim secondary purpose as an interrogation site. The Shatterspear have captured local night elves wandering or defending the surrounding woods, including figures like Sentinel Aynasha and Alanndarian Nightsong. Under the watch of tribal torturers and enforcers, these captives are held under guard, making the stockade a critical flashpoint for Sentinel resistance operating in northern Darkshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Shatterspear War Camp?",a="It is a fortified military base situated north of the Ruins of Mathystra in northern Darkshore. It is operated by the Shatterspear troll tribe with the backing of orc and tauren enforcers.",al={"what is this camp","shatterspear camp","who owns shatterspear war camp"}},{q="Why are there Horde troops here in Darkshore?",a="The Shatterspear trolls have allied with the broader Horde, utilizing orc and tauren military muscle to expand their influence out of the mountains and establish a forward military foothold along the coast.",al={"why is horde in darkshore","why are orcs here","horde presence"}},{q="Who is being held prisoner in the camp?",a="The camp holds several captured night elves, notably Sentinel Aynasha and Alanndarian Nightsong, who are guarded closely by tribal captors and Horde combatants.",al={"night elf prisoners","who is captured","captives in camp"}},{q="Where did the Shatterspear trolls come from?",a="The tribe hails from Shatterspear Vale, a secluded mountain valley tucked away in the rugged heights between Darkshore and northern Kalimdor.",al={"shatterspear origin","where do these trolls live","troll home"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The camp is a grave threat on the northern frontier of Darkshore, demanding swift action to liberate captured Sentinels and check tribal expansion.",["faction:Horde"]="The war camp serves as a vital forward staging ground and beachhead, demonstrating the reach of the Horde's allies along the northern coast."},kw={"aynasha","darkshore","enforcer","mathystra","nightsong","shatterspear","troll","war camp"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:shatterspear-vale","subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","npc:sentinel-aynasha","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","topic:horde","topic:troll","topic:night-elf"},src={"Shatterspear War Camp"}}
E["subzone:tower-of-althalaxx"] = {t="subzone",n="Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient Highborne spire standing in northern Darkshore near the coast. Once an isolated retreat for the sorcerer Athrikus Narassin before the Great Sundering, it has become infested by demonic cultists and warlocks practicing dark arts.",h="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient Highborne spire standing in northern Darkshore near the coast.",sec={{t="A Highborne Retreat",b="Ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara settled favored Highborne servants in the coastal towns of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran, placing the powerful sorcerer Athrikus Narassin in authority over them. Growing distant from civic governance, Athrikus chose to isolate himself within the nearby Tower of Althalaxx. When the Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor, the tower endured along the desolate coastline of Darkshore, standing as a quiet ruin of forgotten elven magics.",sp=0},{t="The Dark Strand",b="In the modern era, the tower has stirred with malignant sorcery. Warlocks, dark cultists calling themselves the Cult of the Dark Strand, and allied satyrs have congregated within the ruin under the leadership of Athrikus Narassin himself. Their rites channel demonic magic and torment the lingering spirits of the ancient dead, serving sinister designs tied directly to the demonic Shadow Council.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="It is an ancient elven mage tower built in northern Darkshore during the reign of Queen Azshara, now occupied by dark sorcerers and cultists.",al={"tower of althalaxx","althalaxx tower","what is althalaxx"}},{q="Who originally built and lived in the tower?",a="Athrikus Narassin, a powerful Highborne sorcerer appointed by Queen Azshara to oversee the nearby settlements of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran, retreated here when he grew bored of his duties.",al={"who lived here","athrikus narassin","who built the tower"}},{q="Who are the cultists occupying the tower now?",a="They belong to the Cult of the Dark Strand, a sect of warlocks, cultists, and satyrs operating in service to the Shadow Council under Athrikus's leadership.",al={"who are the cultists","cult of the dark strand","althalaxx enemies"}},{q="Why are there ghosts and tortured spirits here?",a="The cultists conduct dark rituals and soul-binding magic, subjecting the long-dead elven spirits of ancient Darkshore to agonizing torment for their spells.",al={"why are there ghosts","tortured spirits althalaxx"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The tower represents a grim reminder of Highborne corruption and demonic folly lingering on ancestral lands, demanding swift intervention from Darnassus.",["class:Warlock"]="The dark rites conducted by the Cult of the Dark Strand demonstrate the far-reaching influence and lingering presence of the Shadow Council in Kalimdor."},kw={"althalaxx","ameth'aran","athrikus narassin","bashal'aran","dark strand","darkshore","highborne","satyr","shadow council"},rel={"quest:965","zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","quest:954","topic:highborne","topic:shadow-council","topic:satyr","topic:alliance"},src={"Tower of Althalaxx"}}
E["subzone:twilight-shore-darkshore"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Shore (Darkshore)",z="darkshore",s="The Twilight Shore is a rugged stretch of coast in southern Darkshore, running south from the Long Wash down to the border of Ashenvale. Its gloomy, mist-laden beaches are interrupted by jutting sea cliffs, offshore islets, and treacherous surf. The area is infested with aggressive murloc tribes and ravenous aquatic predators like threshadons.",h="The Twilight Shore is a rugged stretch of coast in southern Darkshore, running south from the Long Wash down...",sec={{t="A Treacherous Coastline",b="Stretching south of the Long Wash past the ruins of Ameth'Aran toward Ashenvale, the Twilight Shore is among the most rugged and inhospitable parts of Darkshore's coastline. Gray sand gives way to sharp, wave-battered cliffs and scattered rocky islands. The waters here are notoriously hostile; swimming off the coast invites attacks from territorial threshadons and sea crawlers, while the beaches themselves are dominated by thriving camps of aggressive murlocs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Twilight Shore located?",a="It encompasses the southernmost coastal strip of Darkshore, beginning south of the Long Wash (roughly west of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran) and continuing southward until reaching the rocky borders of Ashenvale.",al={"twilight shore location","where is twilight shore","twilight shore map"}},{q="What threats can be found along the Twilight Shore?",a="The shoreline is heavily settled by aggressive murloc tribes, while the surrounding cold surf is home to territorial threshadons, lurkers, and giant crabs that prey upon unwary travelers.",al={"twilight shore mobs","dangers at twilight shore","what is at twilight shore"}},{q="Why is the terrain so rugged here?",a="Unlike the flatter, expansive beaches farther north, the Twilight Shore is fragmented by sharp sea cliffs, rocky shoals, and small offshore islands shaped by the relentless pounding of the Veiled Sea.",al={"why are there cliffs","twilight shore geography"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Twilight Shore marks the lonely, mist-shrouded threshold between the haunted ruins of Darkshore and the sacred ancestral forests of Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","coast","darkshore","long wash","murlocs","threshadons","twilight shore"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:long-wash","zone:ashenvale","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:murloc"},src={"Twilight Shore (Darkshore)"}}
E["subzone:twilight-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Vale",z="darkshore",s="Twilight Vale encompasses the dense, shadowed southern woodlands of Darkshore stretching toward the Ashenvale border. Beneath its gloom, corrupted furbolgs, rabid bears, and vicious nightsabers prowl the undergrowth, making off-road passage perilous. It serves as a grim threshold between the tainted coast of Darkshore and the sacred canopies to the south.",h="Twilight Vale encompasses the dense, shadowed southern woodlands of Darkshore stretching toward the Ashenvale...",sec={{t="A Perilous Threshold",b="Running from the south of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran all the way to the border of Ashenvale, the Twilight Vale blankets the southern reaches of Darkshore in perpetual dusk. The encroaching corruption plaguing northern Kalimdor has bitten deep into the wildlife here. Rabid bears roam alongside feral nightsabers, and hostile furbolg tribes stalk the dark wood. Sentinels and travelers alike advise sticking strictly to the main road, as straying even a few paces into the trees invites swift and deadly ambushes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Twilight Vale located?",a="Twilight Vale forms the southern portion of Darkshore. It begins just south of the highborne ruins of Ameth'Aran and extends all the way to the border pass that enters Ashenvale.",al={"twilight vale location","where is twilight vale","twilight vale map"}},{q="What threats wander this forest?",a="The vale is infested with afflicted wildlife and hostile tribes. Travelers will encounter rabid bears, aggressive nightsabers, and corrupted furbolgs who attack anyone intruding upon their territory.",al={"twilight vale monsters","what is in twilight vale","danger twilight vale"}},{q="Is it safe to travel through the vale?",a="No wilderness in Darkshore is entirely safe, but sticking firmly to the established dirt road is far safer than cutting through the underbrush. Straying off the beaten track puts you directly in the path of feral beasts.",al={"is twilight vale safe","safe path darkshore to ashenvale"}},{q="Why is the wildlife in the vale corrupted?",a="Darkshore has suffered heavily since the Third War and the sundering magic lingering across northern Kalimdor. Tainted water and dark magical residue have maddened the local wildlife and turned peaceful furbolgs violent.",al={"why are bears rabid in darkshore","furbolg corruption twilight vale"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The degradation of the southern woods weighs heavily on the night elves, who mourn the corruption of the native beasts and the fall of their furbolg neighbors so close to Ashenvale's threshold.",["class:Druid"]="Druids passing between Darkshore and Ashenvale witness firsthand the sickness afflicting the vale's creatures, underscoring the urgent need to cleanse the land."},kw={"ameth'aran","ashenvale","darkshore","furbolgs","nightsabers","rabid bears","twilight vale"},rel={"zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:furbolg","topic:druid","topic:alliance"},src={"Twilight Vale"}}
E["subzone:wildbend-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Wildbend River",z="darkshore",s="Wildbend River is a tainted waterway winding through the southern forests of Darkshore near the Grove of the Ancients. Flowing down directly from the corrupted heights of Felwood, its waters carry demonic poison toward the sea, endangering the surrounding wilderness.",h="Wildbend River is a tainted waterway winding through the southern forests of Darkshore near the Grove of the...",sec={{t="A Toxic Mountain Stream",b="Wildbend River cuts through the southern reaches of Darkshore, flowing westward past the sacred Grove of the Ancients before emptying into the sea. Rather than offering clean nourishment to the woodland, it brings corruption down from the mountains. The river is the direct continuation of Felwood's Bloodvenom River, tumbling through the rocky ridges and dragging foul, corrupted runoff into Darkshore's ecosystem. The night elves monitor its banks closely, watching for twisted wildlife and the creeping spread of demonic blight.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Wildbend River corrupted?",a="The river originates high in the mountains of Felwood, where it is known as the Bloodvenom River. Felwood was thoroughly saturated with demonic magic during the Third War, and that foul runoff spills down the cliffs into Darkshore as the Wildbend River.",al={"why is water tainted","wildbend river poison","darkshore dirty water"}},{q="Where does the river flow?",a="Cascading down from the eastern ridges that separate Felwood from Darkshore, the river winds through southern Darkshore near the Grove of the Ancients before flowing into the Veiled Sea.",al={"where is wildbend river","wildbend path","wildbend river location"}},{q="Does the river affect the Grove of the Ancients?",a="The river passes close to the Grove of the Ancients, posing a constant environmental threat to the ancient protectors rooted there. The night elves work tirelessly to contain the blight and prevent the poisoned water from rotting the sacred groves.",al={"grove of the ancients water","is grove of ancients corrupted"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The polluted waters cascading from Felwood threaten the ancient roots of Darkshore, making the riverbanks a frequent concern for night elf wardens.",["class:Druid"]="Druids studying the ecological aftermath of the Third War keep a wary eye on the river, monitoring how deeply Felwood's corruption penetrates downstream flora and fauna."},kw={"bloodvenom river","darkshore","felwood","grove of the ancients","tainted water","wildbend river"},rel={"zone:darkshore","zone:felwood","subzone:bloodvenom-river","quest:952"},src={"Wildbend River"}}
E["subzone:withering-thicket"] = {t="subzone",n="Withering Thicket",z="darkshore",s="The Withering Thicket is a shadowed stretch of woodland nestled along the coast of Darkshore north of Auberdine. Haunted by native predators like moonstalkers, the thicket reflects the lingering distress and sorrow that burdens northern Kalimdor's wilderness.",h="The Withering Thicket is a shadowed stretch of woodland nestled along the coast of Darkshore north of...",sec={{t="A Troubled Woodland",b="Located along Darkshore's mist-shrouded coast just north of the port settlement of Auberdine, the Withering Thicket embodies the uneasy quiet of the coastal forests. Densely shaded by ancient boughs, the area is prowled by fierce moonstalkers and other native beasts. Like much of Darkshore in the wake of the Third War, the land carries a subtle gloom, demanding wariness from travelers venturing off the main paths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Withering Thicket located?",a="The Withering Thicket lies in northern Darkshore, set along the coast just north of the night elf harbor settlement of Auberdine.",al={"withering thicket location","where is withering thicket","how to get to withering thicket"}},{q="What creatures are found in the Withering Thicket?",a="The woods are primarily home to native wildlife, most notably predatory moonstalkers that stalk the shaded coastal terrain.",al={"withering thicket mobs","creatures in withering thicket","what lives in withering thicket"}},{q="Why is the thicket called 'Withering'?",a="Much of Darkshore suffers from persistent ecological decay and corruption following the Third War, giving many of its groves and coastlines a sickly, faded demeanor.",al={"why is it called withering thicket","withering thicket name origin"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The uneasy balance and troubled wildlife of groves like the Withering Thicket serve as constant reminders of the ongoing healing work required across Darkshore.",["race:NightElf"]="Close to the haven of Auberdine, the Withering Thicket is part of the ancestral territory kaldorei rangers and Sentinels must vigilantly monitor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","kaldorei","kalimdor","moonstalkers","withering thicket"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:druid","topic:sentinels"},src={"Withering Thicket"}}
E["subzone:wreckage-of-the-silver-dawning"] = {t="subzone",n="Wreckage of the Silver Dawning",z="darkshore",s="The Wreckage of the Silver Dawning marks the submerged remains of an Alliance frigate resting off the northern coastline of Darkshore. Sunk by aggressive coastal murlocs while approaching port at Auberdine, its drowned hull serves as a grim testament to the hazards plaguing local shipping.",h="The Wreckage of the Silver Dawning marks the submerged remains of an Alliance frigate resting off the...",sec={{t="A Perilous Voyage Cut Short",b="Having successfully braved the perils of the Great Sea, the crew of the frigate Silver Dawning came within sight of their destination at Auberdine before tragedy struck. Rather than reef or storm, the vessel was ambushed by coastal murlocs lurking in the northern waters of Darkshore. Overwhelmed just south of the Mist Veil, the ship took on water and sank into the shallow sea floor. While some crew members managed to swim to the safety of the shore, their captain tragically went down with the ship, leaving its sunken cargo and belongings scattered in the tide.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Silver Dawning?",a="The Silver Dawning was an Alliance frigate that journeyed across the Great Sea toward Kalimdor. It was ambushed and sunk just offshore from Auberdine in northern Darkshore.",al={"what is silver dawning","silver dawning ship","wreck of silver dawning"}},{q="How did the ship sink?",a="The vessel was attacked by local murlocs as it made its final approach to port. The sea creatures overwhelmed the frigate, causing it to founder and sink into the shallows.",al={"how did it sink","who sank the silver dawning","why did silver dawning wreck"}},{q="Did anyone survive the sinking?",a="Yes, several members of the crew managed to escape into the water and swim safely to the Darkshore coast. However, the vessel's captain remained behind and drowned with the ship.",al={"any survivors","did crew survive","who lived"}},{q="Where is the wreckage located?",a="The sunken hull lies submerged in the waters off the northern coast of Darkshore, situated just south of the Mist Veil and north of Auberdine.",al={"where is it","silver dawning location","where is the shipwreck"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The loss of the Silver Dawning highlights how fragile the maritime supply and travel routes have become along the coast of Kalimdor, even within sight of friendly harbors like Auberdine."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","frigate","mist veil","murloc","shipwreck","silver dawning"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc","quest:938"},src={"Wreckage of the Silver Dawning"}}
E["zone:darkshore"] = {t="zone",n="Darkshore",z="darkshore",s="Darkshore is a cold, mist-shrouded strip of coast lining northwestern Kalimdor, dotted with ancient Kaldorei ruins and troubled wildlife. Anchored by the Alliance harbor town of Auberdine, it serves as the primary continental gateway for travelers arriving from Teldrassil and the Eastern Kingdoms. Beyond the patrolled road, demonic cults, encroaching naga, and a creeping corruption from the highlands threaten the region's delicate balance.",h="Darkshore is a cold, mist-shrouded strip of coast lining northwestern Kalimdor, dotted with ancient Kaldorei...",sec={{t="A Land of Mist and Memory",b="Stretching beneath the western shadows of Mount Hyjal and Felwood, Darkshore is characterized by pine groves, sea fog, and rocky beaches beaten by cold waves. Millennia ago, this coast was home to the flourishing Kaldorei twin cities of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran. Shattered during the Great Sundering, their skeletal pillars and marble arches now lie half-drowned in the surf or overgrown with roots, haunted by restless Highborne spirits and overrun by scavenger murlocs and invasive naga.",sp=0},{t="The Haven of Auberdine",b="Following the Third War and the planting of Teldrassil, the night elves established Auberdine as a bustling maritime haven amidst the wilderness. Featuring wooden piers that welcome regular vessels from Rut'theran Village and Menethil Harbor in the distant Wetlands, Auberdine is the lifeline linking night elf territory to the rest of the Alliance. Sentinels diligently patrol the trade highway south toward Ashenvale, though their small garrison struggles to police the deep wilds beyond the path.",sp=0},{t="Poisoned Waters and Whispering Depths",b="Despite its shelter against the eastern mountains, Darkshore suffers from a slow, malignant rot. Corrupted run-off trickling down from Felwood poisons sources like Cliffspring Falls, fouling the water table and driving the local bears, stags, and furbolgs of Blackwood Den into violent madness. Worse still, sinister organizations have established footholds in the shadows: the Dark Strand and Twilight's Hammer cultists perform foul rituals at the Tower of Althalaxx and convene around the terrifying, ancient monument known as the Master's Glaive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to Darkshore?",a="Alliance players can take a boat directly to Auberdine from either Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil or from Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Horde travelers journeying north must walk through Ashenvale, following the main road northeast from Zoram'gar Outpost up across the border.",al={"getting to darkshore","how to reach auberdine","darkshore boat"}},{q="What is wrong with the local wildlife and furbolgs?",a="Rivers running out of the tainted heights of Felwood, such as the Cliffspring River, wash demonic pollution straight down into Darkshore's water table. Drinking from these foul streams has driven the native furbolg tribes feral and infected the local deer and predators with disease and aggression.",al={"why are animals sick","furbolg corruption","darkshore taint"}},{q="What happened to Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran?",a="They were prosperous twin Kaldorei cities destroyed ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering. Their ruler, Athrikus Narassin, claimed he would rescue his people from the cataclysm, but he instead bound their souls into gems to preserve them as eternal power sources for himself, leaving the ruins full of weeping ghosts.",al={"ameth'aran history","bashal'aran lore","ruins in darkshore"},sp=1},{q="What is the Master's Glaive?",a="Located in southern Darkshore, the Master's Glaive is a massive petrified skull impaled by an enormous stone weapon. It is an ancient relic associated with the primordial Old Gods and their servitors, and it currently attracts dangerous cultists from the Twilight's Hammer.",al={"what is the masters glaive","giant skull darkshore","masters glaive monster"}},{q="Who is the giant tree in the Grove of the Ancients?",a="That is Onu, a wise and venerable Ancient of Lore. Resting in his tranquil grove south of Auberdine, he ponders the disturbing encroachment of the Twilight's Hammer cult and assists travelers in investigating disturbances throughout the forest.",al={"ancient of lore darkshore","who is onu","tree person darkshore"}},{q="Who lives in the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The tower is occupied by the Dark Strand, a vicious cult practicing dark sorcery and summoning demonic entities. Their cabal actively ambushes unwary travelers along the northern reaches of the coastal woods.",al={"tower of althalaxx","darkshore tower cultists","althalaxx cult"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Darkshore serves as the front line for Cenarion Circle initiates answering summons from Moonglade to diagnose tainted waterways and brew cleansers for sick forest creatures.",["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves leaving Teldrassil, Darkshore is their first step onto mainland Kalimdor, confronting the painful ruins of their ancient civilization and the spreading corruption of the wild.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine represents the Alliance's primary trade nexus in northern Kalimdor, maintaining the direct maritime link connecting Stormwind and Ironforge to the night elf capital of Darnassus.",["faction:Horde"]="A remote, heavily patrolled Alliance bastion, Darkshore sits directly north of Horde encampments in Ashenvale, offering a treacherous coastline prowled by hostile sentinels and dangerous cults."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","bashal'aran","blackwood den","cliffspring falls","darkshore","master's glaive","onu","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","subzone:ameth-aran","subzone:master-s-glaive","quest:952","quest:965","quest:6122","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:ashenvale"},m={levels="10-20"},src={"Darkshore (Classic)","Darkshore"}}
